tml', 'snippet': 'The Rams earned their program-record 12th victory by beating Sacred Heart, 37-27, in a Football Championship Subdivision playoff game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reminders of the glory days of Fordham football are everywhere. The famed Seven Blocks of Granite are honored with a monument erected in 2008. Vince Lombardi, a guard on that unit and later a renowned coach, will forever be celebrated as a towering figure in the university’s history.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Fordham, a Special Season Lives On ', 'kicker': 'Fordham 37, Sacred Heart 27', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Fordham, a Special Season Lives On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pedulla, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fordham University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sacred Heart University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T00:47:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98c8a3cc-ab66-5476-a194-3749f36eb349', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98c8a3cc-ab66-5476-a194-3749f36eb349'}, {'abstract': 'New zoning rules will open northwestern Mexico’s agricultural heartland to denser housing and golf courses, but there is concern that the Guadalupe Valley cannot sustain this intensified development.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/world/americas/a-rustic-paradise-open-for-development.html', 'snippet': 'New zoning rules will open northwestern Mexico’s agricultural heartland to denser housing and golf courses, but there is concern that the Guadalupe Valley cannot sustain this intensified development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUADALUPE VALLEY, Mexico — The doors were locked. The lights were out. When Hugo D’Acosta and 60 of his neighbors reached Ensenada City Hall after being tipped off to a nighttime vote that would open their beloved wine region to Florida-style housing and golf courses, they had to shout just to get in.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/world/bull-baja1/bull-baja1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/world/bull-baja1/bull-baja1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/world/bull-baja1/bull-baja1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/world/bull-baja1/bull-baja1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/world/bull-baja1/bull-baja1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/world/bull-baja1/bull-baja1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/world/bull-baja1/bull-baja1-thumbL