ited States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ShopperTrak', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T01:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cca2a719-a14f-551b-a5ff-43b1f1408996', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cca2a719-a14f-551b-a5ff-43b1f1408996'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks have lost eight straight games, their longest stretch since 2010, and have been left with little by which to assess their progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/sports/basketball/knicks-find-solace-in-quality-of-losses.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks have lost eight straight games, their longest stretch since 2010, and have been left with little by which to assess their progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — The mood lifted in the Knicks’ locker room after Friday night’s game here. Raymond Felton said that they had “turned this thing around.” Carmelo Anthony said he could sense “the trust in one another out there.” J. R. Smith seemed relieved that the Knicks were “getting over the hump.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 782}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sports/knicks-1/knicks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'heig