426e4fdb-0b0c-55b1-9f72-1d64245ddd14'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe discusses the challenges facing Blackberry, H.P. and Cisco.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-nov-29-2013/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe discusses the challenges facing Blackberry, H.P. and Cisco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of iconic companies in the tech sector like H.P., Cisco and Blackberry have been struggling recently. This week on Money Talking, regular contributors Joe Nocera and Rana Foroohar of Time magazine consider if the challenges are the result of problems at the company or external forces. Are these tech companies canaries in the coal mine for an impending stock market correction? Also, a look ahead to a Supreme Court case involving Halliburton, and how sanctions being lifted in Iran could affect that country’s economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s “Money Talking”: Nov. 29, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T01:36:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b93e1ad-d091-52ab-8f10-ccdb0c1272a3', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b93e1ad-d091-52ab-8f10-ccdb0c1272a3'}, {'abstract': 'Alabama was ambushed by Auburn on a last-second, length-of-the-field runback on the Crimson Tide’s fourth missed field-goal attempt of the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/sports/ncaafootball/one-second-dooms-no-1-alabama.html', 'snippet': 'Alabama was ambushed by Auburn on a last-second, length-of-the-field runback on the Crimson Tide