mber 1, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/pageoneplus/corrections-december-1-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on December 1, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: December 1, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T08:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46c4dc97-1d55-598c-b54e-1ec8a5274002', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46c4dc97-1d55-598c-b54e-1ec8a5274002'}, {'abstract': 'Many of the women who visit slum health-care facilities can’t consider family planning until they’re persuaded that the children they have will survive.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/in-areas-where-children-die-young-family-planning-is-a-hard-sell/', 'snippet': 'Many of the women who visit slum health-care facilities can’t consider family planning until they’re persuaded that the children they have will survive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nairobi, Kenya There are a variety of reasons why women in traditional or less-developed societies give birth to many children: religious, cultural, economic, status and lack of adequate information. But one reason that seems so obvious once you think about it — but which seldom tops the list — is the fear that the children they do bear might not survive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/style/motherlode-jane-otai/motherlode-jane-otai-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xla