ps://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/us/politics/obama-administration-says-health-care-web-site-is-vastly-improved.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of software fixes and hardware upgrades later, the administration said that as many as 50,000 people can now use HealthCare.gov simultaneously.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration said on Sunday that it had met its goal for improving HealthCare.gov so that the website now “will work smoothly for the vast majority of users.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/us/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/us/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/us/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/us/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/us/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/27/us/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/us/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3/20131130_HEALTH-slide-GAG3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Administration Says Health Care Website Is Vastly Improved', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zients, Jeffrey D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebelius, Kathleen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T15:17:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225c90c5-2c73-56b8-bdec-3b0ec1b2bfed', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225c90c5-2c73-56b8-bdec-3b0ec1b2bfed'}, {'abstract': 'Wrong predictions matter.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/inflationistas-at-bayes/', 'snippet': 'Wrong predictions matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m putting together a syllabus for one of the courses I’ll be teaching this spring – Econ 348, The Great Recession – and in the course of searching for various views about inflation, ended up looking at a dispute from a while back involving some of the usual suspects. Brad DeLong poked fun at John Cochrane for having declared, back in 2009, that “the danger now is inflation.” Cochrane angrily denied that this was of any significance – he only said that it was a danger, he didn’t necessarily predict that it would happen within any particular time frame. (He thereby provided a demonstration of another key fact about our economic debate: nobody ever admits that they were wrong about anything, and nobody changes views in the light of evidence.) Noah Smith, characteristically, tried to find some extenuating circumstances. Etc., etc.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflationistas at Bayes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T15:39:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9f8824c-2738-5521-a6ff-80aa093496ef', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9f8824c-2738-5521-a6ff-80aa093496ef'}, {'abstract': 'If the mission succeeds, China will be the third country to achieve a “soft” landing on the moon, one that allows a craft to operate after descending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/world/asia/china-prepares-to-launch-moon-rover-mission.html', 'snippet': 'If the mission succeeds, China will be the third country to achieve a “soft” landing on the moon, one that allows a craft to operate after descending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — China’s latest display of ambition in space involves sending a Jade Rabbit roaming ac