view', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf9cac9-41f9-52f1-9721-9b39ca5481f1', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf9cac9-41f9-52f1-9721-9b39ca5481f1'}, {'abstract': 'In a much-needed course corrective, many women have begun taking a more laissez-faire approach to that most private of regions.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/on-beauty-for-women-a-new-look-down-under/', 'snippet': 'In a much-needed course corrective, many women have begun taking a more laissez-faire approach to that most private of regions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of razors, wax and lasers reducing pubic hair to the bare minimum — or nothing at all — there’s a return to a more natural state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Beauty | For Women, a New Look Down Under', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T22:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7306db0-a692-57d3-8ae5-1602d80a39c0', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7306db0-a692-57d3-8ae5-1602d80a39c0'}, {'abstract': 'An updated Elvis Presley exhibit at the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and Museum in Cleveland has opened featuring more than 40 artifacts on loan from his Graceland Mansion in Memphis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/arts/music/updated-presley-exhibit-features-graceland-items.html', 'snippet': 'An updated Elvis Presley exhibit at the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and Museum in Cleveland has opened featuring more than 40 artifacts on loan from his Graceland Mansion in Memphis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An updated Elvis Presley exhibit at the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and Museum in Cleveland has opened featuring more than 40 artifacts on loan from his Graceland Mansion in Memphis, The Associated Press reported. Highlights include a 1975 custom-made “SuperTrike” motorcycle; a selection of Presley’s jewelry, like a walnut-size 41-carat ruby-and-diamond ring and a 25.5-carat opal ring; and a white suit he wore during the NBC special “Elvis” in 1968. Presley was among the first class of artists to be inducted into the hall of fame, in 1986.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updated Presley Exhibit Features Graceland Items', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Updated Presley Exhibit Features Graceland Items', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Presley, Elvis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T22:43:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d41ef220-5bb5-5082-8759-47e738b55bb9', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d41ef220-5bb5-5082-8759-47e738b55bb9'}, {'abstract': 'Account assignments, executive appointments and miscellaneous news from advertising agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/business/media/news-from-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Account assignments, executive appointments and miscellaneous news from advertising agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Accounts', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News From the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News From the Advertising Industry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-01T22:47:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9b97226-8bd2-5f88-abe4-22aa511f8aee', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9b97226-8bd2-5f88-abe4-22aa511f8aee'}, {'abstract': 'A mixed breed dog named Elwood, who was named the “World’s Ugliest Dog” in 2007 and inspired his owner to write a children’s book about self-acceptance, has died, The Associated Press reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/arts/rest-in-peace-elwood-worlds-ugliest-dog.html', 'snippet': 'A mixed breed dog named Elwood, who was named the “World’s Ugliest Dog” in 2007 and inspired his owner to write a children’s book about self-acceptance, has died, The Associated Press reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mixed breed dog named Elwood (below), who was named the “World’s Ugliest Dog” in 2007 and inspired his owner to write a children’s book about self-acceptance, has died, The Associated Press reported. He was 8 years old. Karen Quigley, 52, of Sewell, N.J., adopted Elwood, a dark-colored, nearly hairless Chinese crested and Chihuahua mix, after a breeder decided that he was too ugly to sell and would euthanize him. His odd appearance, which included heavy eyelids, a protruded tongue that hung out the side of his mouth and a white tuft of hair on his head, was a hit at the Sonoma-Marin County Fair in California, where the ugly dog contest is held. The experience motivated Ms. Quigley to write and self-publish a children’s book that promoted acceptance called “Everybody Loves Elwood.” The dog later developed an online following, being referred to as Yoda or E.T. by his fans. Elwood appeared at more than 200 events to help raise money for animal rescue groups and nonprofit animal organizations.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/arts2/arts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/arts2/arts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 670}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/arts2/arts2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 917, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/arts2/arts2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1834, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/arts2/arts2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rest in Peace, El