bat, may be an advantage. | November is shaping up to be the month that puts many hedge funds solidly in the black for the year. | T-Mobile’s chief executive is shaking up the mobile in...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael L. Corbat has kept a relatively low profile since taking the helm of Citigroup in October 2012. And that appears to be just fine with the bank he runs, Susanne Craig and Jessica Silver-Greenberg report in DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citigroup’s Low-Key Chief', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T13:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f90b384-3844-5792-aaed-8ced6183744b', 'word_count': 1994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f90b384-3844-5792-aaed-8ced6183744b'}, {'abstract': 'Russians are looking on longingly at the early success of the protest movement in Ukraine.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/a-whiter-shade-of-envy/', 'snippet': 'Russians are looking on longingly at the early success of the protest movement in Ukraine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — In Russian, envy comes in two colors: black and white. The former is mean and resentful: “It should be me, not you.” The latter is aspirational: “I want to be you.” “Black envy” affirms a despondent world view; “white envy” affords a hopeful one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Whiter Shade of Envy', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '