laims that the insurgents, known as Boko Haram, had been pushed into remote areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/world/africa/insurgents-strike-in-major-nigerian-city.html', 'snippet': 'The attack in Maiduguri raised doubts about official claims that the insurgents, known as Boko Haram, had been pushed into remote areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The authorities in northeastern Nigeria imposed a 24-hour curfew around the region’s main city on Monday after Islamic militants staged an audacious attack apparently aimed at a government air base, news reports said, describing the assault as among the most dramatic in the insurgents’ campaign to create an Islamic state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insurgents Strike in Major Nigerian City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nigeria: Curfew Imposed After Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maiduguri (Nigeria)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T15:23:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5e4571f-bbc9-52bc-813e-a5864296ffa1', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5e4571f-bbc9-52bc-813e-a5864296ffa1'}, {'abstract': 'As the morning commute got underway on Monday, any complaints about inconvenience were tempered by the knowledge of Sunday’s deadly train accident.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/nyregion/after-fatal-crash-metro-north-commuters-reflect-on-a-daily-routine.html', 'snippet': 'As the morning commute got underway on Monday, any complaints about inconvenience were tempered by the knowledge of Sunday’s deadly train accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York commuters have had their travel plans disrupted by storms, delayed by power failures and slowed by equipment malfunctions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Fatal Crash, Metro-North Commuters Reflect on a Daily Routine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-North Commuter Railroad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T15:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora and Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f97223-86fe-53a7-8552-3162133796dc', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f97223-86fe-53a7-8552-3162133796dc'}, {'abstract': 'Fatalities have more than tripled this year, making the country by far the most dangerous place in the world for relief work, according to United Nations officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/world/asia/attacks-rise-on-aid-workers-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Fatalities have more than tripled this year, making the country by far the most dangerous place in the world for relief work, according to United Nations officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The number of aid workers killed in Afghanistan has more than tripled this year, making the country by far the most dangerous place in the world for relief work, according to data released by United Nations officials here.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1340, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub