nadian Opera Company in Toronto has commissioned Mr. Wainwright’s second opera, “Hadrian.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rufus Wainwright’s experience in the opera world may have seemed bruising to an observer. His first opera, “Prima Donna,” was commissioned by the Metropolitan Opera and Lincoln Center, but the Met withdrew when Mr. Wainwright insisted on writing in French instead of English; and though it was performed around the world, and by the New York City Opera at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, it was beat upon by critics for the thinness of its plot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-rufus/02artsbeat-rufus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-rufus/02artsbeat-rufus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 875}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-rufus/02artsbeat-rufus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-rufus/02artsbeat-rufus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1404, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-rufus/02artsbeat-rufus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-rufus/02artsbeat-rufus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':