tests in the streets of their capital. As my colleague Thomas Fuller writes, the miniature drones have circulated videos of the battles, including one between riot police outside the prime minister’s office and protesters attacking the barricades. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Thailand, a Drone’s Eye View of Protests', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T19:56:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e24035-b442-59eb-8017-5ea4c5269e47', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e24035-b442-59eb-8017-5ea4c5269e47'}, {'abstract': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: a book of maps designed to get you delightfully lost.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/holiday-the-daily-gift-visual-editions-where-you-are/', 'snippet': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: a book of maps designed to get you delightfully lost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday | The Daily Gift: Visual Editions’ ‘Where You Are’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T19:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Haramis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haramis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8e5fb6f-adcd-514d-9b2d-8218b868d01d', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8e5fb6f-adcd-514d-9b2d-8218b868d01d'}, {'abstract': 'A holiday weekend in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/the-gun-report-thanksgiving-weekend-edition/', 'snippet': 'A holiday weekend in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marissa Alexander, the Florida woman who unsuccessfully argued last year that the state’s Stand Your Ground law made her immune from prosecution after she fired a\xa0bullet into a wall in her home\xa0to scare off her abusive husband, has been released from prison as she awaits a new trial. Though no one was hurt, she received a 20-year prison sentence. Alexander had argued that she fired a warning shot from a legally licensed gun to defend herself from a beating at the hands of her estranged husband, a man who had testified to abusing her in the past.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: Thanksgiving Weekend Edition', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T20:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiza