/12/02/new-strides-in-spaying-and-neutering/', 'snippet': 'Nonsurgical sterilization treatments for dogs and cats are emerging that could reduce or even eliminate the need for traditional neutering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Todd Bruce, a herd manager on a farm in Oregon City, Ore., had long resisted neutering his 5-year-old Australian cattle dog, Cody, for fear of losing the extra set (or two) of legs in the field.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/science/03NEUT_SPAN/03NEUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/science/03NEUT_SPAN/03NEUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/science/03NEUT_SPAN/03NEUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/science/03NEUT_SPAN/03NEUT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1390, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/science/03NEUT_SPAN/03NEUT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/03/science/03NEUT_SPAN/03NEUT_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/science/03NEUT_SPAN/03NEUT_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Strides in Spaying and Neutering', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Approach to an Old Pet Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterinary Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T20:17:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ab360b-db21-582c-86ae-9e4aef155ae8', 'word_count': 1264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ab360b-db21-582c-86ae-9e4aef155ae8'}, {'abstract': 'My son’s kindergarten report card brought out the worst in me.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/a-first-report-card-fails-to-exceed-expectations/', 'snippet': 'My son’s kindergarten report card brought out the worst in me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t compare yourself to others. Let go of striving and accept the world as it is, not as you’d like it to be. Practice humility and gratitude. Forty-three years, and this is the Buddhist wisdom I’ve learned to embrace, the foundation on which my inner peace rests. Until I got my son’s first report card.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A First Report Card Fails to ‘Exceed Expectations’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grading of Students', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-02T20:18:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Devorah Blachor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Devorah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blachor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/089a313e-1b4d-5df5-90a0-100c00099914', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/089a313e-1b4d-5df5-90a0-100c00099914'}, {'abstract': 'The site with rare Biblical texts went live on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/02/rare-biblical-texts-from-bodleian-and-vatican-libraries-digitized/', 'snippet': 'The site with rare Biblical texts went live on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Gutenberg Bible, a dazzlingly illuminated 15th-century Hebrew Bible from Spain and a copy of Maimonides’s 12th-century commentary on the Mishnah written in the philosopher’s own hand are among the rare bibles and biblical commentaries from the Vatican Library and the Bodleian Libraries at Oxford that have been digitized and posted online, as part of a collaboration between the institutions that went live on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-bible/02artsbeat-bible-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-bible/02artsbeat-bible-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/02/arts/02artsbeat-bible/02artsbeat-bible-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 885, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy