eatrical production.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Peter & the Wolf” quickly became a holiday tradition at the Guggenheim Museum after it was first presented in 2007. Each year, a different artist creates installations to visually interpret the tale, punctuated by the narration of Isaac Mizrahi, the fashion and design impresario. This year, for the first time, Mr. Mizrahi is transforming a concert with art and storytelling into a full theatrical production under his command: He is directing the actors and designed the set and the costumes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/PETER/PETER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/PETER/PETER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 575}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/PETER/PETER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 981, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/PETER/PETER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1962, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/PETER/PETER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/PETER/PETER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/PETER/PETER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'c