dicted Tomás Yarrington Ruvalcaba, a former governor of a Mexican state and a member of the Institutional Revolutionary Party, on racketeering and money laundering charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/world/americas/mexico-us-indicts-a-former-governor.html', 'snippet': 'The United States has indicted Tomás Yarrington Ruvalcaba, a former governor of a Mexican state and a member of the Institutional Revolutionary Party, on racketeering and money laundering charges.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States has indicted a former governor of a Mexican state that borders Texas in a case that has come to illustrate concerns over political corruption and has embarrassed the governing Institutional Revolutionary Party. Federal prosecutors on Monday unsealed the indictment charging the former official, Tomás Yarrington Ruvalcaba, who served as governor of Tamaulipas State from 1999 to 2005, with racketeering and money laundering. Mr. Yarrington, who is being sought, funneled payments from drug traffickers into Texas banks, real estate and false businesses, prosecutors said. Mr. Yarrington, a member of the Institutional Revolutionary Party, or PRI, ran for president in 2005. But he was ejected from the party in 2012 as the inquiry came to light during the presidential campaign of Enrique Peña Nieto, who promised a new PRI, free of corruption. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: U.S. Indicts a Former Governor', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: U.S. Indicts a Former Governor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racketeering and Racketeers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Laundering', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institutional Revolutionary Party (Mexico)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tamaulipas (Mexico)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yarrington Ruvalcaba, Tomas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T01:38:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/114acaa3-ca17-5dcb-91bc-0fd6e5f77a8b', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/114acaa3-ca17-5dcb-91bc-0fd6e5f77a8b'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Vincent C. Gray of Washington said Monday that he would run for re-election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/us/washington-mayor-will-seek-re-election.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Vincent C. Gray of Washington said Monday that he would run for re-election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Vincent C. Gray of Washington said Monday that he would run for re-election. A spokesman for the mayor’s office, Robert Marus, said Mr. Gray had picked up petitions to begin gathering the 2,000 signatures required to participate in the Democratic primary on April 1. Mr. Gray was elected in 2010, and his tenure has been shadowed by investigations into that campaign, which was financed in part by $650,000 that was not reported to the election authorities. Mr. Gray has denied any knowledge of wrongdoing and has never been charged with a crime, but the investigation is still open and three of the mayor’s associates have been found guilty. Mr. Gray’s decision ended months of speculation and was likely to reshape the crowded Democratic field, which includes four members of the District of Columbia Council. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington Mayor Will Seek Re-election', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor Will Seek Re-election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Siddons, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Vincent C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T01:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Siddons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siddons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e467fee5-e126-5769-ac08-5c1f13546e5b', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e467fee5-e126-5769-ac08-5c1f13546e5b'}, {'abstract': 'After a man was killed on the front steps of their school, a community of educators described the task of protecting their young students and helping them cope with tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/nyregion/new-job-after-shots-are-fired-keeping-students-feeling-safe.html', 'snippet': 'After a man was killed on the front steps of their school, a community of educators described the task of protecting their young students and helping them cope with tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a chill autumn morning, sun poured through the high windows as a young elementary school principal, Meghan Dunn, sat with her staff. On the fifth floor, a middle school principal in the same