ject', 'value': 'ART BASEL (FESTIVAL)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T01:42:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b9eb6c7-bae0-50ea-8d62-af721acc273b', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b9eb6c7-bae0-50ea-8d62-af721acc273b'}, {'abstract': 'Britain’s new envoy to Tehran will travel to Iran on Tuesday, the first diplomatic visit by a British official since Britain’s embassy in Tehran was stormed more than two years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/world/europe/britain-envoy-aims-to-mend-iran-ties.html', 'snippet': 'Britain’s new envoy to Tehran will travel to Iran on Tuesday, the first diplomatic visit by a British official since Britain’s embassy in Tehran was stormed more than two years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Britain’s new envoy to Tehran will travel to Iran on Tuesday, the first diplomatic visit by a British official since Britain’s embassy in Tehran was stormed more than two years ago. The visit of the envoy, Ajay Sharma, who has the rank of a nonresident chargé d’affaires, was announced by his Iranian counterpart, Hassan Habibollah-Zadeh, to the official news agency IRNA. Foreign Secretary William Hague confirmed the report in a Twitter message, adding, “We’ll improve U.K.-Iran ties on a step-by-step, reciprocal basis.” Mr. Habibollah-Zadeh said that Mr. Sharma’s visit would include a look at British diplomatic buildings and talks with Iranian Foreign Ministry officials, and that he would then make a similar visit to London. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: E