Mob City,” starting on Wednesday, Ed Burns, who portrays Bugsy Siegel in that show, and the TCM host Robert Osborne, introduce four classic thrillers: Raoul Walsh’s “White Heat” (1949), starring James Cagney as a gangster trying to stay a step ahead of an undercover agent, at 8; Walsh’s “The Roaring Twenties” (1939), with Cagney and Humphrey Bogart as war veterans involved in bootlegging, at 10; Fritz Lang’s “The Big Heat” (1953), with Glenn Ford as a determined cop who infiltrates the criminal underworld after his wife’s murder, at midnight; and John Huston’s “Key Largo” (1948), with Edward G. Robinson as a gang leader who holds a group of people hostage in a Florida hotel during a tropical storm, and Bogart (above left, with Robinson) as the World War II veteran who tries to take him down, at 2 a.m.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ad9b667-c46a-5170-8f9d-c96546025b47', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ad9b667-c46a-5170-8f9d-c96546025b47'}, {'abstract': 'The virus’s spread to Hong Kong is alarming given the city’s status as an international transportation hub and its history as the epicenter of the SARS epidemic.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/hong-kong-gets-first-case-of-avian-flu-virus/', 'snippet': 'The virus’s spread to Hong Kong is alarming given the city’s status as an international transportation hub and its history as the epicenter of the SARS epidemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hong Kong health officials raised avian influenza alert levels to serious late Monday after a domestic worker in the city became critically ill with the virus, the first reported case in the territory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Gets First Case of Avian Flu Virus', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SARS (Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leung Chun-ying', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shenzhen (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T06:36:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/447249cd-a0e9-5918-a4cb-e7daadb6ca26', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447249cd-a0e9-5918-a4cb-e7daadb6ca26'}, {'abstract': 'Students in the United States scored in the middle of the developed world in reading and science, but lower in math, according to results released on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/0