esident Viktor F. Yanukovich on Tuesday unsuccessfully demanded his resignation as protesters continued a siege of government buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/world/europe/ukraine-unrest.html', 'snippet': 'Opponents of President Viktor F. Yanukovich on Tuesday unsuccessfully demanded his resignation as protesters continued a siege of government buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — Refusing to grant a central demand of protesters who have laid siege to public buildings and occupied a landmark plaza in this rattled capital, the Ukrainian Parliament on Tuesday defeated a measure calling for the resignation of Prime Minister Mykola Azarov and his government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/europe/04Ukraine5_cnd/04Ukraine5_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/04/world/europe/04Ukraine5_cnd/04Ukraine5_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/europe/04Ukraine5_cnd/04Ukraine5_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/europe/04Ukraine5_cnd/04Ukraine5_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/europe/04Ukraine5_cnd/04Ukraine5_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/04/world/europe/04Ukraine5_cnd/04Ukraine5_cnd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/europe/04Ukraine5_cnd/04Ukraine5_cnd-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine Protests Persist as Bid to Oust Government Fails ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine Protests Persist as Bid to Oust Government Fails', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanukovich, Viktor F', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Azarov, Mykola', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kiev (Ukraine)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T11:34:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn and Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/652c5473-42a1-574e-9d4c-ff7c7ea9eb5f', 'word_count': 1325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/652c5473-42a1-574e-9d4c-ff7c7ea9eb5f'}, {'abstract': 'Parents, fearing homophobic prejudice in college admissions, want to know how to persuade their daughter from revealing her sexual orientation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/booming/should-a-student-conceal-her-lesbian-identity-in-college-application-essays.html', 'snippet': 'Parents, fearing homophobic prejudice in college admissions, want to know how to persuade their daughter from revealing her sexual orientation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Dear Civil Behavior: Our daughter is a senior in high school and quite comfortable with her lesbian identity. We support her 100 percent, but we know the world is not always so tolerant. As she’s writing her college application essays this fall, she’s “coming out” in them — and we think that’s a bad idea. You just never know who’s reading these essays, so why risk revealing your orientation to someone who might be biased against you? We’ve strongly suggested she think over the ramifications of what she’s doing, but she doesn’t seem to have any doubt about it. Deadlines are approaching and we are at an impasse. How can we persuade her to keep some things private if they might hurt her chances of admission?” — Anonymous', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/booming/03civil-booming-college/03civil-booming-college-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/booming/03civil-booming-college/03civil-booming-college-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/booming/03civil-booming-college/03civil-booming-college-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/booming/03civil-booming-college/03civil-booming-college-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1228, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'