ure', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/59ab125f-2c9e-5eee-9544-c388048e95f4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/59ab125f-2c9e-5eee-9544-c388048e95f4'}, {'abstract': 'Was an engagement outside Knoxville, Tenn. the real turning point of the Civil War?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/the-battle-of-fort-sanders/', 'snippet': 'Was an engagement outside Knoxville, Tenn. the real turning point of the Civil War?', 'lead_paragraph': 'By Nov. 29, 1863, Union-held Knoxville, Tenn., had been under Confederate siege for 12 days. The city itself was a war zone. Sharpshooters from increasingly closer vantage points picked off officers and men alike, so accurately that only one civilian was killed among dozens of dead soldiers. Artillery positions exchanged fire around the line. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Battle of Fort Sanders', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Knoxville (Tenn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T16:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joan Markel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88be868b-d62b-5fc6-b59b-673392b38617', 'word_count': 1484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88be868b-d62b-5fc6-b59b-673392b38617'}, {'abstract': 'Some state National Guards are defying the order that same-sex spouses of military personnel be given full benefits.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/no-spousal-benefits-for-you/', 'snippet': 'Some state National Guards are defying the order that same-sex spouses of military personnel be given full benefits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following valid orders from higher-ups is central to how the military functions.\xa0 At least, it’s supposed to be.\xa0 But getting every state National Guard unit to comply with Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel’s order that same-sex spouses of military personnel be given full spousal and family benefits is proving difficult.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No (Spousal) Benefits for You', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagel, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Guard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T16:36:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62957c6b-b548-5105-9ddc-921f91503d16', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62957c6b-b548-5105-9ddc-921f91503d16'}, {'abstract': 'A group representing Croatians in France filed a complaint over a remark Mr. Dylan made in a Rolling Stone interview last year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/bob-dylan-charged-with-inciting-hate-under-french-law/', 'snippet': 'A group representing Croatians in France filed a complaint over a remark Mr. Dylan made in a Rolling Stone interview last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To people who follow the pronouncements of Bob Dylan, his comment in a Rolling Stone interview in September 2012 suggesting that American blacks could sense whether whites had slave-master blood “just like Jews can sense Nazi blood and the Serbs can sense Croatian blood” may have seemed just the sort of vaporously impressionistic, emotionally pointed kind of thing that Mr. Dylan has been known to say for decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/03artsbeat-dylan/03artsbeat-dylan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/03artsbeat-dylan/03artsbeat-dylan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 759}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/03artsbeat-dylan/03artsbeat-dylan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/03artsbeat-dylan/03artsbeat-dylan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1511, 'width': 1195, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 