e putting the final touches on an exhibition of cars as art. The Swiss-minimal garage at 1111 Lincoln Road, designed by Herzog & de Meuron, has become the apogee of Art Basel lavishness and excess since opening in 2010, with pop-ups galore (like this year’s Colette-sponsored Art Drive Thru, which opened yesterday), and events like 2011’s Ferrari fete, during which hot rods paraded up and down the structure’s seven levels of open-air ramps all night long.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Art Basel, Miami’s Swankiest Garage Becomes a Gallery Yet Again', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art Basel Miami Beach', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herzog & de Meuron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T17:53:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2b46fa3-84f1-5d4c-b485-108227a826f6', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2b46fa3-84f1-5d4c-b485-108227a826f6'}, {'abstract': 'We were sad when our first I.V.F. failed. But we were also surprised at how quickly so much of our savings could disappear.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/how-much-would-you-pay-to-have-a-baby/', 'snippet': 'We were sad when our first I.V.F. failed. But we were also surprised at how quickly so much of our savings could disappear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I love casinos. The sounds, the lights, the corny decadence. … I love it all, except for one thing: I hate losing money. So in the handful of times I’ve visited one, I’d give myself a high-low limit. If I lost $100 or won $200, I’d have to leave. I guess I’m not much of a gambler.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/style/motherlode-baby-money/motherlode-baby-money-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/style/motherlode-baby-money/motherlode-baby-money-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/style/motherlode-baby-money/motherlode-baby-money-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/style/motherlode-baby-money/motherlode-baby-money-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1632, 'width': 1224, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/style/motherlode-baby-money/motherlode-baby-money-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/03/style/motherlode-baby-money/motherlode-baby-money-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/style/motherlode-baby-money/motherlode-baby-money-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Much Would You Pay to Have a Baby?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': 