-b045-9dba10d9086e', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdf325db-693d-54b1-b045-9dba10d9086e'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian fashion house reckons it is worth more than 1 billion euros, or $1.36 billion, and could triple in value in three years. That’s a big price tag for a skimpy minority stake next to a powerful family, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/versace-valuation-may-be-as-over-the-top-as-its-clothes/', 'snippet': 'The Italian fashion house reckons it is worth more than 1 billion euros, or $1.36 billion, and could triple in value in three years. That’s a big price tag for a skimpy minority stake next to a powerful family, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Versace’s valuation looks as aggressive as its outfits. The Italian fashion house, which is sizing up buyout firms and sovereign wealth funds to finance a capital increase, believes it is worth more than 1 billion euros, or $1.36 billion, and could triple in value in three years. There is real potential, because Versace has fallen behind industry trends. But a big price tag for a skimpy minority stake next to a powerful family? That’s hard to pull off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Versace Valuation May Be as Over the Top as Its Clothes', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sovereign Wealth Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferraris, Gian Giacomo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Versace, Santo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Versace, Gianni, SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T19:09:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Webb', 'person':