s and told her to do what she had to do. She fired one shot into his chest, killing him. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: December 3, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T19:21:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e93aae9-41d1-5f8d-a1eb-26cf224ad618', 'word_count': 1592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e93aae9-41d1-5f8d-a1eb-26cf224ad618'}, {'abstract': 'FIFA on Tuesday announced which teams will be in each of the four pots ahead of Friday’s World Cup draw in Brazil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/sports/soccer/for-world-cup-draw-32-divided-by-4.html', 'snippet': 'FIFA on Tuesday announced which teams will be in each of the four pots ahead of Friday’s World Cup draw in Brazil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FIFA announced which teams would be in each of the four pots for Friday’s World Cup draw in Brazil during a news conference on Tuesday in Bahia, Brazil.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/sports/soccer/04worldcuppots1/04worldcuppots1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/04/sports/soccer/04worldcuppots1/04worldcuppots1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/sports/soccer/04worldcuppots1/04worldcuppots1-jumbo.jpg', 'heigh