ne, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9947d558-ad66-561c-bff6-4b8ce5a6a6ce', 'word_count': 2587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9947d558-ad66-561c-bff6-4b8ce5a6a6ce'}, {'abstract': 'Diverse options await diners in the capital city. Here are four places where you can sample textures from Austin’s palate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/travel/beyond-brisket-and-burritos-in-austin-tex.html', 'snippet': 'Diverse options await diners in the capital city. Here are four places where you can sample textures from Austin’s palate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who say that Austin isn’t at all like the rest of Texas should look a little harder. The capital city may swaddle its Lone Star bravado in slacker irony, swap out big hair for cycling musculature and express its rugged individualism with six-strings rather than six-shooters ... but really, we’re talking about the same prideful, gabby, strangely infectious psychodynamic. Even for Austin’s most rabid Gov. Rick Perry haters, defecting from the state is not an option: they adore being Texans, one and all, and appreciate that the term sets them apart somehow.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/travel/08CHOICE_SPAN-sf/08CHOICE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/travel/08CHOICE_SPAN-sf/08CHOICE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/travel/08CHOICE_SPAN-sf/08CHOICE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'