nds on the sales abilities of its recruiters.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/how-a-growing-business-set-itself-apart/', 'snippet': 'Recruiting is mostly about sales, one owner said, which is why the success of an office depends on the sales abilities of its recruiters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the most recent meeting of the She Owns It business group, the owners were joined by a guest, Rebecca Cenni, founder of Atrium Staffing. This post continues the conversation with Ms. Cenni, who explained how her $140 million staffing and payroll firm differentiates itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Growing Business Set Itself Apart', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cenni, Rebecca', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atrium Staffing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T21:05:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/618f51e3-3ee1-5310-8971-35aac702dc64', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/618f51e3-3ee1-5310-8971-35aac702dc64'}, {'abstract': 'The African Union, invoking old demons of racism and imperialism, claims that the International Criminal Court should back off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/world/africa/casting-a-critical-eye-on-justice.html', 'snippet': 'The African Union, invoking old demons of racism and imperialism, claims that the International Criminal Court should back off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Little noticed outside Africa, a movement against the International Criminal Court has been brewing on the continent this fall, challenging a unique but often polarizing international mechanism to prosecute grave human rights abuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/africa/04letter-kenyatta/04letter-kenyatta-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/04/world/africa/04letter-kenyatta/04letter-kenyatta-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/africa/04letter-kenyatta/04letter-kenyatta-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/africa/04letter-kenyatta/04letter-kenyatta-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1291, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/africa/04letter-kenyatta/04letter-kenyatta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/04/world/africa/04letter-kenyatta/04letter-kenyatta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/africa/04letter-kenyatta/04letter-kenyatta-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Is Accused of Unfairly Targeting a Continent’s Leaders', 'kicker': 'Letter From Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenyatta, Uhuru Muigai', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T21:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a913842c-9252-5682-bb1a-2264e99a08ef', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a913842c-9252-5682-bb1a-2264e99a08ef'}, {'abstract': 'The nations that adhere to the International Criminal Court have agreed to special rules for national leaders, but human rights groups warned that a category of privileged defendant had been created.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/world/africa/as-kenyans-trial-looms-international-court-bends-for-diplomacy.html', 'snippet': 'The nations that adhere to the International Criminal Court have agreed to special rules for national leaders, but human rights groups warned that a category of privileged defendant had been created.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — As the International Criminal Court takes up its highest-profile trials to date — the case of President Uhuru Kenyatta of Kenya and his deputy, William Ruto — it is wrestling with a questio