esday to extend a law banning firearms that can pass undetected through X-ray machines, but did not include provisions regulating guns made with 3-D printers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The House voted on Tuesday to extend a law banning firearms that can pass undetected through airport X-ray machines, but left out provisions that law enforcement officials say are necessary to combat the growing threat of guns made with 3-D printers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Votes to Extend Gun Law Without New Provisions for 3-D Printed Firearms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Votes to Extend Gun Law Without New Provisions for 3-D Printed Firearms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T22:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/966e52e4-7da0-54c3-95b8-8f31d1093e46', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/966e52e4-7da0-54c3-95b8-8f31d1093e46'}, {'abstract': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: superhero shirts packed with a heavy dose of nostalgia.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/holiday-the-daily-gift-black-action-tees/', 'snippet': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: superhero shirts packed with a heavy dose of nostalgia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday | The Daily Gift: Black Action Tees', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T22:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5772cc12-e941-5160-b485-cbc5caeccaa3', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5772cc12-e941-5160-b485-cbc5caeccaa3'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama said glitches were clouding the fact that the old insurance system wasn’t working, and that Republicans have no alternative.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/03/the-real-health-care-distraction/', 'snippet': 'President Obama said glitches were clouding the fact that the old insurance system wasn’t working, and that Republicans have no alternative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last few weeks it’s been trendy, in Republican circles, to claim that anything Democrats do or say unrelated to the Affordable Care Act is a ploy to “distract” attention away from the problematic HealthCare.gov rollout. (Really, anything: filibuster reform or a diplomatic breakthrough with Iran.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Health Care Distraction?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-03T22:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06c44262-5885-5bca-be01-1ff2b8ee2449', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06c44262-5885-5bca-be01-1ff2b8ee2449'}, {'abstract': 'TV Land has added “Kirstie,” featuring Kirstie Alley as a narcissistic Broadway actress, to its lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/arts/television/kirstie-a-tv-land-sitcom-stars-kirstie-alley.html', 'snippet': 'TV Land has added “Kirstie,” featuring Kirstie Alley as a narcissistic Broadway actress, to its lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On TV Land, you don’t sweat the details. Three Hollywood harpies accidentally land in Ohio, move in with Betty White and date young cornfed hunks (“Hot in Cleveland”)? Of course. Three men share an apartment owned by their wacky divorce lawyer (“The Exes”)? Why not.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/arts/04KIRSTIE1/04KIRSTIE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy':