the-first-time-a-former-player-tony-clark-will-lead-the-baseball-players-union.html', 'snippet': 'Tony Clark, a former first baseman, was on Tuesday named to succeed Michael Weiner, who died last month, as the union’s executive director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than two weeks after the death of the union leader Michael Weiner, the executive board of the baseball players’ association named Tony Clark as his replacement on Tuesday. Clark, a former first baseman for several teams, including the Yankees and the Mets, will formally assume the role after a vote by the general membership. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For the First Time, a Former Player Will Lead the Baseball Players’ Union', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Player to Head Union', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Tony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball Players Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T00:36:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1651468-546e-5d2c-8342-e02bdf18a196', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1651468-546e-5d2c-8342-e02bdf18a196'}, {'abstract': 'City officials hope a judge’s ruling allowing bankruptcy will release Detroit from the grip of creditors and move it towar