ink, asked for a pen and paper after hearing that a victim in the shooting might have been left paralyzed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Handwritten Apology', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunton, Corey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bryant Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Skating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T00:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5db75fb9-d60d-5040-b9e2-ee056f64b562', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5db75fb9-d60d-5040-b9e2-ee056f64b562'}, {'abstract': 'The crew of a Greenpeace ship seized by Russian authorities in the Arctic in September described a prosecution bound by the letter of the law but remarkably opaque.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/world/europe/greenpeace-activists-detail-russias-capricious-justice-system.html', 'snippet': 'The crew of a Greenpeace ship seized by Russian authorities in the Arctic in September described a prosecution bound by the letter of the law but remarkably opaque.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Russia — An odd thing about the investigation into what exactly happened in the Arctic on Sept. 18 between activists on a Greenpeace International ship and the Russian authorities was how little the investigators asked about the episode when they called the 30 crew members in for questioning, one by one, from their isolated holding cells.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The N