e': 'Shrimp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T00:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fd29dc1-df4d-55d5-b44e-ae5a7c704913', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fd29dc1-df4d-55d5-b44e-ae5a7c704913'}, {'abstract': 'The Scottish historian wrote “Measuring America,” which stressed government surveying of the westward expansion, rather than the lone-wolf perception of pioneers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/arts/andro-linklater-writer-who-re-examined-american-frontierism-dies-at-68.html', 'snippet': 'The Scottish historian wrote “Measuring America,” which stressed government surveying of the westward expansion, rather than the lone-wolf perception of pioneers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While on a book tour of the United States in the 1990s, Andro Linklater, a Scottish journalist and popular historian, peered from his plane at the vast checkerboard orderliness of America’s former wilderness frontier and asked himself a historian’s sort of question: Which came first, the pioneers or the surveyors?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/Linklater-obit-web/Linklater-obit-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/Linklater-obit-web/Linklater-obit-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 790}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/Linklater-obit-web/Linklater-obit-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/Linklater-obit-web/Linklater-obit-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1557, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/Linklater-obit-web/Linklater-obit-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/Linklater-obit-web/Linklater-obit-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/03/arts/Linklater-obit-web/Linklater-obit-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andro Linklater, Who Re-Examined American Frontierism, Dies at 68', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Andro Linklater Dies at 68; Historian of American West', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vitello, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linklater, Andro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T00:56:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/28c5770b-1c06-5ac9-9ecf-2e25cc93ff70', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28c5770b-1c06-5ac9-9ecf-2e25cc93ff70'}, {'abstract': 'French investigators’ conclusion partly contradicted and partly confirmed those of Swiss scientists who found abnormal polonium-210 levels in the remains of Yasir Arafat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/world/middleeast/tests-on-arafat-find-no-proof-of-radiation-poisoning.html', 'snippet': 'French investigators’ conclusion partly contradicted and partly confirmed those of Swiss scientists who found abnormal polonium-210 levels in the remains of Yasir Arafat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — French investigators studying the remains of Yasir Arafat have concluded that the Palestinian leader most likely did not die of radiation poisoning, Mr. Arafat’s widow, Suha, said here Tuesday. She noted, however, that the investigators did find unusually elevated levels of radioactivity in and around his body.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tests on Arafat Find No Proof of Radiation Poisoning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tests on Arafat Find No Proof Of Poisoning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARAFAT, YASIR', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ramallah (West Bank)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons