, 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (NBC) CHRISTMAS IN ROCKEFELLER CENTER In this 81st tree-lighting ceremony, Mary J. Blige; Toni Braxton; Mariah Carey; Kelly Clarkson; Kenny Edmonds, known as Babyface; the Goo Goo Dolls; Ariana Grande; Jewel; and others will gather around a 76-foot Norway spruce. Donated by the Vargoshe family of Shelton, Conn., the tree, being hoisted into place, above, will be covered with 45,000 LED lights and topped with a Swarovski crystal star through Jan. 7. Then it will be milled for lumber for Habitat for Humanity. The Rockettes will add their kicks to the festivities, presided over by Matt Lauer, Savannah Guthrie, Al Roker and Natalie Morales of the “Today” show on NBC. The entertainment before the lighting will feature performances by Ashanti and Lauren Alaina. “SNL Christmas,” at 9, offers holiday sketches from “Saturday Night Live.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T06:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/75d29667-17c6-5c3d-9b96-62a1f575827f', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75d29667-17c6-5c3d-9b96-62a1f575827f'}, {'abstract': 'China said the new zone, which has ignited tensions with Japan, was permanent, but indicated no decision had been made on how aggressively to enforce it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/world/asia/biden-arrives-in-china-seeking-restraint-from-beijing.html', 'snippet': 'China said the new zone, which has ignited tensions with Japan, was permanent, but indicated no decision had been made on how aggressively to enforce it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Chinese leaders pushed back at visiting Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. on Wednesday over what they assert is their right to control a wide swath of airspace in the bitterly contested East China Sea. But the Chinese also indicated that they had not decided how aggressively to enforce their so-called air defense identification zone, which has ignited tensions with Japan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Urges Restraint by China in Airspace Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Biden Urges Restraint by China in Airspace Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East China Sea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T06:26:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/444fb93b-b530-5439-a8f5-de082db3349e', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/444fb93b-b530-5439-a8f5-de082db3349e'}, {'abstract': 'In the last election cycle, residents of Sangam Vihar were told their unauthorized colony would get government services like sewage and water. They are still waiting.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/as-delhi-heads-to-polls-a-poor-neighborhood-recalls-empty-promises/', 'snippet': 'In the last election cycle, residents of Sangam Vihar were told their unauthorized colony would get government services like sewage and water. They are still waiting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — On Tuesday, the crowded lanes of Sangam Vihar were without those rickshaws outfitted with loudspeakers, which had been blaring political slogans in the lead-up to the state legislative assembly vote the next day. The last pamphlets had been doled out before being trampled under foot or used as napkins. No more mega rallies were planned, with most of the biggest political names having come and gone in the past few weeks as they campaigned for a contest seen as a preview for the national elections next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/asia/04-dikshit-IndiaInk/04-dikshit-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/04/world/asia/04-dikshit-IndiaInk/04-dikshit-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/asia/04-dikshit-IndiaInk/04-dikshit-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/world/asia/04-dikshit-IndiaInk/04-dikshit-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 's