 publish information on government spying.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/parliament-versus-the-press/', 'snippet': 'Members of the British Parliament grilled a newspaper editor for daring to publish information on government spying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Edward Snowden leaked documents on the National Security Agency’s data-mining programs, governments of countries such as the United States and Great Britain have tried to dismiss the concern that mass, secret surveillance is incompatible with an open, democratic society. So it was chilling and more than a little ironic to see members of the British Parliament grill a newspaper editor on Tuesday for daring to publish information on government spying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parliament Versus the Press', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Carl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rusbridger, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T17:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de1da161-7bf9-5c14-9c69-6281bfe67223', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de1da161-7bf9-5c14-9c69-6281bfe67223'}, {'abstract': 'Inside the research, drama and, at times, staggering economics of trying to take the family pet on an overseas move.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08