 Our Truth: 10-Minute Plays on Trayvon, Race and Privilege” will be performed at the City University of New York Graduate Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A free showcase of short plays and a folk opera about race in the United States, inspired by debates over the Trayvon Martin case, will have its premiere on Thursday at the City University of New York Graduate Center. Called “Facing Our Truth: 10-Minute Plays on Trayvon, Race and Privilege,” the project comes from the New Black Fest, which supports innovative plays by and about black people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Work Inspired by Trayvon Martin Case to Have Premiere on Thursday', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City University of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T22:17:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e380120-84e5-5b2c-afe4-73f3bfe58b4c', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e380120-84e5-5b2c-afe4-73f3bfe58b4c'}, {'abstract': 'Elton John promoted his new album during his concert at Madison Square Garden, but hits dominated the show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/arts/music/elton-john-in-concert-at-madison-square-garden.html', 'snippet': 'Elton John promoted his new album durin