Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52fae06d-f733-5946-9d20-c3dae2dc951f', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52fae06d-f733-5946-9d20-c3dae2dc951f'}, {'abstract': 'Summaries of every film in the competitions announced so far for the next Sundance Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/sundance-film-by-film/', 'snippet': 'Summaries of every film in the competitions announced so far for the next Sundance Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Sundance Film Festival has released its competition lineups for its 30th edition in January, and as the Bagger’s colleague Brooks Barnes reports here, though the programmers largely opted for films along themes they know well — race and family — they also took an unusual turn into horror. “Over all, we’re seeing films that are of much higher quality,” John Cooper, Sundance’s director, said. “We think a lot of that is coming from technology, which has freed filmmakers from limitations, including financial ones. You can do special effects now.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance, Film by Film', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T22:31:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acab3389-51e8-5a02-acf3-a38236347df8', 'word_count': 3682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acab3389-51e