ars at Andy Warhol’s Factory, and by curating the artist’s multifarious acquisitions, creating order and beauty at Warhol’s townhouse. The other was more formally (if not quite traditionally) educated, at Berkeley, Harvard and by a fresh-out-of-grad-school job as a young architect at I.\xa0M. Pei. Together, Jed Johnson and Alan Wanzenberg formed one of the most influential design partnerships of the 1980s and early 1990s, making sensuous, modern environments for celebrity and art world heavies like Richard Gere, Mick Jagger and Jerry Hall, Peter and Sandy Brant, and Beth Rudin De Woody.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alan Wanzenberg: A New View on Life', 'kicker': 'On Location | Upper West Side', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New View on Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Penelope', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wanzenberg, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-04T23:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Penelope Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Penelope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c67630-f5ba-5b18-9d4e-91ab26755d8e', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c67630-f5ba-5b18-9d4e-91ab26755d8e'}, {'abstract': 'Readers discuss aging research and the b