he door to the prospect of pork cheek street tacos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The dance plays out daily in MacArthur Park, Boyle Heights, South Los Angeles and elsewhere across this sprawling metropolis: A lone police car rolls slowly past a popular corner, sending dozens of street vendors scrambling for cover, pushing tamale carts around corners and into the doorways of nearby shops.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Carts in Los Angeles Come Out of the Shadows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Carts Come Out of the Shadows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Street Vendors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Trucks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T01:50:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/204d6ec2-33c7-5b4e-a134-90954116280c', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/204d6ec2-33c7-5b4e-a134-90954116280c'}, {'abstract': 'Commercials featuring cast members of shows were common when advertisers and agencies owned the programs they sponsored, but the concept is now enjoying something of a comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/business/media/recalling-tvs-golden-age-stars-pitch-products-tied-to-their-shows.html', 'snippet': 'Commercials featuring cast members of shows were common when advertisers and agencies owned the programs they sponsored, but the concept is now enjoying something of a comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURING the golden age of radio and the early years of television, when advertisers and agencies owned the programs they sponsored, a popular way to pitch products was with what were known as cast commercials: Cast members of the programs would deliver a spiel or two during their shows, often in character and usually with a gentler touch that soft-pedaled the hard-selling tactics of typical commercials.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/05/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 331}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1130, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/05/business/Adco/Adco