ring by reinforcing the power of institutions that have long held Egypt in an iron grip.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Latest Constitution', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Latest Constitution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T02:16:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ef530dd-49af-5027-adbf-873d0f5ec5b1', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ef530dd-49af-5027-adbf-873d0f5ec5b1'}, {'abstract': 'A report on ethics in Albany reads like an encyclopedia of scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/opinion/new-yorks-legalized-bribery.html', 'snippet': 'A report on ethics in Albany reads like an encyclopedia of scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The panel deputized this summer to investigate corruption in Albany released its first report this week. It is, quite properly, scathing — a damning list of the ways that New York State politicians twist, abuse and sometimes break the law to enjoy the fruits of a pay-to-play government where “large donors set the legislative agenda.” The 25-member panel — The Commission to Investigate Public Corruption — has done New Yorkers a great service. It has provided one of the best guidebooks for reforming Albany’s corrosive culture in many decades.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s ‘Legalized Bribery’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s ‘Legalized Bribery’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moreland Commission to Investigate Public Corruption (NYS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T02:18:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6942fe2c-2caf-5d35-906c-655b43200e3d', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6942fe2c-2caf-5d35-906c-655b43200e3d'}, {'abstract': 'The solar installer says a battery system created with Tesla Motors will allow the use of stored electricity in times of highest demand, which would reduce usage at peak periods and associated fees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/business/energy-environment/solarcity-to-use-batteries-from-tesla-for-energy-storage.html', 'snippet': 'The solar installer says a battery system created with Tesla Motors will allow the use of stored electricity in times of highest d