o than earlier in the week. Tricky, but carefully tread that tightrope between challenging the solver and making it overcomplicated. Keep it simple. You can tell I liked this one by Dan Schoenholz. It’s just so simple in its theme design, I didn’t even care that there were four cheaters in the grid (I am a bit biased toward themed puzzles. Sue me.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Puzzlement', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T03:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72d8ea62-690d-5ab6-b06b-5c759cebb91d', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72d8ea62-690d-5ab6-b06b-5c759cebb91d'}, {'abstract': 'The National Security Agency is tracking the movements of hundreds of millions of cellphones in an effort to find suspicious travel patterns or activities by intelligence targets, according to documents leaked by Edward J. Snowden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/us/politics/documents-say-phones-outside-us-are-tracked.html', 'snippet': 'The National Security Agency is tracking the movements of hundreds of millions of cellphones in an effort to find suspicious travel patterns or activities by intelligence targets, according to documents leaked by Edward J. Snowden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Security Agency is tracking the location and movements of hundreds of millions of cellphones outside the United States in an effort to find suspicious travel patterns or coordinated activities by intelligence targets, according to secret documents leaked by the former N.S.A. contractor Edward J. Snowden.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documents Say Phones Outside U.S. Are Tracked', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Documents Say Phones Outside U.S. Are Tracked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glanz, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T03:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Glanz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glanz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/230f14c6-46d1-5f5e-8d4d-a612d887174e', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/230f14c6-46d1-5f5e-8d4d-a612d887174e'}, {'abstract': 'An assistant to a Manhattan art dealer, now accused of antiquities smuggling, pled guilty to charges Wednesday related to what authorities said was an elaborate scheme to sell items looted from India.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/04/assistant-to-accused-antiquities-smuggler-pleads-guilty-to-possessing-looted-items/', 'snippet': 'An assistant to a Manhattan art dealer, now accused of antiquities smuggling, pled guilty to charges Wednesday related to what authorities said was an elaborate scheme to sell items looted from India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aaron M. Freedman spent nearly 20 years managing the fine details of life at Subhash Kapoor’s art gallery on Madison Avenue in Manhattan. Over that period, ending in 2012, the two men became good friends, shared an expertise in rare Indian artifacts and co-wrote several scholarly works.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assistant to Accused Antiquities Smuggler Pleads Guilty to Possessing Looted Items', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guilty Plea in Case Of Indian Antiquities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kapoor, Subhash (1949- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T03:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Mashberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/979118e5-edc4-51d3-87f7-46056122f836', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/979118e5-edc4-51d3-87f7-46056122f836'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Elizabeth Warren, who has been mentioned as a possible presidential candidate in 2016, confirmed she would not run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/us/massachusetts-warren-rules-out-a-run-for-president.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Elizabeth Warren, who has been mentioned as a possible presidential candidate in 2016, confirmed she would not run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Elizabeth Warren, the freshman Massachusetts Democrat who has been mentioned as a possible presidential candidate in 2016, said Wednesday that she would not run. “I pledge to serve out my term,” which expires in January 2019, she told reporters. “I am not running for president,” she said. “I am working as hard as I can to be the best possible senator that I can be.” She had been promoted by some liberals, without her encouragement, as a populist alternative to Hillary Rodham Clinton. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Warren Rules Out a Run for President', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Warren Rules Out a Run For President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T03:26:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/852ddb9b-d249-5b4d-bcc9-eb75e89f6f13', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/852ddb9b-d249-5b4d-bcc9-eb75e89f6f13'}, {'abstract': 'Rory McIlroy, who began the season ranked No. 1 in the world but has since fallen to No. 6, earned his first victory of 2013 on Sunday at the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/sports/golf/rediscovering-form-mcilroy-also-finds-some-perspective.html', 'snippet': 'Rory McIlroy, who began the season ranked No. 1 in the world but has since fallen to No. 6, earned his first victory of 2013 on Sunday at the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THOUSAND OAKS, Calif. — For Rory McIlroy, fans shouting his name have become background noise, as natural as the pounding surf in nearby Malibu. It is rare that a single cry of “Rory” can turn his head, as happened Wednesday after McIlroy walked off the first tee box at Sherwood Country Club during the pro-am for the World Challenge, hosted by Tiger Woods.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/sports/SUB-CITY-GOLF/SUB-CITY-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/05/sports/SUB-CITY-GOLF/SUB-CITY-GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/sports/SUB-CITY-GOLF/SUB-CITY-GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/sports/SUB-CITY-GOLF/SUB-CITY-GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1527, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/sports/SUB-CITY-GOLF/SUB-CITY-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/05/sports/SUB-CITY-GOLF/SUB-CITY-GOLF-thumb