nd-hopes-in-bolivia/', 'snippet': 'Marcelo Pérez del Carpio returned to the Bolivian countryside to find migrants and peasants abandoning traditional crops for the promise of quick cash with coca.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The landscape Marcelo Pérez del Carpio remembered from childhood days at his grandparents’ farm about four hours northeast of La Paz has changed over the last 20 years. Back then, the town of Challa was home to a few people who devoted themselves to agriculture. But when he returned this year, he found a boomtown that had turned its back on traditional fruit and vegetable crops, luring to its lush acres migrants intent on cultivating coca.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/blogs/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/04/blogs/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/blogs/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/blogs/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/blogs/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/04/blogs/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/04/blogs/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP/20131204-lens-marcelo-slide-Q6YP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raising Coca and Hopes in Bolivia', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af4a3d97-d927-5c88-b2e1-eac86e7c5ae9', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af4a3d97-d927-5c88-b2e1-eac86e7c5ae9'}, {'abstract': 'What if you discovered an invasive species that seems drawn to electricity — in your outlets, appliances, laptops and TVs — and no one would listen?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/magazine/crazy-ants.html', 'snippet': 'What if you discovered an invasive species that seems drawn to electricity — in your outlets, appliances, laptops and TVs — and no one would listen?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time Mike the Hog-a-Nator noticed the ants, they were piled outside his cardiologist’s office. This was two summers ago, in Pearland, a suburb of Houston. There was a forbidding, fibrous heap of dead ants on either side of the building’s double doors, each a couple of feet long. And there were also legions of living ants shuffling over the dead ones — though Mike the Hog-a-Nator had to bend down to see these. Otherwise, so many individual ants were moving so chaotically, and so fast, that the entire reddish-brown tangle at his feet looked as if it were shimmering. Mike the Hog-a-Nator remembers thinking: What the world? Then he went inside for his weekly appointment.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08ants1/mag-08Ants-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08ants1/mag-08Ants-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08ants1/mag-08Ants-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08ants1/mag-08Ants-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08ants1/mag-08Ants-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08ants1/mag-08Ants-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08ants1/mag-08Ants-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s a Reason They Call Them ‘Crazy Ants’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Swarm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Invasive Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Mooallem', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mooallem', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d340ac-ba27-597a-8dd7-042b0a3780e8', 'word_count': 4655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d340ac-ba27-597a-8dd7-042b0a3780e8'}, {'abstract': 'How much do you think tests like PISA and NAEP tell us about American students and what they know and are able to do? How much weight do you think we should give them as a nation? Why? How much time do you spend prepping for and taking standardized tests yourself?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/how-seriously-should-we-take-standardized-tests/', 'snippet': 'How much do you think tests like PISA and NAEP tell us about American students and what they know and are able to do? How much weight do you think we should give them as a nation? Why? How much time do you spend prepping for and taking standardize...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Times article this week about the international PISA test announced “American 15-Year-Olds Lag, Mainly in Math, on International Standardized Tests.” In November, an article about a national test, the National Assessment of Educational Progress, showed that though there have been gains, “achievement gaps between whites and blacks, whites and Hispanics, and low-income and more affluent students stubbornly persist.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime