thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/06/automobiles/06WHEELIES/06WHEELIES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/automobiles/06WHEELIES/06WHEELIES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Bargain Mitsubishi E.V. Edition', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACOUSTICAL SOCIETY OF AMERICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Experian Group Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North America', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T17:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8ea1e5c-1b45-503c-be5f-ddd20858df19', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8ea1e5c-1b45-503c-be5f-ddd20858df19'}, {'abstract': 'China’s regulatory assault undermines the narrative that bitcoin is in the vanguard of a global shift toward new, computer-generated forms of money, writes Peter Thal Larsen of Reuters Breakingviews', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/shaking-the-bitcoin-believers/', 'snippet': 'China’s regulatory assault undermines the narrative that bitcoin is in the vanguard of a global shift toward new, computer-generated forms of money, writes Peter Thal Larsen of Reuters Breakingviews', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much for China’s willingness to tolerate financial innovation. Regulators have barred the country’s banks from trading Bitcoin, while denying the pseudo-money legal status and cracking down on anonymous users. Though China has stopped short of an outright ban, the move dashes hopes the country might allow start-up currencies to exist alongside the official renminbi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shaking the Bitcoin Believers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bitcoin (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Bank of China", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T17:03:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Thal Larsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'Thal', 'lastname': 'Larsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eac7a124-ff8b-5864-a8fe-5dcd5e86cbc4', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eac7a124-ff8b-5864-a8fe-5dcd5e86cbc4'}, {'abstract': 'How the Tennessee city legalized prostitution during the Civil War.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/the-nashville-experiment/', 'snippet': 'How the Tennessee city legalized prostitution during the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emaline Cameron was among the thousands of refugees who poured into occupied Nashville, Tenn., in 1863. While the strains of war may have contributed to her flight from her native Smithville, about 50 miles to the east, Emaline crossed Union lines to distance herself from an imploded marriage. James Hayes, known as Toy, had divorced her on the grounds that he was not the father of their eldest child. She admitted as much in court: while growing up Emaline had worked as a chambermaid at the Smithville Hotel, which was run by her parents. After a boarder left the 15-year-old pregnant, they quickly married her off to the naïve Toy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Nashville Experiment', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexually Transmitted Diseases', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T17:06:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Moss Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'Moss', 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dfd412a-686b-565d-a332-2511df24c926', 'word_count': 1300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dfd412a-686b-565d-a332-2511df24c926'}, {'abstract': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: an all-I-want-for-Christmas splurge.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/