it seemed as though only one photograph of Nelson Mandela existed. It showed him with bushy hair, plump cheeks, and a look of serious determination. But it was a black-and-white shot, so grainy it looked ancient — a visual documentation of an era and an individual whose time had long passed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/opinion/05MANDELA-IMG/05MANDELA-IMG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/05/opinion/05MANDELA-IMG/05MANDELA-IMG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/opinion/05MANDELA-IMG/05MANDELA-IMG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/opinion/05MANDELA-IMG/05MANDELA-IMG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1477, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/opinion/05MANDELA-IMG/05MANDELA-IMG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/05/opinion/05MANDELA-IMG/05MANDELA-IMG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/05/opinion/05MANDELA-IMG/05MANDELA-IMG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mandela Taught a Continent to Forgive', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Taught a Continent to Forgive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahama, John Dramani', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN NATIONAL CONGRESS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Dramani Mahama', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Dramani', 'lastname': 'Mahama', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6e63d0d-dff4-5b39-83e8-78294e9212db', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6e63d0d-dff4-5b39-83e8-78294e9212db'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Mandela’s quest for freedom in South Africa’s system of white rule took him from the court of tribal royalty to the liberation underground to a prison cell to the presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/world/africa/nelson-mandela_obit.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Mandela’s quest for freedom in South Africa’s system of white rule took him from the court of tribal royalty to the liberation underground to a prison cell to the presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson Mandela, who led the emancipation of South Africa from white minority rule and served as his country’s first black president, becoming an international emblem of dignity and forbearance, died Thursday night. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nelson Mandela, South Africa’s Liberator as Prisoner and President, Dies at 95', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nelson Mandela, South Africa’s Liberator and Leader, Dies at 95', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/45f34fe5-d09a-5f19-96c0-407e32b41824', 'word_count': 6508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45f34fe5-d09a-5f19-96c0-407e32b41824'}, {'abstract': 'Can the right offer anything on policy that addresses the residue of slavery and segregation in our national life?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/conservatives-and-structural-racism/', 'snippet': 'Can the right offer anything on policy that addresses the residue of slavery and segregation in our national life?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to some of the discussion\xa0(my own contribution perhaps included)\xa0around Jonathan Chait’s controversials thoughts\xa0on conservatives and “12 Years a Slave,” The Daily Beast’s Jamelle Bouie tweeted: “Empathy about racial issues is nice, but actual policy to ameliorate effects of structural racism would be better, and I’m not sure conservatism is equipped to do that. I would be happy to be wrong though.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservatives and Structural Racism', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:08:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1c734fe-7035-5f97-a41d-d8963e72c632', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1c734fe-7035-5f97-a41d-d8963e72c632'}, {'abstract': 'The designer opened up his New York studio on the eve of his prefall presentation to share his personal inspirations and how it all came together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/12/05/t-magazine/making-of-altuzarra.html', 'snippet': 'The designer opened up his New York studio on the eve of his prefall presentation to share his personal inspirations and how it all came together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer opened up his New York studio on the eve of his prefall presentation to share his personal inspirations and how it all came together.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making Of', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:09:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f6f30fde-6c63-5517-a811-65f8d124e263', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f6f30fde-6c63-5517-a811-65f8d124e263'}, {'abstract': 'He left South Africa a proud legacy of freedom and tolerance. Alas, some of his compatriots are trampling on it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/opinion/the-contradictions-of-mandela.html', 'snippet': 'He left South Africa a proud legacy of freedom and tolerance. Alas, some of his compatriots are trampling on it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I REMEMBER Nelson Mandela. No, not the universally adored elder statesman who successfully resisted the megalomania that comes with deification, and who died Thursday at age 95, but the young lawyer who used to sit in my parents’ living room until the early hours of the morning, debating African nationalism with my father, Ashby Peter Mda. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Contradictions of Mandela', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mandela I Knew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'S