0'}, {'abstract': '“Danish Paintings From the Golden Age to the Modern Breakthough,” at Scandinavia House, traces a growing dialogue between native restraint and early modern French currents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/arts/design/danish-paintings-show-at-scandinavia-house.html', 'snippet': '“Danish Paintings From the Golden Age to the Modern Breakthough,” at Scandinavia House, traces a growing dialogue between native restraint and early modern French currents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the movie “Babette’s Feast,” a Frenchwoman comes to a remote Danish fishing village seeking political asylum after losing her husband and son in the Paris Commune of 1871. \xa0 The local residents are puritanical Protestants; Babette is a Roman Catholic sensualist. She wins over her gloomy hosts by staging a lavish multicourse dinner that awakens them to their own bodily appetites. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Desire and Prudery, Wrestling to a Draw', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desire and Prudery, Wrestling to a Draw', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scandinavia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scandinavia House', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammershoi, Vilhelm', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:25:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c86cd7d-af2f-50a5-8484-1c6619c1af3e', 'word_count': 900