a-burns-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memories of Mandela: John F. Burns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:26:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'Stefania Rousselle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefania', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rousselle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/09111e61-acbf-5490-b479-7f68301f77e1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/09111e61-acbf-5490-b479-7f68301f77e1'}, {'abstract': 'Memories of Nelson Mandela by John F. Burns, who was Johannesburg bureau chief from 1976 to 1980.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/11/world/africa/a-day-of-adulation-and-hope.html', 'snippet': 'Memories of Nelson Mandela by John F. Burns, who was Johannesburg bureau chief from 1976 to 1980.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was late afternoon on one of the sky-blue summer days common in the verdant landscape of South Africa’s Western Cape, during a return visit nearly a quarter of a century ago, that I first glimpsed Nelson Mandela as a free man, walking to his destiny through the gates of Victor Verster Prison after 27 years as the world’s most celebrated political prisoner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day of Adulation and Hope', 'kicker': 'Memories of Mandela', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38f625fe-0400-551e-95aa-0c5a458d6dff', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38f625fe-0400-551e-95aa-0c5a458d6dff'}, {'abstract': '“Twice Born” features Penélope Cruz in a drama that uses the 1990s Balkans as a backdrop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/movies/twice-born-stars-penelope-cruz-and-emile-hirsch.html', 'snippet': '“Twice Born” features Penélope Cruz in a drama that uses the 1990s Balkans as a backdrop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an actor, Sergio Castellitto, a brooding and playful screen presence, especially in films directed by Jacques Rivette, is capable of impressive subtlety. As a director, though — notably of “Don’t Move” (2005) and now “Twice Born,” both starring Penélope Cruz — he seems to go out of his way to discourage precisely that quality. A throbbing melodrama set partly during the Balkan wars of the early 1990s (and based on a novel by Margaret Mazzantini, Mr. Castellitto’s wife), “Twice Born” generously allows each member of its talented, cosmopolitan cast an opportunity to howl and scream and tremble and generally overdo it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/06TWICE_SPAN/TWICE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlar