': 'By Ronda Kaysen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaysen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/73663df0-59c2-5df9-9f40-c72bde75b466', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73663df0-59c2-5df9-9f40-c72bde75b466'}, {'abstract': 'Donald G. McNeil Jr. was a Johannesburg correspondent from 1995 to 1999.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/africa/100000001987417/memories-of-mandela-donald-g-mcneil.html', 'snippet': 'Donald G. McNeil Jr. was a Johannesburg correspondent from 1995 to 1999.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald G. McNeil Jr. was a Johannesburg correspondent from 1995 to 1999.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-mandela-mcneil/video-mandela-mcneil-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-mandela-mcneil/video-mandela-mcneil-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-mandela-mcneil/video-mandela-mcneil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/multimedia/video-mandela-mcneil/video-mandela-mcneil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memories of Mandela: Donald G. McNeil', 'kicker': 'OBITUARIES', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/d25ab4d2-fc8d-53bf-93e8-822241073425', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/d25ab4d2-fc8d-53bf-93e8-822241073425'}, {'abstract': 'Memories of Nelson Mandela by Donald G. McNeil Jr., who was a Johannesburg correspondent from 1995 to 1999.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/world/africa/-almost-meeting-mandela.html', 'snippet': 'Memories of Nelson Mandela by Donald G. McNeil Jr., who was a Johannesburg correspondent from 1995 to 1999.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I never interviewed Nelson Mandela, but toward the end of my time in Johannesburg, he spoke at the annual dinner of the Foreign Correspondents Association. At the end, everyone got in line to shake his hand as he exited. Normally, I don’t buddy up to important people — I think it’s compromising. But this time I was telling myself off: “Oh, for Christ’s sake, Donald, stop being such a prig. It’s Madiba, he’s a living saint, and he’s 80 years old. He’s not going to be around much longer. Get in line and shake his hand.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '(Almost) Meeting Mandela', 'kicker': 'Memories of Mandela', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:32:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0ab8b20-4cda-56a1-a420-5970b6ddb3ba', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0ab8b20-4cda-56a1-a420-5970b6ddb3ba'}, {'abstract': 'Ian Fisher was Nairobi bureau chief from 1998 to 2001.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/africa/100000001987283/memories-of-mandela-ian-fisher.html', 'snippet': 'Ian Fisher was Nairobi bureau chief from 1998 to 2001.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ian Fisher was Nairobi bureau chief from 1998 to 2001.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/world/video-mandela-fisher/video-mandela-fisher-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/01/04/world/video-mandela-fisher/video-mandela-fisher-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/01/04/world/video-mandela-fisher/video-mandela-fisher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/01/04/world/video-mandela-fisher/video-mandela-fisher-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memories of Mandela: Ian Fisher', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:33:08+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/9036348c-48ce-5a2f-931d-003e7f61c7bc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/9036348c-48ce-5a2f-931d-003e7f61c7bc'}, {'abstract': 'The designer opened up his New York studio on the eve of his prefall presentation to share his personal inspirations and how it all came together.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/the-making-of-a-wardrobe-fitting-for-joseph-altuzarras-fictional-leading-lady/', 'snippet': 'The designer opened up his New York studio on the eve of his prefall presentation to share his personal inspirations and how it all came together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, Joseph Altuzarra was hard at work in his New York studio, putting the finishing touches on the prefall 2014 looks he began designing in September, right after his spring/summer 2014 runway. For this fifth anniversary collection, which hits stores in May 2014, the newly engaged designer is looking back to move forward. “In the past couple of years we were really developing the brand around this kind of woman,” says Altuzarra about his imaginary muse, who balances French sensuality with effortless American style. “I think it is a powerful thing to look at a show and have it superdesirable and have it superwearable.” To achieve that balance this time around, his nearly 80 designs are fraught with layers of contrast. Body-hugging sheath dresses are understatedly sexy thanks to preppy madras fabric. Innocent, collegiate-striped skirts have dangerously high slits, an Altuzarra signature. The resurfacing of his other popular standbys — cropped peacoats, oxford shirt dresses, simple knits and soft, draped cocktail dresses — round out the collection so that it essentially becomes a complete wardrobe for the Altuzarra woman. Here, a look at just who that is, along with a behind-the-scenes look at how it all come together.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making Of | A Wardrobe Fitting for Joseph Altuzarra’s Fictional Leading Lady', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altuzarra, Joseph', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:33:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/051292ca-a1a2-5afb-a97e-4ed724ae4fbf', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/051292ca-a1a2-5afb-a97e-4ed724ae4fbf'}, {'abstract': 'F.H.A.-backed loans cater to first-time buyers because they require as little as 3.5 percent down, but insurance premiums are high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/realestate/the-downside-to-fha-loans.html', 'snippet': 'F.H.A.-backed loans cater to first-time buyers because they require as little as 3.5 percent down, but insurance premiums are high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mortgages insured by the Federal Housing Administration are the go-to product for borrowers who don’t have much cash for a down payment. But the required mortgage insurance premiums have become so costly that some critics argue that the agency is taking advantage of borrowers who have few other options. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credi