ca/a-racial-acceptance-that-resonates.html', 'snippet': 'Memories of covering Nelson Mandela by Lydia Polgreen, who has been Johannesburg bureau chief sine 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1980, when I was 4 years old, my family moved to Kenya for my father’s job as a development consultant. My mother is from Ethiopia, and my father is a white American, but in the swirl of expat life in Nairobi, there was nothing unusual about that. My elementary school classes were full of kids who were half Kenyan, half British; half Chinese, half Rwandan; half Indian, half Filipino.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Racial Acceptance That Resonates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polgreen, Lydia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:38:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca2251c4-8428-51f5-9bce-3e0b5d160679', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca2251c4-8428-51f5-9bce-3e0b5d160679'}, {'abstract': '“I was sorry to see the big paintings go,” said William Stuart, who bought back two smaller works.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/not-breaking-ties-retaining-rockwell-family-heirlooms/', 'snippet': '“I was sorry to see the big paintings go,” said William Stuart, who bought back two smaller works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although all eyes were on three of Norman Rockwell’s best-loved paintings, which brought a total of $57.8 million at Sotheby’s on Wednesday morning, two smaller works by the artist were snapped back up by William Stuart, one of the brothers who had inherited them from their father, Kenneth J. Stuart, Sr., the Saturday Evening Post’s longtime art director. The elder Mr. Stuart died in 1993. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Breaking Ties: Retaining Rockwell Family Heirlooms', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockwell, Norman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2c76407-ad59-537e-8c15-627ef5ac2295', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2c76407-ad59-537e-8c15-627ef5ac2295'}, {'abstract': 'The man who led a people to end apartheid in South Africa and set a moral example for the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/opinion/nelson-mandela.html', 'snippet': 'The man who led a people to end apartheid in South Africa and set a moral example for the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson Mandela, who died on Thursday at age 95, fully deserved the legendary stature he enjoyed around the world for the last quarter-century of his life. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nelson Mandela', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nelson Mandela', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN NATIONAL CONGRESS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:40:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e7d1c7b-b7ab-5d7f-9582-4642cb61dcc5', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e7d1c7b-b7ab-5d7f-9582-4642cb61dcc5'}, {'abstract': 'Memories of Nelson Mandela by Barry Bearak, who was Johannesburg bureau chief from 2008 to 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/05/world/africa/memories-of-mandela-clinging-to-a-frail-presence-a-living-symbol.html', 'snippet': 'Memories of Nelson Mandela by Barry Bearak, who was Johannesburg bureau chief from 2008 to 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time I arrived in South Africa in 2008, a frail and declining Nelson Mandela was rarely seen in public anymore, and yet his presence was everywhere, his name on every set of lips and his face never far from any mind’s eye.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/mandela-obit-memories-bearak/mandela-obit-memories-bearak-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/03/28/world/mandela-obit-memories-bearak/mandela-obit-memories-bearak-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/mandela-obit-memories-bearak/mandela-obit-memories-bearak-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/mandela-obit-memories-bearak/mandela-obit-memories-bearak-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/mandela-obit-memories-bearak/mandela-obit-memories-bearak-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/03/28/world/mandela-obit-memories-bearak/mandela-obit-memories-bearak-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/03/28/world/mandela-obit-memories-bearak/mandela-obit-memories-bearak-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinging to a Frail Presence, a Living Symbol', 'kicker': 'Memories of Mandela', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T22:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Bearak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5403387-bc77-5c53-aa4f-a07b4c0442ce', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5403387-bc77-5c53-aa4f-a07b4c0442ce'}, {'abstract': 'Once known as a “special-occasion place,” 42 in White Plains, on the 42nd floor of the Ritz-Carlton, has a completely revamped look and a less high-concept, but excellent, menu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/nyregion/a-review-of-42-in-the-ritz-carlton-in-white-plains.html', 'snippet': 'Once known as a “special-occasion place,” 42 in White Plains, on the 42nd floor of the Ritz-Carlton, has a completely revamped look and a less high-concept, but excellent, menu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When 42 opened six years ago, jackets were required and guests were treated to complex molecular gastronomy designed to dazzle and even shock, like a vinegar turned into powder and served on a mirror with octopus. Tweaks came after the financial crisis (jackets were no longer necessary, and a $79 prix fixe menu was offered), but the restaurant remained, in the words of its celebrated chef-owner, Anthony Goncalves, “a special-occasion place.”', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/nyregion/08DINEWE3/08DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 522, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/nyregion/08DINEWE3/08DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 522}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/nyregion/08DINEWE3/08DINEWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank'