e property rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wastewater Case Raises the Concept of Underground Trespassing', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wastewater Case and the Concept of Underground Trespassing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wells', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FPL Farming Ltd', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Processing Services', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-05T23:25:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Malewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80cdd885-9c5a-5e14-82a6-cc9c0a51a6fe', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80cdd885-9c5a-5e14-82a6-cc9c0a51a6fe'}, {'abstract': 'In the Australian thriller “Swerve,” a fatal car accident draws a passer-by into intrigue with a femme fatale and a briefcase full of money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/movies/swerve-a-thriller-set-in-the-australian-desert.html', 'snippet': 'In the Australian thriller “Swerve,” a fatal car accident draws a passer-by into intrigue with a femme fatale and a briefcase full of money.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Swerve,” a would-be thriller set in the Australian outback, throws a handful of familiar genre bits at the screen, including a very bad man, a menacing husband, a wily wife, a rootless stranger and a chunk of change. Certainly there’s promise in the setting, which with its swaths of desert and roads to nowhere evokes the violent sun-scorched world of “Red Rock West,” John Dahl’s 1993 cowboy noir about a chunk of change, a rootless stranger, a wily wife, a menacing husband and a very bad man. Yet to say that the films have similar parts is about as meaningful as pointing out that a 1970 Pontiac G.T.O. and a 1971 Ford Pinto both have internal combustion engines, when only one is worth the ride. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/06SWERVE_SPAN/06SWERVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/06SWERVE_SPAN/06SWERVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/06SWERVE_SPAN/06SWERVE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/06SWERVE_SPAN/06SWERVE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/06SWERVE_SPAN/06SWERVE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'w