None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/26f20755-f4cb-5c19-b2d0-605d51f8d938', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26f20755-f4cb-5c19-b2d0-605d51f8d938'}, {'abstract': 'A suicide car bomber struck a security force’s convoy on Thursday in northern Somalia, killing at least seven people and wounding 37.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/world/africa/somalia-suicide-bomber-attacks-convoy-in-the-north.html', 'snippet': 'A suicide car bomber struck a security force’s convoy on Thursday in northern Somalia, killing at least seven people and wounding 37.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A suicide car bomber struck a security force’s convoy on Thursday in northern Somalia, killing at least seven people and wounding 37, local officials and witnesses said. The convoy, which was attacked in the town of Boosaaso in the semiautonomous region of Puntland, included members of the Puntland Marine Forces and two foreigners who were training the local security forces. Details about the casualties were not immediately available, and no group claimed responsibility after the explosion. President Hassan Sheik Mohamud of Somalia condemned the attack, saying that “terrorists have lost the war on the battlefield and are now devoting all their efforts in harming innocent civilians.” The Shabab rebel movement has been waging an insurgency for years to impose a strict interpretation of Islamic law in Somalia, but Puntland has been relatively peaceful compared with other parts of the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somalia: Suicide Bomber Attacks Convoy in the North', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Somalia: Suicide Bomber Attacks Convoy in the North', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Mohammed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puntland (Somalia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohamud, Hassan Sheikh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T01:54:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b614e36-ea75-5513-94d4-346933726f15', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b614e36-ea75-5513-94d4-346933726f15'}, {'abstract': 'Little-known and long out of print, the children’s book “Your Police” was discovered by William J. Bratton in a library when he was a boy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/nyregion/picture-book-will-preside-with-bratton.html', 'snippet': 'Little-known and long out of print, the children’s book “Your Police” was discovered by William J. Bratton in a library when he was a boy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there was an unexpected star at the news conference on Thursday announcing that William J. Bratton would be New York City’s next police commissioner, it was a faded yellow copy of “Your Police,” a children’s picture book published in 1956, that Mr. Bratton tenderly held in his hands.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/nyregion/zaffo/zaffo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'l