', 'value': 'Malaria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T02:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8297afb6-c106-56b3-ac81-8805ef2bc829', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8297afb6-c106-56b3-ac81-8805ef2bc829'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-dec-5-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dec. 5, 2013', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Lottery Numbers for Dec. 5, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T02:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ac3d8ff-761f-5550-a65b-48d391eac36a', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ac3d8ff-761f-5550-a65b-48d391eac36a'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor-elect made two solid appointments: Anthony Shorris as first deputy mayor and William Bratton as New York police commissioner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/opinion/the-de-blasio-team-takes-shape.html', 'snippet': 'The mayor-elect made two solid appointments: Anthony Shorris as first deputy mayor and William Bratton as New York police commissioner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor-elect Bill de Blasio, who has promised a new vision for New York, has appointed two familiar, seasoned veterans to help him manage the nation’s largest city government. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The de Blasio Team Takes Shape', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The de Blasio Team Takes Shape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bratton, William J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shorris, Anthony E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T02:13:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/07a1fb97-9073-5328-a8c1-281d4e746e63', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07a1fb97-9073-5328-a8c1-281d4e746e63'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama recalled that his public career began at an anti-apartheid rally in 1979, imbued with the hope Nelson Mandela had generated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/world/africa/obama-mandela.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama recalled that his public career began at an anti-apartheid rally in 1979, imbued with the hope