rks', 'value': 'Lenny Cooke (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Out of the Furnace (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coen, Joel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coen, Ethan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Affleck, Casey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrelson, Woody', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bale, Christian', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T05:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Gabe Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/fd577905-396e-564a-865c-68cd3baa2a59', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/fd577905-396e-564a-865c-68cd3baa2a59'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7 P.M. (Sundance) VANILLA SKY (2001) David Aames (Tom Cruise), a 33-year-old master of the universe, finds his life upended after a car crash in Cameron Crowe’s erotic science-fiction adaptation of “Abre los Ojos,” Alejandro Amenábar’s Spanish romantic thriller. Cameron Diaz plays Julie Gianni, the latest plaything in David’s endless succession of beautiful women. Penélope Cruz (above, with Mr. Cruise), who starred in Mr. Amenábar’s original, is Sofia Serrano, whom Julie discovers David flirting with at the birthday party he neglected to invite her to. And suddenly the simple offer of a ride the next morning becomes a suicide leap as Julie drives her car off a bridge, leaving her dead and David condemned to wearing a latex mask. “With its roller-coaster plot and surreal special effects, ‘Vanilla Sky’ is not the kind of film one associates with Mr. Crowe,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times. “The most warmhearted of mainstream Hollywood directors, Mr. Crowe has in the past extended to his characters the affection of an unusually careful and sympathetic listener.” In this film, “that ear is not as sharp,” he continued. “Still, the movie carries a lingering tug of sweetness, most apparent in the film’s heady soundtrack,” which “evokes the dream of eternal youth that infuses ‘Vanilla Sky.’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/303078bd-82b4-586b-ae0a-3b7346dcc9c1', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/303078bd-82b4-586b-ae0a-3b7346dcc9c1'}, {'abstract': 'The death of Nelson Mandela drew tributes from both Chinese leaders and dissidents, reflecting his complicated legacy in a country that is struggling with human rights issues.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/in-china-mandela-is-claimed-by-authorities-and-dissidents-alike/', 'snippet': 'The death of Nelson Mandela drew tributes from both Chinese leaders and dissidents, reflecting his complicated legacy in a country that is struggling with human rights issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death of Nelson Mandela prompted widespread expressions of sympathy in China, an indication of how his many roles — campaigner in the fight against racial inequality, political prisoner, national leader and senior African statesman — appealed to numerous segments of Chinese society.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In China, Mandela Is Claimed by Authorities and Dissidents Alike', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snow, Edgar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN NATIONAL CONGRESS', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sina Weibo', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T06:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy and Mia Li', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Li', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9ac378e-