/2013/12/06/my-health-insurance-was-canceled/', 'snippet': 'Now I am panicked and irritated — but also hopeful that I can get a reasonably priced policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m one of the many people in the United States who have had their individual health insurance policy canceled since the full implementation of the Affordable Care Act began Oct. 1. I own the Quintessence Group, a marketing consulting company based in Philadelphia. I have seven employees, but I’ve dodged the staff health insurance bullet for years because all of my employees have either had insurance through their spouses or have worked as independent contractors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Health Insurance Was Canceled', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T14:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melinda F. Emerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melinda', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Emerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f78d1cf9-0f87-5ebf-8f91-9f42bf2a64b1', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f78d1cf9-0f87-5ebf-8f91-9f42bf2a64b1'}, {'abstract': 'The Times has backed an effort to fight restrictions on photographers but could go further.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/when-white-house-photos-are