ial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1143229f-c53a-5de1-a9c7-71103d075cb0', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1143229f-c53a-5de1-a9c7-71103d075cb0'}, {'abstract': 'Self-doubt can be a powerful ally in the battle against bad writing. It can also be a powerful obstacle to writing anything at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/magazine/the-dutch-elm-disease-of-creative-minds.html', 'snippet': 'Self-doubt can be a powerful ally in the battle against bad writing. It can also be a powerful obstacle to writing anything at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, I attended something called the Web Summit, a massive tech-industry conference held in Dublin over the course of a couple of days. The event had a two-tier structure: on one level, it was a vast, teeming trade show at which early-stage start-ups were given the opportunity to set out their stalls and sell themselves — to venture capitalists, angel investors, media people — and to network with one another; but on a more elevated plane, it was a grand conclave of the tech industry’s high priests, who came from all over the world (though mostly Northern California) to deliver talks and public interviews to audiences of several thousand. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08riff/mag-08Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 84, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08riff/mag-08Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 84}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08riff/mag-08Riff-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 144, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08riff/mag-08Riff-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 288, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08riff/mag-08Riff-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08riff/mag-08Riff-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08riff/mag-08Riff-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dutch-Elm Disease of Creative Minds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Sorry, Chief, but That’s Not Going to Cut It’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T15:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': "By Mark O'Connell", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connell", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa41d549-f2af-5afd-95d4-0760208782aa', 'word_count': 1871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa41d549-f2af-5afd-95d4-0760208782aa'}, {'abstract': 'The middle of the country is gorgeous from the air — and a very hard place on the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/magazine/life-along-the-100th-meridian.html', 'snippet': 'The middle of the country is gorgeous from the air — and a very hard place on the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the western panhandle of Nebraska, where it is not uncommon for newcomers to be asked, “So how long are you staying in our country?” the question of continuity repeats itself each day anew.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Along the 100th Meridian', 'kicker': 'Photo Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America at its Plainest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verzemnieks, Inara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Dakota', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T15:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Text by Inara Verzemnieks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Text', 'middlename': 'Inara', 'lastname': 'Verzemnieks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57a293b2-b401-5a94-9f9a-8aabf29f413c', 'word_count': 3767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57a293b2-b401-5a94-9f9a-8aabf29f413c'}, {'abstract': 'Partisan discrimination vs. racial discrimination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/magazine/is-voter-suppression-ok.html', 'snippet': 'Partisan discrimination vs. racial discrimination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I own a small manufacturing company, and recently I made a special order for a friend. He and I agreed on a certain price. My bookkeeper misunderstood my billing instructions and sent an invoice for less than the agreed-upon price. I discovered the mistake two weeks later. I contacted my friend to notify him of the mistake and to tell him we were sending out a corrected invoice. He said, “Your mistake is not my problem,” and that he would only pay the incorrect amount on the original invoice. Who is right? STEVE COHEN, BRIARCLIFF MANOR, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Costly Mistakes and Voter Suppression', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Costly Mistakes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klosterman, Chuck', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T15:37:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fa91cb9-571c-5527-82df-56861f5b06de', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fa91cb9-571c-5527-82df-56861f5b06de'}, {'abstract': 'The terror of having my very own employee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/magazine/i-guess-ill-manage.html', 'snippet': 'The terror of having my very own employee.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You’re in management,” my mother said. “You have to wear a bra.” She looked as if I’d shown up for breakfast wearing a codpiece and snorkel. I glanced down and realized that, indeed, I’d forgotten to wear a bra beneath my sweater. It hardly made a difference in the geography of the region, but I was ashamed of my absent-mindedness. A mother’s reproach is never sharper than at 7:30 on a Monday morning.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '74', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08lives/mag-08Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08lives/mag-08Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08lives/mag-08Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08lives/mag-08Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/magazine/08lives/mag-08Lives-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Guess I’ll Manage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Guess I’ll Manage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Molly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T15:37:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Molly Young', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Molly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Young', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab7e1a7-ae30-5012-be68-8a8b1f742295', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab7e1a7-ae30-5012-be68-8a8b1f742295'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/magazine/the-11-24-13-issue.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 