 reminds us, this quest isn’t always about food. Frequently — to borrow from Woody Allen — there must be a beverage.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208-bks-Travel/1208-bks-Travel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 559, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208-bks-Travel/1208-bks-Travel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 559}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208-bks-Travel/1208-bks-Travel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 954, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208-bks-Travel/1208-bks-Travel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1769, 'width': 1899, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208-bks-Travel/1208-bks-Travel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208-bks-Travel/1208-bks-Travel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208-bks-Travel/1208-bks-Travel-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Travel', 'kicker': 'Holiday Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Travel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammer, Joshua', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T16:02:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Hammer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hammer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d385792a-4f4a-566e-8626-3b6b9947c460', 'word_count': 2477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d385792a-4f4a-566e-8626-3b6b9947c460'}, {'abstract': 'Books that look back to the past stir the imagination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/books/review/beatrix-potters-gardening-life-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Books that look back to the past stir the imagination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'December is, of course, the holiday season, but for gardeners it’s also the reading season. In the garden, we play out fantasies, desires and longings, and the ensuing tussle with nature — sometimes gentle, sometimes violent — is for a beauty we can make. Like sex, quite a lot of gardening happens in the mind. This season, a few books that look back to the past may well stir your imagination. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208NEEDLEMANsub/1208NEEDLEMANsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208NEEDLEMANsub/1208NEEDLEMANsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208NEEDLEMANsub/1208NEEDLEMANsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208NEEDLEMANsub/1208NEEDLEMANsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1191, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208NEEDLEMANsub/1208NEEDLEMANsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208NEEDLEMANsub/1208NEEDLEMANsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208NEEDLEMANsub/1208NEEDLEMANsub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gardening Yesterday', 'kicker': 'Holiday Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gardening Yesterday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDowell, Marta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T16:02:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Needleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Needleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bda31859-8362-530b-83fb-480fb83550e8', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bda31859-8362-530b-83fb-480fb83550e8'}, {'abstract': 'Portfolios and visual memoirs by decorators attest to lives rich with clients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/books/review/howard-slatkins-fifth-avenue-style-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Portfolios and visual memoirs by decorators attest to lives rich with clients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It must be the whisper of time as it bends over the horizon, a susurration of mortality none can escape. What else could have prompted so many decorators to publish their portfolios, visual memoirs that attest to lives rich with clients? Decorating is one of the most evanescent of the visual arts. It’s painful to walk into a room in which every inch has been lavished with attention, imagination and money, only to learn that the wrecking ball is about to arrive, commissioned by the next decorator. Devastating — when it isn’t good riddance to bad rubbish. Sometimes it takes a while to tell the difference.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '76', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BROWNING/1208BROWNING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BROWNING/1208BROWNING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 640}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BROWNING/1208BROWNING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 961, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BROWNING/1208BROWNING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 1334, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BROWNING/1208BROWNING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BROWNING/1208BROWNING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BROWNING/1208BROWNING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Interiors', 'kicker': 'Holiday Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Interiors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Browning, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T16:03:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dominique Browning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dominique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfc004ba-e604-5288-890c-e1de25aae1ea', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfc004ba-e604-5288-890c-e1de25aae1ea'}, {'abstract': 'New books of photography by Sergio Larrain, Josef Koudelka and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/books/review/josef-koudelkas-wall-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'New books of photography by Sergio Larrain, Josef Koudelka and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes the world of photography books can seem not unlike that of popular music on disc, with endless repackaging of the classics — each new volume containing pictures that haven’t been previously reprinted, so that if you are a devotee or a completist you will have to shell out for another tome. And yet major surprises continue to arrive, dispatches from the past. Consider, for example, the work of the Chilean photographer Sergio Larrain (1931-2012), whose career was both extraordinary and unusually abbreviated. It was only after studying forestry at Berkeley that he began seriously taking pictures in the mid-1950s, and then an encounter with the Bolivian mystic Oscar Ichazo in 1968 caused him to retreat for the remainder of his life into meditation and yoga, taking small, quiet photos only occasionally, as complements to his inner quest. But for the decade or so that he was in the world and regularly taking pictures, his work, as amply illustrated in SERGIO LARRAIN (Aperture, $85), edited by Agnès Sire, was a constant source of wonder.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 200, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 200}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03/1208PHOTOGRAPHY03-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photography', 'kicker': 'Holiday Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Photography', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sante, Luc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T16:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luc Sante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec8dbac3-17b3-51b1-a74b-c29a3a5093e6', 'word_count': 1498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec8dbac3-17b3-51b1-a74b-c29a3a5093e6'}, {'abstract': 'Five books offer gardeners a chance to study other people’s work and pick up a few pointers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/books/review/catie-marrons-city-parks-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Five books offer gardeners a chance to study other people’s work and pick up a few pointers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For gardeners, winter is a period of rest, if not entirely of relaxation. The trees are bare, the flower beds dormant, the pruners and trowels packed away in the toolshed. All those hours once spent weeding and mowing can now be devoted to recalling our triumphs and brooding over our failures. There’s also, finally, enough leisure time to study other people’s gardens and pick up a few pointers. And yet, infuriatingly, many of those gardens are also in sleep mode. What to do? The answer to that question — as to so many others — can be found in a book. Five of them, to be precise. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '53', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BECKER/1208BECKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BECKER/1208BECKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 526}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BECKER/1208BECKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 897, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BECKER/1208BECKER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 1871, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BECKER/1208BECKER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BECKER/1208BECKER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208BECKER/1208BECKER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gardening Today', 'kicker': 'Holiday Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gardening Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T16:04:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alida Becker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Becker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb1bcd2-864b-57b6-a4b2-36f0cb3839a8', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb1bcd2-864b-57b6-a4b2-36f0cb3839a8'}, {'abstract': 'Two new books show off the staggering beauty of Antarctica and consider the future of this last clean place on earth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/books/review/southern-light-and-the-last-ocean.html', 'snippet': 'Two new books show off the staggering beauty of Antarctica and consider the future of this last clean place on earth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Antarctica is a life-changing place. From its first explorers to today’s hardy souls who live and work there, it has always drawn certain people to its austere and compelling majesty. If you go to Antarctica, it may or may not change your life. But what matters is that Antarctica itself is changing and, at the same time, changing us. These two books will first open your eyes to the staggering beauty of the place. Then they will chill you. At the bottom of the world, strange and terrifying things are happening miles above and beneath the icy surface, some of them understood, some not; many man-made, some irreversible and all determining the future of this last clean place on earth, and of earth itself. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208SINKLER/1208SINKLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 281, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208SINKLER/1208SINKLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 281}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208SINKLER/1208SINKLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208SINKLER/1208SINKLER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 958, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208SINKLER/1208SINKLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208SINKLER/1208SINKLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/books/review/1208SINKLER/1208SINKLER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Antarctica', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headl