ticular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HEIR APPARENT: A Life of Edward VII, the Playboy Prince,  by Jane Ridley. (Random House, $35.) He was vain, gluttonous, promiscuous and none too bright, but “Bertie” emerges as an appealing character in Ridley’s superb book.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '80', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T17:24:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/826090d3-7371-5bba-b017-6dc3f58b186a', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/826090d3-7371-5bba-b017-6dc3f58b186a'}, {'abstract': 'As Christians ask how their faith requires them to treat animals, they may force animal rights activists, a mostly secular lot, to reconsider their views on Christians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/us/exploring-christian-perspectives-on-animal-rights.html', 'snippet': 'As Christians ask how their faith requires them to treat animals, they may force animal rights activists, a mostly secular lot, to reconsider their views on Christians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — “There was a time when Rebecca, our eldest, was desperate to have a pet,” David Clough told me when we met at the American Academy of Religion conference, held in Baltimore before Thanksgiving. “And she was in the unhappy position of having a father who had reflected ethically on the question at some length” — a father with misgivings about the human use of animals, even for companionship.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/us/07beliefs-cnd/07beliefs-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/07/us/07beliefs-cnd/07beliefs-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/us/07beliefs-cnd/07beliefs-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/us/07beliefs-cnd/07beliefs-cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/us/07beliefs-cnd/07beliefs-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/07/us/07beliefs-cnd/07beliefs-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/us/07beliefs-cnd/07beliefs-cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scholars Explore Christian Perspectives on Animal Rights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scholars Explore Christian Perspectives on Animal Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T17:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6f1cd96-7305-5af5-b96f-317c3772f3d0', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6f1cd96-7305-5af5-b96f-317c3772f3d0'}, {'abstract': 'Since the downturn began in December 2007, the economy has had a net decline of about 1 percent in its nonfarm payroll jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/getting-back-to-even/', 'snippet': 'Since the downturn began in December 2007, the economy has had a net decline of about 1 percent in its nonfarm payroll jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the 38th consecutive month, the country added jobs: 203,000 nonfarm payroll jobs in November, to be more precise.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Back to Even', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Back to Even', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T17:29:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1f437a0-f3e1-5d2d-a2ea-43ece2868d6c', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1f437a0-f3e1-5d2d-a2ea-43ece2868d6c'}, {'abstract': 'VSPs, for real.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/what-i-said/', 'snippet': 'VSPs, for real.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m in a meeting of the Bavarian Illuminati Group of 30; very interesting discussion, all off the record. But I can’t resist mentioning that one participant, arguing that we should end easy-money policies despite the continuing depressed state of the economy, warned of potential costs and declared that these costs have been stressed by “very serious people.” The participant clearly did not have capital letters on the words, even implicitly. But I did have a hard time not laughing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Said', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T17:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cfe5be0-9119-5da6-b60e-cb12e5d45d15', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cfe5be0-9119-5da6-b60e-cb12e5d45d15'}, {'abstract': 'William B. Helmreich, armed with a pedometer and a tape recorder, explored a “city with 120,000 blocks” and came out with “The New York Nobody Knows.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/realestate/an-authors-legwork-6000-miles-on-new-york-streets.html', 'snippet': 'William B. Helmreich, armed with a pedometer and a tape recorder, explored a “city with 120,000 blocks” and came out with “The New York Nobody Knows.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the golden weeks of autumn, it seemed as if everyone in the world wanted to go for a walk with William B. Helmreich. The journalist from Norway. Students who have lapped up his courses at City College and the Graduate Center of the City University of New York. The publicist at Princeton University Press, which just published “The New York Nobody Knows: Walking 6,000 Miles in the City,” his doorstop-size account of four years of trekking into every corner of the five boroughs, dead-end streets and desolate industrial areas included.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/realestate/08SUBCOV2/08SUBCOV2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/realestate/08SUBCOV2/08SUBCOV2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/realestate/08SUBCOV2/08SUBCOV2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/realestate/08SUBCOV2/08SUBCOV2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/realestate/08SUBCOV2/08SUBCOV2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/reale