e historically been even worse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial-Crisis Recoveries, Compared', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Great Depression (1930's)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reinhart, Carmen M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogoff, Kenneth S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T19:14:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d65c151-c4c3-5144-ad55-9268eef5d9dd', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d65c151-c4c3-5144-ad55-9268eef5d9dd'}, {'abstract': 'The newer banking services appeal to younger people because they shun most fees and have no minimum balance requirements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/your-money/mobile-banks-gaining-popularity-with-young-consumers.html', 'snippet': 'The newer banking services appeal to younger people because they shun most fees and have no minimum balance requirements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TURIYA GOETZE, a 23-year-old teaching assistant in Kansas City, Kan., found herself looking for a new bank this summer. Her student checking account at a large national bank had expired, and she was worried about paying lots of fees on a traditional account.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'sub