iments. Now, with his death, his stature as a saintly wise man seems confirmed for eternity: there are Hollywood movies about him — he was impersonated by Morgan Freeman, who also, by the way, played the role of God in another film; rock stars and religious leaders, sportsmen and politicians from Bill Clinton to Fidel Castro are all united in his beatification.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mandela’s Socialist Failure', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitalism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socialism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T19:15:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Slavoj Zizek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Slavoj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zizek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4a2c75c-7387-517c-aad6-96fdc05454ac', 'word_count': 1017, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4a2c75c-7387-517c-aad6-96fdc05454ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Times critic Nicolas Rapold reviews "Lenny Cooke."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000002589308/movie-review-lenny-cooke.html', 'snippet': 'The Times critic Nicolas Rapold reviews "Lenny Cooke."', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times critic Nicolas Rapold reviews "Lenny Cooke."', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/video-movies-lenny