_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d29c3cf-3859-54d1-81e3-1427a34145ae', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d29c3cf-3859-54d1-81e3-1427a34145ae'}, {'abstract': 'Almost 10,000 New York City buildings damaged by Sandy were outside the official FEMA flood zones.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/what-if-the-flood-maps-are-just-plain-wrong/', 'snippet': 'Almost 10,000 New York City buildings damaged by Sandy were outside the official FEMA flood zones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Hurricane Sandy approached the Northeast coastline last year, hundreds of families felt secure that they would remain safely above the worst of it. Their confidence came from longstanding assurances that federal flood maps were correct, that their homes and businesses were officially outside the\xa0flood plains predicted for even the worst of storms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What if the Flood Maps Are Just Plain Wrong?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ProPublica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Randolph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Randolph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c865f140-069d-5cb1-af27-2aa6661ba1f1', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c865f140-069d-5cb1-af27-2aa6661ba1f1'}, {'abstract': 'Allowing second baseman Robinson Cano to leave for Seattle rather than significantly increase their offer of $175 million for seven years was a victory for the Yankees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/sports/baseball/yankees-try-a-new-strategy-restraint.html', 'snippet': 'Allowing second baseman Robinson Cano to leave for Seattle rather than significantly increase their offer of $175 million for seven years was a victory for the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This was their test. The Yankees, having already absorbed the costly and crippling embarrassment of a 10-year contract to a player over 30, were asked to do it again. They said no. They lost their best hitter Friday, yet it was a victory for the organization.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/07kepner1/07kepner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/07kepner1/07kepner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/07kepner1/07kepner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/07kepner1/07kepner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1468, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/07kepner1/07kepner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/07kepner1/07kepner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/07kepner1/07kepner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yanks Try a New Tactic: Restraint', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yanks Try a New Tactic: Restraint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Mariners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac5e1507-948e-51fb-a085-df9249ae7bf0', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac5e1507-948e-51fb-a085-df9249ae7bf0'}, {'abstract': 'The rigors of a police academy’s physical training tests don’t always translate to life as an officer.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/following-a-recruit-and-sizing-up-the-atlanta-police-force/', 'snippet': 'The rigors of a police academy’s physical training tests don’t always translate to life as an officer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In mid-August 2012, I was reporting the article that appears in this Sunday’s magazine about Jacob Deng Mach, a Sudanese refugee — one of the so-called Lost Boys — who was hoping to become an Atlanta police officer. The 22-week training was notoriously grueling, and on his sixth day at the academy, Mach pulled up lame during a one-and-half-mile run. Academy officials sent him to an orthopedic clinic that saw a steady stream of injured recruits, and I followed in my car along with the video reporter, Brent McDonald, and the photographer, Béatrice de Géa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/06-mach-workou/06-mach-workou-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/06-mach-workou/06-mach-workou-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/06-mach-workou/06-mach-workou-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/06-mach-workou/06-mach-workou-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1322, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/06-mach-workou/06-mach-workou-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/06-mach-workou/06-mach-workou-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/06-mach-workou/06-mach-workou-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Following a Recruit, and Sizing Up the Atlanta Police Force', 'kicker': 'The 6