 the Scandinavia-focused New York design gallery Hostler Burrows, says of the pieces: “They sell out as soon as we put them on the floor.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three’s a Trend | Wild, Woolly Chairs at Design Miami', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Delavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5ae0ec1-eeef-5bc9-9aec-ecad1c2baece', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5ae0ec1-eeef-5bc9-9aec-ecad1c2baece'}, {'abstract': 'After a fatal train derailment on Sunday, the Federal Railroad Administration ordered Metro-North to make changes in the interest of passenger safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/12/07/nyregion/emergency-order-for-metro-north.html', 'snippet': 'After a fatal train derailment on Sunday, the Federal Railroad Administration ordered Metro-North to make changes in the interest of passenger safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a fatal train derailment on Sunday, the Federal Railroad Administration ordered Metro-North to make changes in the interest of passenger safety.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emergency Order for Metro-North', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-North Commuter Railroad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Railroad Administration', 'rank': 3