insurance-exchange.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration said Friday that the enrollment records for roughly a quarter of all the people who signed up for health insurance on its website in October and November could contain errors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration said Friday that the enrollment records for roughly a quarter of all the people who signed up for health insurance on its website in October and November could contain errors, raising questions about whether those consumers would get coverage in time to pay for their medical care next month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Enrollment Errors Put Medical Coverage at Risk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enrollment Errors Put Medical Coverage at Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:29:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fac0c063-e1b2-5861-a710-4504287944cb', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fac0c063-e1b2-5861-a710-4504287944cb'}, {'abstract': '“Six by Sondheim,” an HBO documentary on Monday, looks at the car