TION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hyundai Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guarantees and Warranties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:39:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8491148f-f154-5c72-91e7-195a47f52b78', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8491148f-f154-5c72-91e7-195a47f52b78'}, {'abstract': 'The battlefront of photographic traffic enforcement is moving to the dashboard, where an increasing number of gadgets are alerting drivers to the locations of cameras.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/automobiles/on-alert-for-red-light-cameras.html', 'snippet': 'The battlefront of photographic traffic enforcement is moving to the dashboard, where an increasing number of gadgets are alerting drivers to the locations of cameras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Banished by voters in Houston, facing legal challenges in Missouri and working undercover in New York City, traffic-monitoring cameras, promoted as accident-reducing tools by safety advocates and decried as intrusive revenue-generators by opponents, are nothing if not controversial. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/automobiles/REDLIGHT/REDLIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/automobiles/REDLIGHT/RE