rts/television/holliday-grainger-on-becoming-bonnie-parker.html', 'snippet': 'The British actress Holliday Grainger, of “The Borgias” and “Great Expectations,” discusses how she trained for her title role in “Bonnie & Clyde.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why would an English rose portray a Texas thistle?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT/08SNAPSHOT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT/08SNAPSHOT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1018}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT/08SNAPSHOT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 604, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT/08SNAPSHOT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1625, 'width': 958, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT/08SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT/08SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/arts/08SNAPSHOT/08SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Picking Up a Gun and an Accent', 'kicker': 'Snapshot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Picking Up a Gun and an Accent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grainger, Holliday', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Kathryn', 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf01dee-a738-5e19-a047-63a35f7479c8', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf01dee-a738-5e19-a047-63a35f7479c8'}, {'abstract': 'Cécile McLorin Salvant is the latest answer to the question of what jazz has to do with you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/arts/music/a-singer-is-part-of-the-big-picture.html', 'snippet': 'Cécile McLorin Salvant is the latest answer to the question of what jazz has to do with you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, a 25-foot-tall photograph of the jazz singer Cécile McLorin Salvant has been on view outside the main entrance to Jazz at Lincoln Center, at 60th Street and Broadway. Such a distinction happened quickly by jazz-world standards. She’s 24, and her first album with any distribution, “WomanChild” (Mack Avenue), came out only six months ago. But it’s not surprising that Jazz at Lincoln Center should want to go out on a limb to promote her. Though she writes her own songs, she puts original, idiosyncratic and virtuosic force on old repertory, some of it from the high era of American songbook standards, some of it older than jazz itself. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Singer Is Part of the Big Picture', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Singer Is Part Of the Big Picture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:46:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da219968-c9db-50c4-af70-2e00d375c30e', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da219968-c9db-50c4-af70-2e00d375c30e'}, {'abstract': 'The superb violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter is back in town this week, and celebration is on her agenda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/arts/music/commemoration-and-celebration.html', 'snippet': 'The superb violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter is back in town this week, and celebration is on her agenda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The superb violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter is back in town this week, and celebration is on her agenda. On Tuesday night, she will join the New York Philharmonic to herald her new Deutsche Grammophon CD, a red-blooded account of Dvorak’s rich, robust Violin Concerto. Manfred Honeck, who conducts the Berlin Philharmonic on the disc, will also direct her Philharmonic rendition of the work, presented alongside Dvorak’s “Carnival” Overture and “New World” Symphony. (7:30 p.m. Tuesday, Avery Fisher Hall, Lincoln Center, 212-875-5656, nyphil.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commemoration and Celebration', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Commemoration And Celebration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:46:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dc7b662-8614-5120-828e-ee55f3209768', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dc7b662-8614-5120-828e-ee55f3209768'}, {'abstract': 'Is it possible to have a catfight on horseback? We may find out thanks to “Rodeo Girls.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/arts/television/even-cowgirls-get-a-show.html', 'snippet': 'Is it possible to have a catfight on horseback? We may find out thanks to “Rodeo Girls.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it possible to have a catfight on horseback? We may find out thanks to “Rodeo Girls,” a reality series that begins on Wednesday at 11 p.m. on A&E.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Cowgirls Get a Show', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even Cowgirls Get a Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4823897f-9482-53e9-9840-1f255e775b1c', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4823897f-9482-53e9-9840-1f255e775b1c'}, {'abstract': 'The eclectic, genre-busting festival Migrating Forms, now in its fifth year, has itself migrated — to BAMcinématek.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/movies/new-home-for-a-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The eclectic, genre-busting festival Migrating Forms, now in its fifth year, has itself migrated — to BAMcinématek.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The eclectic, genre-busting festival Migrating Forms, now in its fifth year, has itself migrated — to BAMcinématek. As for forms, expect all types, from experimental shorts to features by the Hong Kong auteur Johnnie To. The festival opens on Wednesday with an art-gallery-meets art-house punch: four shorts by Ryan Trecartin first presented as an installation at the Venice Biennale. Mr. Trecartin — he “seems bound for greatness,” the art critic Roberta Smith wrote in The New York Times — will introduce the films.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Home for a Festival', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Home For a Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:47:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f129f85b-3f06-5129-a306-58312354af1a', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f129f85b-3f06-5129-a306-58312354af1a'}, {'abstract': 'It’s easy to associate flamenco with wild stamping, and Soledad Barrio can stamp with fury.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/arts/dance/footwork-with-fury.html', 'snippet': 'It’s easy to associate flamenco with wild stamping, and Soledad Barrio can stamp with fury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s easy to associate flamenco with wild stamping, and Soledad Barrio can stamp with fury. But she can also do more than that — much more. Her dynamic and emotional range helps make her one of today’s leading exponents of this traditional Spanish form. In her company, Noche Flamenca, she is surrounded by excellent dancing partners, guitarists and singers, and the little troupe can seem like a family onstage. In her solos, Ms. Barrio invests old flamenco forms with new life, showing herself capable of both light dartings and outbursts of raw passion, her footwork recalling laughter at one moment and gunfire the next. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Footwork With Fury', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footwork With Fury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flamenco (Dance)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac4534e9-cd34-5d4f-a32f-d9cf2f791b6a', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac4534e9-cd34-5d4f-a32f-d9cf2f791b6a'}, {'abstract': 'The oldest man-made, outdoor object in New York is the towering, granite obelisk in Central Park known as Cleopatra’s Needle: It’s nearly 3,500 years old.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/arts/design/a-big-bit-of-egypt-in-central-park.html', 'snippet': 'The oldest man-made, outdoor object in New York is the towering, granite obelisk in Central Park known as Cleopatra’s Needle: It’s nearly 3,500 years old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The oldest man-made, outdoor object in New York is the towering, granite obelisk in Central Park known as Cleopatra’s Needle: It’s nearly 3,500 years old. The story of the 69-foot-tall, 220-ton, hieroglyphic-covered, Egyptian monolith is examined in “Cleopatra’s Needle,” an exhibition at the Metropolitan Museum of Art that includes drawings, prints, photographs and textiles. One of a pair — the other, with the same name, is in London — the ancient obelisk and its companion were commissioned by Thutmose III in about 1450 B.C. for a sun temple in Heliopolis. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A (Big) Bit of Egypt in Central Park', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A (Big) Bit of Egypt In Central Park', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T21:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c91a84c-0725-5811-89e1-8ac59acc0f26', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c91a84c-0725-5811-89e1-8ac59acc0f26'}, {'abstract': 'New releases include vintage sets from Thelonious Monk and Neil Young, a Nina Simone tribute by Xiu Xiu and an EP by Shelby Lynne.', 'web_url': 'https://www.ny