 {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiNapoli, Thomas P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T22:20:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/434a6f80-6a9a-50ce-af8d-a2f240ecc4e8', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/434a6f80-6a9a-50ce-af8d-a2f240ecc4e8'}, {'abstract': 'David Zinman, music director of the Tonhalle in Zurich, is leading the New York Philharmonic in a Mendelssohn, Mozart and Adès program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/arts/music/david-zinman-leads-philharmonic-in-mendelssohn-and-mozart.html', 'snippet': 'David Zinman, music director of the Tonhalle in Zurich, is leading the New York Philharmonic in a Mendelssohn, Mozart and Adès program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many guest conductors come to the New York Philharmonic angling to make an impression. Not so the respected American conductor David Zinman, who led the orchestra on Thursday night at Avery Fisher Hall like a musician who had nothing to prove. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/arts/07PHIL/07PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/07/arts/07PHIL/07PHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/arts/07PHIL/07PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo',