0-bb60-6151ef3fd75f'}, {'abstract': 'Stacey Kent is performing wistful songs from her latest album at Birdland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/arts/music/stacey-kent-at-birdland.html', 'snippet': 'Stacey Kent is performing wistful songs from her latest album at Birdland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The narrator of the exquisite title song of Stacey Kent’s new album, “The Changing Lights,” remembers a carefree conversation years earlier in the back seat of a cab, in which she and her companion “vowed to guard our dreams from all the storms that lay ahead” and “laughed about the hopelessness of so many people’s lives as we slowly moved toward the changing lights.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spectral Lure of the Magic That Faded', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spectral Lure Of the Magic That Faded', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kent, Stacey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Birdland (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T22:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ce9e1ca-9813-5950-a883-6f3cec89413e', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ce9e1ca-9813-5950-a883-6f3cec89413e'}, {'abstract': 'Beth McCarthy-Miller, who directed “The Sound of Music” for NBC on Thursday, discussed what went right and wrong during the telecast.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/sound-of-music-director-on-what-went-right-and-wrong/', 'snippet': 'Beth McCarthy-Miller, who directed “The Sound of Music” for NBC on Thursday, discussed what went right and wrong during the telecast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twitter had its fun and the critics were largely unimpressed, but mathematically speaking, NBC’s live “Sound of Music” ended up being a success for the network. Roughly 18.5 million viewers tuned in to watch Carrie Underwood and the rest of the cast rework the Von Trapp saga.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/sound/sound-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/sound/sound-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/sound/sound-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/sound/sound-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1268, 'width': 1941, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/sound/sound-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/sound/sound-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/arts/sound/sound-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Sound of Music’ Director on What Went Right — and Wrong', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy-Miller, Beth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-06T22:21:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/156eb13e-97e4-5a76-ae54-58901aada2ed', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/156eb13e-97e4-5a76-ae54-58901aada2ed'}, {'abstract': 'The photographers João Silva, David C. Turnley and Louise Gubb remember what it was like to photograph Nelson Mandela’s life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/12/06/world/africa/mandela-photographers.html', 'snippet': 'The photographers João Silva, David C. Turnley and Louise Gubb remember what it was like to photograph Nelson Mandela’s life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographers João Silva, David C. Turnley and Louise Gubb remember what it was like to photograph Nelson Mandela’s life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/07/01/world/africa/turnley_mandela-slide-AHXU/turnley_mandela-slide-AHXU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/07/01/world/africa/turnley_mandela-slide-AHXU/turnley_mandela-slide-AHXU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',