r': None, 'print_headline': 'Asbestos and Cigarettes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asbestos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lung Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T00:33:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/55fc95b7-132f-5916-84f1-60b8f6d3f26d', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55fc95b7-132f-5916-84f1-60b8f6d3f26d'}, {'abstract': 'An alien would have met his match with New Yorkers in high-tech style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/fashion/Bill-Cunningham-on-the-street-Futurism-in-Mens-Wear-street-style.html', 'snippet': 'An alien would have met his match with New Yorkers in high-tech style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cutting edge of fashion is definitely reflected in the young men experimenting with new technologies in fabrics and daring cuts and colors. Last Saturday, a multiday pop-up art installation caught the spirit of this fashion wave. From the upper left, diagonally to the lower right, two artists from Atlanta, Trey Wadsworth and Trever Nichols, landed in New York at 2 a.m. with an alien in a spaceship “crashing” near the Flatiron Building. They built their creation, including statues of revelers on park benches. Mr. Wadsworth is shown seated next to his “wino,” Mr. Nichols is to Mr. Wadsworth’s left. The alien met his match with New Yorkers in high-tech style. In October in Paris, one man wore a suit with contrasting fabric inserted in the jacket (bottom row, first four photos from left). One Parisian had enough piercings to scare any alien.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Futurism in Men’s Wear', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flatiron District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T00:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b697184-a7a5-5fd6-b666-6ad756e3205d', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b697184-a7a5-5fd6-b666-6ad756e3205d'}, {'abstract': 'Cinthia Schuman Ottinger of the Aspen Institute endorses a congressional proposal to reduce fraud by nonprofits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/opinion/transparency-on-charities.html', 'snippet': 'Cinthia Schuman Ottinger of the Aspen Institute endorses a congressional proposal to reduce fraud by nonprofits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transparency on Charities', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transparency on Charities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T00:34:56+0000', 'document_type': 'articl