o: He had reservations about the mayor-elect’s impending choice for police commissioner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio Style Evident in Effort to Sway Critics of Bratton', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio Style Evident in Effort to Sway Critics of Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bratton, William J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T02:47:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ec83b0-1af7-52e6-b2e5-a59725d42bce', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ec83b0-1af7-52e6-b2e5-a59725d42bce'}, {'abstract': 'After decades of Vatican indifference and evasion, the new church leader will seek reform proposals from a global commission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/opinion/a-popes-new-path-on-child-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'After decades of Vatican indifference and evasion, the new church leader will seek reform proposals from a global commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After decades of Vatican indifference and evasion, Pope Francis has ordered the creation of a commission to study the rape and intimidation of schoolchildren by priests and to recommend measures for effective reform. The new commission, long overdue, will be composed of international experts, both lay and religious, reflecting the global scope of the scandal. Its task is to propose concrete recommendations for firmer safeguarding of schoolchildren and better training of Roman Catholic priests. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pope’s New Path on Child Abuse', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pope’s New Path on Child Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T02:50:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6032be53-55b3-528d-961f-87c7b0e7a4cf', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6032be53-55b3-528d-961f-87c7b0e7a4cf'}, {'abstract': 'Forcibly returning detainees to countries where they reasonably fear for their safety is a perverse move.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/opinion/a-bad-decision-at-guantanamo.html', 'snippet': 'Forcibly returning detainees to countries where they reasonably fear for their safety is a perverse move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a perverse move, the Defense Department announced on Thursday that it had sent two of the longest-held detainees at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, both Algerian citizens, back to Algeria against their will.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bad Decision at Guantánamo', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bad Decision at Guantánamo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bensayah, Belkacem', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ameziane, Djamel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T02:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddf2aaa1-2cf5-53e4-ae11-ab7ddfc57d52', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddf2aaa1-2cf5-53e4-ae11-ab7ddfc57d52'}, {'abstract': 'The Neediest Cases Fund helps a young woman find a room of her own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/opinion/finding-a-quiet-space.html', 'snippet': 'The Neediest Cases Fund helps a young woman find a room of her own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dionne Parsons grew up in her aunt’s home among seven siblings and three cousins, sharing a bedroom with four girls. There was plenty of noise and an occasional good time, but no privacy. “I want my own space,” said Ms. Parsons, who is 23. “That’s my whole thing.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding a Quiet Space', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding a Quiet Space', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Community Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T02:53:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/436ba134-8b96-5516-aedf-707e6e14d249', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/436ba134-8b96-5516-aedf-707e6e14d249'}, {'abstract': 'The incoming commissioner, William J. Bratton, relied on many of the aggressive techniques that have proved divisive in New York, while navigating complicated racial tensions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/nyregion/brattons-time-in-california-may-offer-clues-to-his-plans-for-new-york-police.html', 'snippet': 'The incoming commissioner, William J. Bratton, relied on many of the aggressive techniques that have proved divisive in New York, while navigating complicated racial tensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — It was a moment of crisis for the Los Angeles Police Department, and it threatened to derail William J. Bratton’s tenure as its chief. Tens of thousands had gathered for a long-planned immigration rally on May 1, 2007, at a city park. As protesters began to block the street, a police helicopter blasted orders for the crowd to disperse. Moments later, dozens of officers wielded batons and shot 240 rounds of rubber bullets into the crowd.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'c