.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/decades-after-the-cultural-revolution-a-rare-letter-of-remorse/', 'snippet': 'The son of a famed Chinese official posted a letter apologizing for his role in the abuse of his teachers during the Cultural Revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an apology for his actions as a student during the Cultural Revolution, Chen Xiaolu, the son of China’s famed Foreign Minister, Chen Yi, published a notice in his school alumni blog in August. A profile based on interviews with Mr. Chen in the Saturday editions of the New York Times and the International New York Times refers to the apology, a rare expression of remorse from someone involved in carrying out Mao’s orders. Mr. Chen explains the apology was too long in coming, and says reflections on the past are necessary in order for China to move forward.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/world/08sino-xiaolu02/08sino-xiaolu02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/world/08sino-xiaolu02/08sino-xiaolu02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/world/08sino-xiaolu02/08sino-xiaolu02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/world/08sino-xiaolu02/08sino-xiaolu02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/world/08sino-xiaolu02/08sino-xiaolu02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/world/08sino-xiaolu02/08sino-xiaolu02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/world/08sino-xiaolu02/08sino-xiaolu02-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Decades After the Cultural Revolution, a Rare Letter of Remorse', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forced Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen Yi (1901-72)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International New York Times', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T03:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5796b4af-2e11-5680-9e40-a442907449de', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5796b4af-2e11-5680-9e40-a442907449de'}, {'abstract': 'In T’s final issue of the year, we get into the festive mood of the season and pay tribute to the creative genius of Rei Kawakubo, the enduring allure of iconic old restaurants, the seduction of Tangier and more.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/06/now-online-the-holiday-issue/', 'snippet': 'In T’s final issue of the year, we get into the festive mood of the season and pay tribute to the creative genius of Rei Kawakubo, the enduring allure of iconic old restaurants, the seduction of Tangier and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T’s final issue of 2013 is a festive affair. In our cover story, Suzy Menkes celebrates the enigmatic designer Rei Kawakubo of Comme des Garçons, who is bringing the “beautiful chaos” of Dover Street Market, her multibrand fashion bazaar, to New York’s Kips Bay neighborhood. Elsewhere, we visit four prominent artists — Jeff Koons, KAWS, Ugo Rondidone and Chuck Close — to find out what sorts of work they themselves collect, and what their collections say about them. At the Park Avenue apartment of Renee and Mark Rockefeller, we find that the color beige doesn’t have to be tepid and uninspired; deployed with a discerning eye, it can be smart and seductive. We capture the zany wit of Kristen Wiig, who appears in the forthcoming film “The Secret Life of Walter Mitty,” by asking her to fill in the blanks in a Mad Lib that (sort of) describes her career trajectory to date. We visit the Moroccan city of Tangier, which, as home to expats like Pierre Bergé, Bernard-Henry Lévy and Roger Vivier, remains one of the world’s great melting pots for creative types. We meditate on the magic touch of the hotelier André Balazs. We pay tribute to the enduring glamour of well-preserved old restaurants, from Paris’s La Grenouille to New York City’s “21” Club, that feel trapped in amber. And finally, in the spirit of the season, we offer the very best gifts you can give, from food to fragrances to jewelry to adventures of a lifetime. See all stories from the issue >> ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Holiday Issue', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Close, Chuck', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kawakubo, Rei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menkes, Suzy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T03:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0c1aa9f-8e11-505f-9487-648dfa7695fb', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0c1aa9f-8e11-505f-9487-648dfa7695fb'}, {'abstract': 'Too few charitable deductions actually serve the public good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/opinion/how-the-government-gives.html', 'snippet': 'Too few charitable deductions actually serve the public good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWTON, Mass. — THIS is the season of giving, the time when Americans from all income levels make donations to support food pantries, health centers, art and educational institutions, and other organizations that are so important for our civic society. Many donors work hard to stretch their charitable dollars to provide the maximum benefit for those in need. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype':