d-against-minorities-judge-says.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge ruled that Garden City’s zoning change that favored the building of single-family homes over modestly priced apartments in 2004 “tended to perpetuate segregation.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge ruled on Friday that the predominantly white Long Island village of Garden City had intentionally discriminated against blacks and Hispanics when it enacted a zoning change in 2004 that favored the building of townhouses or single-family homes over modestly priced apartments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Island Village Intentionally Discriminated Against Minorities, Judge Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Island Village Intentionally Discriminated Against Minorities, Judge Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Garden City (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T04:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89cf1e3e-987d-5e25-aae0-425b07823e33', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89cf1e3e-987d-5e25-aae0-425b07823e33'}, {'abstract': 'A group r