 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/BELTRAN/BELTRAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/BELTRAN/BELTRAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1444, 'width': 1040, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/BELTRAN/BELTRAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/BELTRAN/BELTRAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/BELTRAN/BELTRAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Reportedly Sign Beltran to Three-Year, $45 Million Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Sign Beltran, 36, To 3-Year Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T05:18:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b05b785-75c4-58c6-8adc-8026ef301337', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b05b785-75c4-58c6-8adc-8026ef301337'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) STOKER (2013) In his English-language debut, the South Korean director Park Chan-wook (“Oldboy,” “Lady Vengeance”) tells the story of India Stoker (Mia Wasikowska), a solitary Connecticut teenager embroiled in a landscape of family secrets, sexual subtext and aristocratic entitlement after her father (Dermot Mulroney) dies in a car accident on her 18th birthday. Then her handsome Uncle Charlie (Matthew Goode), whom she never knew, comes to visit her mother (Nicole Kidman, above left, with Ms. Wasikowska), who seems insufficiently grief-stricken to her daughter. That’s when the family’s housekeeper (Phyllis Somerville) disappears, and a worried relative (Jacki Weaver) alludes to further danger ahead. “A great deal of information has been withheld, perhaps from India and certainly from us, and Mr. Park, with sadistic relish, takes his time with revelations that are both ghastly and a bit disappointing,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “The exquisite sense of mystery that has built up around India begins to dissipate as the focus shifts to Charlie, and tantalizing ambiguities are resolved into a tale of madness and murder.” Which, he added, “is not so bad, though the final act of ‘Stoker’ walks a fine line between the sensational and the silly.” Learning the truth about Charlie, Mr. Scott said, “does not so much explain what had come before as turn everything upside down, scattering the puzzle pieces in a colorful, brutal cascade.” The actor Wentworth Miller (“Prison Break”) wrote the screenplay.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d7dc68d-a39d-51f3-9f5c-6dda17c09051', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d7dc68d-a39d-51f3-9f5c-6dda17c09051'}, {'abstract': 'In the 51 years that the Mets and the Yankees have shared New York, more than 100 players have worn the uniforms of both teams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/sports/baseball/goodbye-bronx-hello-queens.html', 'snippet': 'In the 51 years that the Mets and the Yankees have shared New York, more than 100 players have worn the uniforms of both teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 51 years that the Mets and the Yankees have shared New York, although hardly equally, more than 100 players have worn the uniforms of both teams. And that figure doesn’t include Casey Stengel, who managed both clubs. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/YOGI/YOGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/YOGI/YOGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 667}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/07/sports/YOGI/YOGI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name'