turtles-armorclads-and-the-civil-war-on-the-rivers/', 'snippet': 'Forget the Monitor and the Merrimac: The real ironclad war was on the nation’s interior rivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Battle of Hampton Roads, in March 1862, was the world’s first engagement between armored warships. Yet the Union’s Monitor and the Confederacy’s Virginia were far from the world’s first ironclads. The British, French and Russians had used armored floating batteries in the previous decade’s Crimean War. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pook Turtles, Armorclads and the Civil War on the Rivers', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T16:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Devin Poore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Devin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51fb823d-5bd9-5a90-868a-b1041583737a', 'word_count': 1547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51fb823d-5bd9-5a90-868a-b1041583737a'}, {'abstract': 'A power failure interrupted the Super Bowl in February. The organizers of the Super Bowl at MetLife Stadium want to make sure there’s no repeat in February.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/sports/football/hoping-to-keep-the-lights-on-at-this-seasons-super-bowl.html', 'snippet': 'A power failure interrupted the Super Bowl in February. The organizers of the Super Bowl at MetLife Stadium want to make sure there’s no repeat in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Kelly, the head of the host committee for this season’s Super Bowl, was with Woody Johnson, the Jets’ owner, when the lights went out at the Super Bowl in New Orleans in February. As they struggled in Johnson’s dimly lit suite to comprehend what had happened, Kelly had an additional thought.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/DOG-power/DOG-power-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/DOG-power/DOG-power-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/DOG-power/DOG-power-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/DOG-power/DOG-power-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1154, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/DOG-power/DOG-power-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/DOG-power/DOG-power-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/DOG-power/DOG-power-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Working to Keep the Lights On at This Season’s Super Bowl', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Working to