rent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/sports/football/Russell-Wilson-Colin-Kaepernick-on-rise-and-on-collision-course.html', 'snippet': 'The Seahawks’ Russell Wilson and 49ers’ Colin Kaepernick appear to be quarterback stars in the making, but in many ways, they could not be more different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the next great quarterback rivalry percolates on the West Coast, Sunday’s game between the Seattle Seahawks and the San Francisco 49ers represents more than another fight for playoff positioning. It is a clash of public personas between Russell Wilson and Colin Kaepernick. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/football/08quarterbacks1/08quarterbacks1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/football/08quarterbacks1/08quarterbacks1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/football/08quarterbacks1/08quarterbacks1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/football/08quarterbacks1/08quarterbacks1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1426, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/football/08quarterbacks1/08quarterbacks1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/football/08quarterbacks1/08quarterbacks1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sports/football/08quarterbacks1/08quarterbacks1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Quarterbacks on Rise, and on Collision Course', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wilson and Kaepernick Grow Into Their Roles as Rising Stars Differently', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Russell', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:28:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75abb1bd-4052-52d0-b108-a5b8cd1a1e13', 'word_count': 1372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75abb1bd-4052-52d0-b108-a5b8cd1a1e13'}, {'abstract': 'This year, I was a judge for the National Book Awards. A day when I got through only a single book felt like a day of delinquency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/opinion/sunday/caution-reading-can-be-hazardous.html', 'snippet': 'This year, I was a judge for the National Book Awards. A day when I got through only a single book felt like a day of delinquency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT long ago I had to be treated for a retinal tear. My eye doctor says this could have happened at just about any time and was most likely the result of nothing more than middle age, but I think he’s wrong. I’m pretty sure I tore my retina from reading too much. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08MCGRATH/08MCGRATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 986, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08MCGRATH/08MCGRATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 986}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08MCGRATH/08MCGRATH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 624, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08MCGRATH/08MCGRATH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1247, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08MCGRATH/08MCGRATH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08MCGRATH/08MCGRATH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08MCGRATH/08MCGRATH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Caution: Reading Can Be Hazardous', 'kicker': 'Dispatch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caution: Reading Can Be Hazardous', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Book Awards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:28:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/58a6fb56-3230-5d72-915a-84c6a2795bbc', 'word_count': 1258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58a6fb56-3230-5d72-915a-84c6a2795bbc'}, {'abstract': 'The death of the South African leader Nelson Mandela and the interim Iranian nuclear deal are expected to dominate the discussion on Sunday’s news shows.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/sunday-breakfast-menu-dec-8/', 'snippet': 'The death of the South African leader Nelson Mandela and the interim Iranian nuclear deal are expected to dominate the discussion on Sunday’s news shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson Mandela, the first black president of South Africa, died Thursday, leaving many to eulogize and honor the world leader. Mr. Mandela led his country’s emancipation from white minority control, after spending 27 years in prison for opposing apartheid rule. Many Sunday shows will celebrate the life and legacy of Mr. Mandela, gathering guests who knew him both personally and professionally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, Dec. 8', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:28:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f9f0363-6766-56c4-903d-fd9e14019455', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f9f0363-6766-56c4-903d-fd9e14019455'}, {'abstract': 'Woodrow Wilson was nicknamed Tiger — for Princeton, for feeling caged in the White House, and for his passion as a lover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/opinion/sunday/woodrow-wilson-stud-muffin.html', 'snippet': 'Woodrow Wilson was nicknamed Tiger — for Princeton, for feeling caged in the White House, and for his passion as a lover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — ON Thursday night, we sat around, talking about the lawyer and constitutional expert in the White House, a leader both didactic and charming, peacenik and hawk; the Ivy League academic who improbably ascended to the Oval Office on brains, not beholden to anyone; the Democrat, eager to fight economic inequality and help the 99 percent, who would give a government bailout if he had to; the dapper man with large ears, elegant speeches he wrote himself, a love of golf. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/maureen-dowd/maureen-dowd-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/maureen-dowd/maureen-dowd-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/maureen-dowd/maureen-dowd-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam