Sunday Dialogue: Partisanship in the Media', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4407f3da-1760-59ef-9df1-18f2ace36b3e', 'word_count': 1916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4407f3da-1760-59ef-9df1-18f2ace36b3e'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a big hole to fill.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/secular-stagnation-arithmetic/', 'snippet': 'There’s a big hole to fill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still playing around with the question of secular stagnation. Based on some recent conversations, it seems to me that it’s useful to put some numbers to the issue – to quantify, at least roughly, the hole that seems to have developed in sustainable demand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secular Stagnation Arithmetic', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb0acb6-d423-5d26-884b-3ef8c4cde835', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb0acb6-d423-5d26-884b-3ef8c4cde835'}, {'abstract': 'America turned back a Canadian who was traveling for a vacation cruise because she had been hospitalized for depression the previous year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/opinion/sunday/shameful-profiling-of-the-mentally-ill.html', 'snippet': 'America turned back a Canadian who was traveling for a vacation cruise because she had been hospitalized for depression the previous year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A CANADIAN woman was denied entry to the United States last month because she had been hospitalized for depression in 2012. Ellen Richardson could not visit, she was told, unless she obtained “medical clearance” from one of three Toronto doctors approved by the Department of Homeland Security. Endorsement by her own psychiatrist, which she could presumably have obtained more efficiently, “would not suffice.” She had been en route to New York, where she had intended to board a cruise to the Caribbean.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08SOLOMON/08SOLOMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08SOLOMON/08SOLOMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08SOLOMON/08SOLOMON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08SOLOMON/08SOLOMON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1499, 'width': 1199, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08SOLOMON/08SOLOMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08SOLOMON/08SOLOMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/sunday-review/08SOLOMON/08SOLOMON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shameful Profiling of the Mentally Ill', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shameful Profiling of the Mentally Ill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solomon, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Customs and Border Protection (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson, Ellen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:33:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6173d23-0885-5805-9cb1-8c753c69d739', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6173d23-0885-5805-9cb1-8c753c69d739'}, {'abstract': 'Arctic states have asserted exclusive drilling rights, but the region is not likely to surrender its resources easily.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/opinion/sunday/rushing-for-the-arctics-riches.html', 'snippet': 'Arctic states have asserted exclusive drilling rights, but the region is not likely to surrender its resources easily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMHERST, Mass. — WHILE many existing oil and gas reserves in other parts of the world are facing steep decline, the Arctic is thought to possess vast untapped reservoirs. Approximately 13 percent of the world’s undiscovered oil deposits and 30 percent of its natural gas reserves are above the Arctic Circle, according to the United States Geological Survey. Eager to tap into this largess, Russia and its Arctic neighbors — Canada, Norway, the United States, Iceland and Denmark (by virtue of its authority over Greenland) — have encouraged energy companies to drill in the region. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/opinion/08arctic-img/08arctic-img-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 538, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/opinion/08arctic-img/08arctic-img-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1075, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rushing for the Arctic’s Riches', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rushing for the Arctic’s Riches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:34:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael T. Klare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Klare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d8df915-496a-59cb-ba35-2f3c1ae82a42', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d8df915-496a-59cb-ba35-2f3c1ae82a42'}, {'abstract': 'Digital: maybe the big stuff is just starting to arrive.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/07/gordon-versus-the-androids/', 'snippet': 'Digital: maybe the big stuff is just starting to arrive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We just had a session with Bob Gordon and Joel Mokyr on the outlook for future growth, and I think I have a new way to explain why my gut feeling is that Bob, while making a persuasive case (pdf), is probably wrong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gordon Versus The Androids', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-07T19:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d08d075-f28f-58c0-8464-e649cbb6c976', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d08d075-f28f-58c0-8464-e649cbb6c976'}, {'abstract': 'As cities and states face shortfalls, there is a need for more disclosure, not less, about pension funds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/business/playing-pension-games.html', 'snippet': 'As cities and states face shortfalls, there is a need for more disclosure, not less, about pension funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pity the municipal bondholder. Between Detroit’s bankruptcy and the rising concerns over unfunded pensions in Illinois and elsewhere, it has been a rough year for many muni bond investors. While the Standard & Poor’s municipal bond index has recovered from its September lows, it is still off 2.7 percent for the year. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height