, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/396ecfc2-c3ae-59a5-8394-42de910b4618', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/396ecfc2-c3ae-59a5-8394-42de910b4618'}, {'abstract': 'Ohio State needed a victory in the Big Ten title game to keep pace with Florida State and Auburn. Instead, Michigan State handed the Buckeyes their first loss under Urban Meyer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/sports/ncaafootball/spartans-squash-buckeyes-and-debate-over-bcs-title-game.html', 'snippet': 'Ohio State needed a victory in the Big Ten title game to keep pace with Florida State and Auburn. Instead, Michigan State handed the Buckeyes their first loss under Urban Meyer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — By late Saturday, the debate had ended. There would be no arguments about quality of opposition, or the strength of one conference relative to another. There would be no clamor for Ohio State to appear in the Bowl Championship Series title game.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spartans Squash Buckeyes and Debate Over B.C.S. Title Game', 'kicker': 'Michigan State 34, Ohio State 24', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spartans Squash Buckeyes and Debate Over Title Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Braxton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Urban', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-08T05:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e34b185-324d-5b5c-b440-2d4fb994d99d', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e34b185-324d-5b5c-b440-2d4fb994d99d'}, {'abstract': 'What’s On Sunday, December 8, 2013', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/arts/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'What’s On Sunday, December 8, 2013', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (A&E, History, Lifetime) BONNIE & CLYDE Bruce Beresford puts his spin on the doomed love affair of the 1930s gangsters Bonnie Parker and Clyde Barrow in this two-night mini-series starring Holliday Grainger and Emile Hirsch. William Hurt portrays Frank Hamer, the retired Texas Ranger who led the team that killed Parker and Barrow in 1934. Holly Hunter (above left, with Ms. Grainger) plays Parker’s mother. “Mr. Beresford (‘Tender Mercies,’ ‘Driving Miss Daisy’) gives the sentimental material a corresponding autumnal glow, and there are sweeping, lovely images of Texas fields under big skies, a shimmering crescent moon and an oil refinery sparkling in the night,” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times. Comparing Mr. Beresford’s work to Arthur Penn’s 1967 film with Faye Dunaway and Warren Beatty, Mr. Hale adds: “In the end, ‘Bonnie & Clyde’ has the one thing in common with ‘Bonnie and Clyde’ that you’d expect: the fusillade of machine-gun fire, and Barrow and Parker’s bodies twitching and bursting as they’re torn apart. While it doesn’t have the force of Penn’s brutal choreography, it’s a surprisingly graphic scene for basic cable. Less surprising is a gratuitous, last-minute plot twist that serves to cement the film’s portrayal of Barrow as a tragic, star-crossed hero. Apparently, only the misunderstood die young.” ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-08T06:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b16fc6-99e7-5ef9-876f-d858a5562e34', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b16fc6-99e7-5ef9-876f-d858a5562e34'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections: December 8, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/pageoneplus/corrections-december-8-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections: December 8, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: December 8, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-08T06:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c42d37e-d968-578d-a067-4c325b952176', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c42d37e-d968-578d-a067-4c325b952176'}, {'abstract': 'Paulie Malignaggi rebounded from being knocked down in the second round to record a unanimous decision over Zab Judah in a welterweight bout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/sports/malignaggi-dominates-judah-to-claim-battle-of-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Paulie Malignaggi rebounded from being knocked down in the second round to record a unanimous decision over Zab Judah in a welterweight bout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Paulie Malignaggi believes he has been wronged, he does not quietly stand by. When he has been on the losing side of a controversial decision, he has ranted about everything from incompetent judges and crooked scorecards to the influence of promoters. His tantrums have become well-known. It was the same story Saturday night in Brooklyn. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malignaggi Dominates Judah to Claim Battle of Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Malignaggi Dominates Judah to Claim Battle of Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malignaggi, Paulie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Judah, Zab', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-08T06:53:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Golianopoulos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Golianopoulos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3008040e-4399-572d-ba29-8b1ddb33f394', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3008040e-4399-572d-ba29-8b1ddb33f394'}, {'abstract': 'Exports rose 12.7 percent in November compared with last year, far higher than expectations, and analysts say it could be more evidence the Chinese economy is recovering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/business/international/china-on-track-for-big-trade-surplus-after-exports-surge.html', 'snippet': 'Exports rose 12.7 percent in November compared with last year, far higher than expectations, and analysts say it could be more evidence the Chinese economy is recovering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — China’s exports rose more than expected last month, government figures released Sunday showed, as resurgent demand from consumers in the United States and the European Union helped put the Asian manufacturing juggernaut on track for its biggest annual trade surplus since 2008.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Export Surge Sets Up Big Surplus for China ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Export Surge Sets Up Big Surplus for China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gough, Neil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-08T07:05:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c79ed1eb-13ab-541d-849c-63887ab291e6', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c79ed1eb-13ab-541d-849c-63887ab291e6'}, {'abstract': 'The results signaled the waning power of the dynasty that has dominated Indian politics for nearly all the post-Independence era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/world/asia/india-state-elections.html', 'snippet': 'The results signaled the waning power of the dynasty that has dominated Indian politics for nearly all the post-Independence era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The results of state elections in four states dealt a blow to the Indian National Congress on Sunday, signaling the waning power of the dynasty that had dominated Indian politics for nearly all of the post-independence era and giving momentum to the opposition Bharatiya Janata Party ahead of general elections in May.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/world/INDIA-1/INDIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/world/INDIA-1/INDIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/world/INDIA-1/INDIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/world/INDIA-1/INDIA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/world/INDIA-1/INDIA-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/09/world/INDIA-1/INDIA-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/world/INDIA-1/INDIA-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Party Defeated in Indian State Elections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress Party Defeated In Indian State Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name