nzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9373fd79-d81b-52b7-a5ea-9e76360c2272', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9373fd79-d81b-52b7-a5ea-9e76360c2272'}, {'abstract': 'The production, based on interviews with people affected by the Gulf of Mexico oil rig explosion in 2010, is to have its premiere this spring.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/08/a-new-play-brings-the-deepwater-horizon-disaster-to-the-stage/', 'snippet': 'The production, based on interviews with people affected by the Gulf of Mexico oil rig explosion in 2010, is to have its premiere this spring.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Spill,” a new play based on interviews with dozens of people affected by the Gulf of Mexico oil rig explosion in 2010, will have its premiere production this spring in the state that was at the center of the environmental disaster. The drama, which features some 30 real-life characters speaking in the verbatim style of the documentary-like “Laramie Project” plays, will run March 12 through 30, at the Swine Palace theater on the Louisiana State University campus in Baton Rouge, the theater and the play’s creators announced on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Play Brings the Deepwater Horizon Disaster to the Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tectonic Theater Project', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-08T20:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5682b864-4db0-542d-82cc-4b28b8fef739', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5682b864-4db0-542d-82cc-4b28b8fef739'}, {'abstract': 'The Celtics scored the first 12 points and led by as many as 45 as they handed the Knicks an embarrassing loss in a matinee at the Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/sports/basketball/reverting-to-familiar-rhythm-knicks-take-beating-from-celtics.html', 'snippet': 'The Celtics scored the first 12 points and led by as many as 45 as they handed the Knicks an embarrassing loss in a matinee at the Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid a season already brimming with poor performances, the Knicks seemed strangely determined to set new benchmarks for futility when they arrived at Madison Square Garden on Sunday morning. How many shots could they miss? How many points could they allow? How many more paying customers could they disappoint?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/nyt-knicks/nyt-knicks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/nyt-knicks/nyt-knicks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 624}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/nyt-knicks/nyt-knicks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 985, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/nyt-knicks/nyt-knicks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1970, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,