, {'abstract': 'Jon Kinzel’s “Someone Once Called Me a Sound Man,” which had its premiere at the Chocolate Factory, is mostly gentle in tone except for a sudden hammer blow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/arts/dance/jon-kinzels-new-work-debuted-at-chocolate-factory.html', 'snippet': 'Jon Kinzel’s “Someone Once Called Me a Sound Man,” which had its premiere at the Chocolate Factory, is mostly gentle in tone except for a sudden hammer blow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Near the end of Jon Kinzel’s “Someone Once Called Me a Sound Man,” the choreographer, joined by the dancers Simon Courchel and Stuart Shugg, arranges and rearranges maybe a dozen knee-high panels propped on the ground. Some are a single hue: red, white, black. Some have patterns. The reshuffling of their order is like a demonstration of color theory, each panel affecting perception of the others. It’s all very subtle. And then Mr. Kinzel picks up one panel and suddenly punches a hole in it with a hammer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/KINZEL/KINZEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/KINZEL/KINZEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 231}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/KINZEL/KINZEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/KINZEL/KINZEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image