un at City Center on Thursday and Friday nights with two more showings of “Revelations,” a gorgeous rendition of Ronald K. Brown’s “Grace” and a ponderous addition to the repertory that takes advantage of the Ailey dancers but gives them little in return. In Aszure Barton’s “LIFT,” bare chests, thigh slaps and a pseudo-tribal sensibility elicit one cringe after another. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Haze of Bare Chests, Thigh Slaps and Squalls of Vertical Flight', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Haze of Bare Chests, Thigh Slaps and Squalls of Vertical Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barton, Aszure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macdonald, Curtis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-08T21:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad1248cc-4931-5687-9c77-2e2b9a944999', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad1248cc-4931-5687-9c77-2e2b9a944999'}, {'abstract': 'A tenor saxophone blended and provided counterpoint to Middle Eastern reed instruments at the Asia Society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/arts/music/basel-rajoub-and-saeid-shanbehzadeh-at-asia-society.html', 'snippet': 'A tenor saxophone blended and provided counterpoint to Middle Eastern reed instruments at the Asia Society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday