lm-wins-honors-in-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Paolo Sorrentino’s “The Great Beauty” from Italy claimed three top prizes at the 26th annual European Film Awards on Saturday in Berlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paolo Sorrentino’s “The Great Beauty” from Italy claimed three top prizes at the 26th annual European Film Awards on Saturday in Berlin, where it won for best picture and best director for Mr. Sorrentino, and best actor for Toni Servillo. The film follows Mr. Servillo’s character after his 65th birthday as he takes in the sights and sounds of Rome. Voted on by 2,900 members of the European Film Academy, Joshua Oppenheimer’s “The Act of Killing” won the prize for best documentary, and Veerle Baetens took the best actress award for her role in the Belgian film “The Broken Circle Breakdown.” “Blue Is the Warmest Color,” which won the Palme d’Or at the Cannes International Film Festival in May, was shut out.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Film Wins Honors in Europe', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italian Film Wins Honors in Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorrentino, Paolo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Film Academy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baetens, Veerle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppenheimer, Joshua', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Act of Killing (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Great Beauty (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Broken Circle Breakdown (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-1