abstract': 'The merger of US Airways and American Airlines is set to become final, and the F.C.C. will meet to consider ending the ban on the use of cellphones on flights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/business/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-dec-9.html', 'snippet': 'The merger of US Airways and American Airlines is set to become final, and the F.C.C. will meet to consider ending the ban on the use of cellphones on flights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AIRLINE MERGER After two years of fits and starts, the merger of US Airways and American Airlines is set to become final on Monday, clearing the way for what will be the world’s largest carrier valued at nearly $18 billion. The newly formed airline, which survived a federal lawsuit over the summer, will continue to operate as two carriers under a single management until the task of combining them can be completed. The process is expected to take years, though frequent fliers could start to see changes early next year. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/business/9Ahead/9Ahead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/business/9Ahead/9Ahead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/business/9Ahead/9Ahead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/business/9Ahead/9Ahead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i