spects. He identified the threat to economic stability, social cohesion and democratic legitimacy posed by soaring inequality of income and wealth. He put to rest the myths that inequality is mostly a problem afflicting poor minorities, that expanding the economy and reducing inequality are conflicting goals, and that the government cannot do much about the matter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Obama Left Out of His Inequality Speech: Regulation', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitalism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T00:59:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas O. McGarity', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'McGarity', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e875346d-afd7-55cb-b4e9-a172bcb2757c', 'word_count': 2382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e875346d-afd7-55cb-b4e9-a172bcb2757c'}, {'abstract': 'When a few Taxis of Tomorrow finally hit the streets of New York in October, they came with a much bolder logo, one as large as the wheels of the cabs themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/nyregion/new-bigger-and-bolder-t-