erg’s proposal for a balanced budget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael Bloomberg last month presented his successor, Bill de Blasio, with a housewarming gift: a balanced budget for the fiscal year beginning July 1. What loomed as an imminent crisis for the new administration — an expected $2 billion deficit — had vanished, Mr. Bloomberg declared, thanks to new savings and higher-than-expected revenues. The sudden infusion of black ink doesn’t necessarily make the next mayor’s job easy, he said, “but it reduces the pain.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. de Blasio’s Fiscal Challenge', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. de Blasio’s Fiscal Challenge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T02:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8ed9f54-0679-568b-a38c-72f40f95814f', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8ed9f54-0679-568b-a38c-72f40f95814f'}, {'abstract': 'A lawsuit filed on behalf of a Michigan woman highlights the conflict between religious mandates and a hospital’s duty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/opinion/when-bishops-direct-medical-care.html', 'snippet': 'A lawsuit filed on behalf of a Michigan woman highlights the conflict between religious mandates and a hospital’s duty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beyond new state efforts to restrict women’s access to proper reproductive health care, another, if quieter, threat is posed by mergers between secular hospitals and Catholic hospitals operating under religious directives from the nation’s Roman Catholic bishops. These directives, which oppose abortions, inevitably collide with a hospital’s duty to provide care to pregnant women in medical distress. This tension lies at the heart of a federal lawsuit filed last week by the American Civil Liberties Union. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Bishops Direct Medical Care', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Bishops Direct Medical Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Conference of Catholic Bishops', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T02:50:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff3e2b89-d12c-540a-9d3d-8bf8c6b3499a', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff3e2b89-d12c-540a-9d3d-8bf8c6b3499a'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed legislation aims to treat prostitutes as exploited and abused victims rather than as criminals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/opinion/frances-new-approach-to-curbing-prostitution.html', 'snippet': 'Proposed legislation aims to treat prostitutes as exploited and abused victims rather than as criminals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lower house of the French Parliament overwhelmingly passed a bill last Wednesday that would impose stiff fines on anyone paying for sex, while offering assistance to prostitutes to leave the sex industry. The law, which is expected to be passed by the Senate by summer, has been bitterly debated. But it would bring France more in line with a growing consensus among European and American governments that it makes better sense to treat prostitutes as exploited and abused victims rather than as criminals. That has become increasingly true in Europe with the increase in the trafficking of foreign women, including underage girls, to work in richer countries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France’s New Approach to Curbing Prostitution', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France’s New Approach to Curbing Prostitution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T02:52:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/178d7f88-2925-53a7-91f6-e584850b53f9', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/178d7f88-2925-53a7-91f6-e584850b53f9'}, {'abstract': 'In the Kliptown section of Soweto, $180-a-night hotel rooms sit 30 yards from tin shacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/world/africa/soweto-mandela.html', 'snippet': 'In the Kliptown section of Soweto, $180-a-night hotel rooms sit 30 yards from tin shacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOWETO, South Africa — A cool pitcher of ginger-infused water greets guests at the Soweto Hotel and Conference Center in the Kliptown section of this township, which grew over decades of racial oppression to segregate black workers from the rest of Johannesburg.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Rows of Tin Shacks, a Luxury Hotel Rises', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Rows of Tin Shacks, A Luxury Hotel Rises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soweto Hotel and Conference Center (Soweto, South Africa)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyman, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Soweto (South Africa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Makeba, Miriam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisulu, Albertina', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T02:59:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Lyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ca8abd2-8591-55