jured last season was heralded by a two-minute video produced by the Lakers and nonstop discussions on Los Angeles sports radio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The messianic trailer previewing one of the most anticipated events of the year in Hollywoodland ended with the words “The Legend Continues December 8.” Before Ron Burgundy’s return to the big screen in “Anchorman 2,” the larger-than-celluloid star of the Lakers, Kobe Bryant, reappeared on the N.B.A. stage for his first game since sustaining a torn Achilles’ tendon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/sub-kobe/sub-kobe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/sub-kobe/sub-kobe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 672}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/sub-kobe/sub-kobe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 915, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/sub-kobe/sub-kobe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1829, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/sub-kobe/sub-kobe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/sub-kobe/sub-kobe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/sports/sub-kobe/sub-kobe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'heig