 is Albert, Victoria’s first cousin and the eventual love of her life. “Despite the filmmakers’ efforts to persuade us that ‘The Young Victoria’ is a serious work, and despite some tense moments and gunfire, the movie’s pleasures are as light as its story,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about this “frivolously entertaining film,” directed by Jean-Marc Vallée and written by Julian Fellowes. “No matter. Albert may never rip Victoria’s bodice, but he does eventually loosen it, to her delight and ours.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T05:17:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/4634d25b-4a82-544e-bb6e-dd212cbfbdfc', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4634d25b-4a82-544e-bb6e-dd212cbfbdfc'}, {'abstract': 'Sports can be structured upon strategy, grace and athleticism. At other times, the plan seems to be “leap, clutch, grab, and just hang on tight.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/12/09/sports/WeekInPictures.html', 'snippet': 'Sports can be structured upon strategy, grace and athleticism. At other times, the plan seems to be “leap, clutch, grab, and just hang on tight.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sports can be structured upon strategy, grace and athleticism. At other times, the plan seems to be “leap, clutch, grab, and just hang on tight.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge',