/lessons-from-the-exxon-valdez-oil-spill.html', 'snippet': 'A Retro Report looks at the poor planning and technological challenges that contributed to the nation’s worst oil disasters, the 1989 Exxon spill and the 2010 BP blowout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a cold March night in 1989, the tanker Exxon Valdez ran aground off the coast of Alaska, spilling 11 million gallons of crude oil into the waters of Prince William Sound and creating one of the worst oil spills in American history. This week’s Retro Report examines how that spill happened and follows its impact over the past twenty-five years. Watch the video above for the complete story. Below, a Times reporter who covered the BP oil disaster of 2010 writes about how containment and cleanup evolved. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons From the Exxon Valdez Oil Spill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Spills', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exxon Valdez (Tanker)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T11:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef9fb373-e2ca-52a4-9716-ad5f6304b235', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef9fb373-e2ca-52a4-9716-ad5f6304b235'}, {'abstract': 'The author of this week’s cover story explains how complicated it can be to write about someone who’s a friend.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/behind-the-cover-story-kevin-sack-on-his-friendship-with-a-lost-boy/', 'snippet': 'The author of this week’s cover story explains how complicated it can be to write about someone who’s a friend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin Sack, who wrote this week’s cover story about the American life of Jacob Mach, one of the Lost Boys of Sudan, is a senior reporter at The Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/6-sack-headshot/6-sack-headshot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 437, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/6-sack-headshot/6-sack-headshot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 437, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/6-sack-headshot/6-sack-headshot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/6-sack-headshot/6-sack-headshot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/06/magazine/6-sack-headshot/6-sack-headshot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Kevin Sack on His Friendship with a Lost Boy', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sack, Kevin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':