o-make-banking-comeback-in-africa/', 'snippet': 'The former chief executive of Barclays is raising money for a $250 million vehicle that would invest in the banking business in Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Robert E. Diamond Jr., who was ousted as chief executive of Barclays nearly 18 months ago amid a rate-fixing scandal, is planning a banking comeback.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/dbpix-bob-diamond-2/dbpix-bob-diamond-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/business/dbpix-bob-diamond-2/dbpix-bob-diamond-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/dbpix-bob-diamond-2/dbpix-bob-diamond-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/dbpix-bob-diamond-2/dbpix-bob-diamond-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/dbpix-bob-diamond-2/dbpix-bob-diamond-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/business/dbpix-bob-diamond-2/dbpix-bob-diamond-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/dbpix-bob-diamond-2/dbpix-bob-diamond-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Diamond Aims to Make Banking Comeback – in Africa', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Returning To Banking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diamond, Robert E Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London Stock Exchange', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T13:44:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16746d95-1434-532b-9b91-737ea7094519', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16746d95-1434-532b-9b91-737ea7094519'}, {'abstract': 'Another Lenin effigy is dismantled, in Kiev, but can Ukraine do better than Russia at shedding the Soviet legacy?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/statue-symbols/', 'snippet': 'Another Lenin effigy is dismantled, in Kiev, but can Ukraine do better than Russia at shedding the Soviet legacy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The envious Ukraine-watch of many Russians culminated Sunday when a statue of Lenin was toppled in Kiev. It evoked the memory of one of the most richly symbolic, joyous and ultimately disappointing moments in Russia’s own history, when, after a hard-line coup failed in August 1991, a monument to Felix Dzerzhinsky, the founder of the secret police, in front of the K.G.B. headquarters in Moscow was topple