ganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad7e873-19e8-51c4-921c-e4708a384356', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad7e873-19e8-51c4-921c-e4708a384356'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge in Washington State issued a stinging rebuke of the public-defense systems of two towns near Seattle.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/the-right-to-an-attorney-who-actually-does-his-job/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge in Washington State issued a stinging rebuke of the public-defense systems of two towns near Seattle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 4, a federal judge in Washington State issued a stinging rebuke of the public-defense systems of two towns near Seattle, finding them so inadequate that they violate the Sixth Amendment right to the assistance of counsel in criminal prosecutions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right to an Attorney Who Actually Does His Job', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Defenders and Court-Appointed Lawyers (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sixth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T16:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cdab7cb-4414-54e8-b743-93bb5fa724ec', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cdab7cb-4414-54e8-b743-93bb5fa724ec'}, {'abstract': 'Many families are looking for ways to stretch out the pleasures of Christmas morning without stretching their budget (or their storage space).', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/will-there-be-too-much-stuff-under-your-tree/', 'snippet': 'Many families are looking for ways to stretch out the pleasures of Christmas morning without stretching their budget (or their storage space).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, I sent myself an iCal reminder on Dec. 1 that read “too much stuff last year.” The year before’s Christmas morning had lasted well into the afternoon, and a few days later, new toys that would have been greeted with delight on any other day sat untouched by the recipients. It was a festival of materialism that no one over the age of 10 in my family had any desire to repeat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/style/motherlode-presents/motherlode-presents-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/style/motherlode-presents/motherlode-presents-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 772}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/style/motherlode-presents/motherlode-presents-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/style/motherlode-presents/motherlode-presents-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 623, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/style/motherlode-presents/motherlode-presents-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/09/style/motherlode-presents/motherlode-presents-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/style/motherlode-presents/motherlode-presents-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will There Be ‘Too Much Stuff’ Under Your Tree?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Orderliness and Clutter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winerip, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T16:10:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b60f9b3b-fe87-58ed-91ee-74c20ce84441', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b60f9b3b-fe87-58ed-91ee-74c20ce84441'}, {'abstract': 'A stenciled Banksy work from 2008 that was removed from a Los Angeles gas station brought less than its estimate at auction.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/gas-station-banksy-brings-209000-at-auction/', 'snippet': 'A stenciled Banksy work from 2008 that was removed from a Los Angeles gas station brought less than its estimate at auction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As auctions of Banksy works go, the sale of “Flower Girl” at Julien’s Auctions on Thursday had none of the cloak-and-dagger elements of earlier sales. And perhaps that lack of intrigue accounts for the work’s relatively low sale price of $209,000, nearly a third less than the auction house’s highest estimate, and a fraction of the  $1.1 million fetched by another Banksy work, “Slave Labor,” at a London auction in June. Or maybe Banksymania is on the wane.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/09artsbeat-banksy/09artsbeat-banksy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/09artsbeat-banksy/09artsbeat-banksy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/09artsbeat-banksy/09artsbeat-banksy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/09artsbeat-banksy/09artsbeat-banksy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1331, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/09artsbeat-banksy/09artsbeat-banksy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/09artsbeat-banksy/09artsbeat-banksy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/arts/09artsbeat-banksy/09artsbeat-banksy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gas-Station Banksy Brings $209,000 at Auction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gas-Station Banksy Brings $209,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banksy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Julien's Auctions", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T16:26:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98e4000c-cc75-5d5a-b379-acd66c14befc', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98e4000c-cc75-5d5a-b379-acd66c14befc'}, {'abstract': 'This time she’s not named Kim.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/pixies-name-a-bassist-for-upcoming-tour/', 'snippet': 'This time she’s not named Kim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This time she’s not named Kim.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pixies Name a Bassist for Coming Tour', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pixies (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T16:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47884220-a315-50e3-adc1-bc3c0353348e', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47884220-a315-50e3-adc1-bc3c0353348e'}, {'abstract': 'With the war going well, the president struggled to find the right way to bring the Confederate states back into the Union.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/lincolns-10-percent-plan/', 'snippet': 'With the war going well, the president struggled to find the right way to bring the Confederate states back into the Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By early November 1863, Abraham Lincoln found himself frustrated with the glacial pace of wartime reconstruction efforts, particularly in Louisiana. In an August letter to Maj. Gen. Nathaniel Banks, the president had outlined “what I would like Louisiana to do.” His wish list included a new constitution, statewide adoption of emancipation, a system to help ease the transition from slavery to freedom for blacks and whites and education for young freedmen and women. He went on to assure his abolitionist general that “I shall not … retract the emancipation proclamation; nor … ever return to slavery any person who is free by the terms of that proclamation, or by any of the acts of Congress.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln’s 10 Percent Plan', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reconstruction Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T16:40:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Beard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5202090-faec-51e9-9f1b-1c5977b9e1c3', 'word_count': 1973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5202090-faec-51e9-9f1b-1c5977b9e1c3'}, {'abstract': 'The development of Bitcoin, the virtual currency that is not issued by any government, presents challenges for the authorities to use laws that were not designed for the digital world to combat illegal conduct, Peter J. Henning writes in the White Collar Watch column.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/for-bitcoin-square-peg-meets-round-hole-under-the-law/', 'snippet': 'The development of Bitcoin, the virtual currency that is not issued by any government, presents challenges for the authorities to use laws that were not designed for the digital world to combat illegal conduct, Peter J. Henning writes in the White...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The advent of a new medium to conduct business inevitably means avenues for criminals to swoop in to take advantage. The development of Bitcoin, the virtual currency that is not issued by any government, presents challenges for the authorities to use laws that were not designed for the digital world to combat illegal conduct.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/business/dealbook/dbpix-bitcoin/dbpix-bitcoin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/business/dealbook/dbpix-bitcoin/dbpix-bitcoin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/business/dealbook/dbpix-bitcoin/dbpix-bitcoin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr