ps://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000002592839/times-minute-tighter-pollution-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Also on the Minute, spies snoop on video games and Mayor Bloomberg fights to ban foam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Also on the Minute, spies snoop on video games and Mayor Bloomberg fights to ban foam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/multimedia/video-nytm-120913-noon/video-nytm-120913-noon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/09/multimedia/video-nytm-120913-noon/video-nytm-120913-noon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/multimedia/video-nytm-120913-noon/video-nytm-120913-noon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/09/multimedia/video-nytm-120913-noon/video-nytm-120913-noon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/09/multimedia/video-nytm-120913-noon/video-nytm-120913-noon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Minute | Tighter Pollution Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T16:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Alyssa Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alyssa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4bdfdaf8-8f28-5311-8539-a40c431bba7e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4bdfdaf8-8f28-5311-8539-a40c431bba7e'}, {'abstract': 'After the rapid ascent of his deeply personal debut album, released last week, the singer-songwriter Mutual Benefit goes slo-mo for his latest video.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/listen-up-a-baroque-folk-troubadour-takes-flight/', 'snippet': 'After the rapid ascent of his deeply personal debut album, released last week, the singer-songwriter Mutual Benefit goes slo-mo for his latest video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weighty confessionals captured on “Love’s Crushing Diamond” — the recent breakout album from the singer-songwriter Jordan Lee’s ironically corporate-sounding nom de musique, Mutual Benefit — weren’t originally meant for mass appeal. The 25-year-old had initially intended to distribute the deeply personal album as a limited release on his D.I.Y., cassette-only label, Kassette Klub. The tracks document the strain that a rootless lifestyle took on his relationships when, for the better part of 2012, he rambled across the country from Austin, Tex., to Brooklyn. “I don’t want to sound corny, but it was a kind of soul-searching journey,” Lee says. “The big lesson I learned is you’re not supposed to feel good all the time — that it’s easier to just be O.K. with things you can’t control.” As a result, the album carries a haunting power that couldn’t help but find a larger audience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | A Baroque-Folk Troubadour Takes Flight', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': No