7b3-3399-53fd-afe5-14f6af4447df'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Young will perform at four benefit concerts to raise money for the Athabasca Chipewyan First Nation, a group based in Alberta that is fighting tar sands', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/neil-young-to-play-benefit-shows-for-native-american-group/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Young will perform at four benefit concerts to raise money for the Athabasca Chipewyan First Nation, a group based in Alberta that is fighting tar sands', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neil Young will play four benefit concerts in Canadian cities to raise money for the legal defense fund of the Athabasca Chipewyan First Nation, a Native American group based in Alberta that is suing Shell Canada to prevent it from undertaking oil sands extraction projects that the group says will encroach on lands and resources protected by an 1899 treaty. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neil Young to Play Benefit Shows for Native American Group', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Neil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shell Canada Limited', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T18:44:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbdd339a-8357-52ea-b4db-ad96beb270a4', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbdd339a-8357-52ea-b4db-ad96beb270a4'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard to say what’s more astonishing about “Nutcracker Rouge,” an irreverent restaging of the holiday classic — its virtuosity or its bawdiness.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/after-hours-an-nc-17-retelling-of-the-nutcracker/', 'snippet': 'It’s hard to say what’s more astonishing about “Nutcracker Rouge,” an irreverent restaging of the holiday classic — its virtuosity or its bawdiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jewel-box-small, down-at-the-heels Minetta Lane Theater is the perfect setting for this opulently burlesque and deliciously Freudian retelling of “The Nutcracker,” which has shades of Cirque du Soleil, “Sleep No More” and “Fanny and Alexander” (with a dash of “Satyricon”). It’s the work of the Brooklyn-based, largely Juilliard-trained dance-and-acrobatics ensemble Company XIV. On a proscenium framed by heavy red curtains, with candelabra where the footlights would usually be, Tchaikovsky’s darling little Clara (a radiant Laura Careless) is a mini-Marie Antoinette with a comeuppance in store, to be delivered by Drosselmeyer, her godfather, played like a smarmy satyr pimp by Jeff Takacs. The genius of this production, which includes eye-dazzling physical feats performed on giant hula hoops and from silken swings, is its transformation of traditional ballet into louche vaudeville: the famous Spanish dance becomes a foot-stomping, castanet-clicking striptease; in the storied Kingdom of the Sweets, Clara wields a fat black whip to play gleeful dominatrix over a troupe of bare-bottomed, harnessed Licorice Boys.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | An NC-17 Retelling of ‘The Nutcracker’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minetta Lane Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2517658a-4689-5175-ae5b-56df4de6812f', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2517658a-4689-5175-ae5b-56df4de6812f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers are invited to participate in a Q&A with Op-Ed columnist Nicholas Kristof.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/ask-nick-kristof/', 'snippet': 'Readers are invited to participate in a Q&A with Op-Ed columnist Nicholas Kristof.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UPDATE: Read Part 1 of Nick’s answers to your questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask Nick Kristof', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T19:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a19f62df-00b2-5d91-ab64-3cd60fab4122', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a19f62df-00b2-5d91-ab64-3cd60fab4122'}, {'abstract': 'The former mayor, Bob Filner, also received three years of probation for harassing women while in office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/us/home-confinement-for-Bob-Filner-former-san-diego-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'The former mayor, Bob Filner, also received three years of probation for harassing women while in office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Bob Filner, the former mayor of San Diego, was senten