spired by forms from the physical world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The futuristic curves of Zaha Hadid were few and far between at this year’s just-completed edition of Design Miami. Instead, the fair offered numerous treatments of flora and fauna, many of which imbued these natural phenomena with a loving sense of preciousness. A few examples: a bird encased in a glass purse by the Dutch jewelry designer Ted Noten at Ornamentum; a tree by the Parisian furniture designer Maria Pergay at Demisch Danant; and a sculpture of a carnivorous plant dotted with dragonflies by Taher Chemirick at Galerie BSL.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three’s a Trend | Precious Nature at Design Miami', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadid, Zaha', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noten, Ted', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pergay, Maria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T20:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Delavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a204cc2-30e7-5dc6-9ae3-7ae11d3c3739', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a204cc2-30e7-5dc6-9ae3-7ae11d3c3739'}, {'abstract': 'The American Film Institute released its list of the year’s 10 best, and it often is considered a predictor of what will make the cut for the Academy.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/afis-top-10-could-be-a-clue-to-oscar-nominees/', 'snippet': 'The American Film Institute released its list of the year’s 10 best, and it often is considered a predictor of what will make the cut for the Academy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Film Institute, dedicated to preservation and a fairly reliable predictor of the Academy’s tastes, announced its 10 best films and TV series of the year on Monday. On the big screen, its picks were: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The American Film Institute’s Top 10 Could Be a Clue to Oscar Nominees', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FILM INSTITUTE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T20:17:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f78893cf-8ecd-53cb-ab35-1079d9f78a7d', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f78893cf-8ecd-53cb-ab35-1079d9f78a7d'}, {'abstract': 'His reservoir of elaborate contraptions that mutated simple tasks into madcap feats of ingenuity made Rube Goldberg rich and famous. But he was also an all-around cartoon man and artist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/100000002588110/rube-goldberg-man-behind-the-machines.html', 'snippet': 'His reservoir of elaborate contraptions that mutated simple tasks into madcap feats of ingenuity made Rube Goldberg rich and famous. But he was also an all-around cartoon man and artist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'His reservoir of elaborate contraptions that mutated simple tasks into madcap feats of ingenuity made Rube Goldberg rich and famous. But he was also an all-around cartoon man and artist.', 'source': 'The New Yor