er-on-arabs-got-talent/', 'snippet': 'Jennifer Grout, an American singer who has surprised many with her renditions of Arab songs, was a finalist on the television show “Arabs Got Talent.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'An American singer, Jennifer Grout, made it to the top three in the finals of the hit television show “Arabs Got Talent” in Beirut, Lebanon, on Saturday but ultimately fell short of the top honor. Ms. Grout, 23, had become a sensation across the Arab world after her surprisingly adept performances of classical Arab music, a genre that is largely fading among younger generations in the Middle East. She speaks little Arabic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Singer Is a Finalist, but Not a Winner on ‘Arabs Got Talent’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grout, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beirut (Lebanon)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T20:52:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d643af9d-f49c-5233-ab4f-22aa820fa3d5', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d643af9d-f49c-5233-ab4f-22aa820fa3d5'}, {'abstract': 'After an eight-week hiatus, construction materials will be allowed in again starting Tuesday, but only for United Nations projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/world/middleeast/israel-building-materials-gaza.html', 'snippet': 'After an eight-week hiatus, construction materials will be allowed in again starting Tuesday, but only fo