w performances.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/strong-week-for-broadways-carole-king-show-still-in-previews/', 'snippet': '“Beautiful,” the new Broadway musical about Ms. King’s early years, has seen strong sales in the show’s first weeks of preview performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carole King songlist in “Beautiful,” the new Broadway musical about Ms. King’s early years as a singer, has been drawing strong numbers of fans and others in the show’s first weeks of preview performances. The production had its best ticket sales yet last week, grossing $814,141 for eight performances, or 80 percent of the maximum possible amount, according to box-office data released on Monday by the Broadway League. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strong Week for Broadway’s Carole King Show, Still in Previews', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T21:52:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By PATRICK HEALY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HEALY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28adcf3a-0c4b-57ec-8fca-455d16a164ea', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28adcf3a-0c4b-57ec-8fca-455d16a164ea'}, {'abstract': 'The Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center offered a lithe performance of Gallo’s Trio Sonata as part of its annual Baroque Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/arts/music/chamber-music-societys-baroque-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center offered a lithe performance of Gallo’s Trio Sonata as part of its annual Baroque Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consumers will buy generic or obscure brands if the cost is lower or the quality rivals that of an established product. But the 18th-century Scottish music publisher Robert Bremner wasn’t willing to take a chance with the little-known composer Domenico Gallo, publishing his 12 Trio Sonatas as those of Giovanni Pergolesi, a name-brand composer. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Composers Redeemed From Oblivion', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Composers Redeemed From Oblivion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T21:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/67d1ecbf-2a1d-5d67-ab2e-d6eed72a0368', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67d1ecbf-2a1d-5d67-ab2e-d6eed72a0368'}, {'abstract': 'Martin Frost, on clarinet, soared from Stravinsky to klezmerlike strains with the Orpheus Chamber Orchestra at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/arts/music/martin-frost-clarinetist-and-the-orpheus-chamber-orchestra.html', 'snippet': 'Martin Frost, on clarinet, soared from Stravinsky to klezmerlike strains with the Orpheus Chamber Orchestra at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Orpheus Chamber Orchestra’s concert at Carnegie Hall on Saturday evening was mainly mellow and mellifluous, with lovely works by Handel and Mozart, and even subdued for a time, with Irving Fine’s “Serious Song.” But halfway through, it ran delightfully amok, when Martin Frost — the soloist for the evening, in a superb performance of Mozart’s sublime Clarinet Concerto — broke loose in an encore.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/orpheus/orpheus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/orpheus/orpheus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/orpheus/orpheus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/orpheus/orpheus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/orpheus/orpheus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/orpheus/orpheus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/orpheus/orpheus-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Magic Wand, Fluidly Sliding Through Genres', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Magic Wand, Fluidly Sliding Through Genres', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orpheus Chamber Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frost, Martin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-09T21:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe936335-f22b-58f7-b5be-0496cedea9ae', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe936335-f22b-58f7-b5be-0496cedea9ae'}, {'abstract': 'Tornado scientists clarify what is and isn’t known about how tornadoes may be influenced by global warming.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/09/a-closer-look-at-tornadoes-and-global-warming/', 'snippet': 'Tornado scientists clarify what is and isn’t known about how tornadoes may be influenced by global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m slow blogging these days, given the constraints that come with balancing teaching, journalism, family life and (these days) my music. I apologize for the delay here:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Closer Look at Tornadoes in a Human-Heated Climate', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diffenbaugh, Noah S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'n