cle/be493040-7af1-54b6-bd39-66e6fb0a758b'}, {'abstract': 'After the death of its most beloved leader, the African National Congress could face its most competitive elections since it came to power in 1994.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/world/africa/after-mandela-a-test-at-the-polls-for-his-party.html', 'snippet': 'After the death of its most beloved leader, the African National Congress could face its most competitive elections since it came to power in 1994.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DIEPSLOOT, South Africa — Isaac Makhura gestured toward the squalid sprawl of shacks outside his house in this informal settlement, where some of the country’s most desperate people live. Was it any wonder, he said, that he no longer had any qualms about voting against the African National Congress, the party of his entire family for three generations?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Mandela, a Test at the Polls for His Party', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Mandela, a Test at the Polls for His Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polgreen, Lydia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN NATIONAL CONGRESS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T01:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9518785a-0fad-57af-8c47-cec558b06d91', 'word_count': 1420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9518785a-0fad-57af-8c47-cec558b06d91'}, {'abstract': 'People post on Twitter or write stories for online news organizations like The Huffington Post or Gawker that spread quickly on the web as if factual, when they really aren’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/business/media/if-a-story-is-viral-truth-may-be-taking-a-beating.html', 'snippet': 'People post on Twitter or write stories for online news organizations like The Huffington Post or Gawker that spread quickly on the web as if factual, when they really aren’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Truth has never been an essential ingredient of viral content on the Internet. But in the stepped-up competition for readers, digital news sites are increasingly blurring the line between fact and fiction, and saying that it is all part of doing business in the rough-and-tumble world of online journalism. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/SUB-VIRIAL/SUB-VIRIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/business/SUB-VIRIAL/SUB-VIRIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 751}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/SUB-VIRIAL/SUB-VIRIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/SUB-VIRIAL/SUB-VIRIAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1744, 'width': 1394, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/SUB-VIRIAL/SUB-VIRIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/business/SUB-VIRIAL/SUB-VIRIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/business/SUB-VIRIAL/SUB-VIRIAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If a Story Is Viral, Truth May Be Taking a Beating', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If a Story Is Viral, Truth May Be Taking a Beating', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaufman, Leslie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mashable Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BuzzFeed Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gawker.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoaxes and Pranks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T01:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya and Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0230801a-3044-5eb9-9759-168565d6ab29', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0230801a-3044-5eb9-9759-168565d6ab29'}, {'abstract': 'Pete Festersen, a Democratic candidate for Congress in Nebraska, ended his campaign on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/us/nebraska-candidate-quits-congressional-race.html', 'snippet': 'Pete Festersen, a Democratic candidate for Congress in Nebraska, ended his campaign on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pete Festersen, a Democratic candidate for Congress in Nebraska, ended his campaign\xa0on Monday, two months after saying he would run because of voter anger over the Republican-led shutdown of the federal government. He told The Omaha World-Herald that he was leaving the race because it was not the right timing for him and his family. Mr. Festersen was running against Lee Terry, a Republican who has held his seat since 1999. Republicans said that Mr. Festersen’s decision signaled that Democrats were worried about losing support in the 2014 election because of problems with the rollout of the health care law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nebraska: Candidate Quits Congressional Race', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Plains', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nebraska: Candidate Quits Congressional Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzsimmons, Emma G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Festersen, Pete', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T01:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news