aragraph': 'They have been glaring in their absence, two standout players who have sat and watched, and grimaced, as their respective teams, the Nets and the Knicks, have combined to outdo each other in displays of bad basketball.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Williams Is Set to Return, and Chandler Is Preparing To', 'kicker': 'N.B.A. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Williams Is Set to Return, and Chandler Is Preparing To', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Deron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandler, Tyson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T01:34:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh and Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85bda4f7-c3d5-5180-9ae5-f499338ac6a1', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85bda4f7-c3d5-5180-9ae5-f499338ac6a1'}, {'abstract': 'Police officers in 14 of the country’s 23 provinces have staged work stoppages in recent days, local news media said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/world/americas/argentina-looting-spreads-as-police-officers-stage-strikes.html', 'snippet': 'Police officers in 14 of the country’s 23 provinces have staged work stoppages in recent days, local news media said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Strikes by police officers demanding higher salaries opened the way for looting in cities across Argentina over the weekend. Police officers in 14 of the country’s 23 provinces have staged work stoppages in recent days, local news media said. Some of the strikes have been settled with agreements for pay increases, but officers of at least nine police departments were still protesting on Monday afternoon. One person died during looting in the city of Concordia, on the border with Uruguay, on Sunday night, raising the death toll linked to the chaos to three. Thousands of federal troops have been deployed to the provinces, according to the Security Ministry and Argentina’s national news agency. Government officials accused opposition politicians of fomenting the new wave of looting, but some analysts criticized the focus of the government’s efforts to reduce poverty. “There is still a nucleus that remains impoverished, that sees nothing positive on the horizon,” said Carlos F. De Angelis, a sociologist at the University of Buenos Aires.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: Looting Spreads as Police Officers Stage Strikes', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina: Looting Spreads As Police Officers Stage Strikes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Looting (Crime)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T01:35:16+0000', 'docu