: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/opinion/35-and-single.html', 'snippet': 'An Argentine woman shares her intimate search for love and answers: must she settle down or remain a free spirit in order to be happy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past 10 years, I’ve been compulsively filming everyone and everything for no particular reason. All my love stories and breakups have been recorded and systematically kept.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘35 and Single’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T02:11:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Schargorodsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schargorodsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c791625-eee8-5e75-a7f2-e3201a2f7b73', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c791625-eee8-5e75-a7f2-e3201a2f7b73'}, {'abstract': 'After meeting with the Rev. Al Sharpton and other civil rights advocates, New York City retailers released a policy document in a response to accusations of racial profiling of black shoppers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/nyregion/macys-and-barneys-among-stores-to-post-shoppers-bill-of-rights.html', 'snippet': 'After meeting with the Rev. Al Sharpton and other civil rights advocates, New York City retailers released a policy document in a response to accusations of racial profiling of black shoppers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shoppers will find an unusual addition to the traditional decorations at Macy’s, Barneys New York and other major stores this holiday season: a “Customers’ Bill of Rights” that addresses racial profiling. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Macy’s and Barneys Among Stores to Post Shoppers’ ‘Bill of Rights’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Stores to Post Shoppers’ ‘Bill of Rights,’ Addressing Racial Profiling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barneys New York', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Bloomingdale's", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lord & Taylor', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saks Fifth Avenue', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elefterakis, John', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T02:17:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aeafd31-22e6-5c82-a14f-0f5800262f96', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aeafd31-22e6-5c82-a14f-0f5800262f96'}, {'abstract': 'What modes of thought will be most valuable in a future economy defined by machine intelligence?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/opinion/brooks-thinking-for-the-future.html', 'snippet': 'What modes of thought will be most valuable in a future economy defined by machine intelligence?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re living in an era of mechanized intelligence, an age in which you’re probably going to find yourself in a workplace with diagnostic systems, different algorithms and computer-driven data analysis. If you want to thrive in this era, you probably want to be good at working with intelligent machines. As Tyler Cowen puts it in his relentlessly provocative recent book, “Average Is Over,” “If you and your skills are a complement to the computer, your wage and labor market prospects are likely to be cheery. If your skills do not complement the computer, you may want to address that mismatch.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'sup