ulton, Cedric', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baroni, Bill', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wisniewski, John S', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T03:53:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43f53213-1352-53ea-96a5-a0c65a08c4ba', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43f53213-1352-53ea-96a5-a0c65a08c4ba'}, {'abstract': 'Sandy Alderson’s No. 1 need seems to be finding a veteran pitcher for the team’s rotation who is not very expensive, but said he would be hesitant to give a free agent a multiyear deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/sports/baseball/alderson-considers-best-way-to-flesh-out-mets-rotation.html', 'snippet': 'Sandy Alderson’s No. 1 need seems to be finding a veteran pitcher for the team’s rotation who is not very expensive, but said he would be hesitant to give a free agent a multiyear deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKE BUENA VISTA, Fla. — As baseball’s annual winter meetings kicked into gear Monday, the Mets were busy working on complementary deals that would fill out their roster. Sandy Alderson, the no-longer-impoverished general manager, had three or four more needs to address, some trade chips available and roughly $10 million to $12 million to spend. He said that he had been so busy that he missed Sunday night’s episode of “Homeland.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit