a-is-tied-to-spying-on-european-diplomats.html', 'snippet': 'The foreign ministries of five countries were reportedly breached by Chinese hackers using emails as bait.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Computer breaches at the foreign ministries of the Czech Republic, Portugal, Bulgaria, Latvia and Hungary have been traced to Chinese hackers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Is Tied to Spying on European Diplomats', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Is Tied to Spying On European Diplomats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FireEye Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bulgaria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latvia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T05:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/872b7158-2b77-5e0d-973f-340eab198dec', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/872b7158-2b77-5e0d-973f-340eab198dec'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (CBS) THE VICTORIA’S SECRET FASHION SHOW Earthly beauties like Adriana Lima, Alessandra Ambrosio, Lily Aldridge, Lindsay Ellingson, Karlie Kloss, Doutzen Kroes and Behati Prinsloo don angel wings and skimpies — including a gem-encrusted piece said to be worth $10 million, designed by Mouawad and worn by Candice Swanepoel — to strut the runway at the 69th Regiment Armory in Manhattan in this extravaganza, taped (twice, to get every angle just right) on Nov. 13. Taylor Swift, above in foreground; Fall Out Boy; a Great Big World; and Neon Jungle serenade the models in segments titled “British Invasion,” “Birds of Paradise,” “Parisian Nights,” “Shipwrecked,” “Snow Angels” and “Pink Network.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c02be23-2125-5a97-a271-bae6ae48c9c9', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c02be23-2125-5a97-a271-bae6ae48c9c9'}, {'abstract': 'Nelson Mandela’s rain-swept memorial service drew tens of thousands of South Africans and a large crowd of global V.I.P.’s, including President Obama and more than 90 other heads of state and government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/world/africa/nelson-mandela-south-africa-farewell.html', 'snippet': 'Nelson Mandela’s rain-swept memorial service drew tens of thousands of South Africans and a large crowd of global V.I.P.’s, including President Obama and more than 90 other heads of state and government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOWETO, South Africa — For a day, the world came to Nelson Mandela’s adopted hometown. There were celebrities: Bono, Naomi Campbell, Charlize Theron. There were kings-in-waiting: Crown Prince Haakon of Norway and Crown Prince Felipe of Spain. There were more presidents and prime ministers than at just about any other setting outside a United Nations General Assembly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/SAFRICA-1/SAFRICA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/world/SAFRICA-1/SAFRICA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/SAFRICA-1/SAFRICA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/SAFRICA-1/SAFRICA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/SAFRICA-1/SAFRICA-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/world/SAFRICA-1/SAFRICA-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/SAFRICA-1/SAFRICA-1-thumbLa