3-5672-af0b-e06cb8d4aaa8'}, {'abstract': 'Watch your back! If it’s not a Yorkiepoo, don’t even try to lift it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/booming/even-superwoman-can-have-back-problems.html', 'snippet': 'Watch your back! If it’s not a Yorkiepoo, don’t even try to lift it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are two kinds of people, my sister says. People with back problems, and people who don’t have back problems yet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/booming/10mystory-booming-back/10mystory-booming-back-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 922, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/booming/10mystory-booming-back/10mystory-booming-back-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 922}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/booming/10mystory-booming-back/10mystory-booming-back-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/booming/10mystory-booming-back/10mystory-booming-back-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1654, 'width': 1076, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/booming/10mystory-booming-back/10mystory-booming-back-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/booming/10mystory-booming-back/10mystory-booming-back-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/booming/10mystory-booming-back/10mystory-booming-back-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Superwoman Can Have Back Problems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Back (Human Body Part)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T12:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roz Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccef0587-d913-5f9a-81c3-8fc5badae391', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccef0587-d913-5f9a-81c3-8fc5badae391'}, {'abstract': 'If you get into Stanford’s business school, go. If you get into Harvard’s business school, go. Otherwise, make sure your program gives you real-world experience.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/assessing-whether-entrepreneurs-should-get-m-b-a-s/', 'snippet': 'If you get into Stanford’s business school, go. If you get into Harvard’s business school, go. Otherwise, make sure your program gives you real-world experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you noticed how many universities are rushing to create entrepreneurship programs as part of their M.B.A. offerings? As The Wall Street Journal recently noted, the answer is quite a few. One might say better late than never — or even think that the traditional M.B.A. program is finally gaining some relevance and teaching people how to build a business. Think again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assessing Whether Entrepreneurs Should Get M.B.A.’s', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T12:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cliff Oxford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cliff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oxford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc5c1104-8950-5d0e-b218-feaae651abe1', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5c1104-8950-5d0e-b218-feaae651abe1'}, {'abstract': 'Hopeful economic indicators did nothing to improve the American public’s negative opinion of President Obama’s stewardship of the nation’s economy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/despite-improving-indicators-poll-finds-harsh-view-of-obama-on-economy/', 'snippet': 'Hopeful economic indicators did nothing to improve the American public’s negative opinion of President Obama’s stewardship of the nation’s economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s reports of hopeful economic indicators did nothing to improve the American public’s negative opinion of President Obama’s stewardship of the nation’s economy. However, while most Americans describe the economy as in bad condition, there has been a slight uptick in the number who view the nation’s fiscal circumstances positively, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Improving Indicators, Poll Finds Harsh View of Obama on Economy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T12:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/853d1f87-747e-572a-ba34-2c721f6feb08', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/853d1f87-747e-572a-ba34-2c721f6feb08'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street is entering an uncertain new era as the Volcker Rule takes hold. | Mandela’s complicated journey to support free markets and a free economy. | Bitcoin operates in ways that make it harder to prosecute violations. | The government bailout of General Motors came to a close on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/morning-agenda-whats-in-the-volcker-rule/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street is entering an uncertain new era as the Volcker Rule takes hold. | Mandela’s complicated journey to support free markets and a free economy. | Bitcoin operates in ways that make it harder to prosecute violations. | The government bailo...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street is entering an uncertain new era as the Volcker Rule — the regulation at the heart of Washington’s efforts to rein in financial risk-taking — takes hold, Ben Protess and Peter Eavis report in DealBook. The rule, a copy of which was reviewed by The New York Times, imposes some requirements that are tougher than the banks had wanted. Five federal agencies are expected to vote to approve it on Tuesday — though some might do so in private because of inclement weather in the Washington area. (One of them, the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, has canceled its public meeting.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s in the Volcker Rule', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T12:19:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27fa19d1-dee4-5f04-9a8c-1188232df2ab', 'word_count': 1957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27fa19d1-dee4-5f04-9a8c-1188232df2ab'}, {'abstract': 'The actress performs an excerpt from a new staged reading of Samuel Taylor Coleridge’s 1798 poem.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/in-performance-fiona-shaw-of-rime-of-the-ancient-mariner/', 'snippet': 'The actress performs an excerpt from a new staged reading of Samuel Taylor Coleridge’s 1798 poem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s In Performance video is with Fiona Shaw, in an excerpt from a new staged reading of Samuel Taylor Coleridge’s 1798 poem “The Rime of the Ancient Mariner.” This scene features the passage that birthed the expression “albatross around your neck.” The show, directed by Phyllida Lloyd, continues through Dec. 22 at the Harvey Theater of the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Fiona Shaw of ‘Rime of the Ancient Mariner’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleridge, Samuel Taylor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaw, Fiona', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T13:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70e9f30d-e474-598b-921b-57ac6ef89cf2', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70e9f30d-e474-598b-921b-57ac6ef89cf2'}, {'abstract': 'Slang and colloquialisms have their place, for special effect or to deliberately convey an informal, conversational tone. But otherwise, they can seem trite or hackneyed, and can undercut the serious and literate tone we seek.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/the-slang-patrol-2/', 'snippet': 'Slang and colloquialisms have their place, for special effect or to deliberately convey an informal, conversational tone. But otherwise, they can seem trite or hackneyed, and can undercut the serious and literate tone we seek.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Slang and colloquialisms have their place, for special effect or to deliberately convey an informal, conversational tone. But otherwise, they can seem trite or hackneyed, and can undercut the serious and literate tone we seek.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slang Patrol', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T13:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By PHILIP B.