ctor Peter Berg insisted Emile Hirsch go to the gym six days a week, for three months, before he could even be given a role in the film “Lone Survivor.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christian Bale gained 50 pounds to play a 1970s grifter in “American Hustle.” Robert Redford did tricky water stunts in “All Is Lost.” The cast of “12 Years a Slave” was subjected to countless period tortures. For actors, awards-caliber movies often mean feats of physical endurance. As his audition for the coming film “Lone Survivor,” Peter Berg’s adaptation of the true story of a Navy SEAL unit under attack in Afghanistan, Emile Hirsch had to hit the gym, six days a week at 6 a.m., for three months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/lonesurvivor/lonesurvivor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/lonesurvivor/lonesurvivor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/lonesurvivor/lonesurvivor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/lonesurvivor/lonesurvivor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/lonesurvivor/lonesurvivor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/arts/lonesurvivor/lonesurvivor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty