a67', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/ef449b55-cca5-5654-a17b-9493660a1a67'}, {'abstract': 'A former star ballerina resigns as artistic director of the Vaganova Ballet Academy in St. Petersburg.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/another-shuffle-in-russian-ballet-world-as-scandal-fallout-continues/', 'snippet': 'A former star ballerina resigns as artistic director of the Vaganova Ballet Academy in St. Petersburg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A former star ballerina has resigned as artistic director of the Vaganova Ballet Academy in St. Petersburg and been hired by the city’s Mikhailovsky Theater in the latest fallout from the scandal that has rocked Russian classical dance since the acid attack on the Bolshoi Ballet’s artistic director, Sergei Filin, last January.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Shuffle in Russian Ballet World as Scandal Fallout Continues', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asylmuratova, Altynai', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dmitrichenko, Pavel V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eifman, Boris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Filin, Sergei', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsiskaridze, Nikolay', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Ballet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mikhailovsky Opera and Ballet Theater', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vaganova Ballet Academy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Petersburg (Russia)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T17:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Kishkovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kishkovsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5896ba5-ed48-599b-ba01-07969e492364', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5896ba5-ed48-599b-ba01-07969e492364'}, {'abstract': 'First, we have to agree on precisely what constitutes a small business.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/three-ways-to-improve-small-business-lending/', 'snippet': 'First, we have to agree on precisely what constitutes a small business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, the House Small Business Committee met to examine the post-recession, small-business lending environment. Witnesses before the committee included representatives of credit unions, bankers, the Federal Reserve and private businesses involved in small-business lending and credit reporting. A summary of their testimony can be found in an interesting article by Kent Hoover.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Ways to Improve Small-Business Lending', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T18:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3d1369a-025c-5ec6-9807-5c96dbced52d', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3d1369a-025c-5ec6-9807-5c96dbced52d'}, {'abstract': 'Mary Barra’s appointment as chief of General Motors signifies a culture shift at the automaker, where six of the top two dozen executives are women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/business/changing-of-the-guard-in-a-traditionally-male-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Mary Barra’s appointment as chief of General Motors signifies a culture shift at the automaker, where six of the top two dozen executives are women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The announcement that Mary T. Barra will become the first female chief executive of General Motors is more than a human resources changeup. It’s a nod to the changing times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/11women/11women-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/business/11women/11women-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/11women/11women-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/11women/11women-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/11women/11women-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/business/11women/11women-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/11women/11women-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_na