s most common grade is an “A” have now gone viral. But despite the breathless tone of the coverage, this is actually very old news — at Harvard, and at colleges nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/as-have-been-harvards-most-common-grade-for-20-years/', 'snippet': 'Reports that Harvard’s most common grade is an “A” have now gone viral. But despite the breathless tone of the coverage, this is actually very old news — at Harvard, and at colleges nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In the last few days, reports that Harvard’s most common grade is an “A” have\xa0 now gone viral. But despite the shocked-shocked! tone of some of the coverage, this is actually very old news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A’s Have Been Harvard’s Most Common Grade for 20 Years', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rojstaczer, Stuart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T18:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6e13a0a-78c2-56d7-a831-3a5d97991dbc', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6e13a0a-78c2-56d7-a831-3a5d97991dbc'}, {'abstract': 'Commentators tried to decipher the meaning of a handshake between President Obama and President Raúl Castro of Cuba at Nelson Mandela’s memorial service.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/the-distraction-of-a-handshake-in-south-africa/', 'snippet': 'Commentators tried to decipher the meaning of a handshake between President Obama and President Raúl Castro of Cuba at Nelson Mandela’s memorial service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes what happens on the sidelines of a main event attended by world leaders can steal a bit of the spotlight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Distraction of a Handshake in South Africa', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brazile, Donna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Fidel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Raul', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Yoani', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Herald', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami New Times', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T18:36:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/791d2d69-3166-5e57-9991-a47e66829dee', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/791d2d69-3166-5e57-9991-a47e66829dee'}, {'abstract': 'Patricia Millett has been named to the D.C. Circuit: the first confirmation of the post-nuclear age.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/the-world-after-filibuster-reform/', 'snippet': 'Patricia Millett has been named to the D.C. Circuit: the first confirmation of the post-nuclear age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By a vote of 56-38, the Senate on Tuesday confirmed Patricia Millett to the D.C. Circuit Court of Appeals — thereby filling the 8-year vacancy created when John G. Roberts Jr. left the powerful court for a higher calling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The World After Filibuster Reform', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Millett, Patricia A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T18:36:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3f2637b-2cc8-58f0-a5fd-b812b26131fe', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3f2637b-2cc8-58f0-a5fd-b812b26131fe'}, {'abstract': 'The holiday installation includes, among many other sci-fi-inspired creations, a “Cyclopto” snowman; a full-scale spaceship built with slot machine parts, and a pathway of peppermint skulls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/garden/kenny-irwins-creations-on-view-in-baltimore.html', 'snippet': 'The holiday installation includes, among many other sci-fi-inspired creations, a “Cyclopto” snowman; a full-scale spaceship built with slot machine parts, and a pathway of peppermint skulls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Southern Californians have flocked at Christmastime to the Palm Springs yard of Kenny Irwin Jr., to see his extensive “Robo Lights” holiday display. This year, East Coast residents have an opportunity to view the artist’s work with “Have Yourself a Happy Little Robotmas,” part of “Human, Soul and Machine: The Coming Singularity!” on view through August at the American Visionary Art Museum, or AVAM, in Baltimore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/garden/10shows/10shows-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/garden/10shows/10shows-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/garden/10shows/10shows-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/garden/10shows/10shows-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/garden/10shows/10shows-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/garden/10shows/10shows-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/garden/10shows/10shows-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenny Irwin’s Creations on View in Baltimore', 'kicker': 'Currents | Shows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irwin, Kenny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN VISIONARY ART MUSEUM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T18:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db94706f-07a8-5480-8be2-eb4fdc9e6d85', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db94706f-07a8-5480-8be2-eb4fdc9e6d85'}, {'abstract': 'One more microtrend at this year’s just-closed Design Miami: a preponderance of thoughtful jewelry.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/threes-a-trend-designers-turn-to-jewelry/', 'snippet': 'One more microtrend at this year’s just-closed Design Miami: a preponderance of thoughtful jewelry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps it was the economics of shipping furniture as opposed to smaller, wearable items, but Design Miami seemed to have far more than its fair share of jewelry this year. In addition to the pieces by blue-chip artists like Alexander Calder and Moriko Mori at Louisa Guinness, there were amazing works by Gerd Rothman, like a necklace with fingerprints, at Ornamentum; cool vintage pieces by Gijs Bakker, a founder of Droog, including a brooch of a high jumper at Caroline Van Hoek; and colorful Op Art-inspired pieces by Carlos Cruz-Diez at Elizabetta Cipriani.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three’s a Trend | Designers Turn to Jewelry', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T18:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Delavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf4d9383-8e40-5443-ae0b-37c854ca5cf4', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf4d9383-8e40-5443-ae0b-37c854ca5cf4'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker’s new chief executive, Mary Barra, is an engineer by training who has a reputation for both good design and keeping a firm handle on costs, writes Antony Currie of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/good-governance-at-g-m/', 'snippet': 'The automaker’s new chief executive, Mary Barra, is an engineer by training who has a reputation for both good design and keeping a firm handle on costs, writes Antony Currie of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Motors has navigated a smart route to succession. Daniel F. Akerson, who has run the company since mid-2010, is stepping down in January. Replacing him as chief executive is Mary Barra, who despite 33 years of service at the automaker, has mostly sidestepped the taint of prebankruptcy failures. G.M., freshly liberated from the government bailout, also on Tuesday appointed an independent chairman for good governance measure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/dbpix-mary-barra/dbpix-mary-barra-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/business/dbpix-mary-barra/dbpix-mary-barra-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/dbpix-mary-barra/dbpix-mary-barra-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/dbpix-mary-barra/dbpix-mary-barra-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/dbpix-mary-barra/dbpix-mary-barra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/business/dbpix-mary-barra/dbpix-mary-barra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/business/dbpix-mary-barra/dbpix-mary-barra-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Governance at G.M.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akerson, Daniel F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barra, Mary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T18:48:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c20569b4-a22b-5203-b3e4-0bda29b4ce7d', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c20569b4-a22b-5203-b3e4-0bda29b4ce7d'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama and President Raúl Castro of Cuba exchanged a handshake at Nelson Mandela’s memorial, raising questions over what the gesture could mean for ties between the United States and Cuba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/africa/100000002594991/obama-shakes-hands-with-castro.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama and President Raúl Castro of Cuba exchanged a handshake at Nelson Mandela’s memorial, raising questions over what the gesture could mean for ties between the United States and Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and President Raúl Castro of Cuba exchanged a handshake at Nelson Mandela’s memorial, raising questions over what the gesture could mean for ties between the United States and Cuba.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/africa/11handshake-copy/11handshake-copy-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/world/africa/11handshake-copy/11handshake-copy-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/africa/11handshake-copy/11handshake