ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Marc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viceroy New York (Manhattan, NY, Hotel)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T20:04:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bebbb944-db1a-5356-beba-deeb9c4b1f15', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bebbb944-db1a-5356-beba-deeb9c4b1f15'}, {'abstract': 'The Macgregor Transformation Model proposes to decrease Defense Department’s spending without leaving the armed forces less-than-ready for combat — a problem with other downsizing plans.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/a-plan-for-a-more-powerful-military-that-costs-less/', 'snippet': 'The Macgregor Transformation Model proposes to decrease Defense Department’s spending without leaving the armed forces less-than-ready for combat — a problem with other downsizing plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON – In October, the Army chief of staff, Gen. Ray Odierno, said that because of budget cuts, only two of the Army’s 42 combat brigades were ready for battle. In November, he warned members of the Senate Armed Services Committee that if the nation had to fight in the near term, “it is unlikely that the Army would be able to defeat an adversary quickly and decisively.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Plan for a More Powerful Military That Costs Less', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, '