e': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T21:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/040a8881-6742-5d28-9122-dab1944ffe07', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/040a8881-6742-5d28-9122-dab1944ffe07'}, {'abstract': 'Mary T. Barra, who will be the next chief executive of General Motors, visited The New York Times in November and sat down with reporters and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/business/mary-barra-gms-new-chief-speaking-her-mind.html', 'snippet': 'Mary T. Barra, who will be the next chief executive of General Motors, visited The New York Times in November and sat down with reporters and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary T. Barra, who was named the next chief executive of General Motors on Tuesday, visited The New York Times in November and talked with reporters and editors. What follows is an edited, condensed version of the interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary Barra, G.M.’s New Chief, Speaking Her Mind', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barra, Mary T', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T21:52:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0979ea25-daad-5a3b-986d-3f7f0ade9bd1', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0979ea25-daad-5a3b-986d-3f7f0ade9bd1'}, {'abstract': 'Watch the crazy ants.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/ants-to-keep-out-of-your-pants/', 'snippet': 'Watch the crazy ants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In last weekend’s magazine article about invasive ants in Texas, Jon Mooallem refers to the psychological torment that comes from feeling like something is crawling all over your body. Well, try watching the video above without getting squirmy and . . . yes, antsy. You might think these are regular old ants that happened to get worked up over something, but no, this is what they’re like all the time. They never go marching one by one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ants to Keep Out of Your Pants', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mooallem, Jon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T21:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7736142-8d01-5e5c-a416-1b73acc2b46d', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7736142-8d01-5e5c-a416-1b73acc2b46d'}, {'abstract': 'A university president who has probably done more to encourage interest in science and math among minority and low-income students than any other educator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/opinion/q-a-with-freeman-hrabowski.html', 'snippet': 'A university president who has probably done more to encourage interest in science and math among minority and low-income students than any other educator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Freeman Hrabowski has probably done more to encourage interest in science and math among minority and low-income students than any other educator. As president of the University of Maryland, Baltimore County, Dr. Hrabowski has turned his campus into one of the top sources of African-American postgraduate degrees in science and engineering, and he has helped develop several pioneering scholarship programs to get disadvantaged students interested in the subject and to become teachers in those fields. In 2011, he led a National Academy of Sciences study on increasing minority participation in science and technology, which recommended a series of ways to improve early childhood preparation, stimulate interest among high school students, and make college more affordable. He recently discussed some of those ideas with David Firestone of The New York Times editorial board.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/opinion/11stem-hrabowski-img/11stem-hrabowski-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/opinion/11stem-hrabowski-img/11stem-hrabowski-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/opinion/11stem-hrabowski-img/11stem-hrabowski-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/opinion/11stem-hrabowski-img/11stem-hrabowski-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy':