at limits on trading by big banks have been approved, the focus turns to enforcement and disclosure of trading activities, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, former chief economist of the International Monetary Fund, is the Ronald A. Kurtz Professor of Entrepreneurship at the M.I.T. Sloan School of Management and co-author of “White House Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Volcker Rule Work', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volcker, Paul A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T22:22:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82ee6abc-42e4-5d1b-b918-568665ab1634', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82ee6abc-42e4-5d1b-b918-568665ab1634'}, {'abstract': 'Don and Mera Rubell, who have spent 12 years collecting art in China, are displaying highlights at the Rubell museum in Miami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/arts/design/art-collectors-show-their-chinese-prizes.html', 'snippet': 'Don and Mera Rubell, who have spent 12 years collecting art in China, are displaying highlights at the Rubell museum in Miami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the prodigious Miami collectors Don and Mera Rubell first visited China, in 2001, they found the artists they met fascinating, but they were frankly unimpressed by the art itself. “It was our most intense trip with the least amount of art,” Mr. Rubell said. “Many of the artists seemed to be making work for export.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11RUBELLjp/11RUBELLjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11RUBELLjp/11RUBELLjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11RUBELLjp/11RUBELLjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11RUBELLjp/11RUBELLjp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11RUBELLjp/11RUBELLjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11RUBELLjp/11RUBELLjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11RUBELLjp/11RUBELLjp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Collectors Show Their Chinese Prizes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Collectors Show Their Chinese Prizes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art Basel Miami Beach', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubell, Donald', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubell, Mera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T22:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37a03c5e-7e8a-513e-a7a5-0c1dee14cb27', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37a03c5e-7e8a-513e-a7a5-0c1dee14cb27'}, {'abstract': 'Greg Baxter’s debut novel, “The Apartment,” spends a day with a newly wealthy American veteran of the Iraq war looking for a place in an unnamed European city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/books/the-apartment-a-debut-novel-by-greg-baxter.html', 'snippet': 'Greg Baxter’s debut novel, “The Apartment,” spends a day with a newly wealthy American veteran of the Iraq war looking for a place in an unnamed European city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first, the setup may seem familiar. An American military veteran — alienated and adrift after a war — wanders through a chilly European city in December. He pals around with an intelligent and alluring young woman, about half his age; at bars and cafes, he encounters fellow expatriates, as well as natives who view his wealth and nationality with envy and suspicion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/subbook1/subbook1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/subbook1/subbook1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/subbook1/subbook1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/subbook1/subbook1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1801, 'width': 1392, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/subbook1/subbook1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/subbook1/subbook1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/subbook1/subbook1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This American Abroad Is Far From Innocent', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This American Abroad Is Far From Innocent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'per