int_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11COMEDY/11COMEDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11COMEDY/11COMEDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11COMEDY/11COMEDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11COMEDY/11COMEDY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11COMEDY/11COMEDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11COMEDY/11COMEDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/arts/11COMEDY/11COMEDY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One’s Crude, the Other’s Cerebral', 'kicker': 'On Comedy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One’s Crude, the Other’s Cerebral', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Independent Film Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Murderfist', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Birthday Boys, The', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Birthday Boys (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T22:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18298c47-600b-5176-ae03-f29bdb62cdd5', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18298c47-600b-5176-ae03-f29bdb62cdd5'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “Maus” shares his appreciation for the late abstract painter, who was renowned for his monochromatic canvases but also had a lesser-known career as a cartoonist.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/10/artists-on-artists-art-spiegelman-on-the-varied-craft-of-ad-reinhardt/', 'snippet': 'The author of “Maus” shares his appreciation for the late abstract painter, who was renowned for his monochromatic canvases but also had a lesser-known career as a cartoonist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a banner year for the cartoonist Art Spiegelman, regarded by many as the father of the contemporary graphic novel. Long revered for “Maus,” his Pulitzer Prize-winning concentration camp epic (published in two parts in 1986 and 1991), the artist’s work is broader than many realize, as his retrospective at the Jewish Museum in New York (through March 23, 2014) reveals. The show, which has already appeared in Europe and Canada, includes Spiegelman’s early Wacky Pack and Garbage Pail Kids sketches, and closes with more recent projects, like a performance he choreographed and designed with the dance troupe Pilobolus and a colored-glass window representing an art student’s life that he made for his alma mater, the High School of Art & Design in New York. In October, Spiegelman published his monograph, “Co-Mix” (Drawn & Quarterly), and premiered his hybrid slide-show-talk-concert “Wordless!,” which focuses on the woodcut novels of early-20th-century artists like Lynd Ward, at the Sydney Opera House. It runs for one night at the Brooklyn Academy of Music on Jan. 18.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artists on Artists | Art Spiegelman on the Varied Craft of Ad Reinhardt', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T22:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Kino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43653e2b-5ede-58af-bf08-6aefa221af82', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43653e2b-5ede-58af-bf08-6aefa221af82'}, {'abstract': 'Anna Thorvaldsdottir was in the spotlight at the Composer Portraits series, with Either/Or, at Columbia University’s Miller Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/arts/music/anna-thorvaldsdottirs-works-at-columbias-miller-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Anna Thorvaldsdottir was in the spotlight at the Composer Portraits series, with Either/Or, at Columbia University’s Miller Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A quiet revolution underway for some time now at Columbia University’s Miller Theater continued apace on Thursday night, when the enterprising new-music ensemble Either/Or devoted a Composer Portraits program to works by Anna Thorvaldsdottir. Under the watch of Melissa Smey, the theater’s executive director since 2009, Miller has devoted considerable resources to presenting music by female composers, both established and emerging — and has done so with a lack of fanfare that characterizes the initiative as no anomaly, but simply business as usual.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Composed of Bumps, Murmurs and Sighs', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Composed Of Bumps, Murmurs And Sighs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thorvaldsdottir, Anna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Either/Or', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-10T22:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9b5053f-31a3-51b5-b0ab-41983de44c42', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9b5053f-31a3-51b5-b0ab-41983de44c42'}, {'abstract': 'The handsome bar is now dedicated exclusively to Bordeaux wines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/dining/bar-bordeaux-opens-at-the-seafood-brasserie-millesime.html', 'snippet': 'The handsome bar is now dedicated exclusively to Bordeaux wines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Headliner ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/dining/11OFF_SPAN/11OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/dining/11OFF_SPAN/11OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'cap