ad they had skipped the ceremony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Wednesday, 6:08 p.m. | As boos rained down on South Africa’s president, Jacob Zuma, during the memorial service for Nelson Mandela on Tuesday, and American conservatives reacted with fury over President Obama’s handshake with President Raúl Castro of Cuba, it was not hard to imagine sighs of relief being breathed by top officials in Israel and Iran who decided that they were too busy, ill, or frugal to make the trip themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaders of Israel and Iran Praise Mandela, From a Safe Distance', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peres, Shimon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T00:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/459e7556-470a-5aee-95e2-263c68e0b26a', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/459e7556-470a-5aee-95e2-263c68e0b26a'}, {'abstract': 'The minimum wage has lost much of its power to lift workers out of poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive