o. 3 — Babe Ruth’s number — with the Mets, is a home run hitter, but he also struck out a club-record 195 times in his last full season with the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKE BUENA VISTA, Fla. — Curtis Granderson, who was brought to the Mets to hit home runs, now wears the number of a man who swatted 714, mostly for the Yankees. That would be No. 3, as in Babe Ruth. Granderson chose it because he wanted a single-digit number for his trim frame — “I’m a little guy,” he said — and because he was born in March, the third month.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/sports/METS/METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/sports/METS/METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/sports/METS/METS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cr