l at the time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTIAGO, Chile — The Truth Commission in São Paulo, Brazil’s largest city, said Tuesday that Juscelino Kubitschek, the country’s president from 1956 to 1961, was murdered in 1976 in a conspiracy by the military dictatorship ruling Brazil at the time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazilian Panel Says Ex-Leader Was Murdered', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazilian Panel Says Ex-Leader Was Murdered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kubitschek, Juscelino', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Truth Commission (Brazil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T03:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4355a63f-b228-5dd9-b6ff-4926bc99e785', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4355a63f-b228-5dd9-b6ff-4926bc99e785'}, {'abstract': 'The Hopi and San Carlos Apache Indians of Arizona learned that 24 of their items bought by a foundation are going to be returned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/us/arizona-auctioned-artifacts-to-be-returned-to-tribes.html', 'snippet': 'The Hopi and San Carlos Apache Indians of Arizona learned that 24 of their items bought by a foundation are going to be returned.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A day after more than 27 of their sacred artifacts were sold at a contested auction in Paris for $757,000, the Hopi and San Carlos Apache Indians of Arizona learned Tuesday that 24 of the items had been bought by a foundation that plans to return them to the tribes. The Hopi artifacts are colorful and intricate masklike items held to be imbued with divine spirits. Gregory Annenberg Weingarten, a vice president of the Los Angeles-based Annenberg Foundation, said it had decided to buy the items, at a cost of $530,000, once it became clear that the Paris auction house EVE would not delay the sale to allow the tribes time to gather proof that the items had been stolen from their lands long ago. “These are not trophies to have on one’s mantel,” he said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: Auctioned Artifacts to Be Returned to Tribes', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: Auctioned Artifacts to Be Returned to Tribes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mashberg, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hopi Indians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANNENBERG FOUNDATION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APACHE INDIANS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T03:29:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Mashberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_o