ing cigarette filters up your nostrils is no way to safeguard your lungs from China’s stubborn pollution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some sensible medical advice: Jamming cigarette butts up your nostrils will not ward off the acrid smog enveloping China, and is positively risky for your health. Thus some Chinese newspapers have told readers, in the most giddying example yet of how chronic air pollution is forcing citizens to desperate inventiveness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Novel Tactics for Dealing with Pollution', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Daily", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SINA Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T04:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d09513f-b3be-59d5-ba41-0f2ac9d29855', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d09513f-b3be-59d5-ba41-0f2ac9d29855'}, {'abstract': 'New York City F.C., which will begin Major League Soccer play in 2015, announced that it had hired Jason Kreis as the club’s first coach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/sports/soccer/coach-named-for-new-york-mls-team.html', 'snippet': 'New York City F.C., which will begin Major League Soccer play in 2015, announced that it had hired Jason Kreis as the club’s first coach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City F.C., which will begin Major League Soccer play in 2015, announced that it had hired Jason Kreis as the club’s first coach. Last Saturday, Kreis was the losing coach when Real Salt Lake fell to Sporting Kansas City in a penalty kick shootout in the M.L.S. Cup. His contract with Real Salt Lake, where he has been the coach since 2007, is to expire at the end of the year. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coach Named for New York M.L.S. Team', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coach for New York Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Jack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kreis, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Football Club (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T04:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4be63b6-ea12-55a2-9ab0-2eab636d8cbd', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4be63b6-ea12-55a2-9ab0-2eab636d8cbd'}, {'abstract': 'Following is a statement by Secretary of State John Kerry on events in Ukraine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/world/europe/kerrys-statement-on-ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'Following is a statement by Secretary of State John Kerry on events in Ukraine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following is a statement by Secretary of State John Kerry on events in Ukraine:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry’s Statement on Ukraine', 'kicker': 'Text', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T04:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6f98986-2e74-531e-9367-bf1ddc2d8fc2', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6f98986-2e74-531e-9367-bf1ddc2d8fc2'}, {'abstract': 'The French government announced the death of two French paratroopers in the Central African Republic, the country’s first casualties since its military force arrived to help stem increasing violence there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/world/africa/french-paratroopers-killed-in-central-african-republic.html', 'snippet': 'The French government announced the death of two French paratroopers in the Central African Republic, the country’s first casualties since its military force arrived to help stem increasing violence there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — President François Hollande of France arrived Tuesday in the Central African Republic just hours after the French government announced the death of two French paratroopers. The paratroopers were part of the newly augmented French military force that arrived over the weekend to help stem the increasing violence in the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 French Paratroopers Killed in Central African Republic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paratroopers From France Die in Unrest In Africa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Alissa Johannsen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central African Republic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T04:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe4cecbb-6553-5190-b276-659531142d0c', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe4cecbb-6553-5190-b276-659531142d0c'}, {'abstract': 'The awarding of the Olympics in 2007 to Sochi, so tantalizingly close, had for a time raised hopes that Abkhazia would share in the bounty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/world/europe/close-to-the-olympics-far-from-the-bounty.html', 'snippet': 'The awarding of the Olympics in 2007 to Sochi, so tantalizingly close, had for a time raised hopes that Abkhazia would share in the bounty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GULRIPSHI, Georgia — A little less than three miles from Sochi’s main Olympic Stadium, the site of the opening and closing ceremonies of the Winter Games in February, the Psou River stands as Russia’s border with Georgia. But no one directly on either side of the derelict border post considers any part of the region Georgia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/ABKHAZIA-1/ABKHAZIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/world/ABKHAZIA-1/ABKHAZIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/ABKHAZIA-1/ABKHAZIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/ABKHAZIA-1/ABKHAZIA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/ABKHAZIA-1/ABKHAZIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/world/ABKHAZIA-1/ABKHAZIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/world/ABKHAZIA-1/ABKHAZIA-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Close to the Olympics, Far From the Bounty', 'kicker': 'Gulripshi Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Close to the Olympics, Far From the Bounty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ABKHAZIA (GEORGIAN REPUBLIC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sochi (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T04:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d004ea9-4fc0-58f8-8856-4827cf8e2998', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d004ea9-4fc0-58f8-8856-4827cf8e2998'}, {'abstract': 'The 2013 edition of the fair had a throwback feel, with numerous appealingly intimate objects from the ’40s to the ’70s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/t-magazine/10-best-pieces-at-this-years-design-miami.html', 'snippet': 'The 2013 edition of the fair had a throwback feel, with numerous appealingly intimate objects from the ’40s to the ’70s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Design Miami, the nine-year-old satellite fair to Art Basel in Miami Beach, is known for showcasing works by modern masters like Jean Prouvé and Charlotte Perriand. This year proved no different, with prefab houses by both on display (Prouvé’s built within the Design Miami tent, Perriand’s on the beach behind the Raleigh Hotel). But in addition to the large-scale showstoppers, there were numerous more intimate works of interest. Many dealers showed jewelry or decorative objects alongside furniture. Several galleries created complete residential settings in which they installed their pieces. Demish Danant, for example, felt like a Parisian apartment from the 1970s with its boiserie and wall-to-wall carpeting. And while a few galleries did show new work, objects from the ’40s to the ’70s were predominant, adding to the fair’s throwback feel. Here is some of the best this year’s Design Miami had to offer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/t-magazine/11miami-delavan1/11miami-delavan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/t-magazine/11miami-delavan1/11miami-delavan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/t-magazine/11miami-delavan1/11miami-delavan1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/t-magazine/11miami-delavan1/11miami-delavan1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/t-magazine/11miami-delavan1/11miami-delavan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/11/t-magazine/11miami-delavan1/11miami-delavan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type