-ddd6e60f7910'}, {'abstract': 'The first phase of a long-troubled project to divert water from the Yangtze River to northern China officially began on Tuesday with little fanfare.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/a-quiet-start-to-south-north-water-transfer/', 'snippet': 'The first phase of a long-troubled project to divert water from the Yangtze River to northern China officially began on Tuesday with little fanfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chinese government has often brandished its feats of building vast dams and channeling rivers as triumphs of engineering. Not this time. This week a first leg of what the government calls the world’s biggest water transfer project officially started in a mood of subdued resignation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quiet Start to South-North Water Transfer', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three Gorges Dam (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma Jun', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Weekend (Chinese Newspaper)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tianjin (China)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T10:39:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename