n Austin, Tex.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/a-bootstrapping-entrepreneur-decides-to-bet-the-family-home/', 'snippet': 'Adriana Rodriguez, a Mexican immigrant and a mother of two, needed more cash flow after she launched a bilingual school in Austin, Tex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not at all uncommon for entrepreneurs to tap into their home equity to finance a business idea. A few years ago, Adriana Rodriguez of Austin, Tex., took an even more striking step: She sold her house to support her education start-up and moved her family into a small rental.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bootstrapping Entrepreneur Decides to Bet the Family Home', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bilingual Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T12:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colleen DeBaise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colleen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeBaise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb4c6253-75fe-520b-a2a8-93bbb439b611', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb4c6253-75fe-520b-a2a8-93bbb439b611'}, {'abstract': 'A program called Saude Criança helps sick children and their families address the social conditions that cause illness to bring sustainable treatments.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/helping-rios-poor-continue-to-heal-at-home/', 'snippet': 'A program called Saude Criança helps sick children and their families address the social conditions that cause illness to bring sustainable treatments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We often hear about the harmful effects of poverty on health, particularly the health of children. But we hear less about the decisive role health plays in triggering, or exacerbating, poverty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helping Brazil’s Poor Heal at Home', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T12:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b06987f6-1c82-57a3-bc41-bf32bed22bf4', 'word_count': 1821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b06987f6-1c82-57a3-bc41-bf32bed22bf4'}, {'abstract': 'The British bank Barclays is ending its sponsorship in 2015 of a bike-rental program in London that inspired a similar bike-sharing program — Citi Bike — in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/barclays-to-end-sponsorship-of-london-bike-program/', 'snippet': 'The British bank Barclays is ending its sponsorship in 2015 of a bike-rental program in London that inspired a similar bike-sharing program — Citi Bike — in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 2:5