637a7', 'word_count': 3633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5205a871-9f62-5b80-bac4-865e2b4637a7'}, {'abstract': 'One of the oldest clichés about Wall Street is that the market can stay irrational longer than you can stay solvent. That is one way to sum up Paulo Santos’s experience with shorting Amazon’s stock.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/amazons-prophet-and-losses/', 'snippet': 'One of the oldest clichés about Wall Street is that the market can stay irrational longer than you can stay solvent. That is one way to sum up Paulo Santos’s experience with shorting Amazon’s stock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three months ago, you could buy a share of Amazon for $300. Today, it would cost you nearly $400. Surely such a run-up was driven by expectations that the company’s all-important fourth quarter would be even better than forecast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/technology/11santos/11santos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 903, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/11/technology/11santos/11santos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 903}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/technology/11santos/11santos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/technology/11santos/11santos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1361, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/11/technology/11santos/11santos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard'