ugh days may be ahead for air travel congestion.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cracks in Air Travel May Widen', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trending: Cracks in Air Travel May Widen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c0626c7-56c2-5404-a597-7112271875de', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c0626c7-56c2-5404-a597-7112271875de'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/classical-playlist-anne-sophie-mutter-christian-tetzlaff-richard-egarr-and-more/', 'snippet': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘DVORAK’Anne-Sophie Mutter, violin, with Berlin Philharmonic, Manfred Honeck, conductor(Deutsche Grammophon)With a sound like molten chocolate and a romantic temperament to match, the violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter is in her element here in a glowing recording of works by Dvorak including the darkly heroic Violin Concerto and the gorgeous Romance in F minor. The Berlin Philharmonic under Manfred Honeck tempers the sweetness with playing that is rich, intense, but also edgy where needed. (Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype