{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mutter, Anne-Sophie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tetzlaff, Christian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vogt, Lars', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MODERN ENSEMBLE', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berlin Philharmonic', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/593dc73e-4e24-53a8-8c93-529fcfd9f7ed', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/593dc73e-4e24-53a8-8c93-529fcfd9f7ed'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers hammered out a budget deal, but still haven’t extended unemployment benefits.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/what-about-unemployment-insurance/', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers hammered out a budget deal, but still haven’t extended unemployment benefits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a lot to say about the Congressional budget deal, and we do that later on the editorial page. For now I wanted to dwell on the outrageous failure of Congress to extend federal long-term unemployment benefits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Needs to Extend Unemployment Insurance', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Ezra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:08:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ba31b15-4b89-54d3-8b57-ad912740943c', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ba31b15-4b89-54d3-8b57-ad912740943c'}, {'abstract': 'The choices offered by the Affordable Care Act are leading some small companies, which don’t have to offer health benefits, to drop their employee plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/business/smallbusiness/changing-the-health-insurance-equation-for-small-employers.html', 'snippet': 'The choices offered by the Affordable Care Act are leading some small companies, which don’t have to offer health benefits, to drop their employee plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nearly 20 years, Keith Perkins offered health insurance to employees of his small electrical contracting company in Greencastle, Pa., and footed most of the bill. This year, with the arrival of the Affordable Care Act’s insurance marketplace, he decided to stop.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/business/Sbiz/Sbiz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1245, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty