thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/selfie-of-obama-was-misinterpreted-photographer-says/', 'snippet': 'The photographer, Roberto Schmidt, offers an explanation of what went on before and after the photo was taken during Nelson Mandela’s memorial ceremony, and Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain also reacts to the concern over it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is an era when one honest image can ignite viral misinterpretation. So an Agence France-Presse photographer, Roberto Schmidt, has provided invaluable context for his photograph of a grinning President Obama joining two prime ministers in taking a snapshot of themselves at Nelson Mandela’s memorial ceremony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Selfie’ of Obama Was Misinterpreted, Photographer Says', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kinnock, Neil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thorning-Schmidt, Helle', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:10:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline':