 a new farm bill passed before the end of the year appeared dim, though lawmakers said they were close.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Prospects for passage of a new farm bill before the end of the year appear dim, with just a week left before Congress adjourns for the holidays, although lawmakers insisted they were close to a deal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/FARM/FARM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 496, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/us/FARM/FARM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 496}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/FARM/FARM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/FARM/FARM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1693, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/FARM/FARM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/us/FARM/FARM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/FARM/FARM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Farm Bill in Sight as Recess Looms for Congress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Deal, but Hint of Progress as Lawmakers Seek Farm Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, Frank D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stabenow, Debbie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab11713a-79b9-5b10-8311-9496d68faf55', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab11713a-79b9-5b10-8311-9496d68faf55'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, Basel and its brethren were a mad blur of dollar signs, branding, V.I.P. check-ins and, of course, Kimye. But as tedious as all that could be, there were still a few moments that mattered.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/art-market-a-social-diary-of-this-years-miami-art-fairs/', 'snippet': 'Yes, Basel and its brethren were a mad blur of dollar signs, branding, V.I.P. check-ins and, of course, Kimye. But as tedious as all that could be, there were still a few moments that mattered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s be honest about the art fairs that concluded on Sunday in Miami. They were about one thing: money — the making of it, by selling art, and the spending of it, on having a decadently good time. And the art sold well. Very well. Dealers at the two biggest fairs, Art Basel in Miami Beach, at the Miami Beach Convention Center, and NADA (the New Art Dealers Alliance), at the Deauville Beach Resort in North Beach, boasted that despite predictions of Basel burnout, plenty of collectors attended and sales were stronger than in recent years. So rest assured that these tropical rituals of end-of-year excess will continue for the foreseeable future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Social Diary of This Year’s Miami Art Fairs', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art Basel Miami Beach', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanco, Mykki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonze, Spike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:22:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/718466a9-cc06-538b-8ae7-1c812ccf63c1', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/718466a9-cc06-538b-8ae7-1c812ccf63c1'}, {'abstract': 'A tough year for Lululemon. How to “repurpose” employees. Did Marissa Mayer buy a funeral home?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/today-in-small-business-who-wants-to-be-a-teen-millionaire/', 'snippet': 'A tough year for Lululemon. How to “repurpose” employees. Did Marissa Mayer buy a funeral home?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 