als’ shootout victory on Tuesday night was memorable, even by Ovechkin standards, and worth another look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Ovechkin of the Washington Capitals has been such a productive goal scorer in his eight N.H.L. seasons that it takes something truly special to make his goals noteworthy these days. The fact that he is leading the league in goals with 26 after 29 games? Yawn. That he became the Capitals’ career leader for power play goals? Insert crickets chirping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/12ovechkin/12ovechkin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/12ovechkin/12ovechkin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/12ovechkin/12ovechkin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/12ovechkin/12ovechkin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/12ovechkin/12ovechkin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/12ovechkin/12ovechkin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/12ovechkin/12ovechkin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Capitals’ Ovechkin Scores Four Goals and Celebrates in Style', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18643da1-614d-58f9-b445-a478924cf9ea', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18643da1-614d-58f9-b445-a478924cf9ea'}, {'abstract': 'Kyle Riabko, of “Spring Awakening” and “Hair” on Broadway, leads the show “What’s It All About? Bacharach Reimagined” at New York Theater Workshop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/theater/kyle-riabko-of-whats-it-all-about-bacharach-reimagined.html', 'snippet': 'Kyle Riabko, of “Spring Awakening” and “Hair” on Broadway, leads the show “What’s It All About? Bacharach Reimagined” at New York Theater Workshop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Burt Bacharach’s canon of effervescent pop classics belongs to the world, no question; a guy who could turn out hits for artists encompassing Perry Como and El DeBarge clearly has no trouble writing for a wide audience. But for generations of pop-music obsessives and fellow musicians, Mr. Bacharach’s distinctive compositional sophistication — those uneven time signatures, the rich jazz chords — has made him a folk hero.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Guy’s in Love With Your Songs', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | Kyle Riabko', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Guy’s in Love With Your Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riabko, Kyle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bacharach, Burt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:28:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Weinert-Kendt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinert-Kendt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f3a594-1346-5b4c-abd8-e34d02954af2', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f3a594-1346-5b4c-abd8-e34d02954af2'}, {'abstract': 'With the country ranked first on a world happiness list, visiting Copenhagen during the festive Christmas season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/travel/denmark-where-joy-is-always-in-season.html', 'snippet': 'With the country ranked first on a world happiness list, visiting Copenhagen during the festive Christmas season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There appears to be nothing rotten in the state of Denmark these days. For the second straight year, Denmark has been named the happiest country, according to a survey of 156 nations called the World Happiness Report. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HEADS2/15HEADS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HEADS2/15HEADS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HEADS2/15HEADS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HEADS2/15HEADS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HEADS2/15HEADS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HEADS2/15HEADS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HEADS2/15HEADS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Denmark, Where Joy Is Always in Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Joy Is Always in Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Copenhagen (Denmark)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Veronica Hackethal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Veronica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hackethal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34e613a7-4465-5b2f-a315-7347a752de87', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34e613a7-4465-5b2f-a315-7347a752de87'}, {'abstract': 'An area on the fringe of Chinatown is making a comeback, drawing people looking for everything from food to fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/travel/cuisine-and-crowds-along-a-stretch-of-singapore.html', 'snippet': 'An area on the fringe of Chinatown is making a comeback, drawing people looking for everything from food to fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Named for its storied past as the home of exclusive clubs for Chinese businessmen in the 1800s and early 1900s, the stretch of Club Street that extends to Ann Siang Road, on the fringe of Singapore’s Chinatown, is making a comeback. With trendy new restaurants and bars and attractive boutiques sprouting up in the historically preserved shop houses lining a winding slope, crowds are thronging to the area. On weekend nights, the enclave is conveniently off limits to cars.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15SURFACING3/15SURFACING3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15SURFACING3/15SURFACING3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15SURFACING3/15SURFACING3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15SURFACING3/15SURFACING3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15SURFACING3/15SURFACING3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15SURFACING3/15SURFACING3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15SURFACING3/15SURFACING3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuisine and Crowds Along a Stretch of Singapore', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Catering Again to Well-Dressed Crowds With an Appetite for the Exotic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Evelyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Singapore', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:32:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e7c786a-ba33-5e20-8150-6448a1cfb1e5', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e7c786a-ba33-5e20-8150-6448a1cfb1e5'}, {'abstract': 'Scott P. Brown is keeping his options open and his profile high a year after his defeat by Elizabeth Warren.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/us/politics/ex-senator-scott-brown-toys-with-new-hampshire-run.html', 'snippet': 'Scott P. Brown is keeping his options open and his profile high a year after his defeat by Elizabeth Warren.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDONDERRY, N.H. — The trademark pickup truck rolled up to the Harold Square restaurant here one rainy night last week and out popped Scott P. Brown, the former senator from Massachusetts. He had been a senator for only three years, but that was long enough to whet his appetite for more.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/12brown-cncd/12brown-cncd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/us/12brown-cncd/12brown-cncd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/12brown-cncd/12brown-cncd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/12brown-cncd/12brown-cncd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/12brown-cncd/12brown-cncd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/us/12brown-cncd/12brown-cncd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/us/12brown-cncd/12brown-cncd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Popular Noncandidate Keeps His Options Open and the Voters Guessing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Popular Noncandidate Keeps His Options Open and the Voters Guessing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/406db7cd-c779-5d0b-9ad2-e3f38b461d17', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/406db7cd-c779-5d0b-9ad2-e3f38b461d17'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a lot of room in the space between “ringing success” and “abject failure.”', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/obamacares-many-possible-futures/', 'snippet': 'There’s a lot of room in the space between “ringing success” and “abject failure.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest data on Obamacare signups is yet another rorschach test for the law’s supporters and skeptics: The accelerating rate of signups is either evidence that enrollment might yet achieve escape velocity or an indicator (given how low, in absolute numbers, private enrollment remains) that even with a smoother website experience the program is never going to reach its “multiple millions of private enrollees” goal. I’ve been writing lately about the latter possibility, and sketching scenarios where low enrollment leads to adverse selection and makes the entire mandate-regulate-subsidize setup unsustainable. But the new numbers provide a good opportunity to note that “unsustainability” is a shorthand phrase that obscures as much as it reveals, and there are many, many likely outcomes for Obamacare that fall somewhere between “meets its supporters expectations” and “collapses under its own weight.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obamacare’s Many Possible Futures', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T17:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f45af65-d657-5ac5-b8b7-55f72bdbc326', 'word_count': 790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f45af65-d657-5ac5-b8b7-55f72bdbc326'}, {'abstract': 'Jacob J. Lew, the Treasury secretary, said Dodd-Frank made the financial system safer, but simply asserting it does not make it so, Jesse Eisinger of ProPublica writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/soothing-words-on-too-big-to-fail-but-with-little-meaning/', 'snippet': 'Jacob J. Lew, the Treasury secretary, said Dodd-Frank made the financial system safer, but simply asserting it does not make it so, Jesse Eisinger of ProPublica writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer, President Obama’s new Treasury secretary, Jacob J. Lew, offered a financial reform litmus test: By the end of 2013, could we say with a straight face that we have solved the “too big to fail” problem? ', 'p