e': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ceaf9f9-f380-596b-910f-c1528d23847d', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ceaf9f9-f380-596b-910f-c1528d23847d'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Zuccarini, the underwater cinematographer for “All Is Lost,” discusses his process.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/below-the-line-underwater-with-all-is-lost/', 'snippet': 'Peter Zuccarini, the underwater cinematographer for “All Is Lost,” discusses his process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'J. C. Chandor’s drama “All Is Lost” is receiving accolades for the stoic, nearly wordless performance of Robert Redford. But the Indian Ocean, where Mr. Redford’s character is stranded, gives a pretty strong performance itself. Working with water, particularly\xa0 underwater, can be a challenge for filmmakers. So while Mr. Chandor used Frank G. DeMarco (“Margin Call”) as his cinematographer for the scenes outside the water, he hired a specialist in underwater photography for the wetter moments. That man, Peter Zuccarini, is one of the industry’s go-to cinematographers for underwater photography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/movies/allislost-2/allislost-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/10/movies/allislost-2/allislost-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/movies/allislost-2/allislost-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/movies/allislost-2/allislost-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1192, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/movies/allislost-2/allislost-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/10/movies/allislost-2/allislost-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/10/movies/allislost-2/allislost-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: Underwater With ‘All Is Lost’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandor, J C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redford, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahama Islands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T18:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f5a3e3a-4236-55fb-bc7d-0f547373d7e2', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f5a3e3a-4236-55fb-bc7d-0f547373d7e2'}, {'abstract': 'In the guise of pressing for the best possible Iran deal, we reward those who want no deal at all.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/irans-hardliners-and-ours/', 'snippet': 'In the guise of pressing for the best possible Iran deal, we reward those who want no deal at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are several reasons to applaud – warily, provisionally – the first steps Iran, the United States and other world powers have taken toward a deal to prevent a Persian bomb. One reason for cheer is that the interim agreement has brought together the hard-liners, theirs and ours, in reciprocal dismay. When John Bolton, the most enthusiastic armchair warrior of the George W. Bush brigade, and Mohammad Reza Naqdi, the head of Iran’s brutal Basij paramilitary, are both unhappy, you’ve probably done something right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Hardliners, and Ours', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tehran (Iran)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T18:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a429125c-6f3b-52b4-89e7-3a74ad4c62fd', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a429125c-6f3b-52b4-89e7-3a74ad4c62fd'}, {'abstract': 'A discussion of Bitcoin’s potential by some of the digital currency’s strongest advocates.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/11/bitcoin-believers-see-a-role-for-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'A discussion of Bitcoin’s potential by some of the digital currency’s strongest advocates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A venture capitalist, a former regulator, a lawyer and a pair of entrepreneurs — Bitcoin evangelists all — gathered on Tuesday in the 