c', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T22:05:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f31c7ea-4c18-5a1f-a742-238f4975b8c9', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f31c7ea-4c18-5a1f-a742-238f4975b8c9'}, {'abstract': 'Consider investment options and ease of use when selecting a provider.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/your-money/shopping-for-a-health-savings-account.html', 'snippet': 'Consider investment options and ease of use when selecting a provider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HEALTH savings accounts have been around for a decade and more people are using them, but comparing the features of various accounts can still be challenging. Alternatives range from basic savings accounts offered by credit unions to those allowing investments in mutual funds or even individual stocks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/business/Adviser1/Adviser1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/14/business/Adviser1/Adviser1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/business/Adviser1/Adviser1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/business/Adviser1/Adviser1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping for Investments in a Health Savings Account', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shopping for Investments in a Health Savings Account', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T22:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd959fcc-1ddb-5000-a051-a3f216489c0d', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd959fcc-1ddb-5000-a051-a3f216489c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Previously unissued works by the Beatles, Bob Dylan and others will be released, albeit in very limited editions, to safeguard their European copyright protections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/arts/music/european-copyright-laws-lead-to-rare-music-releases.html', 'snippet': 'Previously unissued works by the Beatles, Bob Dylan and others will be released, albeit in very limited editions, to safeguard their European copyright protections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to a provision in the European Union’s new copyright law, fans of some musicians who made recordings in the 1960s are likely to be treated, for the foreseeable future, to annual batches of previously unissued material. But because artists and record labels are apparently unhappy about being forced to release material they would rather keep in the vaults, collectors need to be quick and alert: So far, the most tantalizing recordings have turned up in limited, hard-to-find editions. And where labels are normally eager to publicize their releases, they are doing their best to keep these ones secret. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Copyright Laws Lead to Rare Music Releases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Copyright Laws Lead to Rare Music Releases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kozinn, Allan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-11T22:12:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NODESK', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3c195bc-e880-5eba-8358-58f371cbdb4a', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3c195bc-e880-5eba-8358-58f371cbdb4a'}, {'abstract': 'On the final day of the Fall North American Championships in Phoenix, the Reisinger Board-a-Match Teams was won by the defending champions, Team Monaco.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/crosswords/bridge/fall-north-american-championships.html', 'snippet': 'On the final day of the Fall North American Championships in Phoenix, the Reisinger Board-a-Match Teams was won by the defending champions, Team Monaco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — On the final day of the Fall North American Championships here on Sunday, the Reisinger Board-a-Match Teams was won by the defending champions, Team Monaco: Pierre Zimmermann, Franck Multon, Fulvio Fantoni, Claudio Nunes, Geir Helgemo and Tor Helness. They finished just over two boards ahead of Norberto Bocchi and Agustin Madala from Italy, Krzysztof Buras and Grzegorz Narkiewicz from Poland, and Aleksander Dubinin and Andrei Gromov from Russia. Third were Martin Fleisher, Chris Willenken and Zia Mahmood of New York City, Michael Kamil of Holmdel, N.J., Michael Rosenberg of Cupertino, Calif., and Chip Martel of Davis, Calif. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/crosswords/bridge/12cards-img/12cards-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 562, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/crosswords/bridge/12cards-img/12cards-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1063, 'width': 583, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/crosswords/bridge/12cards-img/12cards-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/crosswords/bridge/12cards-img/12cards-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'