rd_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c3685834-146b-53be-b924-903b12f5e77f'}, {'abstract': 'Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater presented an eclectic program of works by Paul Taylor, Rennie Harris, Ohad Naharin and Robert Battle at City Center on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/arts/dance/alvin-ailey-american-dance-theater-at-city-center.html', 'snippet': 'Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater presented an eclectic program of works by Paul Taylor, Rennie Harris, Ohad Naharin and Robert Battle at City Center on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For its second week in residence at City Center, Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater reprised the three works that Robert Battle added to the company’s repertory when he became artistic director in 2011. Paul Taylor’s “Arden Court,” Rennie Harris’s “Home” and Ohad Naharin’s “Minus 16” afford a thorough, generous look at three styles: American modern dance, hip-hop and Gaga, the movement form invented by Mr. Naharin, an Israeli choreographer. How can a performer’s presence alter the stage’s canvas? How does subject matter, however veiled, become universal? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staying Aloft in Different Styles (With or Without Dress Suits)', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staying Aloft in Different Styles (With or Without Dress Suits)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Center Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Rennie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Naharin, Ohad', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'val