duce-packed supermarkets, the stockpiling of cabbage speaks to an era of scarcity that still haunts Chinese of a certain age.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/world/asia/as-winter-nears-china-is-blanketed-in-cabbage.html', 'snippet': 'In a city crowded with BMWs, upscale malls and produce-packed supermarkets, the stockpiling of cabbage speaks to an era of scarcity that still haunts Chinese of a certain age.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Sooty skies are not the only reliable indicator that winter has finally descended on the Chinese capital. Vendors selling roasted sweet potatoes occupy street corners with their repurposed oil-drum ovens. To ward off the sniffles, Beijing cabdrivers nibble on cloves of raw garlic, making taxi rides especially trying.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/beijing1/beijing1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/world/beijing1/beijing1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/beijing1/beijing1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/beijing1/beijing1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/beijing1/beijing1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/world/beijing1/beijing1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/beijing1/beijing1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Winter Nears, Chinese Capital Is Blanketed in Green', 'kicker': 'Beijing Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Winter Nears, China Is Blanketed in Green', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stockpiling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cabbage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T01:28:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30f007c8-9cf9-5f2f-ae04-a3113db50b82', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30f007c8-9cf9-5f2f-ae04-a3113db50b82'}, {'abstract': 'A meaningful way to uphold the spirit of Nelson Mandela would be to speak out for human rights and political freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/opinion/kristof-how-to-truly-honor-mandela.html', 'snippet': 'A meaningful way to uphold the spirit of Nelson Mandela would be to speak out for human rights and political freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'World leaders, including President Obama, are jostling for the chance to celebrate Nelson Mandela this week, which would surely make Mandela smile. He had a mischievous sense of humor, and he knew better than anybody that the United States and other countries now embracing him had spurned him when he could have actually used the help.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '39', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarg