 the storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — A former New Orleans police officer who was convicted three years ago in the shooting death of a civilian in the days after Hurricane Katrina, but was granted a retrial on appeal, was acquitted Wednesday on all counts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Officer Is Cleared in Hurricane Katrina Shooting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Officer Cleared in New Orleans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glover, Henry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Katrina (2005)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T02:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9123066b-a8d4-5b11-af05-c2a80b32095f', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9123066b-a8d4-5b11-af05-c2a80b32095f'}, {'abstract': 'Clippers Coach Doc Rivers received a warm welcome from his former players and from Celtics fans in his first game at TD Garden since he left Boston over the summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/sports/basketball/now-with-clippers-rivers-returns-to-boston-as-an-enemy-though-not-a-hated-one.html', 'snippet': 'Clippers Coach Doc Rivers received a warm welcome from his former players and from Celtics fans in his first game at TD Garden since he left Boston over the summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Doc Rivers spent nine years in Boston, a stretch that lasted longer than his playing career in Atlanta and any other stint in his life since his childhood on the South Side of Chicago. He presided over a team that lost a franchise-record 18 consecutive games in 2007 and a team that won an N.B.A. championship a year later.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/Y-RIVERS/Y-RIVERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/Y-RIVERS/Y-RIVERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/Y-RIVERS/Y-RIVERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/Y-RIVERS/Y-RIVERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/Y-RIVERS/Y-RIVERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/sports/Y-RIVERS/Y-RIVERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type