6cc10c3d'}, {'abstract': 'While the world admires Nelson Mandela as a freedom fighter, residents in his hometown, where he will be buried on Sunday, considered him just another villager.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/world/africa/hometown-remembers-madiba-the-villager-well-before-mandela-the-icon.html', 'snippet': 'While the world admires Nelson Mandela as a freedom fighter, residents in his hometown, where he will be buried on Sunday, considered him just another villager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'QUNU, South Africa — Nelson Mandela was on one of his early morning walks here in his rural home village when he spotted an old friend loosening up the soil on his land with a donkey-drawn plow. Mr. Mandela contemplated the sight, and though he was president at the time, he promptly and inexplicably took over.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/qunu1/qunu1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/world/qunu1/qunu1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/qunu1/qunu1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/qunu1/qunu1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/qunu1/qunu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/world/qunu1/qunu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/qunu1/qunu1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hometown Remembers Madiba the Villager, Well Before Mandela the Icon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hometown Remembers Madiba the Villager, Well Before Mandela the Icon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mandela, Nelson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qunu (South Africa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T02:36:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c75dc58e-1579-562d-bb20-ae958783ca09', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c75dc58e-1579-562d-bb20-ae958783ca09'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the gains made in curbing AIDS, tuberculosis and malaria, there is still a big gap between what’s been accomplished and what more could be done.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/opinion/the-toll-from-three-deadly-diseases.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the gains made in curbing AIDS, tuberculosis and malaria, there is still a big gap between what’s been accomplished and what more could be done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'International health agencies at the United Nations have documented enormous gains made over the past decade to curb three devastating diseases: AIDS, tuberculosis and malaria. Despite this great progress, there is still a big gap between what’s been accomplished and what more could be done with sufficient financing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Toll From Three Deadly Diseases', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Toll From Three Deadly Diseases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuberculosis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T02:40:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/63c582d9-56e3-562a-b9f9-010fb5696b1e', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63c582d9-56e3-562a-b9f9-010fb5696b1e'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Fox in Oneonta, N.Y., was still trying to figure out on Wednesday how its charges came to be so seriously underreported to the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/nyregion/bargain-basement-prices-at-a-new-york-hospital-prove-too-good-to-be-true.html', 'snippet': 'A. O. Fox in Oneonta, N.Y., was still trying to figure out on Wednesday how its charges came to be so seriously underreported to the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Knee joint replacements at one-tenth the next cheapest price statewide! Baby deliveries below what they cost the hospital! At such discounts, one could imagine New Yorkers trekking three hours from Times Square to a small upstate hospital to fix an aching joint or to give birth, considering that some Americans fly overseas for surgery to escape high costs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bargain-Basement Prices at a New York Hospital Prove Too Good to Be True', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bargain Basement Prices at a Hospital Prove Too Good to Be True', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'A O Fox Memorial Hospital', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Nina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health Department (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oneonta (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T02:41:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba3e0997-66f9-52a6-9462-44ec9dfc09ca', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba3e0997-66f9-52a6-9462-44ec9dfc09ca'}, {'abstract': 'The Indian Supreme Court issued a disgraceful ruling against human rights in upholding a law that bans gay sex.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/opinion/indias-reversal-on-gay-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The Indian Supreme Court issued a disgraceful ruling against human rights in upholding a law that bans gay sex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India’s Supreme Court issued a disgraceful ruling against human rights in reinstating a law that bans gay sex. On Wednesday, the court reversed a landmark 2009 decision by the Delhi High Court that decriminalized sex between consenting adults regardless of their gender. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Reversal on Gay Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India’s Reversal on Gay Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court of India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Manmohan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T02:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba1b1d38-1468-54ca-a6ff-2f1ae77cba18', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba1b1d38-1468-54ca-a6ff-2f1ae77cba18'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats are able to reduce the sequester, but Republican-imposed austerity still dominates Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/opinion/the-minimalist-budget-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats are able to reduce the sequester, but Republican-imposed austerity still dominates Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most of this year, the brutal cuts to federal spending known as the sequester have wreaked havoc on important programs, cutting off hundreds of thousands from Head Start and low-income housing assistance, setting back scientific research and environmental protection, and costing more than a million jobs. Getting rid of the sequester for domestic programs was a high priority for Congressional Democrats, and they achieved much of what they wanted in a budget deal reached on Tuesday that in other important respects was disappointing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Minimalist Budget Deal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Minimalist Budget Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Patty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T02:46:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/19956cab-80ee-595e-abe5-ca4e026869b9', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19956cab-80ee-595e-abe5-ca4e026869b9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Bihari created Modern Music Records with his two brothers, Jules and Saul, recording B.B. King, Etta James, John Lee Hooker and other blues legends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/arts/music/joe-bihari-who-put-early-rb-on-record-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Bihari created Modern Music Records with his two brothers, Jules and Saul, recording B.B. King, Etta James, John Lee Hooker and other blues legends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after the Bihari brothers started leasing jukeboxes in black neighborhoods of Los Angeles in the early 1940s, they realized they had a problem. While their business had a solid distribution network of stores, bars and restaurants, they could not find enough records to play in their machines.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/BIHARI-obit/BIHARI-obit-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/BIHARI-obit/BIHARI-obit-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 578}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/BIHARI-obit/BIHARI-obit-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 987, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/BIHARI-obit/BIHARI-obit-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1471, 'width': 1526, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/BIHARI-obit/BIHARI-obit-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name