n studio Grain, a dish stamped with symbols to inspire conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stamped with symbols representing life experiences (a mountain, a torn heart and a pizza slice, to name just a few), Grail, a cassoulet dish from the design firm Grain, is intended to inspire mealtime conversation. “We used contemporary icons of things you would encounter in the city, traveling or online, but applied them to a more timeless piece, almost like Egyptian hieroglyphs,” said James Minola, who founded the Bainbridge Island, Wash., company with his wife, Chelsea. “We imagine people sitting around it at a table; maybe one of these icons speaks to you and reminds you of a story to share.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12GOODS_SPAN/12CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12GOODS_SPAN/12CURR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12GOODS_SPAN/12CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12GOODS_SPAN/12CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12GOODS_SPAN/12CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12GOODS_SPAN/12CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12GOODS_SPAN/12CURR1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pass the Cassoulet ... And the Memories', 'kicker': 'Currents | Goods', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pass the Cassoulet ... And the Memories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeough, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minola, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T04:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/701153a6-66ee-5be9-a590-621754838f8b', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/701153a6-66ee-5be9-a590-621754838f8b'}, {'abstract': 'Christie’s is showing drawings, prototypes and production pieces from the Italian designer’s own collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/garden/rare-gems-from-ettore-sottsass.html', 'snippet': 'Christie’s is showing drawings, prototypes and production pieces from the Italian designer’s own collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ettore Sottsass designed furniture, ceramics, dishware, jewelry, fashion boutiques, an apartment for Gianni Agnelli and, perhaps most famously, the red Valentine typewriter for Olivetti. This Austrian-born, Milan-based architect and designer also led a Zelig-like social life, founding the influential Memphis group and becoming friends with a diverse coterie that included Allen Ginsberg, Helmut Newton and Karl Lagerfeld.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12EVENTS_SPAN/12EVENTS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12EVENTS_SPAN/12EVENTS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12EVENTS_SPAN/12EVENTS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12EVENTS_SPAN/12EVENTS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12EVENTS_SPAN/12EVENTS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12EVENTS_SPAN/12EVENTS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12EVENTS_SPAN/12EVENTS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Gems from Ettore Sottsass', 'kicker': 'Currents | Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Designer’s Rare Gems Up for Sale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sottsass, Ettore Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T04:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6015b970-54a0-5a57-b716-e0ba4c05973d', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6015b970-54a0-5a57-b716-e0ba4c05973d'}, {'abstract': 'From Trove, a wallpaper inspired by a road trip through Yellowstone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/garden/stopping-by-the-woods-at-dusk-or-dawn.html', 'snippet': 'From Trove, a wallpaper inspired by a road trip through Yellowstone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wallpaper company Trove’s latest pattern, called Trace, was inspired by a summer road trip through Yellowstone. “There had been a fire, and as we drove through we saw many stages of the forest, in growth but also in death,” said Jee Levin, a founder of Trove with Randall Buck. The couple, who were introducing their 7-year-old son, Sebastian, to the park, photographed trees that were rugged and imperfect. Back in New York, they designed what Ms. Levin called “our own forest.” The result is a romantic image of a silhouetted woods at dusk sitting above its hand-drawn mirror image. Flip the piece and it looks like a forest at dawn. Trace is one of three patterns in Trove’s winter collection, which will be formally released next month. It is 12 feet high with a 67-inch-wide repeat, and is $16 a square foot. Information: 212-268-2046 or troveline.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12WALLS/12CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12WALLS/12CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 592}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12WALLS/12CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1010, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12WALLS/12CURR4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2019, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12WALLS/12CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12WALLS/12CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12WALLS/12CURR4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stopping by the Woods at Dusk (or Dawn)', 'kicker': 'Currents | Walls', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stopping by Woods At Dusk (or Dawn)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suqi, Rima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wallpaper', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T04:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50cc39a9-8973-531b-be85-a02608ac09da', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50cc39a9-8973-531b-be85-a02608ac09da'}, {'abstract': 'Residents had expressed dismay at the plans, saying that they had not been properly notified and feared crowds and delinquency in their neighborhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/nyregion/new-york-city-backs-off-moving-court-to-tribeca.html', 'snippet': 'Residents had expressed dismay at the plans, saying that they had not been properly notified and feared crowds and delinquency in their neighborhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After an uproar and a lawsuit by TriBeCa residents, New York City agreed in a settlement to withdraw plans to move a criminal summons court there, the plaintiffs announced Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Backs Off Moving Court to TriBeCa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Backs Off Moving Court To TriBeCa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagenknecht, Lynn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T04:05:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9372a0c4-7b12-5523-85fb-6acedcdf4f84', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9372a0c4-7b12-5523-85fb-6acedcdf4f84'}, {'abstract': 'Les Indiennes sells Indian cotton textiles at bargain prices at a new shop in Hudson, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/garden/fabrics-put-through-the-wringer.html', 'snippet': 'Les Indiennes sells Indian cotton textiles at bargain prices at a new shop in Hudson, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2000, Mary Bergtold Mulcahy has been designing block-printed organic cottons with Srinivas Pitchuka, a textile artisan in India. Working in a tradition called kalamkari, Mr. Pitchuka bleaches the textiles in the sun, washes them in the river, beats them against stones to make them soft and boils them. Then he prints them with vegetable dyes. Last month, Ms. Mulcahy opened Les Indiennes, a shop in Hudson, N.Y., that sells the fabric as quilts, pillow covers, tablecloths and yardage, along with miscellaneous home accessories. Most of the items cost up to 70 percent less than the same goods sold online or through other retailers. Eighteen-inch-square pillow covers are $25. Painted eggshell ornaments from the Czech Republic are $5 each. Les Indiennes is at 444 Warren Street, Hudson, N.Y. Information: 518-828-2811 or lesindiennes.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12OPEN_SPAN/12OPEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12OPEN_SPAN/12OPEN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12OPEN_SPAN/12OPEN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12OPEN_SPAN/12OPEN_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12OPEN_SPAN/12OPEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12OPEN_SPAN/12OPEN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12OPEN_SPAN/12OPEN_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fabrics Put Through the Wringer', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fabrics Put Through the Wringer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louie, Elaine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulcahy, Mary Bergtold', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T04:06:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8b738bd-2787-56c6-9fba-cd4c286e2554', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8b738bd-2787-56c6-9fba-cd4c286e2554'}, {'abstract': 'With the right instruments, housekeeping can be quick and almost, well, fun. (Almost.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/garden/with-a-whoosh-and-a-zoom-cleaning-tools.html', 'snippet': 'With the right instruments, housekeeping can be quick and almost, well, fun. (Almost.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'To some, cleaning house means making a casual tour with the vacuum and taking a few jabs at the toilet with a soapy brush. Not Sabrina Fierman. As vice president of New York’s Little Elves, a cleaning firm used by many designers and contractors, she takes the job to a level that would satisfy the most obsessive germaphobe.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12SHOP_395/12SHOP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12SHOP_395/12SHOP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12SHOP_395/12SHOP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12SHOP_395/12SHOP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12SHOP_395/12SHOP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12SHOP_395/12SHOP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12SHOP_395/12SHOP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With a Whoosh and a Zoom: Cleaning Tools', 'kicker': 'Shopping With Sabrina Fierman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whoosh, Zoom!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vacuum Cleaners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleaning Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "New York's Little Elves Inc", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleansers, Detergents and Soaps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T04:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6970b7b-adcc-5b54-8177-8faee5fbad76', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6970b7b-adcc-5b54-8177-8faee5fbad76'}, {'abstract': 'Allan Shulman on his new Miami Center for Architecture and Design and the rapidly changing city it occupies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/garden/embracing-miamis-past-and-future.html', 'snippet': 'Allan Shulman on his new Miami Center for Architecture and Design and the rapidly changing city it occupies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Allan Shulman, the 51-year-old principal of the architectural firm Shulman & Associates in Miami, first became known for historic preservation. He rescued the 1915 Browns Hotel on lower Ocean Drive, which was built of pine. And he found a way to save much of the Art Deco Lincoln Theater on Lincoln Road, turning it into a stylish glass-walled H & M store. His new, 5,000-square-foot Miami Center for Architecture and Design (known as MCAD) opened last Friday in part of the 1912 main Miami Post Office, on Northeast First Avenue, in Downtown Miami. Over the years, the building had suffered much indignity, including a spell as an Office Depot. Now, as the new headquarters of the American Institute of Architects Miami chapter, it will be a place for free community events as well as professional gatherings. Speaking by phone from his office in the Miami Design District, Mr. Shulman, president of the Miami chapter, offered details about MCAD and opinions on the city’s building scene. (The interview has been edited and condensed.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12QNA3_SPAN/12QNA3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12QNA3_SPAN/12QNA3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12QNA3_SPAN/12QNA3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12QNA3_SPAN/12QNA3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/garden/12QNA3_SPAN/12QNA3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legac