s/broader-approach-urged-to-reduce-gun-violence.html', 'snippet': 'The most effective way to reduce gun violence without significantly curtailing Second Amendment rights is to treat the problem as a public health issue, like smoking or drunken driving, a study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most effective way to reduce gun violence without significantly curtailing Second Amendment rights is to treat the problem as a public health issue, like smoking or drunken driving, rather trying to profile potential shooters, according to a report released Thursday by a panel of experts who were commissioned by the American Psychological Association to study the issue in the wake of the Newtown, Conn., massacre. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broader Approach Urged to Reduce Gun Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broader Approach Urged To Reduce Gun Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Benedict', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN PSYCHOLOGICAL ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornell, Dewey G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T05:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/451a714e-f57d-5142-94be-8151a1bc1bc1', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/451a714e-f57d-5142-94be-8151a1bc1bc1'}, {'abstract': 'The rowhouse in Park Slope, Brooklyn, that Mayor-elect Bill de Blasio is leaving and Gracie Mansion, the Upper East Sid