ne, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12253ae7-5bae-50c5-bce5-a62c0260136f', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12253ae7-5bae-50c5-bce5-a62c0260136f'}, {'abstract': 'In the last month, the Rangers and the Knicks have combined for 12 losses in 15 home games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/sports/the-l-train-has-been-rerouted-to-the-garden.html', 'snippet': 'In the last month, the Rangers and the Knicks have combined for 12 losses in 15 home games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost without exception, this has been a bad year for the New York area’s major sports teams. Even the Yankees tumbled. But nothing can quite compare with the almost daily misery being inflicted on fans who show up at Madison Square Garden. In the last month, the Rangers and the Knicks have combined for 12 losses in 15 home games.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The L Train Has Been Rerouted to the Garden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The L Train Has Been Rerouted to the Garden ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T05:53:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a136f386-88cf-5598-b382-b8520a3b2a29', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a136f386-88cf-5598-b382-b8520a3b2a29'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:30 A.M. (Starz) TO ROME WITH LOVE (2012) In Woody Allen’s tribute to the Italian cinema of the 1950s and ’60s, a retired and overly psychoanalyzed music promoter (Mr. Allen) travels with his wife (Judy Davis) to Rome, where their daughter (Alison Pill) has lost her heart to a lawyer devoted to left-wing causes (Flavio Parenti). Meanwhile, in this shuffled anthology, a young newlywed loses her way to the Trevi Fountain and falls into the arms of a movie star while her befuddled husband tries to keep his relatives in the dark, substituting a prostitute (Penélope Cruz) for her at dinner. An ordinary Roman (Roberto Benigni) is plunged into a swirl of media celebrity. And a fledgling architect (Jesse Eisenberg) finds his relationship with his kind, if bland, girlfriend (Greta Gerwig) in shreds when her neurotic actress friend visits. Alec Baldwin plays the older architect — a ghost? a specter of the younger man’s self? — who witnesses the ordeal. “One of the most delightful things about ‘To Rome With Love’ is how casually it blends the plausible and the surreal, and how unabashedly it revels in pure silliness,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. The movie’s limitations, “as frothy as the milk atop a cappuccino, are finally inseparable from its delights.” Complaining, he added, “would be as superfluous — though also, perhaps, as inevitable — as psychoanalysis.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/17969c0a-8d66-55ba-80e1-10656842e05a', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17969c0a-8d66-55ba-80e1-10656842e05a'}, {'abstract': 'As winter’s chill sets in, those living in the Malakpur refugee camp insist they can’t leave without monetary relief, while the Uttar Pradesh government insists they can.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/after-muzaffarnagar-riots-a-standoff-over-government-compensation/', 'snippet': 'As winter’s chill sets in, those living in the Malakpur refugee camp insist they can’t leave without monetary relief, while the Uttar Pradesh government insists they can.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHAMLI, Uttar Pradesh—On a sunny winter afternoon last week, 12-year-old Gulbaar drifted among the dusty pile of rocks that marked the graves of infants and children in a cemetery close to the camp called Malakpur. The camp houses more than 7,000 Muslims who have taken refuge here since violence broke out three months ago between Muslims and the Jat clan of the Hindus in the nearby districts of Shamli and Muzaffarnagar in the northern state of Uttar Pradesh.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/asia/12-Mala-IndiaInk/12-Mala-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/world/asia/12-Mala-IndiaInk/12-Mala-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/asia/12-Mala-IndiaInk/12-Mala-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', '