esk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish, John Eligon and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d31ce48-0747-5aa6-9b4c-a0e00cb8a109', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d31ce48-0747-5aa6-9b4c-a0e00cb8a109'}, {'abstract': 'JPMorgan Chase is nearing settlements over its ties to Bernard L. Madoff. | Hilton Worldwide is set to have its stock market debut. | A skeptical view of the Treasury secretary’s reassurances on “too big to fail.” | Facebook is joining the Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/morning-agenda-jpmorgan-nears-settlement-of-madoff-case/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan Chase is nearing settlements over its ties to Bernard L. Madoff. | Hilton Worldwide is set to have its stock market debut. | A skeptical view of the Treasury secretary’s reassurances on “too big to fail.” | Facebook is joining the Standar...', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase is nearing settlements with federal authorities over its ties to Bernard L. Madoff, reaching tentative deals that would involve roughly $2 billion in penalties and a rare criminal action, Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Ben Protess report in DealBook. The government plans to use a sizable portion of the money to compensate Mr. Madoff’s victims, according to DealBook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Nears Settlement in Madoff Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T12:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56203772-4b3e-5a54-8a09-c916529e20c2', 'word_count': 1823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56203772-4b3e-5a54-8a09-c916529e20c2'}, {'abstract': 'The Delhi High Court ruled that Nokia would be allowed to transfer a phone factory to Microsoft, even though the plant was seized because of a tax dispute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/business/international/indian-court-removes-obstacle-to-microsoft-nokia-merger.html', 'snippet': 'The Delhi High Court ruled that Nokia would be allowed to transfer a phone factory to Microsoft, even though the plant was seized because of a tax dispute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI, India — The Delhi High Court ruled on Thursday that Nokia would be allowed to transfer a phone factory to Microsoft, clearing a major obstacle to Nokia’s $7.4 billion sale of its mobile phone business to Microsoft after the court ordered Nokia to set aside $365 million for potential tax liabilities.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/Nokia/Nokia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/business/Nokia/Nokia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/Nokia/Nokia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/Nokia/Nokia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/Nokia/Nokia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/business/Nokia/Nokia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/Nokia/Nokia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Court Lifts Obstacle to Microsoft-Nokia Merger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Court Lifts Obstacle To Microsoft-Nokia Merger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T12:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani Bagri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': 'Thirani', 'lastname': 'Bagri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dedf2353-2d4c-5828-b26d-caa11f77c4a1', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dedf2353-2d4c-5828-b26d-caa11f77c4a1'}, {'abstract': 'By studying how we and other species make vitamins, scientists hope to find new ways to keep us healthy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/science/learning-from-the-history-of-vitamins.html', 'snippet': 'By studying how we and other species make vitamins, scientists hope to find new ways to keep us healthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our health depends on vitamins, and to understand that dependency, it helps to understand the history of vitamins. As I wrote in an article in Science Times this week, our ancestors have probably needed vitamins for billions of years. By studying how we and other species make vitamins, scientists hope to find new ways to keep us healthy — perhaps even by using vitamins as a weapon against our enemies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/science/12zimmer/12zimmer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/science/12zimmer/12zimmer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/science/12zimmer/12zimmer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/science/12zimmer/12zimmer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1186, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/science/12zimmer/12zimmer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/science/12zimmer/12zimmer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/science/12zimmer/12zimmer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Learning From the History of Vitamins', 'kicker': 'Matter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89e8ba94-fd35-5ff2-8e61-84f7db37716e', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89e8ba94-fd35-5ff2-8e61-84f7db37716e'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers approved the bipartisan budget bill and stronger Pentagon protections for sexual assault victims, but could pass only a one-month extension of the current law involving the farm bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/us/politics/house-budget-vote.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers approved the bipartisan budget bill and stronger Pentagon protections for sexual assault victims, but could pass only a one-month extension of the current law involving the farm bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The House on Thursday approved a bipartisan budget accord and a Pentagon policy bill that would strengthen protections for victims of sexual assault. But as it wrapped up its business for the year, it left unfinished a major piece of domestic policy — the farm bill — making it likely that Congress will not deal with it until January.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/CONG/CONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/us/CONG/CONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/CONG/CONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/CONG/CONG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/CONG/CONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/us/CONG/CONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/CONG/CONG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'House Passes Budget Pact and Military Abuse Protections, but Not Farm Bill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Passes Budget Pact and Military Abuse Protections, but Not Farm Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Patty', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T13:24:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman and Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a683ac70-09cb-5395-9a57-ddebdb252a3c', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a683ac70-09cb-5395-9a57-ddebdb252a3c'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A woman outside a pet shop told her bulldog that it was too early to play with the shop’s cat.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/play-dates-for-pets/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A woman outside a pet shop told her bulldog that it was too early to play with the shop’s cat.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Play Dates for Pets', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T13:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Fleischmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fleischmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3740f6d6-af69-588e-9eff-ffa90b5b9f66', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3740f6d6-af69-588e-9eff-ffa90b5b9f66'}, {'abstract': 'Three destructive years.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/unprecedented-austerity/', 'snippet': 'Three destructive years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As many people have noted, a strange thing has happened on the fiscal policy front. Intellectually, the case for austerity has pretty much collapsed, having been reduced at this point to the Three Stooges Theory: we’re supposed to consider austerity a success because it feels good when you stop, or at least let up. At the same time, however, austerity policies continue to be imposed, on both sides of the Atlantic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unprecedented Austerity', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T13:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c2347bb-9229-554e-8559-017f965a72af', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c2347bb-9229-554e-8559-017f965a72af'}, {'abstract': 'Video snapshots.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/concert-memories-personal/', 'snippet': 'Video snapshots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since I burbled on about how great last weekend’s Lucius concert was, I thought I’d give the curious a couple of links to videos that have since been posted. Here’s Turn it Around, and here’s the John Lennon finale in the audience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Concert Memories (Personal)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T13:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65653127-5e31-54ef-a500-726ca4d0f26e', 'word_count': 42, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65653127-5e31-54ef-a500-726ca4d0f26e'}, {'abstract': 'Financial experts evaluated measures to combat money laundering and concluded that a wide range of measures had been taken by the Holy See to remedy numerous deficiencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/world/europe/european-report-says-vatican-makes-progress-in-policing-its-bank.html', 'snippet': 'Financial experts evaluated measures to combat money laundering and concluded that a wide range of measures had been taken by the Holy See to remedy numerous deficiencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — The Vatican has made significant efforts to comply with international controls to combat terrorism financing and money laundering, but 