olden Globes. It was nominated for best drama and best supporting actor, for Daniel Brühl, who beat out contenders like Jonah Hill in “The Wolf of Wall Street.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/bagger-howard/bagger-howard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/bagger-howard/bagger-howard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/bagger-howard/bagger-howard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/bagger-howard/bagger-howard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/bagger-howard/bagger-howard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/bagger-howard/bagger-howard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/arts/bagger-howard/bagger-howard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ron Howard on His Nerve-Racking Season', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruhl, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemsworth, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauda, Nikki', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood Foreign Press Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T16:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/536aeb8d-a16d-5a2a-ba35-7de6b93f7653', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/536aeb8d-a16d-5a2a-ba35-7de6b93f7653'}, {'abstract': 'How can art deepen the travel experience? Following the trail of artists ranging from Dalí to Vermeer reveals some answers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/travel/drawing-yourself-into-the-scene.html', 'snippet': 'How can art deepen the travel experience? Following the trail of artists ranging from Dalí to Vermeer reveals some answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a sunny Saturday in early fall, a small group gathered for a Surrealist show at Cap de Creus, the craggy easternmost point of Spain where the artist Salvador Dalí had lived. The performers were wearing carnival-type costumes with black lace tutus and gold lamé gloves and were playing guitars and drums. They scrambled across the rocks and those of us in the audience followed — as much participants in the spectacle as viewers of it. When we arrived at a large and particularly oddly shaped outcropping, we were given paper and pens and asked to draw what we saw.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':