'Renoir, Pierre Auguste', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dali, Salvador', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delft (Netherlands)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vermeer, Jan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Costa Brava (Spain)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'British Columbia (Canada)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T16:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Negroni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Negroni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/474df25c-c3c3-59c0-857e-a90f8a9cfb62', 'word_count': 1947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/474df25c-c3c3-59c0-857e-a90f8a9cfb62'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s scheme for bringing the Confederate states back into the Union was savvier than his critics allow.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/the-radicalism-of-lincolns-10-percent-plan/', 'snippet': 'The president’s scheme for bringing the Confederate states back into the Union was savvier than his critics allow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scores of students have been taught that Abraham Lincoln’s Proclamation of Amnesty and Reconstruction, appended to the presidential message to Congress of December 1863, offered rebels an easy way to get back into his good graces: as soon as they took an oath of loyalty to the Union and promised to support emancipation, he would pardon them and return their confiscated property (except for emancipated slaves, of course). Moreover, as soon as 10 percent of the 1860 electorate in any rebel state had taken the oath, he would permit that 10 percent to commence home rule and elect state officials. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Radicalism of Lincoln’s 10 Percent Plan', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reconstruction Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T16:46:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Striner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Striner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e96779d-a9db-5300-913c-eca572598a79', 'word_count': 1371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e96779d-a9db-5300-913c-eca572598a79'}, {'abstract': 'Is it a big deal?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/tpp/', 'snippet': 'Is it a big deal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been getting a fair bit of correspondence wondering why I haven’t written about the negotiations for a Trans Pacific Partnership, which many of my correspondents and commenters regard as something both immense and sinister.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TPP', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T16:48:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Kr