s named professorship, no N.I.H. grant and no plum administrative position in the hospital’s hierarchy. But to the other surgeons-in-training and me, he was exactly who we wanted to be. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/health/13well_surgery/13well_surgery-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/health/13well_surgery/13well_surgery-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 460}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/health/13well_surgery/13well_surgery-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/health/13well_surgery/13well_surgery-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/health/13well_surgery/13well_surgery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/health/13well_surgery/13well_surgery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/health/13well_surgery/13well_surgery-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Today’s New Surgeons Unprepared?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T17:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da1f618e-5003-5d31-a67e-557f780ca5a4', 'word_count': 1306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da1f618e-5003-5d31-a67e-557f780ca5a4'}, {'abstract': 'Guest blogger Lizzie Presser looks at what is fueling massive demonstrations in Thailand, and why we should be hopeful about the outcome.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/what-is-really-at-stake-in-the-thai-protests/', 'snippet': 'Guest blogger Lizzie Presser looks at what is fueling massive demonstrations in Thailand, and why we should be hopeful about the outcome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a trim garden outside her pink plaster house, 62-year-old Amnuay Warayot recounted her past life. Before moving here, she lived in a slum by the trains, where electricity and water were hard to come by and the wooden homes were no match for the northeast Thai rainy season. The man who gave her all this, she tells me, has won over her heart. His name is Thaksin Shinawatra, and he’s the former prime minister.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What is Really at Stake in the Thai Protests', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T17:22:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizzie Presser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizzie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Presser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2693116-c4ac-524d-8668-2ccba176d766', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2693116-c4ac-524d-8668-2ccba176d766'}, {'abstract': 'Movies like “Nebraska,” “Gravity” and “The Wolf of Wall Street” express a creeping sense of powerlessness in modern society.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/movies/stephen-holdens-top-films-of-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Movies like “Nebraska,” “Gravity” and “The Wolf of Wall Street” express a creeping sense of powerlessness in modern society.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Generalized anxiety.” That is by far the most common complaint voiced by the clients of a prominent New York psychiatrist whom I recently asked to identify the malaise of the moment. As much as that term evokes a sense of foreboding behind the glittering facade of Manhattan, it also describes the wary, embattled tone of world cinema in 2013. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15HOLDEN2/15HOLDEN2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15HOLDEN2/15HOLDEN2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15HOLDEN2/15HOLDEN2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15HOLDEN2/15HOLDEN2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': 