efense firm Richards, Kibbe & Orbe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David B. Massey, a federal prosecutor who played a significant role in government’s sweeping investigation into insider trading in the hedge fund industry, is joining the white-collar defense firm Richards Kibbe & Orbe. He becomes the latest government lawyer to move into private practice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutor Who Oversaw Swiss Bank Case Moves to Private Practice', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T17:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATTHEW GOLDSTEIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'GOLDSTEIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eb782cf-129d-5a9c-9842-5a05a7273d86', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eb782cf-129d-5a9c-9842-5a05a7273d86'}, {'abstract': 'A bracket-style competition allows fans to vote on the top moments in U.S. Soccer’s 100-year history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/sports/soccer/best-of-us-soccer-centennial-edition.html', 'snippet': 'A bracket-style competition allows fans to vote on the top moments in U.S. Soccer’s 100-year history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brandi Chastain’s penalty kick (and celebration) at the Women’s World Cup in 1999? The United States victory over England in the 1950 World Cup? The 2-0 win against Mexico at the 2002 World Cup? The 1994 World Cup hosted by the United States?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/sports/soccer/13usa1/13usa1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cro