lt Brecht — a genius of 20th-century theater, yes, but often about as much fun as a doctor’s visit in production — provided more giddy fun than most Broadway musicals. The idea of listening in on eight hours of a phone conversation could hardly sound more tedious, but the show derived from that very source was among the most inspired and imaginative I saw this year. Herewith, in alphabetical order, are the shows that gave me the most pleasure, often by catching me off guard.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Brecht to Jukebox Musicals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Brecht to Jukebox Musicals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T18:04:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1954e8cc-40d7-5427-a4ae-ac29e66c8135', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1954e8cc-40d7-5427-a4ae-ac29e66c8135'}, {'abstract': 'Photos of “The Glass Menagerie,” “Buyer & Cellar” and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/12/15/theater/20131215-BRANTLEY.html', 'snippet': 'Photos of “The Glass Menagerie,” “Buyer & Cellar” and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos of “The Glass Menagerie,” “Buyer & Cellar” and more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/theater/20131215-BRANTLEY-slide-TM1A/20131215-BRANTLEY-slide-TM1A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name':