sed for its new season. (And don’t forget the flood of water.)', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/park-avenue-armory-goes-immersive-in-new-season/', 'snippet': '“Rain and mud and blood and sword play” the armory’s president promised for its new season. (And don’t forget the flood of water.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continuing to push the envelope on what constitutes an arts experience, the Park Avenue Armory will fill its sprawling, 55,000-square-foot Drill Hall with a water installation and present the indie British pop band, the XX, as part of its new season beginning March 19, the armory announced on Thursday. The season will also include a recital series in the armory’s recently renovated Board of Officers Room, so that audiences experience chamber music in a salon setting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Park Avenue Armory Goes Immersive in New Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMORIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Manchester International Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashford, Rob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branagh, Kenneth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Douglas (1966- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimaud, Helene', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ravel, Maurice Joseph', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robertson, Rebecca', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schubert, Franz', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'xx', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manchester (England)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T18:09:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c4cbea0-a1fa-56ee-8e6d-4050ef6d6483', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c4cbea0-a1fa-56ee-8e6d-4050ef6d6483'}, {'abstract': 'A psychologist who has done extensive research on why women tend to avoid careers in math and science.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/opinion/q-a-with-carol-s-dweck.html', 'snippet': 'A psychologist who has done extensive research on why women tend to avoid careers in math and science.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carol S. Dweck, a psychologist at Stanford University, has done extensive research on why women tend to avoid careers in math and science. Her work has shown that women and girls who think that science and math ability are innate tend to perform worse and have less interest in those fields than females who believe that those skills can be acquired through hard work. As she describes the distinction, one is a “gift” mindset and the other a “growth” mindset.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/opinion/carol-dweck/carol-dweck-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/12/opinion/carol-dweck/carol-dweck-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/opinion/carol-dweck/carol-dweck-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/opinion/carol-dweck/carol-dweck-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/opinion/carol-dweck/carol-dweck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/12/opinion/carol-dweck/carol-dweck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/opinion/carol-dweck/carol-dweck-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. & A. With Carol S. Dweck', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T18:13:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '