s. Not the actual South Seas, like Tahiti or Tonga, but to bars and restaurants in and around New York City with fake palm trees, lighted puffer fish, pu pu platters, waterfalls and sweet drinks with umbrellas in them. Not to mention giant tiki heads.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brrrr! Let’s Drive to the South Seas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brrrr! Let’s Drive to the South Seas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stapinski, Helene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fresh Meadows (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Port Richmond (Staten Island, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T22:36:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Stapinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stapinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e62622f0-1b5b-551b-8d00-8dfea04f0844', 'word_count': 1833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e62622f0-1b5b-551b-8d00-8dfea04f0844'}, {'abstract': 'A trip on the A train to Upper Manhattan can take you back over 200 years to the world of founding fathers and Manhattan farmers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/nyregion/manhattan-day-trip-to-the-nations-start.html', 'snippet': 'A trip on the A train to Upper Manhattan can take you back over 200 years to the world of founding fathers and Manhattan farmers.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Forty Part Motet,” Janet Cardiff’s moving sound installation, might have been one of the most popular draws north of the Museum Mile this fall, but the Cloisters, where the show ended last weekend, is not the only stellar attraction in Upper Manhattan. There are three often-overlooked historic homes there where you can stretch your legs and your imagination for a high-flying ride through war, sex scandals and a shooting from over two centuries ago.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN/13REVOLUTIONARY-1_SPAN-thumbS