r': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Huan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Wei', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T22:55:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/724a5794-a235-5eaf-8586-54d57e59a4aa', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/724a5794-a235-5eaf-8586-54d57e59a4aa'}, {'abstract': 'Howard Waldrop’s “Horse of a Different Color” and Catherynne M. Valente’s “The Bread We Eat in Dreams” are short-story collections that season pop-cultural myth with literary bite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/books/stories-by-howard-waldrop-and-catherynne-m-valente.html', 'snippet': 'Howard Waldrop’s “Horse of a Different Color” and Catherynne M. Valente’s “The Bread We Eat in Dreams” are short-story collections that season pop-cultural myth with literary bite.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Fantasy is my heart and love,” the poet and fiction writer Catherynne M. Valente once said in an interview. “And I just want to play in that garden for the rest of my life.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 307}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 524, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN/13BOOKWALDROP_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Light (and Short) Fantastic Told', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Light (and Short) Fantastic Told', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valente, Catherynne M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldrop, Howard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T22:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dana Jennings', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jennings', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8de48310-9040-5c24-a688-98c10d4b329b', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8de48310-9040-5c24-a688-98c10d4b329b'}, {'abstract': '“Brancusi in New York 1913 — 2013” and “Arman the Collector: The Artist’s Collection of African Art” showcase tribal art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/arts/design/arman-the-collector-and-brancusi-celebrate-artifacts.html', 'snippet': '“Brancusi in New York 1913 — 2013” and “Arman the Collector: The Artist’s Collection of African Art” showcase tribal art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is it about African tribal art that so allures us denizens of the modern, industrialized world? I wonder this whenever I encounter tribal artifacts in museums and galleries, and I’m prompted to again by two exhibitions presented by Paul Kasmin Gallery in Chelsea. In Kasmin’s 10th Avenue gallery, there’s “Arman the Collector: The Artist’s Collection of African Art,” a stunning presentation of works collected by the artist known for accumulating many similar objects into absurdist sculptures. Then, around the corner, in Kasmin’s West 27th Street gallery, there’s “Brancusi in New York 1913 – 2013,” a glowing display of five polished bronze works celebrating the 100th anniversary of Constantin Brancusi’s participation in the New York Armory show of 1913.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13KASMIN4_SPAN/13KASMIN4_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 306, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13KASMIN4_SPAN/13KASMIN4_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 306}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13KASMIN4_SPAN/13KASMIN4_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13KASMIN4_SPAN/13KASMIN4_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1045, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13KASMIN4_SPAN/13KASMIN4_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13KASMIN4_SPAN/13KASMIN4_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/arts/13KASMIN4_SPAN/13KASMIN4_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tension Between the Sacred and the Profane', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tension Between the Sacred and the Profane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brancusi, Constantin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arman (1928-2013)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T22:59:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdff6a69-4309-5c67-bc30-fce16b7291ca', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdff6a69-4309-5c67-bc30-fce16b7291ca'}, {'abstract': 'Wine suggestions for several possible types of holiday gatherings, from romantic dinners for two to football takeout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/dining/a-cellar-for-any-situation-any-price.html', 'snippet': 'Wine suggestions for several possible types of holiday gatherings, from romantic dinners for two to football takeout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You don’t need me to remind you the holidays are here (as if you could forget). While it’s easy to bemoan the crass commercialization and artifice, it’s also easy to overlook the opportunities for all sorts of gatherings and the real joys that come with them. Let’s just stipulate that in the hierarchy of pleasures, people come first. Now that we agree on that, good food and drink can help make any party better. Here are some suggestions for several possible types of gatherings. The suggestions are not rigid: if you see something you like better in another, go for it. Above all, these should be gifts to yourself.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/dining/18POUR_SPAN/18POUR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 517, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/18/dining/18POUR_SPAN/18POUR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 517}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/dining/18POUR_SPAN/18POUR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/dining/18POUR_SPAN/18POUR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1763, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur