https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/arts/design/museum-and-gallery-listings-for-dec-13-19.html', 'snippet': 'A critical guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Museums and galleries are in Manhattan unless otherwise noted. Full reviews of recent art shows: nytimes.com/art. A searchable guide to these and many other art shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum and Gallery Listings for Dec. 13-19', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T23:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/55785bae-bcfe-5ea5-a9d9-1f5b7e0c4e43', 'word_count': 7092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55785bae-bcfe-5ea5-a9d9-1f5b7e0c4e43'}, {'abstract': 'In the new documentary “The Carrier,” the first-time director Maggie Betts cuts to the heart of the problem by getting to know the people affected by it.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/now-screening-putting-a-human-face-on-the-african-aids-epidemic/', 'snippet': 'In the new documentary “The Carrier,” the first-time director Maggie Betts cuts to the heart of the problem by getting to know the people affected by it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The central figure in the director Maggie Betts’s affecting documentary, “The Carrier,” 28-year-old Mutinta Mweemba, is H.I.V.-positive and pregnant. A partner in a polygamous marriage in a small Zambian village, Mweemba is following a Prevention of Mother to Child Transmission (P.M.T.C.T.) program, receiving medication to keep the disease from being transmitted to her child. The film tracks Betts’s interactions with her family members (her husband and one of his two other wives are also infected) and her community, creating an unexpectedly intimate, nonjudgmental snapshot of the African AIDS epidemic. It shows how universal a mother’s fear of harming her child is, regardless of social or economic differences. “There’s no way an innocent baby who hasn’t even been born yet could have done anything to deserve this fate,” Betts says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Screening | Putting a Human Face on the African AIDS Epidemic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Carrier (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-12T23:28:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Zafiris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zafiris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/456d779b-3194-5836-beb6-1d0dbd03888b', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/456d779b-3194-5836-beb6-1d0dbd03888b'}, {'abstract': '“Christmas on the Rocks” imagines older versions of Ralphie, Charlie Brown and other characters from holiday classics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/nyregion/a-review-of-christmas-on-the-rocks-at-theaterworks-in-hartford.html', 'snippet': '“Christmas on the Rocks” imagines older versions of Ralphie, Charlie Brown and other characters from holiday classics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last we hear of Tiny Tim Cratchit in