0894013bf02'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the dead appeared to be suspected militants linked to Al Qaeda, tribal leaders said, but there were also reports that several civilians had been killed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/world/middleeast/drone-strike-in-yemen-hits-wedding-convoy-killing-11.html', 'snippet': 'Most of the dead appeared to be suspected militants linked to Al Qaeda, tribal leaders said, but there were also reports that several civilians had been killed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIYADH, Saudi Arabia — Drone-fired missiles struck a convoy of cars returning from a wedding on Thursday afternoon in a remote area of Yemen, witnesses said, killing at least 11 people in what appeared to be the second American drone strike in the past week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drone Strike in Yemen Hits Wedding Convoy, Killing 11', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drone Strike in Yemen Hits Wedding Convoy, Killing 11', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Worth, Robert F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T01:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b4cfd10-bf91-5a6e-a172-85319848ca05', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b4cfd10-bf91-5a6e-a172-85319848ca05'}, {'abstract': 'The wide-ranging recommendations on how to strengthen regulation still leave broad areas of the $7 trillion industry under state oversight.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/12/treasury-urges-more-federal-oversight-of-insurance/', 'snippet': 'The wide-ranging recommendations on how to strengthen regulation still leave broad areas of the $7 trillion industry under state oversight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Treasury called on Thursday for a greater federal role in the regulation of insurance, particularly in areas like mortgage insurance, the collection and use of personal data to set prices, and the use of secretive entities known as captives to keep risks off the books of insurers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Urges More Federal Oversight of Insurance', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Insurance, Treasury Urges More Clarity, More Rigor and More Oversight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Insurance Commissioners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T01:17:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f837112b-51a7-516f-972a-90b69a718b54', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f837112b-51a7-516f-972a-90b69a718b54'}, {'abstract': 'With download sales cooling after a decade of growth, streaming services like Spotify, Pandora and Apple’s new iTunes Radio have become the latest hope for the troubled music business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/business/media/a-stream-of-music-not-revenue.html', 'snippet': 'With download sales cooling after a decade of growth, streaming services like Spotify, Pandora and Apple’s new iTunes Radio have become the latest hope for the troubled music business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Spotify, the digital music company of the moment, announced this week an exclusive deal with Led Zeppelin and free access on mobile devices, it also reported impressive numbers. Its listeners have streamed 4.5 billion hours of music this year, and it has paid more than $1 billion in music royalties since its founding. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/SPOTIFY1/SPOTIFY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/business/SPOTIFY1/SPOTIFY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 786}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/SPOTIFY1/SPOTIFY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 782, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/SPOTIFY1/SPOTIFY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height