has a team of lobbyists who have pushed an agenda that sometimes echoes the interests of its corporate supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The defense contractor Northrop Grumman gave money to the left-leaning Center for American Progress, founded by John D. Podesta, as the nonprofit group at times bemoaned what it called the harmful impact of major reductions in Pentagon spending.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/PODESTA-2/PODESTA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/us/PODESTA-2/PODESTA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/PODESTA-2/PODESTA-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/PODESTA-2/PODESTA-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/PODESTA-2/PODESTA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/13/us/PODESTA-2/PODESTA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/us/PODESTA-2/PODESTA-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Obama Adviser Brings Corporate Ties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Obama Adviser Brings Corporate Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Podesta, John D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for American Progress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T03:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0e810ca-0bb5-5682-911a-ca365d036bd5', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0e810ca-0bb5-5682-911a-ca365d036bd5'}, {'abstract': '“The Rime of the Ancient Mariner” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Harvey Theater brings together poetry and motion in a stage and dance interpretation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/theater/reviews/the-rime-of-the-ancient-mariner-with-fiona-shaw.html', 'snippet': '“The Rime of the Ancient Mariner” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Harvey Theater brings together poetry and motion in a stage and dance interpretation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The formidable Irish actor Fiona Shaw is not encrusted with barnacles or dripping seaweed in portraying the crazed title character in the new stage presentation of “The Rime of the Ancient Mariner,” the celebrated verse ballad by Samuel Taylor Coleridge, at the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Harvey Theater. As