n SeaTac, Wash., has already survived a narrow election and a recount.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — The highest municipal minimum wage in the nation, approved by voters last month in the small city of SeaTac, Wash., at $15 an hour, survived a narrow election and a recount. Now, just weeks before its scheduled Jan. 1 start date – raising the pay of thousands of SeaTac residents and workers at Seattle-Tacoma International Airport, which is within the city limits — opponents are sending in the lawyers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$15 Hourly Minimum Wage in Northwest City Faces Court Challenge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SeaTac (Wash)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALASKA AIRLINES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Restaurant Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle-Tacoma International Airport', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T04:38:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f78fccd9-73cb-579b-9327-a6189bd33073', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f78fccd9-73cb-579b-9327-a6189bd33073'}, {'abstract': 'An intriguing new study suggests that what really draws people to rich desserts and prompts them to eat much more than perhaps they know they should is not the fat that they contain, but primarily the sugar.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/in-food-cravings-sugar-tr