nk': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Overbye, Dennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Overbye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Overbye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1db81f73-7eef-5eb3-be38-e1bbeee4f7c4', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1db81f73-7eef-5eb3-be38-e1bbeee4f7c4'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Animal Planet) WHALE WARS: A COMMANDER RISES For five seasons, the series “Whale Wars” has followed Capt. Paul Watson, the leader of the Sea Shepherd Conservation Society and a founder of Greenpeace, as he guided the Steve Irwin, the society’s flagship vessel, through Antarctic waters to save the lives of whales. Along the way, he has tangled with governments and made some enemies. In this two-hour special, Captain Watson must step down from his post just as his armada leaves for the Southern Ocean, causing those aboard to ask how their mission — and the organization — can succeed without his leadership.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/80b00673-d300-5b61-9410-03e12ac250d6', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80b00673-d300-5b61-9410-03e12ac250d6'}, {'abstract': 'The author argues against the Supreme Court’s contention in its ruling on gay rights that India should be wary of “transplanting Western experience in this country.”', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/love-and-gender-according-to-the-hindu-epics/', 'snippet': 'The author argues against the Supreme Court’s contention in its ruling on gay rights that India should be wary of “transplanting Western experience in this country.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the Supreme Court has restored the 19th-century ban on homosexuality, when all the arguments are done, when we Indians have heard everything about freedom over our bodies and homosexuality being a Western import and the right to privacy and more, maybe it’s time to remember our traditions. Perhaps there are lessons there about homosexuality too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/asia/12-Same-Sex-IndiaInk/12-Same-Sex-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 409, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/12/world/asia/12-Same-Sex-IndiaInk/12-Same-Sex-In