}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Minute | Newtown Anniversary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Change', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown (Conn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T11:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Christian Roman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/545513c7-eb93-551f-a264-9dcbf919df11', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/545513c7-eb93-551f-a264-9dcbf919df11'}, {'abstract': 'Also on the Minute, Big Tobacco makes a move, and a new New York Times/Sienna College poll of New Yorkers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/minute/2013/12/13/times-minute-newtown-anniversary/', 'snippet': 'Also on the Minute, Big Tobacco makes a move, and a new New York Times/Sienna College poll of New Yorkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Video', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Minute | Newtown Anniversary', 'kicker': 'The New York Times News Minute', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T11:02:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christian Roman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b6a83b3-46b4-55a6-afed-f4d652365343', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b6a83b3-46b4-55a6-afed-f4d652365343'}, {'abstract': 'It is peculiarly English to use the word “sorry” to defuse the potential for conflict while drawing attention to it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/opinion/a-poor-apology-of-a-word.html', 'snippet': 'It is peculiarly English to use the word “sorry” to defuse the potential for conflict while drawing attention to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — I am sitting in a cafe in a leafy part of South London. A teenager inadvertently bashes me in the face with his rucksack and I say “sorry,” as if on his behalf. Five minutes later, a young woman flattens my foot with her stroller and each of us blurts another “sorry.” Getting up to leave, I knock over my cup. A waitress descends on this little embarrassment with a cloth and an accusatory “sorry,” while I twice utter the same word.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14hitchings/14hitchings-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14hitchings/14hitchings-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14hitchings/14hitchings-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1021, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14hitchings/14hitchings-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1289, 'width': 1293, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14hitchings/14hitchings-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14hitchings/14hitchings-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14hitchings/14hitchings-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Poor Apology for a Word', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Poor Apology of a Word', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchings, Henry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T11:12:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Hitchings', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hitchings', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/af91979d-ee93-54b2-9d70-89d4a91d2dd2', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af91979d-ee93-54b2-9d70-89d4a91d2dd2'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities questioned whether guards had helped the prisoners, who were facing terrorism charges, escape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/world/middleeast/prisoners-flee-baghdad-jail.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities questioned whether guards had helped the prisoners, who were facing terrorism charges, escape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Twenty-five suspects held on terrorism charges, some facing the death penalty, escaped early Friday from a prison north of Baghdad, killing two guards and raising the question of whether they had received inside help, security officials said. The prison is where Saddam Hussein was hanged in 2006.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '25 Prisoners Flee Baghdad Jail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Day of Violence Includes Prison Break and Pipeline Shooting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adnan, Duraid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T11:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duraid Adnan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duraid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adnan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea74e392-babe-587f-876a-18c6b8f73a40', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea74e392-babe-587f-876a-18c6b8f73a40'}, {'abstract': 'If we cannot determine how World War I happened, how can we hope to avoid another such catastrophe?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/opinion/macmillan-the-great-wars-ominous-echoes.html', 'snippet': 'If we cannot determine how World War I happened, how can we hope to avoid another such catastrophe?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oxford, England — Earlier this year, I was on holiday in Corsica and wandered into the church of a tiny hamlet in the hills where I found a memorial to the dead from World War I. Out of a population that can have been no more than 150, eight young men, bearing among them only three last names, had died in that conflict. Such lists can be found all over Europe, in great cities and in small villages. Similar memorials are spread around the globe, for the Great War, as it was known before 1940, also drew soldiers from Asia, Africa and North America.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14macmillan/14macmillan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14macmillan/14macmillan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14macmillan/14macmillan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14macmillan/14macmillan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1284, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14macmillan/14macmillan-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14macmillan/14macmillan-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/opinion/14macmillan/14macmillan-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great War’s Ominous Echoes', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "The Great War's Ominous Echoes", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacMillan, Margaret', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T11:35:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret MacMillan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacMillan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/46968bc6-57b3-514d-af02-db9e7e0bc500', 'word_count': 2237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46968bc6-57b3-514d-af02-db9e7e0bc500'}, {'abstract': 'The Transportation Department is considering whether it is fair to consumers to allow in-flight voice calls.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/daily-report-u-s-regulators-weigh-cellphone-use-on-airplanes/', 'snippet': 'The Transportation Department is considering whether it is fair to consumers to allow in-flight voice calls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Transportation Department said on Thursday that it would consider banning the use of cellphones for voice calls aboard airplanes, a reaction to public outrage at a Federal Communications Commission proposal to lift a rule that has long forbidden the use of mobile phones during flight, Edward Wyatt reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'th