intense and creative life of Isabella Blow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/arts/international/taking-the-surreal-to-its-very-limit.html', 'snippet': 'A London exhibition celebrates the intense and creative life of Isabella Blow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Let’s start with the hats: an Op-art swirling circle of straw; disembodied Dali-esque lips; a fat, curling serpent of satin and mesh; or denuded feathers spiked into aggressive arrows — crazy concoctions that took headgear to its artistic limits.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Surreal to Its Very Limit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking the Surreal to Its Very Limit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menkes, Suzy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Somerset House', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blow, Isabella', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T13:51:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'International Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzy Menkes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Menkes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a3e8cc8-609d-5b4f-a792-196de251c336', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a3e8cc8-609d-5b4f-a792-196de251c336'}, {'abstract': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: a handmade throw to warm up any home.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/holiday-the-daily-gift-khadi-and-co-blanket/', 'snippet': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: a handmade throw to warm up any home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday | The Daily Gift: Khadi and Co Blanket', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T14:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83547f89-8cd1-564c-bbbf-5e9fcd0dfa8b', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83547f89-8cd1-564c-bbbf-5e9fcd0dfa8b'}, {'abstract': 'Airline passengers have been upset at the possibility that people would be able to talk on their cellphones in flight. Here are some of the most popular questions from readers about the possibly change by the Federal Communications Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/questions-and-answers-to-cell-phones-on-planes/', 'snippet': 'Airline passengers have been upset at the possibility that people would be able to talk on their cellphones in flight. Here are some of the most popular questions from readers about the possibly change by the Federal Communications Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Airline passengers have been in an uproar since news broke that the Federal Communications Commission was planning to overturn a rule that banned the use of cellphones on planes while in flight. The following are some of the most popular questions I get from readers on this topic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'