ons. Here’s what they’re missing by not lingering a little longer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sri Lanka is so jam-packed with alluring outdoorsy activities that visitors often high-tail it out of the capital a day or two after arriving, choosing instead to spend their vacation days lounging on a southern beach, whale-watching off the coast or leopard-spotting in a national park. Yet Colombo is fast becoming a draw in itself. This city of 555,000 people has been on fast-forward since a 25-year civil war ended in 2009. Checkpoints have come down, trendy lounge bars have opened up, and the vibe is one of cautious optimism combined with an increasingly cosmopolitan outlook. Today, this colorful city on the Indian Ocean, with its laid-back island ambience, palm trees, decaying colonial buildings and smattering of modern office blocks, is the perfect place to get a sense of where Sri Lanka is going after so many tumultuous years.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HOURS_SPAN-sf/15HOURS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HOURS_SPAN-sf/15HOURS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 646}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HOURS_SPAN-sf/15HOURS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 952, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HOURS_SPAN-sf/15HOURS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1903, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HOURS_SPAN-sf/15HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HOURS_SPAN-sf/15HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/travel/15HOURS_SPAN-sf/15HOURS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Colombo, Sri Lanka', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Colombo, Sri Lanka', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wulfhart, Nell McShane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombo (Sri Lanka)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T14:13:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nell McShane Wulfhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nell', 'middlename': 'Mcshane', 'lastname': 'Wulfhart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2e4b273-1b4c-5daf-897d-5a6071471b1b', 'word_count': 1713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2e4b273-1b4c-5daf-897d-5a6071471b1b'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker Rithy Panh explains that he made “The Missing Picture” to restore to life the family he lost along with 1.8 million others in the Khmer Rouge genocide.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/rithy-panh-on-the-missing-picture-and-living-with-tragedy/', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker Rithy Panh explains that he made “The Missing Picture” to restore to life the family he lost along with 1.8 million others in the Khmer Rouge genocide.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Of the 76 entries for the Oscar for best foreign-language film, Rithy Panh’s “Missing Picture,” representing Cambodia, is one of only two documentary films submitted in the category. But there’s never been a documentary quite like “The Missing Picture,” in which Mr. Panh uses clay figures, dioramas, period music and archival film footage recovered through detective work to tell the story of how his family — parents, siblings and nephews — and 1.8 million others perished in the Khmer Rouge genocide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rithy Panh on ‘The Missing Picture’ and Living With Tragedy', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T14:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa6fd59-60d0-5491-9077-05fcb42e0c5c', 'word_count': 1406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa6fd59-60d0-5491-9077-05fcb42e0c5c'}, {'abstract': 'President Viktor F. Yanukovich held his first face-to-face meeting with opposition leaders Friday as the country’s richest man, Rinat Akhmetov, expressed support for the demonstrators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/world/europe/ukraine-protests.html', 'snippet': 'President Viktor F. Yanukovich held his first face-to-face meeting with opposition leaders Friday as the country’s richest man, Rinat Akhmetov, expressed support for the demonstrators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — In his 