url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/video-reviews-of-american-hustle-saving-mr-banks-and-the-hobbit/', 'snippet': 'Times critics on “American Hustle,” “Saving Mr. Banks” and “The Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s video, Times critics look at David O. Russell’s latest film “American Hustle,” Peter Jackson’s “Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug” and “Saving Mr. Banks,” featuring Tom Hanks as Walt Disney. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Reviews of ‘American Hustle,’ ‘Saving Mr. Banks’ and ‘The Hobbit’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanks, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, David O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T16:03:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37b1ad07-47e9-569d-b9f3-2b8929bc0927', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37b1ad07-47e9-569d-b9f3-2b8929bc0927'}, {'abstract': 'A batch of books about American cuisine reminds us how food defines who we are, where we’ve been and who we want to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/books/review/biting-through-the-skin-by-nina-mukerjee-furstenau-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'A batch of books about American cuisine reminds us how food defines who we are, where we’ve been and who we want to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, this big, messy country united. Culinarily, at least. We all sat down to our Thanksgiving tables and ate (mostly) the same thing at (mostly) the same time, before retreating to our big, messy corners to cook and eat the diverse, constantly evolving cuisine we call American. The latest batch of narrative food books (not to be confused with strictly recipe-driven cookbooks) explores some of those corners, reminding us how food defines who we are (Patriots? Capitalists? Shameless Worshipers of Celebrity?), where we’ve been and — \xadperhaps most American of all — who we want to be.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1/1215-bks-Rosenstrach-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i