tps://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/books/review/my-mistake-a-memoir-by-daniel-menaker.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Menaker’s memoir recalls his time at The New Yorker and at Random House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Menaker loves words, and you can see it in every clause, in the rhythms of his language, even in the length of the sentences in his bracing memoir, “My Mistake.” A veteran editor at The New Yorker and Random House, an insider who has always felt like an outsider, he was jolted by lung cancer several years ago into re-\xadexamining his past. He grabs the reader with urgency as he grapples with big questions: What shaped me? Where did I go right and wrong? What has my life meant? His clever, fast-paced prose makes you stop and think and wonder, meandering down your own byways, contemplating the ways his story \xadreverberates.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15GORDON/15GORDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15GORDON/15GORDON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15GORDON/15GORDON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 915, 'width': 915, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15GORDON/15GORDON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 915, 'width': 915, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15GORDON/15GORDON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15GORDON/15GORDON-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15GORDON/15GORDON-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Talk of the Town', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talk of the Town', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menaker, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T16:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meryl Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c6236c7-0f28-5680-9eb0-1a948c6c1ea8', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c6236c7-0f28-5680-9eb0-1a948c6c1ea8'}, {'abstract': 'Ivan Klima, the Czech novelist and playwright, reflects on a life spent under Nazi and Communist regimes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/books/review/my-crazy-century-by-ivan-klima.html', 'snippet': 'Ivan Klima, the Czech novelist and playwright, reflects on a life spent under Nazi and Communist regimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why did people join the Communist movement back in the day? Ivan Klima, the distinguished Czech writer, raises the question in the prologue to his memoir, “My Crazy Century,” and he raises the temperature, too, by defining Communism as “a criminal conspiracy against democracy.” People did join, though. Klima acknowledges a little sheepishly that he was among them, in his younger years. He offers a schematic preliminary explanation: Young people need to rebel, they yearn for simple theories of the world and so forth. And then, with his prologue behind him and his anger and mortification exposed, he devotes the next 400 pages to the real explanation, which turns out to be sadder and more complicated. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15BERMAN/15BERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15BERMAN/15BERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 527}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15BERMAN/15BERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15BERMAN/15BERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1039, 'width': 1183, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15BERMAN/15BERMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15BERMAN/15BERMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15BERMAN/15BERMAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'l