ty” — and here it comes, crashing onto the hardcover fiction list at No. 1. That’s a familiar position for Clancy’s books, but it somehow eluded the novel that introduced him (and Ryan) to the world: “The Hunt for Red October” spent 28 weeks on the hardcover list in 1985, but never reached the top spot. (It did hit No. 1 in paper\xadback.) Not that Clancy needed to worry. By the time Ryan made his second appearance, in 1987’s “Patriot Games,” he debuted at No. 1.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15list-img/15list-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 275, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15list-img/15list-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 275, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15list-img/15list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15list-img/15list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/books/review/15list-img/15list-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T16:32:48