nippet': 'The veteran actress, long known as the voice of Lois on Seth MacFarlane’s animated sitcom “Family Guy,” discusses her starring turn on the new black comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Borstein, an Emmy-nominated actress and writer — and the voice of Lois Griffin on the animated Fox series “Family Guy” — currently stars as Nurse Dawn Forchette on HBO’s black comedy “Getting On,” based on the BBC show about a women’s extended care facility in a Long Beach hospital. Alongside her co-stars Laurie Metcalf and Niecy Nash, Borstein brilliantly exercises her comedic chops and exquisite timing to create the most memorable nurse since Ratched. Having honed her gift for impressions, namely as Ms. Swan on “MADtv,” Borstein, a mother of two, will soon not just be recognized for her brilliant voice, but also for her tremendous talent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talking Talent | Alex Borstein, Star of HBO’s ‘Getting On’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T18:06:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Tabach-Bank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabach-Bank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b859201d-865e-50ce-b4ae-e5ab177c12f6', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b859201d-865e-50ce-b4ae-e5ab177c12f6'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations refugee agency said the crisis was worsening in the country, which has been convulsed by sectarian violence and lawlessness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/world/africa/violence-in-central-african-republic.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations refugee agency said the crisis was worsening in the country, which has been convulsed by sectarian violence and lawlessness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — More than 600 people have been killed in the last week in the sectarian violence and lawlessness convulsing Central African Republic, and the crisis is getting worse, the United Nations refugee agency said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14Geneva_1/14Geneva_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14Geneva_1/14Geneva_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14Geneva_1/14Geneva_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14Geneva_1/14Geneva_1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14Geneva_1/14Geneva_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14Geneva_1/14Geneva_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14Geneva_1/14Geneva_1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headlin