t of sight as you take the snaking path past a trim bar toward the back of the restaurant. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15DINEWE1_SPAN/15DINEWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15DINEWE1_SPAN/15DINEWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15DINEWE1_SPAN/15DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15DINEWE1_SPAN/15DINEWE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15DINEWE1_SPAN/15DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15DINEWE1_SPAN/15DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15DINEWE1_SPAN/15DINEWE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Standards New to a Familiar Spot', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italian Standards New to a Familiar Spot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'White Plains (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sapori (White Plains, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T18:49:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbfe74c5-6b3a-5f22-b341-8f0f1c027432', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbfe74c5-6b3a-5f22-b341-8f0f1c027432'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Opera ends with “Anna Nichole” and “Mosè en Egitto,” as Nico Muhly has a debut with a Metropolitan Opera-Lincoln Center Theater coproduction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/arts/music/anthony-tommasini-on-the-year-in-classical-music.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Opera ends with “Anna Nichole” and “Mosè en Egitto,” as Nico Muhly has a debut with a Metropolitan Opera-Lincoln Center Theater coproduction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The year in classical music was rich with memorable orchestra concerts, chamber-music programs and recitals. Yet what stood out most for me were opera performances, not all of them in opera houses. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15TOMMASINI2_SPAN/15TOMMASINI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15TOMMASINI2_SPAN/15TOMMASINI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15TOMMASINI2_SPAN/15TOMMASINI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, '