rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc1d356-1010-56a7-a684-499d5664879a', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc1d356-1010-56a7-a684-499d5664879a'}, {'abstract': 'Four productions of Handel operas — an “Almira,” an “Aci, Galatea e Polifemo” and two takes on “Radamisto” — testify to the popularity of early music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/arts/music/early-handel-operas-are-current-again.html', 'snippet': 'Four productions of Handel operas — an “Almira,” an “Aci, Galatea e Polifemo” and two takes on “Radamisto” — testify to the popularity of early music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York a hotbed of early music? No one would have said so 20 years ago (when some of us were saying the opposite) or even 10 years ago. But a remarkable shift has occurred over the last decade or so, thanks to a web of interlocking factors, including the formation of a curriculum in historical performance at the Juilliard School, the exponential growth of the music program at Trinity Wall Street, the enterprise of groups like Tenet and the Sebastians and the work of the service organization Gotham Early Music Scene.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15OESTREICH1_SPAN/15OESTREICH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 308, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15OESTREICH1_SPAN/15OESTREICH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 308}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15OESTREICH1_SPAN/15OESTREICH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 525, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15OESTREICH1_SPAN/15OESTREICH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15OESTREICH1_SPAN/15OESTREICH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15OESTREICH1_SPAN/15OESTREICH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15OESTREICH1_SPAN/15OESTREICH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Handel Operas Are Current Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Early Handel Operas Are Current Again ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handel, George Frederick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T18:51:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6667ab6b-7e8b-5800-9e1c-64a8792fb05e', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6667ab6b-7e8b-5800-9e1c-64a8792fb05e'}, {'abstract': 'The Pulitzer-winning Caroline Shaw and the opera composer Nico Muhly are among several younger classical stars with early successes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/arts/music/caroline-shaw-and-nico-muhly-represent-a-generational-shift.html', 'snippet': 'The Pulitzer-winning Caroline Shaw and the opera composer Nico Muhly are among several younger classical stars with early successes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You could call 2013 the Year of the 30-Something, as two of classical music’s most prestigious bastions opened their doors to children of the 1980s. The polymathic Nico Muhly, born in 1981, became the youngest composer to have a commissioned work performed at the Metropolitan Opera when his “Two Boys” had its American premiere in October. In April, Caroline Shaw (1982) was the youngest recipient of the Pulitzer Prize in Music for her rapturous “Partita for Eight Voices.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOOLFE1_SPAN/15WOOLFE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOOLFE1_SPAN/15WOOLFE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOOLFE1_SPAN/15WOOLFE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOOLFE1_SPAN/15WOOLFE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1450, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOOLFE1_SPAN/15WOOLFE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOOLFE1_SPAN/15WOOLFE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOOLFE1_SPAN/15WOOLFE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Golden Moments in Their 30s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Golden Moments in Their 30s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaw, Caroline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muhly, Nico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T18:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74d7704a-05a3-5fc5-b51c-4ea84d2b5928', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74d7704a-05a3-5fc5-b51c-4ea84d2b5928'}, {'abstract': 'Janet Cardiff, Rand Steiger, Kevin James and other artists have incorporated room acoustics into provocative compositions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/arts/music/giving-sound-itself-a-starring-role.html', 'snippet': 'Janet Cardiff, Rand Steiger, Kevin James and other artists have incorporated room acoustics into provocative compositions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2013, I stopped taking the sound of music for granted. To be sure, I’ve always experienced music in a visceral way. Reviewing the Budapest Festival Orchestra’s performance in January, I marveled at how, under its conductor, Ivan Fischer, it created “volleys of sound so vividly three-dimensional that you sometimes had to resist the impulse to duck.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN/15WOLLHEIM_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Sound Itself a Starring Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head