 '_id': 'nyt://video/30dafddf-c86c-5364-9ccb-8c0db8769614', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/30dafddf-c86c-5364-9ccb-8c0db8769614'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly 20,000 new Acura MDX utility vehicles, close to 20,000 Harley-Davidson motorcycles and 142 Suzuki motorcycles will be recalled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/automobiles/acura-harley-davidson-and-suzuki-to-issue-recalls.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly 20,000 new Acura MDX utility vehicles, close to 20,000 Harley-Davidson motorcycles and 142 Suzuki motorcycles will be recalled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Acura will recall about 19,000 of its 2014 MDX utility vehicles in the United States because of a powertrain problem, the automaker said in a report posted on the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration website. The automaker said it was possible that one or two of the four bolts securing the propeller shaft could be loose. If the propeller shaft detached the all-wheel-drive system could be damaged and the vehicle would lose power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/automobiles/14RECALLS-acura/14RECALLS-acura-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/14/automobiles/14RECALLS-acura/14RECALLS-acura-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/automobiles/14RECALLS-acura/14RECALLS-acura-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/automobiles/14RECALLS-acura/14RECALLS-acura-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1150, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/automobiles/14RECALLS-acura/14RECALLS-acura-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/14/automobiles/14RECALLS-acura/14RECALLS-acura-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/automobiles/14RECALLS-acura/14RECALLS-acura-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Acura, Harley-Davidson and Suzuki to Issue Recalls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACURA DIVISION OF HONDA MOTOR CO', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Suzuki Motor Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harley-Davidson Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f5ffb17-2856-53c3-80ee-c0fb3ba181c7', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f5ffb17-2856-53c3-80ee-c0fb3ba181c7'}, {'abstract': 'Trisha Brown Dance Company presented what were announced to be her last works, and Pam Tanowitz bounced back from the misstep of “Untitled (Blue Ballet).”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/arts/dance/brian-seibert-on-the-dance-highlights-of-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Trisha Brown Dance Company presented what were announced to be her last works, and Pam Tanowitz bounced back from the misstep of “Untitled (Blue Ballet).”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year in dance dawned with an ending. At the Brooklyn Academy of Music in January, the Trisha Brown Dance Company presented what were announced to be her final works. They weren’t her best, but the whole program, sampling from 45 years of choreographing, was of the quality that sets the high end of my critical scale. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SEIBERT/15SEIBERT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1115, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SEIBERT/15SEIBERT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1115}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SEIBERT/15SEIBERT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 551, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SEIBERT/15SEIBERT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1102, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SEIBERT/15SEIBERT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SEIBERT/15SEIBERT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SEIBERT/15SEIBERT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Time for Farewells and Comebacks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Time for Farewells And Comebacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Trisha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanowitz, Pam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:04:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/763e7a5e-79e1-5757-a700-f62f2a323f33', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/763e7a5e-79e1-5757-a700-f62f2a323f33'}, {'abstract': 'Indelible moments in 2013 from American Ballet Theater, New York City Ballet and downtown dance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/arts/dance/scene-stealers-irina-dvorovenko-lauren-lovette-and-meg-stuart.html', 'snippet': 'Indelible moments in 2013 from American Ballet Theater, New York City Ballet and downtown dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dancers aren’t just the tools of choreographers and directors, but their lifeblood. It comes down to trust: Once a dancer steps onstage, the symbiotic studio relationship is transformed. Alone, the dancer balances that evanescent power of responsibility and freedom.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15KOURLAS/15KOURLAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15KOURLAS/15KOURLAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 821}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15KOURLAS/15KOURLAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 749, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15KOURLAS/15KOURLAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1497, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15KOURLAS/15KOURLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15KOURLAS/15KOURLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15KOURLAS/15KOURLAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Ballerinas Get Brassy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Ballerinas Get Brassy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dvorovenko, Irina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovette, Lauren', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stuart, Meg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc65f0e2-868d-56b5-9c77-3ce8399678b0', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc65f0e2-868d-56b5-9c77-3ce8399678b0'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t expect government surveillance programs to change dramatically any time soon.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/restraining-the-n-s-a/', 'snippet': 'Don’t expect government surveillance programs to change dramatically any time soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Edward Snowden leaks started, President Obama said absolutely everything was being done to safeguard Americans’ privacy and rights. Then he called for a “vigorous public debate” about surveillance and eventually ordered reviews of National Security Agency programs — to make sure that all those promised safeguards were, in fact, in place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restraining the N.S.A.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:07:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd666af7-2cae-5373-8d13-25683ef56305', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd666af7-2cae-5373-8d13-25683ef56305'}, {'abstract': 'When the 2013 Malibu failed to excite critics (and more importantly, buyers), Chevy quickly refreshed it. The 2014 model gets more style, room, power and cornering fun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/automobiles/autoreviews/100000002600600/review-2014-chevy-malibu.html', 'snippet': 'When the 2013 Malibu failed to excite critics (and more importantly, buyers), Chevy quickly refreshed it. The 2014 model gets more style, room, power and cornering fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the 2013 Malibu failed to excite critics (and more importantly, buyers), Chevy quickly refreshed it. The 2014 model gets more style, room, power and cornering fun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/automobiles/video-driven-chevy-malibu/video-driven-chevy-malibu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/16/automobiles/video-driven-chevy-malibu/video-driven-chevy-malibu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/automobiles/video-driven-chevy-malibu/video-driven-chevy-malibu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/16/automobiles/video-driven-chevy-malibu/video-driven-chevy-malibu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/automobiles/video-driven-chevy-malibu/video-driven-chevy-malibu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: 2014 Chevy Malibu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:09:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e1a6aba5-7683-55e4-81b3-c18d7129484e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e1a6aba5-7683-55e4-81b3-c18d7129484e'}, {'abstract': 'Tax policy has stayed out of the headlines, but higher rates, new laws and disappearing deductions mean that higher-income taxpayers are likely to pay more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/your-money/for-top-earners-a-bigger-tax-bite-this-year.html', 'snippet': 'Tax policy has stayed out of the headlines, but higher rates, new laws and disappearing deductions mean that higher-income taxpayers are likely to pay more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LESS than a year ago, people were worried about a variety of tax increases in 2013, from income and investment taxes going up to the exemption on estate and gift taxes going down. This year, without any last-minute negotiation around major tax policy, people are far less focused on taxes, and that has accountants and tax lawyers worried.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/your-money/14wealth/14wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/14/your-money/14wealth/14wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/your-money/14wealth/14wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/your-money/14wealth/14wealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/your-money/14wealth/14wealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/14/your-money/14wealth/14wealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/your-money/14wealth/14wealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Top Earners, a Bigger Tax Bite This Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Unexpectedly Big Tax Bite for Top Earners This Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c28a392-669b-5053-bea5-a6b9d67d2518', 'word_count': 1446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c28a392-669b-5053-bea5-a6b9d67d2518'}, {'abstract': 'Best Buy stock is one of the best-performing stocks in the Standard & Poor’s 500, leading rival retailers to wonder how the company did it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/business/fast-rise-of-best-buy-in-the-face-of-amazon.html', 'snippet': 'Best Buy stock is one of the best-performing stocks in the Standard & Poor’s 500, leading rival retailers to wonder how the company did it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a lonely holiday season last year for David Strasser, an analyst at Janney Montgomery Scott. Of the 25 analysts covering the electronics retailer Best Buy, he was the only one to make a buy recommendation. And the stock kept going down.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-