'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce9e0ef5-69c4-5d87-a7f2-1b82dd7eb962', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce9e0ef5-69c4-5d87-a7f2-1b82dd7eb962'}, {'abstract': 'Many of Mike Hale’s favorite television series this year — “The Hollow Crown,” “Prisoners of War” and “Moone Boy” among them — were produced abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/arts/television/mike-hales-top-12-television-shows-of-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Many of Mike Hale’s favorite television series this year — “The Hollow Crown,” “Prisoners of War” and “Moone Boy” among them — were produced abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are my 12 favorite television shows of 2013 — the ones you won’t find piling up on my DVR, because I have to watch each new episode as soon as it appears. (Which means, of course, by the end of the next day.) Are they the 12 best shows of the year? Who knows. I didn’t come close to watching everything on TV, and neither did anyone else. All I know is that 10 wouldn’t have been enough.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SUBHALE1_SPAN/15SUBHALE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SUBHALE1_SPAN/15SUBHALE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/arts/15SUBHALE1_SPAN/15SUBHALE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'c