: 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a65ffd47-7a33-5616-97ed-a6c4db22fc38', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a65ffd47-7a33-5616-97ed-a6c4db22fc38'}, {'abstract': 'A multiday event at the Manhattan co-working space Neuehouse celebrated the rich history of the instrument and the legacy of one of its great innovators, an 82-year-old Trinidadian named Elliott Mannette.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/art-matters-taking-back-the-steel-drum-from-the-hippies/', 'snippet': 'A multiday event at the Manhattan co-working space Neuehouse celebrated the rich history of the instrument and the legacy of one of its great innovators, an 82-year-old Trinidadian named Elliott Mannette.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The steel drum is the most misunderstood instrument in the world,” says the Trinidadian curator Everard Findlay. He admits that for many people, it evokes “guys on a cruise ship, with a smile and dreadlocks.” On Tuesday and Wednesday, Findlay hosted “7 Drums 7 Artists,” a cross-disciplinary tribute to the steel pan at NeueHouse, a co-working space in the Flatiron district that opened in April. Designed by Rockwell Group, NeueHouse, which bills itself as “a new way to work,” features art magazines hanging from wall-mounted racks and glass-globe chandeliers that lower from pulleys at night when the space becomes a venue. The co-founder, Joshua Abram, says that “learning happens at the edge of one’s network”; as part of that philosophy, NeueHouse offers evening cultural programming for its members that brings together artists, scientists, filmmakers and musicians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Matters | Taking Back the Steel Drum From the Hippies', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dawn Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dawn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/414057f7-2ecc-5388-bbe1-355c1b5bf3be', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414057f7-2ecc-5388-bbe1-355c1b5bf3be'}, {'abstract': 'The director discusses what went into the making of a crucial scene in the film.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/video-david-o-russell-on-american-hustle/', 'snippet': 'The director discusses what went into the making of a crucial scene in the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a good week for “American Hustle.” The film, which opened to very strong reviews today, picked up a nomination from the Screen Actors Guild for best ensemble (the guild’s equivalent to best picture) on Wednesday and the next day picked up seven Golden Globe nominations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: David O. Russell on ‘American Hustle’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, David O', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d86b986-7163-593e-9131-a02bcf08be74', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d86b986-7163-593e-9131-a02bcf08be74'}, {'abstract': 'Two wines made at the Wölffer Estate Vineyard pair well with traditional Christmas dinners, such as glazed baked ham or juicy roast goose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/nyregion/pairing-christmas-dinners-with-white-wines.html', 'snippet': 'Two wines made at the Wölffer Estate Vineyard pair well with traditional Christmas dinners, such as glazed baked ham or juicy roast goose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Winemakers I know across Europe prepare different kinds of culturally rooted, traditional Christmas dinners. Some of the most festive are in Germany. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pairing Christmas Dinners With White Wines', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairing Tradition With White Wines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Riesling (Wine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wolffer Estate Vineyard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Roman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paumanok Vineyards (Aquebogue, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sherwood House Vineyards', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:42:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a81e34ec-5286-5b7a-a3e5-22cb1a44ffcb', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a81e34ec-5286-5b7a-a3e5-22cb1a44ffcb'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas E. Rothman, the chairman of TriStar Productions, must be confirmed before joining the National Council on the Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/obama-nominates-hollywood-exec-to-arts-council/', 'snippet': 'Thomas E. Rothman, the chairman of TriStar Productions, must be confirmed before joining the National Council on the Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES – The National Council on the Arts, which helps manage the National Endowment for the Arts, will have a new high-profile member from Hollywood’s ranks if a nomination from President Obama goes through as expected. The White House announced on Thursday that Thomas E. Rothman, chairman of TriStar Productions, a division of Sony Pictures Entertainment, has been nominated to the 18-member council, which advises on the endowment’s policies and programs and makes recommendations on grant applications. He must be approved by the Senate before joining the Council.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Nominates Hollywood Exec to Arts Council', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hollywood Executive Chosen for Arts Council', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Council on the Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T19:52:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6066cb9b-0e47-590e-a2bd-a0f88a8c4fc8', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6066cb9b-0e47-590e-a2bd-a0f88a8c4fc8'}, {'abstract': 'Syracuse, Ohio State, Duke, Memphis, Flor