w that Clement Clarke Moore is famous for the poem “\xa0’Twas the Night Before Christmas,” but is it true he was the major developer of Chelsea?', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Twas the Night Before Christmas’ and Its Ties to Chelsea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Clement Clarke', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Livingston, Henry Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T20:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Pollak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1abecef-711a-5ae7-9fac-f342b1ee829a', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1abecef-711a-5ae7-9fac-f342b1ee829a'}, {'abstract': 'Readers tell Nick Kristof what topics they are interested in for the coming year.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/your-suggestions-for-2014/', 'snippet': 'Readers tell Nick Kristof what topics they are interested in for the coming year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers, thanks for your many insightful answers to the two questions I asked of you this week. To address your answers to my second question first, it’s great to hear many of you think I do a decent job engaging with you already, and I appreciate your suggestions for ways to try new forms of outreach and social media. That’s something I will try to do in 2014, so stay tuned!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Suggestions For 2014', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T20:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3597e37-7e30-5f34-8170-35828d90a7df', 'word_count': 1947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3597e37-7e30-5f34-8170-35828d90a7df'}, {'abstract': 'The Atlantic herring are running in the shallower bays and shorelines of New York City, and they aren’t very difficult to catch.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/13/a-night-swim-for-atlantic-herring/', 'snippet': 'The Atlantic herring are running in the shallower bays and shorelines of New York City, and they aren’t very difficult to catch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a windless December evening, sunset faded to shimmering violet over Jamaica Bay. Icy Atlantic waters pushed past Canarsie Pier, filling the bay for the second time that day. Now, two hours from high tide and almost dark, overhead lamps cast shadows deep into Brooklyn’s watery depths. It takes a great leap of faith to believe anything survives in the frigid dark below, but thousands of Atlantic herring (Clupea harengus) are hidden there.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Night Swim for Atlantic Herring', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before the Smoker, a Night Swim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, '