ment. And in a sign of where the music world’s sympathies are, they have lined up a few big-name guests, most notably the violinists Itzhak Perlman and Joshua Bell.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Minnesota Orchestra Musicians to Play a 10-Concert Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Minnesota Orchestra, A Season All Its Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-13T20:55:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7960af9-b51e-52dd-9b9b-b790b52026a4', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7960af9-b51e-52dd-9b9b-b790b52026a4'}, {'abstract': 'The actress Taryn Manning, a recent arrival to Greenwich Village, hangs out with her dog and her friends, and sometimes does Buddhist chanting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/nyregion/cleaning-the-place-and-clearing-the-mind.html', 'snippet': 'The actress Taryn Manning, a recent arrival to Greenwich Village, hangs out with her dog and her friends, and sometimes does Buddhist chanting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On screen, Taryn Manning has played a string of troubled characters, from a prostitute in “Hustle and Flow” to Pennsatucky, a meth-user-turned-bible-thumper in the Netflix prison series “Orange Is the New Black.” In her real life as a recent arrival to Greenwich Village — she also has a house in Los Angeles — Ms. Manning, 35, juggles more salubrious identities: actress, musician, D.J. and owner of a dog named Penguin, a mix of Cavalier King Charles spaniel and Maltese. Sundays tend to be a combination of those interests, along with shopping and hanging out.\xa0', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1_SPAN/15ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1_SPAN/15ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1_SPAN/15ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1_SPAN/15ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1_SPAN/15ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1_SPAN/15ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1_SPAN/15ROUTINE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleaning the Place, and Clearing the Mind', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cleaning the Place, and Clearing the Mind', 