pecial grand jury to examine whether officials covered up the crime, and the panel returned indictments against six people. But only some of those charges stem from the first rape case, while others relate to separate accusations investigated by the grand jury, including some stemming from allegations of the sexual assault of a 14-year-old student four months earlier, as well as other charges of theft and stolen property. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio: School Officials Plead Not Guilty After Rape', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ohio: School Officials Plead Not Guilty After Rape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppel, Richard A Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Steubenville High School (Steubenville, Ohio)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McVey, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Steubenville (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T02:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8def7ef5-fbe5-5bed-80ea-f0249b3d72e0', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8def7ef5-fbe5-5bed-80ea-f0249b3d72e0'}, {'abstract': 'Squatters have long been able to settle on others’ land, but after Typhoon Haiyan some landowners have thwarted rebuilding efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/world/asia/land-disputes-slow-recovery-in-philippines.html', 'snippet': 'Squatters have long been able to settle on others’ land, but after Typhoon Haiyan some landowners have thwarted rebuilding efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TACLOBAN, the Philippines — A mile offshore from this typhoon-wrecked city lies a postcard-perfect tropical islet fringed with golden sand beaches and topped with a mansion and swimming pool: the private island of one of this country’s most powerful families, the Romualdez clan of the former first lady, Imelda Marcos.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Land Disputes Slow Recovery in Philippines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Land Disputes Slow Recovery In Philippines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tacloban (Philippines)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squatters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcos, Imelda R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aquino, Benigno S III', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romualdez, Alfred S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T02:35:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42fccf49-92f1-5d84-b453-64e92e58dee0', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42fccf49-92f1-5d84-b453-64e92e58dee0'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s highest court correctly held that state judges must warn noncitizen defendants that a guilty plea could result in deportation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/opinion/a-judges-duty-to-warn-about-deportation.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s highest court correctly held that state judges must warn noncitizen defendants that a guilty plea could result in deportation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The combination of harsh immigration laws and stricter enforcement has made deportation the likely consequence when criminal defendants who are not American citizens plead guilty to a felony offense. Recognizing that “uniquely devastating deprivation of liberty,” New York’s highest court last month correctly held that due process requires state judges to warn noncitizen defendants that a guilty plea could lead to deportation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Judge’s Duty to Warn About Deportation', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Judge&#8217;s Duty to Warn About Deportation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lippman, Jonathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abdus-Salaam, Sheila', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Jenny (1960- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T02:36:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/03181383-aadd-53fd-95ba-0c3fbd6595d1', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03181383-aadd-53fd-95ba-0c3fbd6595d1'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should uphold the Environmental Protection Agency’s rightful authority to clean the air.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/opinion/a-fight-over-cross-state-pollution.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should uphold the Environmental Protection Agency’s rightful authority to clean the air.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency is charged by the Clean Air Act with setting air-quality standards and issuing regulations to limit pollutants like life-threatening particulate matter and ozone. Because bad air often travels far from its source — 93 percent of the air pollution in New Haven, Conn., for example, comes from other states — the act’s “good neighbor” policy requires that every state work to assure that the pollution from its power plants does not “contribute significantly” to the pollution in other states. If a state has no plan or an inadequate one, the E.P.A. can impose its own. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fight Over Cross-State Pollution', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fight Over Cross-State Pollution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T02:36:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f84fb6b-a3bb-596a-992a-bb6bae793726', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f84fb6b-a3bb-596a-992a-bb6bae793726'}, {'abstract': 'A new study may help to give these feared but important predators a better chance of surviving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/opinion/faithful-as-a-mother-shark.html', 'snippet': 'A new study may help to give these feared but important predators a better chance of surviving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The popular view of sharks as wandering predators, roaming the seas like outcast swordsmen in an old samurai movie, will have to be adjusted, what with this month’s big news about lemon sharks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Faithful as a Mother Shark', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Faithful as a Mother Shark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bimini (Bahamas)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Molecular Ecology (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-