ng to raise close to a billion dollars to try to pick up the pieces of Syria’s shattered education system and offset the “staggering decline” in what was once one of the region’s leading school systems after nearly three years of conflict.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14unicef/14unicef-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14unicef/14unicef-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14unicef/14unicef-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14unicef/14unicef-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14unicef/14unicef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14unicef/14unicef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/14/world/14unicef/14unicef-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unicef Urges Aid for Syria’s Shattered School System', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking Aid for Syria’s Students', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United Nations Children's Fund", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T04:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2f9b360-a356-5156-b22f-6ff55c976eb7', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2f9b360-a356-5156-b22f-6ff55c976eb7'}, {'abstract': 'Omar Infante, a 31-year-old free agent, agreed to a four-year deal with the Kansas City Royals, according to a person familiar with the deal, which is pending a physical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/sports/baseball/infante-said-to-join-royals.html', 'snippet': 'Omar Infante, a 31-year-old free agent, agreed to a four-year deal with the Kansas City Royals, according to a person familiar with the deal, which is pending a physical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Omar Infante, a 31-year-old free agent, agreed to a four-year deal with the Kansas City Royals, according to a person familiar with the deal, which is pending a physical. The Yankees had offered Infante, who hit .318 with 10 homers for the Detroit Tigers last year, a three-year deal worth about $24 million to replace Robinson Cano at second base. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Infante Said to Join Royals', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Infante Said to Join Royals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Royals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Infante, Omar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T05:06:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/69519a37-3f9f-57ee-8fea-590e64199812', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69519a37-3f9f-57ee-8fea-590e64199812'}, {'abstract': 'Iranian diplomats interrupted nuclear talks after the United States announced an expanded list of companies and individuals whose trading activities it would try to block for evading sanctions against Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/world/middleeast/iran-nuclear-talks-interrupted.html', 'snippet': 'Iranian diplomats interrupted nuclear talks after the United States announced an expanded list of companies and individuals whose trading activities it would try to block for evading sanctions against Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Iranian diplomats involved in nuclear talks with six world powers in Vienna interrupted the discussions on Friday after the United States announced an expanded list of companies and individuals whose trading activities it would try to block for evading sanctions against Iran. The Iranians, suggesting that they needed to consult with officials in Tehran, responded angrily to what the Obama administration characterized as enforcement actions. They said the measures undermined the interim deal reached last month, when Iran was given sanctions relief in exchange for suspending some parts of its nuclear program for six months. “This two-sided game and confusion we are witnessing is not beneficial for the atmosphere of the talks,” Iran’s top negotiator and deputy foreign minister, Abbas Araghchi, told the semiofficial Tasnim news agency on Friday. A spokesman for Catherine Ashton, the European Union’s foreign policy chief and the coordinator of the negotiations with Iran, said the discussions were expected to resume in the near future. But in Tehran on Friday, some politicians called for the acceleration of Iran’s nuclear program. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Nuclear Talks Interrupted', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Nuclear Talks Interrupted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vienna (Austria)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T05:10:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/64ebc59a-93d2-5771-90cb-32ad1f182a3f', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64ebc59a-93d2-5771-90cb-32ad1f182a3f'}, {'abstract': 'Boston Dynamics and its animal kingdom-themed machines bring significant cachet to Google’s robotic efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nyti