yt://article/8edf6ae3-65de-5b75-a4e1-cd01417dad6a'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Ivory overcame injuries, doubts and a dismissal from his first college program to become the team’s most reliable ball carrier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/sports/football/runner-powers-his-way-onto-the-jets-radar.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Ivory overcame injuries, doubts and a dismissal from his first college program to become the team’s most reliable ball carrier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — Fifteen yards and five would-be tacklers stood in front of Chris Ivory against the Oakland Raiders last Sunday, but the Jets’ running backs coach, Anthony Lynn, watched the play unfold as if it had already happened.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sports/dogIVORY/dogIVORY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 474, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/sports/dogIVORY/dogIVORY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 474}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sports/dogIVORY/dogIVORY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sports/dogIVORY/dogIVORY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1616, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sports/dogIVORY/dogIVORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/sports/dogIVORY/dogIVORY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sports/dogIVORY/dogIVORY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Runner Powers His Way Onto the Jets’ Radar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Runner Powers His Way Onto the Jets’ Radar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ivory, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T16:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bb9faa9-8e5a-56a9-a3f5-feec00572050', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bb9faa9-8e5a-56a9-a3f5-feec00572050'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe discusses the budget deal in the House.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-dec-13-2013/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe discusses the budget deal in the House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House of Representatives just passed a budget deal that will likely avert another government shutdown, which could have come as early as next month. This week on Money Talking, regular contributors Joe Nocera and Rana Foroohar of Time magazine discuss what the deal means for businesses and the economy. Plus, Google and other tech companies are calling on the N.S.A. to limit online surveillance of their users.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s “Money Talking”: Dec. 13, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T17:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea39807c-38eb-5850-98c1-15a48faaeb19', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea39807c-38eb-5850-98c1-15a48faaeb19'}, {'abstract': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon’s acrostic kept me humming.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/variety-a-humming-acrostic/', 'snippet': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon’s acrostic kept me humming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — Well, that was a quick and fun one. Maybe I just enjoyed the musical subject. Or maybe Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon heard me whining a few weeks ago about how one of their acrostics had been tough for me, and they eased up on the cluing. Either way, I tore through this one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: A Humming Acrostic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acrostic Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronstadt, Linda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T17:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67808b0e-80bb-5cf1-ad8c-52137ca52845', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67808b0e-80bb-5cf1-ad8c-52137ca52845'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators remain in the dark partly because the facility where the former National Security Agency contractor Edward J. Snowden worked was not equipped with software to monitor employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/us/officials-say-us-may-never-know-extent-of-snowdens-leaks.html', 'snippet': 'Investigators remain in the dark partly because the facility where the former National Security Agency contractor Edward J. Snowden worked was not equipped with software to monitor employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — American intelligence and law enforcement investigators have concluded that they may never know the entirety of what the former National Security Agency contractor Edward J. Snowden extracted from classified government computers before leaving the United States, according to senior government officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials Say U.S. May Never Know Extent of Snowden’s Leaks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officials Say U.S. May Never Know Extent of Snowden’s Leaks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Internat