s': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polygamy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sister Wives (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waddoups, Clark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Kody', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T17:19:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d0fdc8-682f-5377-8675-3d3c1934e9ae', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d0fdc8-682f-5377-8675-3d3c1934e9ae'}, {'abstract': 'The legislature approved an electronic surveillance law that critics feared would markedly expand electronic surveillance of French residents and businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/world/europe/france-broadens-its-surveillance-power.html', 'snippet': 'The legislature approved an electronic surveillance law that critics feared would markedly expand electronic surveillance of French residents and businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — For all their indignation last summer, when the scope of the United States’ mass data collection began to be made public, the French are hardly innocents in the realm of electronic surveillance. Within days of the reports about the National Security Agency’s activities, it was revealed that French intelligence services operated a similar system, with similarly minimal oversight.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Broadens Its Surveillance Power', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Broadens Its Surveillance Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T17:53:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df4383eb-a769-5fcf-81cc-cb7625f2ed45', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df4383eb-a769-5fcf-81cc-cb7625f2ed45'}, {'abstract': 'The days of celebration of Nelson Mandela’s life and the grief at his death tempted some to limit the accolades to him while forgetting the contributions of others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/world/europe/recalling-the-other-heroes-of-the-anti-apartheid-struggle.html', 'snippet': 'The days of celebration of Nelson Mandela’s life and the grief at his death tempted some to limit the accolades to him while forgetting the contributions of others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUSWELL HILL, England — Far from the crowds pressing to offer a final farewell to Nelson Mandela, a lesser tribute yielded a reminder that he was not alone in the struggle for what he called the rainbow nation.', 'prin