_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beckley Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beckley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e5f03b0-311d-5292-b7a9-e61031239934', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e5f03b0-311d-5292-b7a9-e61031239934'}, {'abstract': 'A convicted murderer says he wouldn’t have killed without access to a gun. And if he had one in prison, he might have killed himself.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/a-perspective-on-guns-murder-suicide-from-attica/', 'snippet': 'A convicted murderer says he wouldn’t have killed without access to a gun. And if he had one in prison, he might have killed himself.', 'lead_paragraph': '(This essay accompanies Nicholas Kristof’s Sunday column on guns in America; please comment below on either the Kristof column or this essay by Lennon.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Perspective on Guns, Murder, Suicide from Attica', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T19:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John J. Lennon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lennon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f6b6ba6-bf02-536d-8bc8-f6658824dfb9', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f6b6ba6-bf02-536d-8bc8-f6658824dfb9'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Cotillo is only a high school senior, but after breaking several national baseball stories in recent weeks, he was clearly a source of intrigue a