'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets’ Smith Situation May Mirror Carolina’s in Quarterback Reboot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets’ Smith Situation May Mirror Carolina’s In Quarterback Reboot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carolina Panthers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newton, Cameron J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T19:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/829b7c61-428a-59c0-aa45-9feaf2ca7f01', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/829b7c61-428a-59c0-aa45-9feaf2ca7f01'}, {'abstract': 'In a year spent learning programming code, I internalized a new logic, a different way of looking at information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/opinion/sunday/the-code-of-life.html', 'snippet': 'In a year spent learning programming code, I internalized a new logic, a different way of looking at information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTREAL — AFTER almost 20 years as a working book critic, I’ve come to accept that my line of work is basically a relic of another age. Book buyers now prefer the collective “wisdom” of Amazon reviews; newspapers and magazines, struggling to survive, are devoting less and less space to book matters; and writers are being forced by the economics of the Internet to give their opinions away for little or nothing.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15TECH/15TECH-articleLarge.png', 'height': 4252, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15TECH/15TECH-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 4252}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15TECH/15TECH-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 145, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15TECH/15TECH-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 289, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15TECH/15TECH-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15TECH/15TECH-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15TECH/15TECH-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Code of Life', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Code of Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eggers, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franzen, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Circle (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T19:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Waters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/da30aef4-af2f-5b7b-b0fa-8b1a9d7e18a6', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da30aef4-af2f-5b7b-b0fa-8b1a9d7e18a6'}, {'abstract': 'The university was overjoyed to welcome me. The students were not.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/opinion/sunday/first-encounter-with-the-enemy.html', 'snippet': 'The university was overjoyed to welcome me. The students were not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the late 1950s self-esteem hadn’t yet been invented. High schools saw their sole mission as preparing students thoroughly for academic work. I was the best prepared student in the girls’ school in my New England town. On graduation I won the English prize and the Spanish prize. The university I chose was overjoyed to welcome me, or so its letter of acceptance implied. How prescient — my intellect would no doubt set it on its ivy-covered ear. Also, men would throw themselves in the river for love of me. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/sunday-review/15PEARLMAN/15PEARLMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/sunday-review/15PEARLMAN/15PEARLMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarge