ble for the environment. As counselor to the president, Mr. Podesta, who served as White House chief of staff during President Clinton’s last three years, will have a broad portfolio touching on the economy and congressional relations. But his biggest contribution will be to bring his passion on environmental and energy issues to a president who has to be constantly reminded of their importance.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Return of John Podesta', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Return of John Podesta', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Podesta, John D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jewell, Sally', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T21:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert B. Semple Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf4f68c3-a9ab-5d8c-915a-587fe43824a6', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf4f68c3-a9ab-5d8c-915a-587fe43824a6'}, {'abstract': 'Every single drawing from the lone sketch artist permitted in the terrorist trials is scrutinized by censors, and sometimes defendants, before the military allows public dissemination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/15/opinion/sunday/the-guantanamo-trials-in-pastel.html', 'snippet': 'Every single drawing from the lone sketch artist permitted in the terrorist trials is scrutinized by censors, and sometimes defendants, before the military allows public dissemination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When future historians search back in time to “Camp Justice” and the rigidly controlled, tightly censored terrorist trials in Guantánamo, Cuba, they will likely linger over the vivid courtroom sketches of Janet Hamlin. She is an artist who has doggedly drawn courtroom scenes for the past seven years as the lone sketch artist permitted for the news media, holding a kind of visual monopoly for one of the grimmest, most severely limited sources of pictorial information imaginable.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15editorial/15editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 524, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15editorial/15editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 524}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15editorial/15editorial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15editorial/15editorial-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1028, 'width': 1176, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/sunday-review/15editorial/15editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub