er met or spoken to her. To this day, her online résumé contains false information about her tenure here.\xa0', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/business/15WORKOLOGIST/25-WORKOLOGIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/08/25/business/15WORKOLOGIST/25-WORKOLOGIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/business/15WORKOLOGIST/25-WORKOLOGIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/business/15WORKOLOGIST/25-WORKOLOGIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1049, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/business/15WORKOLOGIST/25-WORKOLOGIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/08/25/business/15WORKOLOGIST/25-WORKOLOGIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/08/25/business/15WORKOLOGIST/25-WORKOLOGIST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Addressing an Awkward History', 'kicker': 'The Workologist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Addressing an Awkward History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T21:24:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac6fbc59-9262-56eb-b38d-511929206ad2', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac6fbc59-9262-56eb-b38d-511929206ad2'}, {'abstract': 'Small niche publishers are seeking a business model that will help them make money from their mobile apps featuring specialized content.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/14/a-missing-revenue-stream-from-mobile-apps/', 'snippet': 'Small niche publishers are seeking a business model that will help them make money from their mobile apps featuring specialized content.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of my favorite guilty pleasures is Susan Miller, a popular New York astrologer who has a cult following online. I read her horoscopes religiously and enjoy following her on Twitter for the fun mix of quirky updates and planetary advice she dispenses.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/15/business/15-BITS/15-BITS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/15/business/15-BITS/15-BITS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty