ragraph': 'In a post-smokestack age, there is only one way for the United States to avoid a declining standard of living, and that is through innovation. Advancements in science and engineering have extended life, employed millions and accounted for more than half of American economic growth since World War II, but they are slowing. The nation has to enlarge its pool of the best and brightest science and math students and encourage them to pursue careers that will keep the country competitive.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Gifted Students Can’t Keep Up', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even Gifted Students Can’t Keep Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifted Students', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-14T23:22:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/be969928-de43-56c2-aee6-2532efc4a301', 'word_count': 1425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be969928-de43-56c2-aee6-2532efc4a301'}, {'abstract': 'Tiny plastic beads used in hundreds of toiletries from facial scrubs to toothpastes are slipping through water treatment plants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/12/15/us/20131215-BEADS.html', 'snippet': 'T