rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bd72ea4-a86f-582e-a92b-56f00e31a3eb', 'word_count': 1485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bd72ea4-a86f-582e-a92b-56f00e31a3eb'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate’s final week in session this year promises to be memorable for something less inspired than its accomplishments: the vast amount of time it spends doing nothing in particular.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/us/politics/congress-prepares-to-leave-behind-a-sluggish-2013.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate’s final week in session this year promises to be memorable for something less inspired than its accomplishments: the vast amount of time it spends doing nothing in particular.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate’s final week in session this year promises to be memorable not for legislative business like the pending budget and defense bills but for something far less inspired: the vast amount of time it spends doing nothing in particular.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Prepares to Wrap Up Sluggish 2013 ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Prepares to Wrap Up Sluggish 2013', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Jeremy W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-15T22:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d562121-6749-5397-99d6-495d0c4240f7', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d562121-6749-5397-99d6-495d0c4240f7'}, {'abstract': 'The winners of the two main pair events at the Fall Nationals in Phoenix this month had at least two things in common.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/crosswords/bridge/life-master-pairs-and-edgar-kaplan-blue-ribbon-winners.html', 'snippet': 'The winners of the two main pair events at the Fall Nationals in Phoenix this month had at least two things in common.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The winners of the two main pair events at the Fall Nationals in Phoenix this month had at least two things in common. First, the partners had not played together in a pair event before. Second, one player in each pair is an American, and the other was born and raised in one country but has represented another country internationally.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/crosswords/bridge/16card/16card-jumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 269, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/crosswords/bridge/16card/16card-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 500, 'width': 269, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/crosswords/bridge/16card/16card-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/16/crosswords/bridge/16card/16card-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/crosswords/bridge/16card/16card-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Master Pairs and Edgar Kaplan Blue Ribbon Winners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-15T22:04:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd5ef549-ccf3-54ae-b20c-5688061c8b80', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd5ef549-ccf3-54ae-b20c-5688061c8b80'}, {'abstract': 'Isaac Mizrahi directed (and designed) this staged production of “Peter & the Wolf” at the Guggenheim, balancing humor for parents with drama and tension for children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/arts/music/peter-the-wolf-at-guggenheim-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Isaac Mizrahi directed (and designed) this staged production of “Peter & the Wolf” at the Guggenheim, balancing humor for parents with drama and tension for children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Devil has the rights to all the best tunes, nobody told Prokofiev. In his 1936 musical fable, “Peter & the Wolf,” the predatory Wolf doesn’t get much of a melody. His menace is usually rendered instead by creepy harmonies from a trio of horns. Peter, the Cat, the hapless Duck, even the grumpy Grandfather: Theirs are the famous tunes that have introduced generations of children to the instruments of the orchestra.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/WOLF/WOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/WOLF/WOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/WOLF/WOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/WOLF/WOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/WOLF/WOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/WOLF/WOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/WOLF/WOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Well-Dressed Wolf Who Is Still Bad to the Bone', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Well-Dressed Wolf Who Is Still Bad to the Bone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mizrahi, Isaac', 'rank