': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e12dd7ee-0368-51bb-8dde-9ee26e4e15d2', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e12dd7ee-0368-51bb-8dde-9ee26e4e15d2'}, {'abstract': 'Exchanges report sharp rise in applications processed for private and public insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/opinion/medicaid-outpaces-private-plans.html', 'snippet': 'Exchanges report sharp rise in applications processed for private and public insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a botched start, the number of people signing up for health insurance plans under the Affordable Care Act has accelerated greatly, with the most substantial gains occurring in Medicaid programs for the poor. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicaid Outpaces Private Plans', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medicaid Outpaces Private Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T01:55:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/82747eef-d812-5013-91bc-ba60af5a39ad', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82747eef-d812-5013-91bc-ba60af5a39ad'}, {'abstract': 'Congress should make it easier for people to challenge their inclusion on the list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/opinion/the-black-hole-of-terrorism-watch-lists.html', 'snippet': 'Congress should make it easier for people to challenge their inclusion on the list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2005, a Stanford doctoral student named Rahinah Ibrahim tried to check in at the San Francisco airport for a flight to a conference in Hawaii. She was traveling with her 14-year-old daughter. Authorities arrested Dr. Ibrahim, a Malaysian citizen, at the ticket counter and detained her in a holding cell for two hours. After she missed her flight, she was released and told that she had mistakenly been placed on the government’s no-fly list. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Black Hole of Terrorism Watch Lists', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Black Hole of Terrorism Watch Lists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Rahinah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALSUP, WILLIAM', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T02:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/42745333-5259-5567-bd08-e2c7e345238a', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42745333-5259-5567-bd08-e2c7e345238a'}, {'abstract': 'Tobacco companies are using trade and investment agreements to challenge and intimidate developing countries as they try to regulate cigarettes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/opinion/big-tobacco-bullies.html', 'snippet': 'Tobacco companies are using trade and investment agreements to challenge and intimidate developing countries as they try to regulate cigarettes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With ever more Americans and Europeans giving up smoking, tobacco companies have increasingly focused on developing countries as markets for their addictive and deadly products. Now, as some of those nations try to regulate cigarettes by, for example, requiring warning labels, Big Tobacco is using trade and investment agreements to challenge and intimidate them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Tobacco Bullies', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Tobacco Bullies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T02:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7fed4ee-dd5a-5209-b557-2f0b3539afd8', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7fed4ee-dd5a-5209-b557-2f0b3539afd8'}, {'abstract': 'Safety measures have been proposed, and state and federal officials should help finance those improvements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/opinion/safer-speeds-on-commuter-rail.html', 'snippet': 'Safety measures have been proposed, and state and federal officials should help finance those improvements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The search for ways to ensure greater safety on commuter trains continues after four people were killed and more than 70 injured on Dec. 1 as a Metro-North train sped into a treacherous turn in the Bronx at 82 miles per hour when the maximum speed should have been 30 miles per hour. The operator, who was described as “zoned out,” has been suspended without pay. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Safer Speeds on Commuter Rail', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safer Speeds on Commuter Rail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-North Commuter Railroad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blumenthal, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T02:05:44+0000',