Microsofts, Googles and Intels — have moved to open retail stores of their own.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/daily-report-creating-retail-experiences-to-match-the-technology/', 'snippet': 'Electronics retailers like Verizon have gone to great lengths in recent months to overhaul their stores, while the heavyweights behind many of the devices — the Microsofts, Googles and Intels — have moved to open retail stores of their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looking for a holiday gift? Come on in. Relax. Take a seat in the leather chair. Welcome to today’s electronics store, Nick Wingfield reports, a place that is now a little like entering a playground crossed with a cocktail lounge, where employees use apps to pilot toy drones and music thumps from arrays of wireless speakers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width':