edcotes, and follow the money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Greg Sargent has been pointing out for some time, the startup troubles of Obamacare have divided both the general public and the political class into two different intellectual universes. On one side, Republicans — both the base and the political leadership — have decided that health reform is already a failure; that conviction is actually helping the leadership rein in some of the crazies, by telling them that now is the time to wait and let the political payoff from Obamacare’s collapse fall into their laps.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Money Bets on Obamacare', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T15:23:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/809da1e0-dcd7-5d9d-846d-b69bc3d2d090', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/809da1e0-dcd7-5d9d-846d-b69bc3d2d090'}, {'abstract': 'FTI Consulting, the business advisory firm, named Steve Gunby its president and chief executive on Monday, succeeding Jack Dunn, who is stepping down after 21 years at the firm.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/fti-consulting-names-new-chief/', 'snippet': 'FTI Consulting, the business advisory firm, named Steve Gunby its president and chief executive on Monday, succeeding Jack Dunn, who is stepping down after 21 years at the firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FTI Consulting, the business advisory firm, named Steve Gunby its president and chief executive on Monday, succeeding Jack B. Dunn IV, who is stepping down after 21 years at the firm.', 'sour