391582-b162-5cce-b13a-144111d6b995'}, {'abstract': 'From 2007 to 2012, 49 federal contractors were cited 1,776 times for large violations and paid millions in penalties.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/when-federal-contractors-break-federal-labor-laws/', 'snippet': 'From 2007 to 2012, 49 federal contractors were cited 1,776 times for large violations and paid millions in penalties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, the federal government awards contracts worth about $500 billion to private sector companies that employ some 26 million workers, or 22 percent of the nation’s work force.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Federal Contractors Break Federal Labor Laws', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Procurement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Steven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T16:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Tritch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tritch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7f398df-d0bd-575c-b4b9-9d7a89f9e43c', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7f398df-d0bd-575c-b4b9-9d7a89f9e43c'}, {'abstract': 'Take a crack at puzzles from Simon Singh’s new book “The Simpsons and Their Mathematical Secrets.”', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/singh/', 'snippet': 'Take a crack at puzzles from Simon Singh’s new book “The Simpsons and Their Mathematical Secrets.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'America’s longest-running sitcom “The Simpsons” has a secret: It’s also one of the smartest shows on TV. Look past the antics of Homer and Bart and you’ll find the show filled with an abundance of mathematics references, thanks to its remarkably nerdy cast of writers. British science and math writer Simon Singh tells the whole story in his new book, “The Simpsons and Their Mathematical Secrets,” in which he introduces us to the writing team behind “The Simpsons” and uncovers many of the mathematical references in the shows. Dr. Singh will also be joining us this week as we take on three challenges from the book. (Click the book cover to download an excerpt from Chapter 4: The Puzzle of Mathematical Humor.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/crosswords/simpsons0/simpsons0-jumbo.png', 'height': 366, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/crosswords/simpsons0/simpsons0-superJumbo.png', 'height': 366, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/crosswords/simpsons0/simpsons0-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/08/crosswords/simpsons0/simpsons0-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/08/crosswords/simpsons0/simpsons0-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Simon Singh Presents ‘The Simpsons and Their Mathematical Secrets’', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': 