'pub_date': '2013-12-16T17:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/352dc826-1ff9-5a32-b962-ae125c735320', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/352dc826-1ff9-5a32-b962-ae125c735320'}, {'abstract': 'The renowned architect has created a new collection for the Swiss brand Caspita inspired by natural cell structures.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/by-design-zaha-hadid-jewelry-designer/', 'snippet': 'The renowned architect has created a new collection for the Swiss brand Caspita inspired by natural cell structures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Zaha Hadid, the Iraq-born, London-based Pritzker prize-winning architect with more than 40 buildings around the globe, also makes jewelry. In 2010, she created a collection for Swarovski, and now she has followed it up with a set of rings and a cuff from lattices of gold filigree for Caspita, the Swiss jewelry brand. Inspired by naturally occurring cell structures, the pieces in the collection, which is called Skein, look like golden honeycomb, as if assembled by bees. Some are studded with diamonds. Polygons form a delicate mesh that envelops the finger, a shape that is reminiscent of Hadid’s Al Wakrah stadium in Qatar. In fact, she acknowledges, “There is a lot of fluidity now between jewelry design, architecture and art — a lot more cross-pollination in the disciplines.” The collection was introduced earlier this month at Colette’s pop-up at Art Basel in Miami Beach and at the Zaha Hadid Design Gallery in London last week. It goes on sale online today at Latest Revival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By Design | Zaha Hadid, Jewelry Designer', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadid, Zaha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swarovski AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T17:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddb1641e-aeca-5b75-ade3-4dca9cd9c5e5', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddb1641e-aeca-5b75-ade3-4dca9cd9c5e5'}, {'abstract': 'Also on the Minute, music education and bargain shopping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/minute/2013/12/16/times-minute-china-joins-the-moon-club/', 'snippet': 'Also on the Minute, music education and bargain shopping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Video', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Minute | China Joins the Moon Club', 'kicker': 'The New York Times News Minute', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T17:13:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carrie Halperin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carrie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Halperin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a99fdf7-4fd0-5e4f-acee-18b7b9b633a0', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a99fdf7-4fd0-5e4f-acee-18b7b9b633a0'}, {'abstract': 'A woman caught between her gay sister and anti-gay brother wants to know if they can reunite years later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/booming/can-peace-come-to-a-family-a-brother-destroyed-because-his-sister-is-gay.html', 'snippet': 'A woman caught between her gay sister and anti-gay brother wants to know if they can reunite years later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Dear Civil Behavior: Almost 30 years ago, my older brother gave my parents an ultimatum — disown my little sister, who had just revealed she was gay, or he would cut himself and his family off from the rest of us. My parents refused to do such a thing and my brother made good on his threat and destroyed our family. I stood with my sister and have not seen or spoken to my big brother or any of his family since his declaration so long ago. Neither has my sister. Time has not healed the wounds of our family. On his deathbed, my dad asked me never to forget what my brother did to all of us and I promised him I would not — and I refuse to forgive him. My mother has forgiven my brother — and I’m glad for her. I also know my mom dearly wishes to have her family together before she dies. My question: Should I honor my father’s deathbed request or my mother’s final wish? — Straight Sister in the Middle', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/12/18/booming/18civil-booming-inlaws/18civil-booming-inlaws-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Peace Come to a Family a Brother ‘Destroyed’ Because His Sister Is Gay?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T17:14:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Petrow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Petrow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/399819c3-c9a4-5662-ad83-e1e30c349dc0', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/399819c3-c9a4-5662-ad83-e1e30c349dc0'}, {'abstract': 'Also on the Minute, music education and bargain shopping.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000002605617/times-minute-china-joins-the-moon-club.html', 'snippet': 'Also on the Minute, music education and bargain shopping.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Also on the Minute, music education and bargain shopping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ran