 Ayatollah Youssef Saanei, who has preached a reformist politcal line, spoke with The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/interview-with-an-ayatollah/', 'snippet': 'Grand Ayatollah Youssef Saanei, who has preached a reformist politcal line, spoke with The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'QOM, Iran – When it comes to Iranian clerics, Grand Ayatollah Youssef Saanei has long defied convention. Over the years, he has issued edicts that uphold women’s rights. He also preaches what in this society is a reformist political line and advocates rapprochement between Iran and the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interview With an Ayatollah', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T19:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f9cf906-b98d-57c8-aca3-7c16638f27b0', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f9cf906-b98d-57c8-aca3-7c16638f27b0'}, {'abstract': 'A compromise plan now seems to have enough votes to overcome a filibuster threat in the Senate and move on to passage by a simple majority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/us/politics/hatch-joins-other-republicans-in-supporting-budget-deal.html', 'snippet': 'A compromise plan now seems to have enough votes to overcome a filibuster threat in the Senate and move on to passage by a simple majority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Support for a compromise two-year budget deal grew ahead of a Tuesday vote in the Senate as Republicans concluded they could not allow a measure that passed the House with overwhelming bipartisan support to die in Congress’s upper chamber.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/us/CONG/CONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/us/CONG/CONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/us/CONG/CONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/us/CONG/CONG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/us/CONG/CONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/17/us/CONG/CONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/us/CONG/CONG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Budget Deal Heads for Senate Approval as More Republicans Give Support', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Deal Heads for Senate Approval as More Republicans Give Support', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T19:43:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7610568d-ba3d-5f05-8b11-5f2e1b2e0779', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7610568d-ba3d-5f05-8b11-5f2e1b2e0779'}, {'abstract': '“12 Years a Slave” and “American Hustle” pull in a slew of nominations from critics’ groups across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/clarity-grows-for-front-runners-at-least-among-critics-groups/', 'snippet': '“12 Years a Slave” and “American Hustle” pull in a slew of nominations from critics’ groups across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This season’s multitudinous race may finally be getting some shape, as the critical and industry love add up. The Broadcast Film Critics Association, which bills itself as the largest critics group in the United States and Canada, announced its picks Monday, and members were evenly split between “American Hustle” and “12 Years a Slave,” which both earned 13 nominations, including best picture, director, actor, screenplay (original and adapted, respectively) and ensemble.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clarity Grows f