ettlement in the N.F.L. concussion case appointed a special master to help analyze the final agreement, which could be filed in days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The judge overseeing the proposed $765 million settlement between the N.F.L. and more than 6,000 players who sued the league for negligence and fraud has appointed a special master to help analyze the final agreement, which could be filed in days.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In N.F.L. Case, Help in Analyzing Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In N.F.L. Case, Help in Analyzing Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brody, Anita B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morton, Craig', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T21:06:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8d0d8d1-5278-5dd6-a749-f52cb212c67a', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8d0d8d1-5278-5dd6-a749-f52cb212c67a'}, {'abstract': 'Biologists have found that savannah monitor lizards extract oxygen from the air when inhaling and when exhaling — a trait, known as unidirectional breathing, that is most associated with birds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/science/breathe-in-breathe-out.html', 'snippet': 'Biologists have found that savannah monitor lizards extract oxygen from the air when inhaling and when exhaling — a trait, known as unidirectional breathing, that is most associated with birds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Biologists have found that savannah monitor lizards extract oxygen from the air when inhaling and when exhaling — a characteristic, known as unidirectional breathing, that is most associated with birds. The discovery of this trait in lizards, reported in the journal Nature, raises questions about when and why it evolved. Either it developed in the 270-million-year-old common ancestor of lizards, birds and alligators (which were also recently found to practice unilateral breathing) — much longer ago than originally thought — or it developed independently in each evolutionary branch. As for why it evolved, the long-held theory that it aided flight in birds appears to need updating. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17floater/17floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17floater/17floater-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17floater/17floater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17floater/17floater-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17floater/17floater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c