times.com/2013/12/16/conservative-wonks-conservative-politicians-and-recessions/', 'snippet': 'It’s not just the dumb politicos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Barro has a good but incomplete post about the conservative inability to deal in any meaningful way with the reality of recessions. As he says, GOP policy prescriptions — deregulate, cut spending (especially on the poor), and cut taxes (on the rich) — are the same when unemployment is above 9 percent as when it is below 5. “How,” he asks, “can a political ideology have nothing to say about how to address recessions?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservative Wonks, Conservative Politicians, and Recessions', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T21:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5238107b-b170-59f4-9f6b-bd1e49df5dca', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5238107b-b170-59f4-9f6b-bd1e49df5dca'}, {'abstract': 'By recognizing the role of marginal utility, we can avoid the costly mistake of expecting the new shoes we buy today to make us happier than the pair we bought last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/your-money/how-to-react-to-diminishing-returns.html', 'snippet': 'By recognizing the role of marginal utility, we can avoid the costly mistake of expecting the new shoes we buy today to make us happier than the pair we bought last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first piece of pumpkin pie is a real treat. The second piece might be good. But we may almost have to force ourselves to eat the third. Instead of enjoying it, we’re miserable. Why doesn’t the last piece taste as good as the first?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/business/121613bucks-carl-sketch/121613bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/16/business/121613bucks-carl-sketch/121613bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/business/121613bucks-carl-sketch/121613bucks-carl-sketch-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 527, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/business/121613bucks-carl-sketch/121613bucks-carl-sketch-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1054, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/business/121613bucks-carl-sketch/121613bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/16/business/121613bucks-carl-sketch/121613bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/business/121613bucks-carl-sketch/121613bucks-carl-sketch-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to React to Diminishing Returns', 'kicker': 'The Sketch Guy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T21:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78a1181a-36a2-5ad3-83e4-a569a03e5324', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78a1181a-36a2-5ad3-83e4-a569a03e5324'}, {'abstract': 'León won Mexico’s Apertura title on Sunday when it defeated Club América, 3-1, to win the two-game series, 5-1, on aggregate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/sports/soccer/in-mexico-leon-is-on-top.html', 'snippet': 'León won Mexico’s Apertura title on Sunday when it defeated Club América, 3-1, to win the two-game series, 5-1, on aggregate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The culmination of the Apertura (opening) season Sunday night did not quite rise to the suspense and drama of a Mexican telenovela, but it came pretty close.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/sports/soccer/17leon1/17leon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/sports/soccer/17leon1/17leon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/sports/soccer/17leon1/17leon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/sports/soccer/17leon1/17leon1-sup