n her return to fiction writing with “The Signature of All Things,” the author Elizabeth Gilbert found that the process can be familiar yet liberating from the constraints of nonfiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Read Around,” a weekly video feature, authors discuss the when, where and how behind their books. Below, the author Elizabeth Gilbert, who has returned to fiction writing with “The Signature of All Things,” talks about how the process can be familiar yet liberating from the constraints of nonfiction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Read Around: Video of Elizabeth Gilbert', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T21:53:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fabf6faa-5227-5b17-821d-683730694171', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fabf6faa-5227-5b17-821d-683730694171'}, {'abstract': 'Remember how good we thought they were supposed to be for us? Well, not really, some doctors say, with one medical journal editorial arguing that they were a waste of money.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/a-challenge-to-vitamins/', 'snippet': 'Remember how good we thought they were supposed to be for us? Well, not really, some doctors say, with one medical journal editorial arguing that they were a waste of money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One in two adults takes a daily vitamin pill, and Americans spend tens of billions of dollars each year on supplements. Now, a small coterie of physicians writing in a leading medical journal has offered this blunt advice: “Stop wasting money.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17CONSUMER/17CONSUMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17CONSUMER/17CONSUMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17CONSUMER/17CONSUMER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17CONSUMER/17CONSUMER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1261, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17CONSUMER/17CONSUMER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17CONSUMER/17CONSUMER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17CONSUMER/17CONSUMER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should We Toss Our Vitamin Pills?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Challenge to Vitamins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dietary Supplements and Herbal Remedies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'su