s “Wind von West” at the Peter Jay Sharp Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the German choreographer Pina Bausch died in 2009, a wave of melancholy fell over the New York dance world: even though her company is based in Wuppertal, it was a fixture at the Brooklyn Academy of Music. Yet her ties to the city ran even deeper, since she had also studied at the Juilliard School. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Plot, Just Poetry in a Gauzy Landscape', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Plot, Just Poetry In a Gauzy Landscape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bausch, Pina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard School', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Folkwang University of the Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T22:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f7f16fe-33c0-5734-acd8-d7f8d5feec62', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f7f16fe-33c0-5734-acd8-d7f8d5feec62'}, {'abstract': 'A normal toddler and a violent criminal may have much in common. Researchers are discovering that aggression may occur in people who have never outgrown their terrible twos.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/terrible-twos-who-stay-terrible/', 'snippet': 'A normal toddler and a violent criminal may have much in common. Researchers are discovering that aggression may occur in people who have never outgrown their terrible twos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To understand the violent criminal, says Richard E. Tremblay, imagine a 2-year-old boy doing the things that make the terrible twos terrible — grabbing, kicking, pushing, punching, biting.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17MIND/17MIND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17MIND/17MIND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17MIND/17MIND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17MIND/17MIND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1949, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17MIND/17MIND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17MIND/17MIND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/science/17MIND/17MIND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Terrible Twos Who Stay Terrible', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Terrible Twos Who Stay Terrible', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-16T22:31:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Dobbs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dobbs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d6dbeee-c9de-56d8-b093-7ac50ea03736', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d6dbeee-c9de-56d8-b093-7ac50ea03736'}, {'abstract': 'Francis Bacon’s “Three Studies of Lucian Freud,” which sold for $142 million last month, will be shown at the Portland Art Museum in Oregon.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/bacons-triptych-to-be-shown-at-portland-art-museum/', 'snippet': 'Francis Bacon’s “Three Studies of Lucian Freud,” which sold for $142 million last month, will be shown at the Portland Art Museum in Oregon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Portland Art Museum in Oregon announced on Monday afternoon that the world’s most expensive painting ever sold at auction — Francis Bacon’s triptych “Three Studies of Lucian Freud” — which brought $142.4 million at Christie’s in November, will be on view there from Dec. 21 through March 30th.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/16artsbeat-bacon/16artsbeat-bacon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/16/arts/16artsbeat-bacon/16artsbeat-bacon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/art