{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/69a01f94-79ae-54ba-8c50-76b45c46d3e7', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69a01f94-79ae-54ba-8c50-76b45c46d3e7'}, {'abstract': 'The violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter included contemporary and classic works in her program at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/arts/music/anne-sophie-mutter-returns-to-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter included contemporary and classic works in her program at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By her New York recital debut at Carnegie Hall in 1988, the violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter, then 25, had evolved from teenage phenom to mature, adventurous artist. Earlier that year, she had demonstrated her burgeoning interest in contemporary music and her already formidable influence, requesting — and getting — from the eminent composer Witold Lutoslawski a version for violin and orchestra of his 1984 Partita for Violin and Piano.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/17MUTTER/17MUTTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/17MUTTER/17MUTTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/17MUTTER/17MUTTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/17MUTTER/17MUTTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'wid