 for animal husbandry. He was sentenced to five years in jail. But the Supreme Court granted him bail on Friday after noting that most of those convicted with Mr. Prasad in the case had already been freed while their appeals were considered. Such appeals often take many years to be decided. When he emerged from jail on Monday, Mr. Prasad pronounced it a fine place for politicians. “Jail is the birthplace of Lord Krishna,” Mr. Prasad said. “I was never unhappy in jail.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India: Ex-Official Released on Bail', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Ex-Official Released on Bail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prasad, Lalu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Hari', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T01:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e51c6a3-0971-5519-a11d-495cffb2ac04', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e51c6a3-0971-5519-a11d-495cffb2ac04'}, {'abstract': 'Cities still reeling from the recession are challenging the billions of dollars in tax breaks granted to the nation’s nonprofit hospitals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/us/benefits-questioned-in-tax-breaks-for-nonprofit-hospitals.html', 'snippet': 'Cities still reeling