, 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T01:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/72d81452-1e25-5ba3-978c-a877fd7b23de', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72d81452-1e25-5ba3-978c-a877fd7b23de'}, {'abstract': 'Members of Russia’s security services killed four men suspected of being militants when they stormed an apartment building after a tense overnight standoff in the North Caucasus region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/world/europe/russia-north-caucasus-raid.html', 'snippet': 'Members of Russia’s security services killed four men suspected of being militants when they stormed an apartment building after a tense overnight standoff in the North Caucasus region.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Members of Russia’s security services killed four men suspected of being militants on Monday when they stormed an apartment building after a tense overnight standoff in the North Caucasus region, where Russia is trying to stamp out an insurgency. In a statement, the government’s National Antiterrorism Committee said that heavily armed troops supported by armored vehicles surrounded the building in the village of Bedyk in the republic of Kabardino-Balkaria on Sunday evening, acting on a tip that armed men were inside. A woman and a child left the house during the negotiations, but the men refused to surrender, officials said. Troops assaulted the building early Monday morning, killing all four men inside, including the group’s leader, Arsen Khandokhov. The Federal Security Service said that Mr. Khandokhov and his group were behind more than 20 terrorist attacks, including the murder of two tourists in the region in 2010. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'sourc