e/a4370b7a-c98e-5d27-8e46-a766dcb0b59f'}, {'abstract': 'How to make readers want to know more about your characters.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/16/secrets-and-contradictions/', 'snippet': 'How to make readers want to know more about your characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I know a compelling character when I encounter her on the page. Her simplicity betrays an enigmatic complexity, and her known qualities suggest unknown ones. She possesses the one thing I want most from a character: the power to make me want to know more about her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secrets and Contradictions', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T02:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corbett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1dea849-b29c-5f8d-9d2e-98587f1817e0', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1dea849-b29c-5f8d-9d2e-98587f1817e0'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth P. Thompson, in a letter to the departing District Attorney Charles J. Hynes, protested “a potential gross overpayment” for unused vacation to Michael F. Vecchione, who recently retired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/nyregion/brooklyns-next-prosecutor-protests-286000-payment-to-hynes-deputy.html', 'snippet': 'Kenneth P. Thompson, in a letter to the departing District Attorney Charles J. Hynes, protested “a potential gross overpayment” for unused vacation to Michael F. Vecchione, who recently retired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brushing aside the objections of the man who made him an electoral lame duck, Charles J. Hynes, the departing Brooklyn district attorney, announced on Monday that he would pay his retiring top deputy almost $286,000 in unused vacation pay, or almost $100,000 more than what a typical city employee could be entitled to.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/nyregion/HYNES/HYNES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 493, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/nyregion/HYNES/HYNES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 493, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/nyregion/HYNES/HYNES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/17/nyregion/HYNES/HYNES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/nyregion/HYNES/HYNES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn’s Next Prosecutor Protests $286,000 Payment to Hynes Deputy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brooklyn’s Next Prosecutor Protests $286,000 Payment to Hynes Deputy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Kenneth P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, David W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value