pe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25dbafc5-c44e-5502-92c0-55180d62f01a', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25dbafc5-c44e-5502-92c0-55180d62f01a'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the more outlandish ideas held by the iconic inventor and futurist are celebrated in a lovingly produced new tome by the Portland. Ore., graphic designer Cole Gerst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/t-magazine/gallery-paying-tribute-to-buckminster-fuller.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the more outlandish ideas held by the iconic inventor and futurist are celebrated in a lovingly produced new tome by the Portland. Ore., graphic designer Cole Gerst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most architecture aficionados, the name Buckminster Fuller conjures a single structure: the geodesic dome. The geometrically complex sphere, composed of a grid of triangles, may be Fuller’s most famous invention, but the late visionary dedicated himself to solving many of the world’s most vexing design problems, including affordable housing, efficient transportation and ecological preservation. While more than 300,000 geodesic domes have been built according to his plans, Fuller was far more prolific, producing 28 patents in total and publishing 28 books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paying Tribute to the Mad Genius of Buckminster Fuller', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marissa Gluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc7b2cc-711e-51a6-88a3-29ca5a42fa4c', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc7b2cc-711e-51a6-88a3-29ca5a42fa4c'}, {'abstract': 'Even as some conservatives acknowledge the value of a social safety net, public support for aid to the needy is falling, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/who-pays-the-taxes-and-get-the-benefits/', 'snippet': 'Even as some conservatives acknowledge the value of a social safety net, public support for aid to the needy is falling, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform — Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/business/17dec-economist-bartlett2/17dec-economist-bartlett2-articleLarge.png', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/business/17dec-economist-bartlett2/17dec-economist-bartlett2-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/business/17dec-economist-bartlett2/17dec-economist-bartlett2-jumbo.png', 'height': 486, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/business/17dec-economist-bartlett2/17dec-economist-bartlett2-superJumbo.png', 'height': 486, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, '