cy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/17/booming/17match-booming-beatles/17match-booming-beatles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/booming/17match-booming-beatles/17match-booming-beatles-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Beatles’ ‘I Want to Hold Your Hand,’ Then Al Green’s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Al', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'APPLE, FIONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wainwright, Rufus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T05:11:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Val Haller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Val', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a32c54c3-de42-5d57-b13c-018bae1773ec', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a32c54c3-de42-5d57-b13c-018bae1773ec'}, {'abstract': 'The former basketball star Dennis Rodman, who befriended the nation’s leader, Kim Jong-un, was due to arrive Thursday to train its top players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/world/asia/rodman-headed-to-north-korea-again-despite-turmoil.html', 'snippet': 'The former basketball star Dennis Rodman, who befriended the nation’s leader, Kim Jong-un, was due to arrive Thursday to train its top players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dennis Rodman’s trip to North Korea to help train the country’s basketball stars has not been disrupted by the political convulsions there, notably the execution of the leader’s uncle last week for treason and debauchery, the Irish online betting company sponsoring the visit said Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodman Headed to North Korea Again Despite Turmoil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rodman Headed to North Korea Again Despite Turmoil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodman, Dennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T05:28:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2a99f39-3668-5063-9745-9f480bb5688a', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2a99f39-3668-5063-9745-9f480bb5688a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:30 A.M. (MoreMax) ANNA KARENINA (2012) Keira Knightley (above) stars as Anna, the bored wife of a virtuous government official (Jude Law) in mid-19th-century Imperial Russia, who travels from St. Petersburg to Moscow to calm a marital storm in the household of her philandering brother (Matthew Macfadyen) in Joe Wright’s stagy adaptation of this Tolstoy novel. Aaron Taylor-Johnson plays the man who captures her heart: Count Vronsky, a young military officer with the eyes of a poet and a domineering mother (Olivia Williams). And Alicia Vikander is Kitty, a lovely young woman adored by Levin, the gloomy rural landowner (Domhnall Gleeson) widely understood to be Tolstoy’s alter ego, whose idea of love — an ennobling union of souls — is a rebuke to the amorality festering in cities. “I assume you know that it ends badly, but Mr. Wright’s real interest, like Tolstoy’s, is in everything that happens in between Anna’s first meeting with Vronsky and her final encounter with the wheels of a train,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. And while Mr. Wright’s screen versions of Jane Austen’s “Pride and Prejudice” and Ian McEwan’s “Atonement” “remain trapped in literariness,” he added, “Mr. Wright’s ‘Anna Karenina’ is different. It is risky and ambitious enough to count as an act of artistic hubris, and confident enough to triumph on its own slightly — wonderfully — crazy terms. Pious Tolstoyans may knit their brows about the stylistic liberties Mr. Wright and the screenwriter, Tom Stoppard, have taken, but surely Tolstoy can withstand (and may indeed benefit from) their playful, passionate rendering of his masterpiece.” Jacqueline Durran won an Oscar for costume design.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/129c15b0-8216-56d0-817d-54eda18a55a0', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/129c15b0-8216-56d0-817d-54eda18a55a0'}, {'abstract': 'A new book by the New York photographer Briana Blasko, ‘Dance of the Weave,’ captures Indian dancers’ interaction with fabric through movement.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/where-dance-and-textiles-meet/', 'snippet': 'A new book by the New York photographer Briana Blasko, ‘Dance of the Weave,’ captures Indian dancers’ interaction with fabric through movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This “Dance of the Weave” book project — documenting the interplay\xa0of dancers and the myriad hues, textures, drapes and moods of their costumes — began\xa0as a collaboration with\xa0Upasana, a design studio near\xa0Pondicherry\xa0that\xa0works with handloom weavers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Dance and Textiles Meet', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Varanasi (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T06:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Briana Blasko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Briana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blasko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71fc28dd-2602-52b3-a4c1-5b786187f0d6', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71fc28dd-2602-52b3-a4c1-5b786187f0d6'}, {'abstract': 'Farming women gathered outside a provincial government headquarters and formed a human pyramid to highlight what they say is the widespread deprivation of their economic and other rights.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/rural-women-stage-innovative-protest-for-equality/', 'snippet': 'Farming women gathered outside a provincial government headquarters and formed a human pyramid to highlight what they say is the widespread deprivation of their economic and other rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The middle-aged farming women forming a human pyramid in front of the Zhejiang Provincial People’s Government headquarters in Hangzhou last week constituted a small protest that pointed to a big problem: persistent economic and political discrimination against women in rural China, they said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rural Women Stage Innovative Protest for Equality', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Landesa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hangzhou (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T07:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a32a804-02a2-5c51-aed7-df753ed9af18', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a32a804-02a2-5c51-aed7-df753ed9af18'}, {'abstract': 'China has about 350 million smokers, and despite efforts to reduce consumption, tobacco is still widely consumed with about half of adult males smoking regularly, according to surveys.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/amid-chinas-bad-air-a-reminder-that-smoking-still-kills/', 'snippet': 'China has about 350 million smokers, and despite efforts to reduce consumption, tobacco is still widely consumed with about half of adult males smoking regularly, according to surveys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the recognition of the danger of outdoor air pollution in China grows, health authorities are trying to use that knowledge to raise awareness of an even deadlier health threat: smoking. China has about 350 million smokers, and despite efforts to reduce consumption, tobacco is still widely consumed, and about half of adult males are regular smokers, according to surveys.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid China’s Bad Air, a Reminder That Smoking Still Kills', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beijing News, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harbin (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T07:18:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 's