aby Boomers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Dating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Match.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T13:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Hogan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hogan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/589edae8-87e6-5f13-a880-4868bba43a1b', 'word_count': 1376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/589edae8-87e6-5f13-a880-4868bba43a1b'}, {'abstract': 'There are fewer and fewer places we can really be ourselves online. And maybe Instagram Direct is a response to that.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/instagram-direct-and-the-evolution-of-privacy/', 'snippet': 'There are fewer and fewer places we can really be ourselves online. And maybe Instagram Direct is a response to that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Thursday, Kevin Systrom invited members of the press to a fashionably shabby loft in Manhattan to introduce a new messaging service called Instagram Direct.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/technology/16bits-instagram-2/16bits-instagram-2-articleLarge.png', 'height': 1065, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/16/technology/16bits-instagram-2/16bits-instagram-2-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1065}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/technology/16bits-instagram-2/16bits-instagram-2-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/technology/16bits-instagram-2/16bits-instagram-2-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1136, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/technology/16bits-instagram-2/16bits-instagram-2-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/16/technology/16bits-instagram-2/16bits-instagram-2-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/16/technology/16bits-instagram-2/16bits-instagram-2-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Instagram Direct and the Fracturing of Privacy', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T13:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74630df8-aa09-5cf9-9c27-8880d7cb49ad', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74630df8-aa09-5cf9-9c27-8880d7cb49ad'}, {'abstract': 'A performance from the music director and lead performer of a new musical revue featuring the songs of the composer Burt Bacharach.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/in-performance-kyle-riabko-of-whats-it-all-about-bacharach-reimagined/', 'snippet': 'A performance from the music director and lead performer of a new musical revue featuring the songs of the composer Burt Bacharach.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What’s It All About? Bacharach Reimagined” is a new revue devoted to the music of the composer Burt Bacharach and the lyricist Hal David. The production features musical arrangements by the 26-year-old singer Kyle Riabko, who also stars in the show. In this scene Mr. Riabko plays his arrangement of the songs “Anyone Who Had a Heart,” “This Guy’s In Love With You” and “Alfie.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Kyle Riabko of ‘What’s It All About? Bacharach Reimagined’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T13:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7469d1bd-78b7-55c3-b226-dcdbd127ef56', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7469d1bd-78b7-55c3-b226-dcdbd127ef56'}, {'abstract': 'Most anecdotal ledes are fine in themselves. But the device seems rote and shopworn if a reader encounters one story after another with the same approach. There are many, many ways to start a non-straight-news story; we should look harder for alternatives.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/the-stranger-in-the-lede-2/', 'snippet': 'Most anecdotal ledes are fine in themselves. But the device seems rote and shopworn if a reader encounters one story after another with the same approach. There are many, many ways to start a non-straight-news story; we should look harder for alte...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doing holiday duty on Thanksgiving — when breaking news can be hard to find — reminded me just how often our feature and enterprise stories rely on that old journalistic staple, the anecdotal lead. It seemed that practically every story discussed for the front page started out by introducing me, by name, to some stranger whose connection to the point of the article would emerge only with time and patience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Stranger in the Story', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T13:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By PHILIP B. CORBETT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95ba4d38-f1d6-5433-b053-4977d599557d', 'word_count': 2657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95ba4d38-f1d6-5433-b053-4977d599557d'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers on Tuesday demanded Asok Kumar Ganguly, a retired Supreme Court justice, step down from a West Bengal commission after he was accused of harassing a law intern.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/calls-grow-louder-for-human-rights-chairman-to-resign-after-harassment-complaint/', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers on Tuesday demanded Asok Kumar Ganguly, a retired Supreme Court justice, step down from a West Bengal commission after he was accused of harassing a law intern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Lawmakers in the Rajya Sabha, the upper house of Parliament, joined women’s rights groups on Tuesday in calling for the resignation of the West Bengal Human Rights Commission chairman, who is accused of sexually harassing a law intern last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calls Grow Louder for Human Rights Chairman to Resign After Harassment Complaint', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T13:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By HARI KUMAR', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KUMAR', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8548f20a-fa30-5092-819f-dba61043cc66', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8548f20a-fa30-5092-819f-dba61043cc66'}, {'abstract': 'A new collection of Beatles recordings from 1963 appears suddenly on iTunes in a few countries, then vanished.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/a-quick-mystery-tour-for-official-beatles-bootleg/', 'snippet': 'A new collection of Beatles recordings from 1963 appears suddenly on iTunes in a few countries, then vanished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new collection of previously unreleased Beatles tracks that fans have been expecting since word of the project leaked last week has turned out to be a bit like a solar eclipse: if you were on the wrong side of the world, or weren’t paying attention, you missed it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quick Mystery Tour for Official Beatles ‘Bootleg’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': No