laces-postcards-promo-thumbLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Postcards From Our Places to Go in 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T15:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ca7be07b-0ec3-5359-8b36-2e4dedc2a722', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ca7be07b-0ec3-5359-8b36-2e4dedc2a722'}, {'abstract': 'The Black List, an annual look at the best unproduced scripts in circulation, includes two retellings of the making of “Jaws” and two stories involving Mr. Rogers.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/next-years-screenplay-nominees/', 'snippet': 'The Black List, an annual look at the best unproduced scripts in circulation, includes two retellings of the making of “Jaws” and two stories involving Mr. Rogers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the tightest contests in this season’s highly competitive Oscar race are the screenplay categories. For original stories, will the Academy favor ones based on fact, like “American Hustle,” “Inside Llewyn Davis” and “Dallas Buyers Club,” or wholly invented cinema, like the romance “Her”? On the adapted side, will voters go with historical epics like “12 Years a Slave” or reward long character arcs, as in “Before Midnight”? The Bagger will investigate, ponder and pontificate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/jaws/jaws-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 255, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/jaws/jaws-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 255}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/jaws/jaws-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/jaws/jaws-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/jaws/jaws-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/jaws/jaws-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/jaws/jaws-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Next Year’s Screenplay Nominees?', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T15:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab00f0cc-7f1d-5f4f-9721-f7010911c30e', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab00f0cc-7f1d-5f4f-9721-f7010911c30e'}, {'abstract': 'In 1913, The New York Herald described “quaint and curious” toys for the festive season.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/17/1913-toys-for-christmas-are-marked-by-grotesqueness/', 'snippet': 'In 1913, The New York Herald described “quaint and curious” toys for the festive season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — “A Merry Christmas!” The year has passed so rapidly, a year so crowded with so many notable events, historical, political, social, tragical, that one can hardly realize that the season which is supposed to bring with it “peace on earth” is so near. But there it is; “A Merry Christmas!” in flaming electrically illuminated crystal device in front of Gamage’s, the greatest of London’s toy emporiums, and the delight of the children returning home from school for the Christmas holidays.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1913: Toys For Christmas Are Marked by Grotesqueness', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T15:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70a67323-8089-5640-8704-8c4578ca4c8c', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70a67323-8089-5640-8704-8c4578ca4c8c'}, {'abstract': 'A bipartisan tax-and-spending plan cleared its final hurdle on Tuesday, with 67 senators voting to end debate on the measure and bring it to a final vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/us/politics/budget-deal.html', 'snippet': 'A bipartisan tax-and-spending plan cleared its final hurdle on Tuesday, with 67 senators voting to end debate on the measure and bring it to a final vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A bipartisan tax-and-spending plan designed to bring some normalcy to Congress’s budgeting after three years of chaos cleared its final hurdle on Tuesday when 67 senators voted to end debate on the measure and bring it to a final vote before it goes to President Obama for his signature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Ends Budget Debate, Clearing Way for Passage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Patty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T15:37:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4792cc09-09b2-51d9-ad52-dea88f92dc0c', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4792cc09-09b2-51d9-ad52-dea88f92dc0c'}, {'abstract': 'Pitcher Masahiro Tanaka told his Japanese league team that he wants to play in Major League Baseball next season, but the team, Rakuten, does not want him to go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/sports/baseball/tanaka-wants-to-play-in-mlb-but-club-balks-at-the-idea.html', 'snippet': 'Pitcher Masahiro Tanaka told his Japanese league team that he wants to play in Major League Baseball next season, but the team, Rakuten, does not want him to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the battle for Japanese stars, Major League Baseball got its way this week when it persuaded Nippon Professional Baseball to accept a $20 million cap on compensation paid to Japanese teams whose players leave for the United States before they become free agents.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/sports/baseball/18base/18base-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/18/sports/baseball/18base/18base-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 799}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/sports/baseball/18base/18base-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/sports/baseball/18base/18base-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1539, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/sports/baseball/18base/18base-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/18/sports/baseball/18base/18base-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/1