 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T16:20:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/675e3ed6-ca67-5ca3-9482-f2cf8acfbb76', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/675e3ed6-ca67-5ca3-9482-f2cf8acfbb76'}, {'abstract': 'The former National Security Agency contractor Edward J. Snowden, who had requested asylum from Brazil months ago, made the offer in a letter published in a Brazilian newspaper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/world/americas/snowden-offers-to-help-brazil-in-nsa-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'The former National Security Agency contractor Edward J. Snowden, who had requested asylum from Brazil months ago, made the offer in a letter published in a Brazilian newspaper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — Edward J. Snowden, the former contractor for the National Security Agency now living temporarily in Russia, said in comments published on Tuesday that he was prepared to assist Brazilian investigations into American spying in Brazil. But he said he could not speak freely until a country granted him permanent political asylum, which he requested from Brazil months ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snowden Offers Help to Brazil in Spy Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Snowden Offers Help to Brazil in Spy Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-17T16:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0501f5b-4085-5b34-aa37-85142a0e24b8', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0501f5b-4085-5b34-aa37-85142a0e24b8'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Totter is most remembered for her work in the 1940s in movies like “The Postman Always Rings Twice” and “Lady in the Lake.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/movies/audrey-totter-actress-in-noir-films-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Totter is most remembered for her work in the 1940s in movies like “The Postman Always Rings Twice” and “Lady in the Lake.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Audrey Totter, who as a femme-fatale star of Hollywood’s noir films of the 1940s could twist daggers with the subtlest arch of her perfectly plucked eyebrows, died on Thursday in West Hills, Calif. She was 95, and it had been decades since she last committed a crime — most were of the heart — on the silver screen.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/sub-Obit-Totter/sub-Obit-Totter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/sub-Obit-Totter/sub-Obit-Totter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlarg