om/2013/12/17/cocktail-culture-a-gin-thats-designed-to-be-drunk-like-whiskey/', 'snippet': 'Beefeater’s new Reserve Barrel Aged Gin, meant to be enjoyed undiluted by tonic or vermouth, joins the ranks of after-dinner spirits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has become de rigueur for the great spirit houses to put out ultrapremium expressions of their core products. A standout this season is Beefeater’s Burrough’s Reserve Barrel Aged Gin, a fairly radical reimagining of the historic brand’s classic liquid. The company’s Master Distiller Desmond Payne is adding to an already impressive legacy in the gin realm — he came to Beefeater 16 years ago, after a 25-year career at the helm of Plymouth Gin — with this new bottle. “I tried to think of ways to evolve the original recipe into a different space,” Payne says. He wanted to make a spirit that could be drunk alone, as a sophisticated nightcap, rather than in a gin and tonic. “I started to think of how to move it into the after-dinner experience,” he explains, “more alongside whiskeys and cognacs.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/t-magazine/17beefeater-rowan/17beefeater-rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/t-magazine/17beefeater-rowan/17beefeater-rowan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/t-magazine/17beefeater-rowan/17beefeater-rowan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/t-magazine/17beefeater-rowan/17beefeater-rowan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1653, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_nam