3/12/18/nyregion/if-wall-safes-could-talk-the-tales-of-graft-two-could-tell.html', 'snippet': 'The mayor of Jersey City opened two locked and apparently long forgotten safes in a move reminiscent of Geraldo Rivera’s look into Al Capone’s vaults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the rich and storied history of Jersey City’s political corruption, the gold medal still goes to Frank Hague, who ruled as mayor for 30 years from a desk with a special drawer that opened out to visitors, the better to collect his kickbacks. Hague, whose annual salary never exceeded $9,000, retired as a multimillionaire in 1947.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/SAFES2/SAFES2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/SAFES2/SAFES2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/SAFES2/SAFES2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/SAFES2/SAFES2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/SAFES2/SAFES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/SAFES2/SAFES2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2