ast/shiite-pilgrimage-is-target-of-attacks-in-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Pilgrims heading to Karbala to mark Arbaeen were targeted by gunmen and suicide bombers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Shiite Muslims making one of their most important pilgrimages in Iraq were targeted again on Wednesday by gunmen and suicide bombers, medical and police officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shiite Pilgrimage Is Target of Attacks in Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: More Shiite Pilgrims Killed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adnan, Duraid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilgrimages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-18T16:23:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duraid Adnan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duraid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adnan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ac32915-4145-5ef5-ba64-2e4a23fe0ded', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ac32915-4145-5ef5-ba64-2e4a23fe0ded'}, {'abstract': 'Shirley Zafirau, a neighbor of Miles Davis, believed that Davis’s long tenure on the Upper West Side block deserved to be memorialized and so embarked on a campaign to have the street named after him.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/after-a-lengthy-battle-miles-davis-way-is-official/', 'snippet': 'Shirley Zafirau, a neighbor of Miles Davis, believed that Davis’s long tenure on the Upper West Side block deserved to be memorialized and so embarked on a campaign to have the street named after him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For about 25 years, until the mid-1980s, Miles Davis, the legendary jazz trumpeter who died in 1991, lived in an apartment building at 312 West 77th Street, where he enjoyed a well-established New York City tradition: loitering outside on the stoop, greeting passers-by and chatting with neighbors. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/17CITYROOM-davis/17CITYROOM-davis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/17CITYROOM-davis/17CITYROOM-davis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/17CITYROOM-davis/17CITYROOM-davis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/17CITYROOM-davis/17CITYROOM-davis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2047, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/17CITYROOM-davis/17CITYROOM-davis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/17CITYROOM-davis/17CITYROOM-davis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/18/nyregion/17CITYROOM-davis/17CITYROOM-davis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Lengthy Battle, ‘Miles Davis Way’ Is Official', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Miles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-18T16:25:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Krieger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krieger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd929cda-5d3a-50d7-9241-c5e6c2b9b567', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd929cda-5d3a-50d7-9241-c5e6c2b9b567'}, {'abstract': 'Calin Peter Netzer, director of “Child’s Pose,” hopes his film will break Romanian film’s streak of being ignored by the Academy.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/romanias-overlooked-new-wave/', 'snippet': 'Calin Peter Netzer, director of “Child’s Pose,” hopes his film will break Romanian film’s streak of being ignored by the Academy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to the Oscar for best foreign-language film, Romania is a country that can’t get no respect. The Romanian “new wave” is one of the most significant developments in world cinema over the last decade, and Romanian films regularly walk away with top prizes at festivals like Cannes and Berlin. But no Romanian film has ever been nominated for an Oscar, and only one, Cristian Mungiu’s “Beyond the Hills,” released last year, has even been shortlisted.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romania’s Overlooked New Wave', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Mother the Metaphor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netzer, Calin Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-18T16:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2b18512-c98c-58f7-93e8-bf81d2ed34ac', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2b18512-c98c-58f7-93e8-bf81d2ed34ac'}, {'abstract': 'A wish list from researchers at the University of California, San Francisco.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/from-scientists-gift-ideas-for-the-elderly/', 'snippet': 'A wish list from researchers at the University of California, San Francisco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We tried, my sister and I. Every fall and winter, we discussed what extremely practical gift we should get our father for his September birthday and for Hanukkah. A flannel shirt, because his current two were fraying. A warm new sweater, because he disliked paying utility bills and always kept his apartment cool. A leather wallet, because his old one, stuffed with years of photos and credit cards and no-longer-relevant ID’s, was held together with rubber bands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Scientists, Gift Ideas for the Elderly', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-18T16:31:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5515a0c1-0b31-50f1-be56-4d4780d36a66', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5515a0c1-0b31-50f1-be56-4d4780d36a66'}, {'abstract': 'The NBC sitcom returns in January with Dan Harmon, the series creator, back at the helm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/television/100000002608201/excerpt-community.html', 'snippet': 'The NBC sitcom returns in January with Dan Harmon, the series creator, back at the helm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The NBC sitcom returns in January with Dan Harmon, the series creator, back at the helm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/video-community/video-community-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/video-community/video-community-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/arts/video-community/video-community-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legac