iscusses his work on Spike Jonze’s film.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/below-the-line-designing-her/', 'snippet': 'The production designer K. K. Barrett discusses his work on Spike Jonze’s film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some films shout their production design. Others keep it to a dull roar. “Her,” the new Spike Jonze romance about a man falling for his operating system, has a design scheme that is distinct but subtle. That’s the work of K. K. Barrett, who has helped create the many imaginative settings in Mr. Jonze’s movies, from the interiors of John Malkovich’s subconscious (“Being John Malkovich”) to the vast exteriors of a child’s imagination (“Where the Wild Things Are”). With “Her,” Mr. Barrett wanted to build a futuristic world with wide spaces inhabited by a lonely man.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/movies/her9/her9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/17/movies/her9/her9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/movies/her9/her9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/movies/her9/her9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/17/movies/her9/her9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/17/movies/her9/her9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnai