tion and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolly, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-18T20:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/794c5d1d-30ca-5eec-9cad-69c6295a48d1', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/794c5d1d-30ca-5eec-9cad-69c6295a48d1'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks are 5-10 this season in games that have a “clutch” moment; the flaws that hinder them throughout the game are brought into stark relief by the pressure of the final minutes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/sports/basketball/close-games-bring-out-the-worst-in-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks are 5-10 this season in games that have a “clutch” moment; the flaws that hinder them throughout the game are brought into stark relief by the pressure of the final minutes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nothing shapes the perceptions of N.B.A. players and coaches more than how they perform at the end of close games, a time commonly referred to as the clutch. These heightened moments of drama are replayed ad nauseam on TV and in the minds of fans. The big shots may be worth the same number of points as those taken in the first quarter, but the narrative of the game lends them an oversize importance.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xla