 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b294f13d-999e-5a18-b42c-e623f85192d2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b294f13d-999e-5a18-b42c-e623f85192d2'}, {'abstract': 'As the Senate passed a compromise deal, Republicans on the House and Senate Appropriations Committees must contend with a political right flank critical of government spending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/us/politics/senate-64-36-sends-two-year-budget-to-obama.html', 'snippet': 'As the Senate passed a compromise deal, Republicans on the House and Senate Appropriations Committees must contend with a political right flank critical of government spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate’s final passage Wednesday of a two-year, bipartisan budget plan handed the nuts-and-bolts task of funding the government to the House and Senate Appropriations Committees, a mixed blessing for Republican appropriators who relish the chance to direct billions of dollars in federal money but must contend with a political right flank that is critical of government spending and eager to attack.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/us/CONG-2/CONG-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/19/us/CONG-2/CONG-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/us/CONG-2/CONG-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/us/CONG-2/CONG-2-superJumbo.j