s way to its Broadway revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The current Broadway revival of “The Glass Menagerie” has won rave reviews for John Tiffany’s dreamy, minimalist staging and the performances of Cherry Jones and Zachary Quinto as the onetime Southern belle Amanda Wingfield and her rebellious son, Tom. But there have been also exceptional notices for the two lesser-known young actors who round out the cast: Celia Keenan-Bolger, who plays Tom’s disabled, beyond-painfully shy sister, Laura, and Brian J. Smith as Jim, who arrives in the second act as her first, and presumably last, gentleman caller.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/arts/22CALLER1_SPAN/22CALLER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/arts/22CALLER1_SPAN/22CALLER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/arts/22CALLER1_SPAN/22CALLER1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/arts/22CALLER1_SPAN/22CALLER1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/arts/22CALLER1_SPAN/22CALLER1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/arts/22CALLER1_SPAN/22CALLER1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'su