 Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harvard Student Accused of Bomb Hoax to Avoid Final Exam Appears Before Judge', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard Crimson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-18T22:28:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f0b8d19-8b4a-57b2-bd95-e00d09aa0856', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f0b8d19-8b4a-57b2-bd95-e00d09aa0856'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Strauss’s rarely performed opera “Feuersnot” is a lampoon of Munich’s provincialism and Wagnerian bombast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/arts/music/strausss-feuersnot-via-leon-botstein-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Strauss’s rarely performed opera “Feuersnot” is a lampoon of Munich’s provincialism and Wagnerian bombast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The musicologist and conductor Leon Botstein has made a career out of championing works that have been overlooked or neglected. On Sunday afternoon at Carnegie Hall, he conducted a rarely performed one-act comic opera by Richard Strauss, “Feuersnot” (“In Need of Fire”), written 1900-01 as an indictment of Munich and what he saw as the provincialism of its inhabitants — a narrow-mindedness, he felt, that stood in the way of their appreciating both Wagner’s and his own genius. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge',