': 'persons', 'value': 'Nunn, Delores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T00:39:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Home & Garden', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c539c428-d194-5c92-9a40-65a74355ffc7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c539c428-d194-5c92-9a40-65a74355ffc7'}, {'abstract': 'This year, Delores Nunn decorated 15 Christmas trees. “I’m sure there are people who do 20 trees,” she said. “But they can’t get more enjoyment out of it than I do.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/garden/santa-may-need-a-map.html', 'snippet': 'This year, Delores Nunn decorated 15 Christmas trees. “I’m sure there are people who do 20 trees,” she said. “But they can’t get more enjoyment out of it than I do.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week it was reported that Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo of New York and his girlfriend, Sandra Lee, are displaying eight Christmas trees in their home. They’ve got nothing on Delores Nunn, who is 59 and lives in Yorktown, Va. Ms. Nunn recently finished decorating 15 artificial trees for the house she shares with her husband, James, a retired Army colonel. Each tree is trimmed according to a theme, including nuns, travel, sock monkeys, the beach, wine and nature. A small dog-themed tree sits near the food bowl of Mazie, the couple’s springer spaniel-poodle mix. “I’m sure there are people who do 20 trees, but they can’t get more enjoyment out of it than I do,” she told a reporter who visited last month.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santa May Need a Map', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q+A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Santa May Need A Map', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas Trees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value':