': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T01:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38e887c7-97cd-5230-8741-f09870aeb64f', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38e887c7-97cd-5230-8741-f09870aeb64f'}, {'abstract': 'The renovated bar at the St. Regis now draws a younger crowd and early drinkers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/fashion/King-Cole-Bar-and-Salon-at-the-St-Regis-Hotel.html', 'snippet': 'The renovated bar at the St. Regis now draws a younger crowd and early drinkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since its inception in 1948, the King Cole bar at the St. Regis hotel has been the redoubt of a certain Upper East Side set who like their drinks stiff, jackets quilted and daughters educated at Brearley. But earlier this year, the bar underwent a multimillion dollar renovation, and John Delucie, who specializes in resurrecting institutions like Ye Waverly Inn and Bill’s Gay Nineties, took over. In November, it reopened as the King Cole Bar and Salon. Mr. Delucie brought his night life cachet, a war chest of regulars and a younger crowd that buzzes later than before. Even old King Cole, who is depicted in the giant mural behind the bar, seems like a new man, now that years of dust and grit have been removed.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/fashion/19BOITE_SPAN/19ZBOITE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType