prisoned since record keeping began in 1990; the worst was last year, when 232 were held. The report said 52 journalists were killed so far this year. The largest number, 21, were killed in Syria’s civil war. The second largest number of fatalities was in Egypt, with six dead.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey Jailing the Most Journalists', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey Jailing the Most Journalists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Protect Journalists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T02:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah C. Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cd918df-0e35-5688-8aac-e09b6ca3a971', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cd918df-0e35-5688-8aac-e09b6ca3a971'}, {'abstract': 'A federal jury awarded Noel J. Guzman the money after he testified that in 2009 officers kicked, stomped and arrested him after they responded to a fight in which he had not been involved in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/nyregion/man-is-awarded-2-4-million-for-false-arrest-and-beating-by-police.html', 'snippet': 'A federal jury awarded Noel J. Guzman the money after he testified that in 2009 o