'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/sports/baseball/japanese-pitcher-wont-be-let-go-reports-say.html', 'snippet': 'The Japanese pitcher Masahiro Tanaka has said he wants to pitch in Major League Baseball next season, but his team reportedly will not permit him to depart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than two days after the highly sought Japanese pitcher Masahiro Tanaka said he wanted to pitch in Major League Baseball next season, there was still no definitive word from his team, the Rakuten Golden Eagles, whether it would let him leave.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japanese Pitcher Tanaka Won’t Be Let Go, Reports Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pitcher Won’t Be Let Go, Reports Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanaka, Masahiro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rakuten Golden Eagles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T04:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6b6b626-4f79-562d-afdd-07f3230cc424', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6b6b626-4f79-562d-afdd-07f3230cc424'}, {'abstract': 'Li Jinsheng, who is blind, wanted to take the national college entrance examinations to study at university. But the registration deadline passed without the authorities permitting him to do so.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/18/blind-man-barred-from-college-entrance-exams/', 'snippet': 'Li Jinsheng, who is blind, wanted to take the national college entrance examinations to study at university. But the registration deadline passed without the authorities permitting him to do so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Li Jinsheng wanted to study law. But because he is blind, virtually the only profession he could train for in China was massage. So he did that and set up a massage business in Queshan County, Henan Province.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barred From College Entrance Exams, in a Blow for China’s Blind', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Henan Province (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T04:58:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f21db97-2f69-5384-85c5-f6be8517fede', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f21db97-2f69-5384-85c5-f6be8517fede'}, {'abstract': 'David Netto visits the sought-after interior designer, whose projects have included Marc Jacobs’s apartment in Paris and the renovation of the Sunset Tower Hotel, at his home in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/t-magazine/house-tour-of-the-designer-paul-fortunes-laurel-canyon-masterpiece.html', 'snippet': 'David Netto visits the sought-after interior designer, whose projects have included Marc Jacobs’s apartment in Paris and the renovation of the Sunset Tower Hotel, at his home in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The London-born, L.A.-based interior designer Paul Fortune has worked on numerous iconic projects over the years, from Marc Jacobs’s Paris apartment to the Sunset Tower Hotel in Hollywood. This fall, he put his home in Laurel Canyon, known for its warmth and elegance, which he has described as a long-running experiment in design, on the market after 25 years there. Before turning the page, Fortune welcomed the designer and writer David Netto for one final sentimental tour before handing over the keys to the new owner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A House Tour of the Designer Paul Fortune’s Laurel Canyon Masterpiece', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Netto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Netto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41700878-7e31-5d5f-8fc7-0380363cf09f', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41700878-7e31-5d5f-8fc7-0380363cf09f'}, {'abstract': 'Sailor stripes and pearls adorn these luxe pieces that are high-seas inspired but high-tea appropriate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/t-magazine/nautical-style-for-landlocked-ladies-who-lunch.html', 'snippet': 'Sailor stripes and pearls adorn these luxe pieces that are high-seas inspired but high-tea appropriate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sailing stripes are going full steam ahead. Coco Chanel famously employed the motif in her day, and her enduring luxury label is at it again with a new take on its iconic quilted handbag. The traditional stripe also surfaced on a canvas slip-on from Mother of Pearl and a maritime tote from Valentino. For the ultraluxe swashbuckler, a bold streak of white on a rabbit fur stole from Marc Jacobs, wool sweater from Chloé and tailored trousers from Vince would look just as chic at high tea as it would on the high seas. And a Verdura bracelet of pearls and sea-colored sapphires anchors any seafaring look.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19market-barsamian/19market-barsamian-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19market-barsamian/19market-barsamian-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19market-barsamian/19market-barsamian-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19market-barsamian/19market-barsamian-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19market-barsamian/19market-barsamian-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'imag