rs to death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death penalty in the United States continued its pattern of broad decline in 2013, with experts attributing the low numbers to a critical shortage of drugs used for lethal injection, increasing public concern over judicial mistakes and the expense of capital cases, and a growing preference for life without parole.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Death Penalty’s Steady Decline, Some Experts See a Societal Shift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Death Penalty’s Steady Decline, Some Experts See a Societal Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Death Penalty Information Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T05:11:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c056da4-db99-59ec-84f0-0c89bd486ce6', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c056da4-db99-59ec-84f0-0c89bd486ce6'}, {'abstract': 'Executions reached a peak of 98 in 1999. But since then, their numbers have fallen more or less steadily.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/12/19/us/A-Decline-in-Executions.html', 'snippet': 'Executions reached a peak of 98 in 1999. But since then, their numbers have fallen more or less steadily.', 'lead_paragraph': '