on': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4de062c-1be2-535a-8084-40fdab91bbd0', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4de062c-1be2-535a-8084-40fdab91bbd0'}, {'abstract': 'The conviction of a former SAC Capital trader will likely mean more scrutiny of SAC’s founder, Steven A. Cohen. | Drug companies announced more than $6 billion worth of transactions on Thursday. | Darden Restaurants plans to spin out its Red Lobster chain. | Happy holidays, YouTube style, from the Carlyle Group.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/morning-agenda-big-victory-for-government-in-insider-trading-crackdown/', 'snippet': 'The conviction of a former SAC Capital trader will likely mean more scrutiny of SAC’s founder, Steven A. Cohen. | Drug companies announced more than $6 billion worth of transactions on Thursday. | Darden Restaurants plans to spin out its Red Lobst...', 'lead_paragraph': 'No wiretaps. No smoking-gun emails. And a star witness who was testifying to avoid prison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Victory in Government’s Insider Trading Crackdown', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T14:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8da4922a-3557-5697-83e4-71887395bfd8', 'word_count': 1680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8da4922a-3557-5697-83e4-71887395bfd8'}, {'abstract': 'The shelling and raids appeared to be in retaliation for a suicide bombing on Wednesday that killed at least five soldiers in North Waziristan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/world/asia/pakistani-army-kills-23-suspected-of-being-militants.html', 'snippet': 'The shelling and raids appeared to be in retaliation for a suicide bombing on Wednesday that killed at least five soldiers in North Waziristan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — At least 23 people suspected of being militants were killed and 12 were wounded on Thursday when Pakistani Army troops carried out shelling and ground raids in Mir Ali, the second largest town of the restive northwestern tribal district of North Waziristan, according to government officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Army Kills 23 Suspected of Being Militants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Military Strikes Kill At Least 23 in Northwest Area', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mehsud, Ihsanullah Tipu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mehsud, Hakimullah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T14:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsanullah Tipu Mehsud', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsanullah', 'middlename': 'Tipu', 'lastname': 'Mehsud', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e94e5924-bd27-56f5-a349-48b59e1a6281', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e94e5924-bd27-56f5-a349-48b59e1a6281'}, {'abstract': 'Movies don’t do well describing what really happens day to day on Wall Street, and it’s easier — and in many ways more sensible — to do films like “The Wolf of Wall Street.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/movies/martin-scorseses-approach-in-the-wolf-of-wall-street.html', 'snippet': 'Movies don’t do well describing what really happens day to day on Wall Street, and it’s easier — and in many ways more sensible — to do films like “The Wolf of Wall Street.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to know the truth, the Wolf of Wall Street — the person, that is, not the Martin Scorsese-Leonardo DiCaprio movie that opens on Christmas Day — spent only a fleeting few months on the actual Wall Street. In 1987, Jordan Belfort — a.k.a. the wolf himself — took a job at L. F. Rothschild, an old white-shoe firm. It was his first job in the business, and he was given the assignment of cold-calling “prospects” that he would then turn over to a broker. In his memoir — upon which the movie is based — Mr. Belfort claims, among other things, that a successful Rothschild broker (played by Matthew McConaughey on screen) took him to lunch on his first day and told him to masturbate often if he hoped to be a good broker himself. Given Rothschild’s stodgy reputation, I tend to think this story is an exaggeration, an act of salesmanship intended to lure in Hollywood. No matter. Not long after Mr. Belfort began working for L. F. Rothschild, the crash of 1987 wiped out the firm and took his job with it.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sex and Drugs and I.P.O.’s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sex and Drugs and I.P.O.s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belfort, Jordan Ross', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Wolf of Wall Street (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiCaprio, Leonardo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Jonah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConaughey, Matthew', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winter, Terence', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1d58b48-2673-52e7-aa54-691277cb48b0', 'word_count': 1616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1d58b48-2673-52e7-aa54-691277cb48b0'}, {'abstract': 'The Hayden Planetarium director and author, most recently, of “Space Chronicles,” would love to have met Oscar Wilde.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/books/review/neil-degrasse-tyson-by-the-book.html', 'snippet': 'The Hayden Planetarium director and author, most recently, of “Space Chronicles,” would love to have met Oscar Wilde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hayden Planetarium director and author, most recently, of “Space Chronicles,” would love to have met Oscar Wilde: “Anyone who could pen the phrase ‘We are all in the gutter, but some of us are looking at the stars’ gets a seat at my dinner table.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype