xt to his mother-in-law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The real-life Jordan Belfort, the antihero of “The Wolf of Wall Street,” played in the film by Leonardo diCaprio, made an appearance at the Ziegfeld Theater premiere on Tuesday, along with his family. Rob Reiner, who plays his father, Max Belfort, met the real man for the first time. The resemblance is not uncanny: Mr. Reiner is large, Mr. Belfort is not. But “it was a kick for me,” said Mr. Reiner, tasked with characterizing the company overseer once known as Mad Max. “He said he used to scream just like that.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/arts/jbwolf/jbwolf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 861, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/19/arts/jbwolf/jbwolf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 861}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/arts/jbwolf/jbwolf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/arts/jbwolf/jbwolf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1872, 'width': 1304, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/arts/jbwolf/jbwolf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/19/arts/jbwolf/jbwolf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/arts/jbwolf/jbwolf-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cr