{'abstract': '“The Past,” the new film from the Iranian director of “A Separation,” looks at a range of personal struggles in suburban Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/movies/the-past-with-berenice-bejo-directed-by-asghar-farhadi.html', 'snippet': '“The Past,” the new film from the Iranian director of “A Separation,” looks at a range of personal struggles in suburban Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The modest, run-down home at the center of “The Past” is filled with rooms that — much like the characters who are busily, sometimes leisurely passing through them — somehow feel cut off from one another. Set in a characterless Paris suburb that’s as physically and psychically distant from the City of Light as the moon, the movie is both a family melodrama and a relationship story, which perhaps inevitably means it’s about love and loyalty, secrets and lies, and how the past, never being dead, just hovers around waiting to smack us upside the head. All this also makes it something of a haunted house movie, except that its characters are plagued by ghosts of their own design. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PAST_SPAN/20PAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PAST_SPAN/20PAST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PAST_SPAN/20PAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 559, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PAST_SPAN/20PAST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1118, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PAST_SPAN/20PAST_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PAST_SPAN/20PAST_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PAST_SPAN/20PAST_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Backward to Somewhere', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backward To Somewhere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Past (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farhadi, Asghar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bejo, Berenice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rahim, Tahar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T22:50:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/05262473-b52b-5a13-a247-ffc916e91b26', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05262473-b52b-5a13-a247-ffc916e91b26'}, {'abstract': 'At N.Y.U.’s Skirball Center, the Cirque Eloize troupe from Montreal presents a gravity-defying show full of silly, superhuman stunts.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/after-hours-a-goofy-display-of-acrobatics-juggling-and-hula-hooping/', 'snippet': 'At N.Y.U.’s Skirball Center, the Cirque Eloize troupe from Montreal presents a gravity-defying show full of silly, superhuman stunts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Céline Dion, Cirque du Soleil, poutine. Let’s face it: We expect a highly virtuosic level of cheesiness from the Quebecois, and we revel in it. So it goes at N.Y.U.’s Skirball Center, where “Cirkopolis,” the latest body-twisting delight from the Montreal neo-circus troupe Cirque Eloize, is in residency through Jan. 5. The show begins with a single man, a beaten-down bureaucrat in business drab, stamping papers at a desk before giant projections of rotating industrial cogs, à la “Metropolis.” It sounds like the scene is being set for some Weimar-tinged exploration of the alienation of the human worker. Not quite. Those Bauhaus facades are a mere backdrop for a dazzling display of human bodily levitation, contortion and gyration. The acrobats defy gravity in jaw-dropping performances on giant wheel-like contraptions, atop one another’s bodies, suspended from trapezes and ropes, and, astoundingly, up and down a 100-foot pole at frenetic speeds. It’s hard not to deliver an ovation when a pretty young woman in a fluttery red dress whirls inside a massive hula hoop, like a human dreidel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19circus-murphy/19circus-murphy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19circus-murphy/19circus-murphy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19circus-murphy/19circus-murphy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19circus-murphy/19circus-murphy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19circus-murphy/19circus-murphy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19circus-murphy/19circus-murphy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/19/t-magazine/19circus-murphy/19circus-murphy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | A Goofy Display of Acrobatics, Juggling and Hula Hooping', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACROBATS AND ACROBATICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T22:50:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64fdf5a3-c691-5966-b0eb-9867b864e7d5', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64fdf5a3-c691-5966-b0eb-9867b864e7d5'}, {'abstract': 'Videos of eyewitnesses from outside the Apollo Theater, where dozens of people were injured after part of the ceiling collapsed onto the audience during a performance.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/ceiling-at-theater-in-london-collapses-on-audience/', 'snippet': 'Videos of eyewitnesses from outside the Apollo Theater, where dozens of people were injured after part of the ceiling collapsed onto the audience during a performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 6:32 p.m. Dozens of people were injured, including at least seven of them seriously, when part of the ceiling of the Apollo Theater in London’s West End collapsed onto the audience during a performance Thursday night, police and fire officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ceiling at Theater in London Collapses on Audience', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T22:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a3fec41-89f9-5d86-991a-1b09d8730d2f', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a3fec41-89f9-5d86-991a-1b09d8730d2f'}, {'abstract': 'In “The American West in Bronze, 1850-1925,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, focuses on the frontier myths of cowboys, Indians and wild animals immortalized in sculpture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/arts/design/the-american-west-in-bronze-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'In “The American West in Bronze, 1850-1925,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, focuses on the frontier myths of cowboys, Indians and wild animals immortalized in sculpture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around 1905, the city fathers of Denver decided that a monument to honor their pioneering predecessors was in order. The commission went to Frederick William MacMonnies, an American sculptor trained in the Beaux-Arts who lived in France. MacMonnies proposed a multitiered fountain topped by the figure of an Indian chief, but local citizens objected to celebrating a recently feared and despised enemy. So MacMonnies offered instead a sculpture of the all-around frontiersman Kit Carson (1809-68), who, to this day, appears in bronze riding a rearing horse at the summit of the Pioneer Monument in downtown Denver.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manifest Destiny, at the Point of a Gun', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manifest Destiny, At the Point of a Gun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Remington, Frederic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T22:56:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e77137e-3963-5890-90f4-1c181b7fd7f6', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e77137e-3963-5890-90f4-1c181b7fd7f6'}, {'abstract': '“Ileana Sonnabend: Ambassador for the New,” at the Museum of Modern Art, has a big-name collector’s biggest hits and fulfills a pledge to her heirs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/arts/design/ileana-sonnabend-ambassador-for-the-new-at-moma.html', 'snippet': '“Ileana Sonnabend: Ambassador for the New,” at the Museum of Modern Art, has a big-name collector’s biggest hits and fulfills a pledge to her heirs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you think that all art exhibitions result from the natural meeting of laudable subjects and curatorial passion, consider “Ileana Sonnabend: Ambassador for the New,” which opens on Saturday at the Museum of Modern Art. Although the subject is a worthy one — Sonnabend was among the most foresighted art dealers of the late 20th century — the show is a byproduct of legal hassles and diplomatic campaigns surrounding her billion-dollar estate, which may be one reason it feels, as a tribute, cool and impersonal, a portrait-in-art that is only a sketch.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Legendary Dealer’s Eagle Eye', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Legendary Dealer’s Eagle Eye', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sonnabend, Ileana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauschenberg, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T22:57:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9193bc10-e879-58b7-b48e-e9ce7c9db8ff', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9193bc10-e879-58b7-b48e-e9ce7c9db8ff'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to theater productions in New York, with a special note of shows in previews or about to open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/theater/theater-listings-for-dec-20-26.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to theater productions in New York, with a special note of shows in previews or about to open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Approximate running times are in parentheses. Theaters are in Manhattan unless otherwise noted. Full reviews of current productions, additional listings, showtimes and ticket information are at nytimes.com/theater. A searchable, critical guide to theater is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20LISTINGSTHEATER_SPAN/LISTINGS-THEATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20LISTINGSTHEATER_SPAN/LISTINGS-THEATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20LISTINGSTHEATER_SPAN/LISTINGS-THEATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20LISTINGSTHEATER_SPAN/LISTINGS-THEATER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1263, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20LISTINGSTHEATER_SPAN/LISTINGS-THEATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20LISTINGSTHEATER_SPAN/LISTINGS-THEATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20LISTINGSTHEATER_SPAN/LISTINGS-THEATER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Listings for Dec. 20-26', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T22:59:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/06040e54-aaa4-5fae-b71b-f5eba30b9100', 'word_count': 5456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06040e54-aaa4-5fae-b71b-f5eba30b9100'}, {'abstract': '“Jason Rhoades: Four Roads” at the Institute of Contemporary Art in Philadelphia tackles an installation artist who left behind a complicated body of work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/arts/design/jason-rhoades-four-roads-at-penn.html', 'snippet': '“Jason Rhoades: Four Roads” at the Institute of Contemporary Art in Philadelphia tackles an installation artist who left behind a complicated body of work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — When Jason Rhoades died unexpectedly in 2006, at the age of 41, he left behind a vast and bewildering body of work: rambling, porous, performative installations that were as deliriously grandiose as anything by Dieter Roth, Paul McCarthy, Matthew Barney or Thomas Hirschhorn. Curators are still sorting it all out, to judge from “Jason Rhoades: Four Roads,” at the Institute of Contemporary Art here.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SUBRHOADES_SPAN/SUBRHOADES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SUBRHOADES_SPAN/SUBRHOADES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SUBRHOADES_SPAN/SUBRHOADES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SUBRHOADES_SPAN/SUBRHOADES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SUBRHOADES_SPAN/SUBRHOADES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SUBRHOADES_SPAN/SUBRHOADES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SUBRHOADES_SPAN/SUBRHOADES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Obsessions of a Straight American Guy', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Obsessions of a Straight American Guy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhoades, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Contemporary Art Philadelphia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T23:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc4f4816-ef63-53dc-8d19-d299a715332d', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc4f4816-ef63-53dc-8d19-d299a715332d'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to stand-up, improv and comedy shows in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/arts/comedy-listings-for-dec-20-26.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to stand-up, improv and comedy shows in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For news about comedy and humor, including critical commentary: nytimes.com/arts. A searchable guide to these and other shows is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comedy Listings for Dec. 20-26', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Comedy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T23:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bb9cde5-5150-55ab-a7e2-c42ea6fbe5c7', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bb9cde5-5150-55ab-a7e2-c42ea6fbe5c7'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by an Oscar Wilde fairy tale, “The Selfish Giant” depicts two young friends navigating their bleak working-class landscape in Northern England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/movies/the-selfish-giant-directed-by-clio-barnard.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by an Oscar Wilde fairy tale, “The Selfish Giant” depicts two young friends navigating their bleak working-class landscape in Northern England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For today’s socially conscious British filmmakers, northern England is more or less what southern Italy was to the postwar neorealists: a landscape of social misery, both picturesque and harsh. Instead of a disenfranchised peasantry clinging to tradition in the face of modernity, contemporary British cinema finds a demoralized postindustrial underclass fighting for dignity at the margins of the global economy. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SELFISH_SPAN/SELFISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SELFISH_SPAN/SELFISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SELFISH_SPAN/SELFISH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SELFISH_SPAN/SELFISH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SELFISH_SPAN/20SELFISH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SELFISH_SPAN/20SELFISH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20SELFISH_SPAN/20SELFISH_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Desperate Years: To Be Young, British and Lacking', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desperate Years: To Be Young, British and Lacking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnard, Clio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Selfish Giant (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T23:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5571697-f7d1-5a82-a57d-617718723c80', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5571697-f7d1-5a82-a57d-617718723c80'}, {'abstract': 'With art as their currency, Julie Ault and her colleagues lived on New York City’s fringes during decades of depression and inflation, multiculturalism, conservatism, and AIDS.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/arts/design/julie-aults-collection-displayed-at-artists-space.html', 'snippet': 'With art as their currency, Julie Ault and her colleagues lived on New York City’s fringes during decades of depression and inflation, multiculturalism, conservatism, and AIDS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A personal art collection can be displayed as a trophy room or as a diary. The Ileana Sonnabend exhibition at the Museum of Modern Art is cast in greatest-hits mode; MoMA’s the right place for it. “Macho Man, Tell It to My Heart: Collected by Julie Ault” at the nonprofit gallery Artists Space is an intimate document, scrappy, annotated, apartment size. The whole thing, 200 pieces stretched over two locations, could probably fit in a decent-size studio, if you stored some behind furniture and under the bed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20ARTISTSPACE1_SPAN/ARTISTSPACE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20ARTISTSPACE1_SPAN/ARTISTSPACE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20ARTISTSPACE1_SPAN/ARTISTSPACE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20ARTISTSPACE1_SPAN/ARTISTSPACE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20ARTISTSPACE1_SPAN/ARTISTSPACE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20ARTISTSPACE1_SPAN/ARTISTSPACE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20ARTISTSPACE1_SPAN/ARTISTSPACE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A