for children, teenagers and families.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘A Christmas Carol’', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Children for Dec. 20-26', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times: For Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T23:22:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Holcomb and Laurel Graeber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Laurel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graeber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/a37382f6-624e-5025-9574-beaf9aaca518', 'word_count': 5267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a37382f6-624e-5025-9574-beaf9aaca518'}, {'abstract': '“Personal Tailor,” a blend of comedy and satire, centers on a fantasy fabrication service that provides wealthy clients with a taste of the lives they have always wanted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/movies/personal-tailor-directed-by-feng-xiaogang.html', 'snippet': '“Personal Tailor,” a blend of comedy and satire, centers on a fantasy fabrication service that provides wealthy clients with a taste of the lives they have always wanted.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What you don’t dare imagine, we dare to do” is the motto of the dream team known as “Personal Tailor,” a fantasy fabrication service (led by Ge You and Bai Baihe) that provides wealthy clients with a taste of the lives they have always wanted. No request is too outlandish (the “Custom Martyrdom Package” will furnish you with a simulated Nazi interrogation, hunger strike optional) or too elaborate, even if the outcomes are not always as planned.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN/20PERSONALTRAINER_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dream Factory for a Benighted China', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Personal Tailor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feng Xiaogang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Personal Tailor (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-19T23:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1acfaf20-22ee-5905-92db-590047814648', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1acfaf20-22ee-5905-92db-590047814648'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of walking tours, exhibition, cultural activities and Christmas-related events in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/arts/spare-times-for-dec-20-26.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of walking tours, exhibition, cultural activities and Christmas-related events in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christmas at the Metropolitan Museum of Art (through Jan. 6) The museum’s annual Nativity display, featuring a crèche within a Christmas tree, made its debut in 1957. It was the idea of Loretta Hines Howard, an artist and collector who donated over 200 18th-century Neapolitan crèche figures to the museum. After her death in 1982, her family continued the tradition. Visitors circling the tree and this year’s display can see more than 20 cherubs and 50 angels positioned among the branches.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Dec. 20-26', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywor