imes.com/2013/12/22/realestate/the-poetry-of-downsizing.html', 'snippet': 'Jean Hanff Korelitz and Paul Muldoon left Princeton, N.J., for a five-room rental on the Upper West Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last spring, when the novelist Jean Hanff Korelitz and her husband, the Pulitzer Prize-winning Irish poet Paul Muldoon, decided to move to New York City from Princeton, N.J., they figured the hard part would be finding an apartment they liked. Really, that was the easy part. They found lots of apartments they liked.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Poetry of Downsizing', 'kicker': 'What I Love ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Poetry of Downsizing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korelitz, Jean Hanff', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muldoon, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T00:11:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee95f20c-eaf0-52da-8848-320f66c49bf2', 'word_count': 1101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee95f20c-eaf0-52da-8848-320f66c49bf2'}, {'abstract': 'The Orient in Bethpage has no sushi bar and no apologies, just succulent and memorable food in a large, spacious setting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/nyregion/a-review-of-the-orient-in-bethpage.html', 'snippet': 'The Orient in Bethpage has no sushi bar and no apologies, just succulent and memorable food in a large, spacious setting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Orient in Bethpage is the real deal: a Chinese restaurant with no sushi bar, no fusion dishes and no apologies. Twenty years ago, there were many restaurants like this, though most were not nearly as good. Today there are far fewer, and the Orient gets my vote as the best Chinese restaurant on Long Island.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINELI2/22DINELI2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'sub