None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7b48cb3-8e73-5966-bc5e-5e894646d14c', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7b48cb3-8e73-5966-bc5e-5e894646d14c'}, {'abstract': 'Credit experts offered advice for the 40 million Target shoppers whose credit data may have been compromised by cybercriminals, and those in similar straits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/business/for-targets-shoppers-a-new-holiday-to-do-list.html', 'snippet': 'Credit experts offered advice for the 40 million Target shoppers whose credit data may have been compromised by cybercriminals, and those in similar straits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Target confirmed on Thursday that hackers gained access to credit card and debit card information for 40 million of its customers during the crush of the holiday shopping season. The company encouraged everyone who shopped in its United States stores from Nov. 27 through Dec. 15 to be vigilant about monitoring their accounts and their credit. Here are some tips on how to do so. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Target’s Shoppers, a New Holiday To-Do List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Target’s Shoppers, a New Holiday To-Do List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Theft', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Target Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T00:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/72047723-71c4-539b-8292-70f95b6832b4', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72047723-71c4-539b-8292-70f95b6832b4'}, {'abstract': 'Use of the term “natural” is now generating battles similar to previous fights over terms like organic, amid initiatives in several states that seek to label foods in a more transparent way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/business/trade-group-seeks-natural-label-on-modified-food.html', 'snippet': 'Use of the term “natural” is now generating battles similar to previous fights over terms like organic, amid initiatives in several states that seek to label foods in a more transparent way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trade organization representing the nation’s largest food and beverage companies wants permission to label as “natural” products that contain genetically engineered ingredients like corn, soy, canola and sugar, according to a letter sent to the Food and Drug Administration. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Seeks Special Label for Food: ‘Natural’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Food Is Modified, The Label Is ‘Natural’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grocery Manufacturers Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T00:28:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f018679c-e919-57ba-91a1-2ab1ebddcfc2', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f018679c-e919-57ba-91a1-2ab1ebddcfc2'}, {'abstract': 'Diners at a brightly lit country house are offered a New American menu with Italian and Asian accents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/nyregion/a-review-of-2hopewell-in-south-glastonbury.html', 'snippet': 'Diners at a brightly lit country house are offered a New American menu with Italian and Asian accents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a welcoming sight on a cold winter’s eve — a country house, brightly lit, on a country corner. This is 2hopewell Bistro and Bar. Inside you find a cozy basement tavern, and above it dining rooms with ax-hewn posts, flickering candlelight, white walls and wide pine floorboards. Potted palms and Rothko-like prints by the artist Anne Hebebrand, illuminated on the walls, add an apt touch of color. The restaurant is intimate and quiet, with expert service timed perfectly to deliver a luxurious evening. There’s no hurry here. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DIN