rnational Monetary Fund issued on Thursday a scathing report on Ukraine’s financial situation, saying that the government of President Viktor F. Yanukovich had largely abandoned much-needed economic reforms that it had agreed to undertake as part of a deal in 2010 that provided more than $15 billion in loans.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.M.F. Criticizes Ukraine Plan for Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.M.F. Scolds Ukraine Plan For Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T00:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97c171f8-a1e1-581c-9211-8d8d4415bb23', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97c171f8-a1e1-581c-9211-8d8d4415bb23'}, {'abstract': 'Urgent care clinics, a growing option for many Americans, can be more efficient and less costly than an emergency room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/19/your-money/a-quicker-trip-to-the-doctor-for-minor-ailments.html', 'snippet': 'Urgent care clinics, a growing option for many Americans, can be more efficient and less costly than an emergency room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christine O’Rourke, who often travels for her job as a regional sales manager for a laboratory company, says she doesn’t have time to wait to see a doctor when she is ill. So instead, she visits a local urgent care clinic near her home in Morris Plains, N.J.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/business/Adviser/Adviser-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/21/business/Adviser/Adviser-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/business/Adviser/Adviser-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/business/Adviser/Adviser-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/business/Adviser/Adviser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/21/business/Adviser/Adviser-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/business/Adviser/Adviser-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quicker Trip to the Doctor, for Minor Ailments', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Quicker Trip to the Doctor, for Minor Ailments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T00:38:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14fd6c46-39df-5b24-b88a-620f0ef91abd', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14fd6c46-39df-5b24-b88a-620f0ef91abd'}, {'abstract': 'In Congress, two actions have nothing to do with bringing spending into line, and everything to do with a view that the poor are morally inferior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/opinion/egan-good-poor-bad-poor.html', 'snippet': 'In Congress, two actions have nothing to do with bringing spending into line, and everything to do with a view that the poor are morally inferior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sundays, this time of year, my parents would pack a gaggle of us kids into the station wagon for a tour of two Christmas worlds. First, we’d go to the wealthy neighborhoods on a hill — grand Tudor houses glowing with the seasonal incandescence of good fortune. Faces pressed against the car windows, we wondered why their Santa was a better toy-maker than ours.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/opinion/timothy-egan/timothy-egan-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/11/opinion/timothy-egan/timothy-egan-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/opinion/timothy-egan/timothy-egan-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/opinion/timothy-egan/timothy-egan-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/opinion/timothy-egan/timothy-egan-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/11/opinion/timothy-egan/timothy-egan-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/11/opinion/timothy-egan/timothy-egan-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Poor, Bad Poor', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Poor, Bad Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Egan, Timothy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T00:39:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9073588f-f932-574d-a02a-3cac0075ddbf', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9073588f-f932-574d-a02a-3cac0075ddbf'}, {'abstract': 'On the budget deal, Republican leaders sold out conservative values.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/opinion/john-boehners-betrayal.html', 'snippet': 'On the budget deal, Republican leaders sold out conservative values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOODSTOCK, Ga. — THERE’S a political axiom that says if nobody is upset with what you’re doing, you’re not doing your job. We’ve seen this proved time and again in the liberal attacks on conservatives like Sarah Palin and Dr. Benjamin Carson, who provide principled examples to women and minorities and are savaged by the left for doing that job so well.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/opinion/1220OPEDmenchin/1220OPEDmenchin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/opinion/1220OPEDmenchin/1220OPEDmenchin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/opinion/1220OPEDmenchin/1220OPEDmenchin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumb