inistration it loathed, New York City’s taxi industry dispensed with any pretense of mixed emotions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxi Industry Bids the Bloomberg Era a Not-So-Fond Farewell', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taxi Industry Bids the Bloomberg Era a Not-So-Fond Farewell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taxi and Limousine Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yassky, David', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T01:28:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9af4385a-51c1-524b-9a44-da9b6bb1d1c0', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9af4385a-51c1-524b-9a44-da9b6bb1d1c0'}, {'abstract': 'Agreements with American Express, MasterCard and Visa have cleared the way for vendors to institute what is essentially two-tier pricing for shoppers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/business/an-easing-of-rules-on-charges-by-amex.html', 'snippet': 'Agreements with American Express, MasterCard and Visa have cleared the way for vendors to institute what is essentially two-tier pricing for shoppers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a decade of legal battles, the three major credit card companies are backing awa