en taken, had high-profile breaks with an activist neighbor and Christine C. Quinn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They seemed destined to be friends: two women who became next-door neighbors on 111th Street in East Harlem, different generations of Puerto Ricans who were active in community organizing and politics.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trail of Fractured Political Friendships on Way to Advancement in City Council', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Trail of Fractured Political Friendships on the Way to Advancement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mark-Viverito, Melissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Yolanda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, City Councils', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T02:46:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96cc89b8-030f-5348-8224-0c29d0fa6ee7', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96cc89b8-030f-5348-8224-0c29d0fa6ee7'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, December 20, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www