rk Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Injured in 2 Fires in the Bronx', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T05:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c94b9fb-5014-581f-b455-e3855a197d6e', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c94b9fb-5014-581f-b455-e3855a197d6e'}, {'abstract': 'The central bank said it would maintain its bond-buying program, and that the economy was recovering moderately.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/business/international/japan-holds-steady-on-rates.html', 'snippet': 'The central bank said it would maintain its bond-buying program, and that the economy was recovering moderately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan’s central bank decided on Friday to hold steady on its aggressive monetary stimulus program and said the nation’s economy continued to recover moderately. Economists expect the bank to expand its asset-buying program next year to counter any ill effects of a scheduled sales tax increase.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Stays Aggressive on Stimulus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Stays Aggressive on Stimulus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yen (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T05:55:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eac6f945-4a27-56b8-9693-bc8502c11f42', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eac6f945-4a27-56b8-9693-bc8502c11f42'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (TNT) CHRISTMAS IN WASHINGTON 2013 Hugh Jackman hosts this 32nd annual holiday concert benefiting the Children’s National Health System, taped on Sunday at the National Building Museum in Washington and attended by President Obama and his family, above. The Backstreet Boys, Sheryl Crow, Anna Kendrick, Janelle Monáe and Pat Monahan perform; the N.B.A. Hall of Famer Charles Barkley talks about Children’s National programs. “A Christmas Carol” (1999), David Jones’s adaptation of the Charles Dickens classic, starring Patrick Stewart as Ebenezer Scrooge, Richard E. Grant as Bob Cratchit, Saskia Reeves as Mrs. Cratchit and Joel Grey as the First Sprit, follows at 9. Writing in The New York Times, Caryn James called the production glorious: “Its greatest triumph is Mr. Stewart’s performance. (He has played all the parts in his one-man stage version.)” She said, “This impenetrable man will not be easily touched, even by ghosts.” This “Christmas Carol” is a lasting addition to a list of towering renditions, she added. “Evoking the pure joy of the Christmas season and its spirit of giving, it reveals why Dickens’s story has such inexhaustible appeal.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fadb6aba-4216-50a8-89ba-8b513fa90733', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fadb6aba-4216-50a8-89ba-8b513fa90733'}, {'abstract': 'The difference in mortality rates between black women and white women with breast cancer has widened since 1975, in part because black women have not benefited as much from improvements in screening and treatment. Among the states with available data, Tennessee has the largest gap. Massachusetts, where the rates have converged, has the smallest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/12/20/health/a-racial-gap-in-breast-cancer-deaths.html', 'snippet': 'The difference in mortality rates between black women and white women with breast cancer has widened since 1975, in part because black women have not benefited as much from improvements in screening and treatment. Among the states with available d...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The difference in mortality rates between black women and white women with breast cancer has widened since 1975, in part because black women have not benefited as much from improvements in screening and treatment. Among the states with available data, Tennessee has the largest gap. Massachusetts, where the rates have converged, has the smallest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stark Gap in Breast Cancer Deaths', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T06:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Health', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/eeb8ad7a-3b88-5e49-b626-9f1159366e01', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/eeb8ad7a-3b88-5e49-b626-9f1159366e01'}, {'abstract': 'Mary Singleton, 57, learned in July that she had Stage 4 breast cancer. After the diagnosis her son, George, moved home to Memphis to help take care of her and to help run her printing business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/health/100000002608303/the-cancer-divide-mary.html', 'snippet': 'Mary Singleton, 57, learned in July that she had Stage 4 breast cancer. After the diagnosis her son, George, moved home to Memphis to help take care of her and to help run her printing business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary Singleton, 57, learned in July that she had Stage 4 breast cancer. After the diagnosis her son, George, moved home to Memphis to help take care of her and to help run her printing business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/science/video-breast-cancer-memphis/video-breast-cancer-memphis-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'hei