iatory strikes without warning” if anti-Pyongyang rallies by conservative activists in Seoul are not stopped, officials here said on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Letter, North Korea Warns South Over Rallies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Letter, North Korea Warns South Over Rallies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Geun-hye', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jang Song-Thaek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seoul (South Korea)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyongyang (North Korea)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T06:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5bbd6f7-f879-5b78-aa99-783c3fb152bd', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5bbd6f7-f879-5b78-aa99-783c3fb152bd'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Varshney spoke about the politics of citizenship and the rise of Narendra Modi.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/a-conversation-with-political-scientist-ashutosh-varshney/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Varshney spoke about the politics of cit