7e'}, {'abstract': 'Internal tension at the S.E.C. raises questions about whether the agency could have done even more after the crisis to hold Wall Street accountable. | What the jurors in the Michael S. Steinberg case thought. | How real people hurt by the Stratton Oakmont scandal fared. | Ronald O. Perelman’s donation to the NYU Langone Medical Center.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/morning-agenda-s-e-c-mired-in-tensions-over-mortgage-cases/', 'snippet': 'Internal tension at the S.E.C. raises questions about whether the agency could have done even more after the crisis to hold Wall Street accountable. | What the jurors in the Michael S. Steinberg case thought. | How real people hurt by the Stratton...', 'lead_paragraph': ' \xa0|\xa0 TENSION AT S.E.C. OVER MORTGAGE CASES After months of investigating the role of Goldman Sachs, Wells Fargo and others in troubled mortgage securities — and even warning that enforcement actions were possible — the Securities and Exchange Commission shelved those cases and at least two others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Mired in Tensions Over Mortgage Cases', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T14:04:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b4e5054-5e13-502c-ba93-b50d57cc5b5c', 'word_count': 2097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b4e5054-5e13-502c-ba93-b50d57cc5b