: 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lives/mag-22Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lives/mag-22Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lives/mag-22Lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lives/mag-22Lives-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life With Bella', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life With Bella', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABZUG, BELLA S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T15:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Berger Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': 'Berger', 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50dc71a8-00c5-5d3f-8fea-5a26ce50b676', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50dc71a8-00c5-5d3f-8fea-5a26ce50b676'}, {'abstract': 'Lydia Lunch has transformed herself into a self-help guru. Even more surprising, she has followers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/magazine/finding-inner-peace-with-the-angriest-punk-of-70s-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Lydia Lunch has transformed herself into a self-help guru. Even more surprising, she has followers.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We’ve suffered enough as human beings and as women,” Lydia Lunch said one bright morning in Ojai, Calif., as she gazed beneficently around her. Sixteen women, most of them middle-aged, had gathered at Ananda Verandah (“Ananda” is Sanskrit for “bliss”) to take Lunch’s Post-Catastrophe Collaborative workshop.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lunch1/mag-22Lunch-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lunch1/mag-22Lunch-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 753}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lunch1/mag-22Lunch-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 817, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lunch1/mag-22Lunch-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1633, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lunch1/mag-22Lunch-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lunch1/mag-22Lunch-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22lunch1/mag-22Lunch-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Inner Peace With the Angriest Punk of ’70s New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Inner Peace With the Angriest Punk of ’70s New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lunch, Lydia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T15:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ada Calhoun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calhoun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec5af19a-ad0b-5a71-84c6-1478c149beaa', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec5af19a-ad0b-5a71-84c6-1478c149beaa'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “French Women Don’t Get Facelifts” explains why it’s useful to know your limits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/magazine/mireille-guiliano-on-aging-with-french-dignity.html', 'snippet': 'The author of “French Women Don’t Get Facelifts” explains why it’s useful to know your limits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2005, you published “French Women Don’t Get Fat.” What do you think makes our cultures so different? I think half a century ago, things changed drastically. Before those days, women were at home and they were cooking. With feminism, you had to go to work, and if you had to go work — well, you know, forget the cooking. For many French women a job is not the top priority in life — family is. In the U.S. you’re sort of defined by what you do. That’s why so many women are lost when they finish their career.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22talk/mag-22Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1952, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22talk/mag-22Talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1952}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22talk/mag-22Talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 315, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22talk/mag-22Talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 630, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22talk/mag-22Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22talk/mag-22Talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22talk/mag-22Talk-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mireille Guiliano On Aging With French Dignity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "‘They're Being Squeezed Like a Lemon.’", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gross, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guiliano, Mireille', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T15:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Jessica Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Jessica', 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/52ee6a6b-d727-598d-abd5-91f729a66b57', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52ee6a6b-d727-598d-abd5-91f729a66b57'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/magazine/the-12-813-issue.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 12.8.13 Issue', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 12.8.13 Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T15:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9873bcb-cc3b-59a9-84e8-859d59fe6b48', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9873bcb-cc3b-59a9-84e8-859d59fe6b48'}, {'abstract': 'In the movies, men are constantly gathering for a last blowout escape from adult life. One quiet film this year presents a refreshingly different take on manhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/magazine/one-last-time.html', 'snippet': 'In the movies, men are constantly gathering for a last blowout escape from adult life. One quiet film this year presents a refreshingly different take on manhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Christmas Day, Robert De Niro and Sylvester Stallone will open in “Grudge Match,” a movie about a couple of old, rival boxers spoiling for one last fight. This may seem like an unpromising premise, but perhaps the movie will please the same audience that went for the recent comedy “Last Vegas,” which is about three AARP-appropriate Brooklyn guys from the old neighborhood — one married, one divorced and one widowed — who get together for one last ring-a-ding-ding Vegas weekend to toast the impending wedding of their fourth pal, a holdout bachelor who has spontaneously decided to tie the knot. (Gentle life lessons ensue.) The fact that the preternaturally tan and swinging groom to be is played by Michael Douglas (age 69) adds a dribble of amusement to the premise. So does the paycheck-collecting participation of aging movie stars like De Niro (him again), Morgan Freeman and Kevin Kline.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22riff/22riff-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22riff/22riff-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 100}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22riff/22riff-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 171, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22riff/22riff-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22riff/mag-22Riff-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22riff/mag-22Riff-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22riff/mag-22Riff-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One! Last! Time!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Makeovers, Do-Overs and ‘The Hangover’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwarzbaum, Lisa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T15:22:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Schwarzbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarzbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12e54629-a3c4-5408-9548-ac2cce069556', 'word_count': 1770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12e54629-a3c4-5408-9548-ac2cce069556'}, {'abstract': 'From an inexpensive lifesaver to a universal source of irritation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/magazine/who-made-that-smoke-alarm.html', 'snippet': 'From an inexpensive lifesaver to a universal source of irritation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early 1960s, Duane Pearsall tinkered in his engineering lab with a machine he called a “static neutralizer” — an ion generator designed to control static electricity in factories and photo labs. But when one of his technicians lit up a cigarette, a meter measuring the ions went haywire. Pearsall realized he’d just hit on a low-cost, low-power method for sniffing smoke. During the next decade, he and his team developed the SmokeGard, which hung from the ceiling and made a noxious noise whenever it sensed a fire. Soon, smoke detectors were in most homes\xa0in America and had saved hundreds of lives. Yet they could also be irritating. “You have no way of knowing whether it’s operational unless you set fire to your house,” wrote one newspaper humorist in 1977 of a cheap smoke detector he bought in a local store. “Merely holding the smoke detector in your lap while you watch Farrah Fawcett-Majors is not a true test.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22wmt/22wmt-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22wmt/22wmt-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22wmt/22wmt-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22wmt/22wmt-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1215, 'width': 1823, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22wmt/22wmt-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22wmt/22wmt-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/magazine/22wmt/22wmt-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Smoke Alarm?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Smoke Alarm)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoke Detectors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Pagan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T15:22:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pagan Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pagan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a87b77b-dee7-53b2-a7ef-0336bb3e8754', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a87b77b-dee7-53b2-a7ef-0336bb3e8754'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve’s report on industrial production this week shows the United States as a standout among the advanced economies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/business/economy/a-weak-recovery-still-looks-comparatively-good.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve’s report on industrial production this week shows the United States as a standout among the advanced economies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDUSTRIAL production in the United States has returned to its prerecession level, nearly six years after the downturn began and more than four years after the recession officially ended.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weak Recovery, but Comparatively Go