t film, “Her”; Will Ferrell in “Anchorman 2″; and “The Past,” directed by Asghar Farhadi.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/video-reviews-of-anchorman-2-her-and-the-past/', 'snippet': 'Times critics look at Spike Jonze’s latest film, “Her”; Will Ferrell in “Anchorman 2″; and “The Past,” directed by Asghar Farhadi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s video, Times critics look at Spike Jonze’s latest film, “Her,” Will Ferrell in “Anchorman 2″ and “The Past,” directed by Asghar Farhadi. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Reviews of ‘Anchorman 2,’ ‘Her’ and ‘The Past’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T16:43:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/914d18d9-ab47-555f-aa86-4eb8237874e9', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/914d18d9-ab47-555f-aa86-4eb8237874e9'}, {'abstract': 'At A’maree’s, the one-of-a-kind luxury shop in Newport Beach, a friendly crowd gathered last month for an exhibition of work by Mika Damascou, the jewelry designer and mother of the T contributor Konstantin Kakanias, who designed the invitation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/in-store-exotic-jewelry-and-rare-company-in-orange-county/', 'snippet': 'At A’maree’s, the one-of-a-kind luxury shop in Newport Beach, a friendly crowd gathered last month for an exhibition of work by Mika Damascou, the jewelry designer and mother of the T contributor Konstantin Kakanias, who designed the invitation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month A’maree’s, the family-owned fashion and design shop in the surprising location of Newport Beach, Calif., hosted an exhibition of jewels by Mika Damascou, the mother of the artist (and T Magazine contributor) Konstantin Kakanias, who organized the show with the L.A. stylist Danielle King. The occasion was right in line with the spirit of the store, which marches to its own drummer in terms of what it stocks — fashion, furniture, jewelry, bicycles — and who it supports. The current iteration of A’maree’s is run by the sisters Dawn Klohs and Denise and Apryl Schaefer, whose mother founded it in the 1970s. For the past three years it has existed in a sublime 1960 building on the water by Ladd & Kelsey, the architects of Pasadena’s Norton Simon Museum, a dreamlike Modernist pavilion with arched windows and a scalloped roofline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/20amare-netto/20amare-netto-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/20amare-netto/20amare-netto-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 503}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/20amare-netto/20amare-netto-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 868, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/20amare-netto/20amare-netto-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 868, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/20amare-netto/20amare-netto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/20amare-netto/20amare-netto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/20amare-netto/20amare-netto-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Store | Exotic Jewelry and Rare Company in Orange County', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newport Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T16:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Netto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Netto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16337f29-dbc3-5a10-8a3f-dd9a900bf562', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16337f29-dbc3-5a10-8a3f-dd9a900bf562'}, {'abstract': 'With Sochi, Russia, preparing to host the Winter Olympics in February, the author gets an early taste of the area’s developing ski experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/travel/a-test-run-at-russias-olympic-hopeful.html', 'snippet': 'With Sochi, Russia, preparing to host the Winter Olympics in February, the author gets an early taste of the area’s developing ski experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before I could board the gondola at Rosa Khutor, a ski area that is part of Sochi, the site of next year’s Winter Olympics, I first had to trundle through a metal detector manned by Russian soldiers with machine guns and furry hats. This is not something I’m used to. At chairlifts in the American West, where I typically ski, you find cheerful young attendants who are stoked to be on their feet all day because that’s what it takes to live the dream.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22SOCHI5/22SOCHI5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22SOCHI5/22SOCHI5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22SOCHI5/22SOCHI5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22SOCHI5/22SOCHI5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1522, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22SOCHI5/22SOCHI5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22SOCHI5/22SOCHI5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22SOCHI5/22SOCHI5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Test Run at Russia’s Olympic Hopeful', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Test Run at Russia’s Olympic Hopeful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaacson, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sochi (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T16:51:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Isaacson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isaacson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac0e00d0-5be5-5297-aecb-7a829e9ca08a', 'word_count': 2304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac0e00d0-5be5-5297-aecb-7a829e9ca08a'}, {'abstract': 'The author of an article on the ski resort at Sochi, Russia, the site of the coming Winter Olympics, digs up a family connection: ski posters created by his grandfather, some of skiing in Russia.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/a-family-connection-to-skiing-history/', 'snippet': 'The author of an article on the ski resort at Sochi, Russia, the site of the coming Winter Olympics, digs up a family connection: ski posters created by his grandfather, some of skiing in Russia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s ski issue, I write about Rosa Khutor, a new ski resort above the city of Sochi, Russia, that is the site of the alpine events for the coming Winter Games. Built with the Olympics in mind, Rosa Khutor has ambitions to become a world-class ski area that attracts Russian skiers, who might otherwise flee to the Alps, and international visitors, who might otherwise never think of Russia when planning a ski vacation. It’s a great mountain, with great potential.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Family Connection to Skiing History', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Posters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sochi (Russia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T16:52:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Isaacson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isaacson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60e824c4-b8ad-545f-adaf-3af4e985e5c1', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60e824c4-b8ad-545f-adaf-3af4e985e5c1'}, {'abstract': 'Leaving a sultry New York behind, the author escaped to Chile, where she found snowy slopes and even a gold medal or two.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/travel/skiing-in-september-head-south.html', 'snippet': 'Leaving a sultry New York behind, the author escaped to Chile, where she found snowy slopes and even a gold medal or two.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It felt like a scene from a surrealist film. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22EXPLORER5/22EXPLORER5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22EXPLORER5/22EXPLORER5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/travel/22EXPLORE