-0a1d-573f-96c7-0c1e0d9d0dbc'}, {'abstract': 'The agency has not “fostered an environment that tolerates inappropriate behavior,” the inspector general of the Homeland Security Department said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/us/politics/secret-service-gets-good-marks-after-inquiry-spurred-by-prostitute-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'The agency has not “fostered an environment that tolerates inappropriate behavior,” the inspector general of the Homeland Security Department said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Secret Service does not have widespread misconduct, and the agency’s leadership has not “fostered an environment that tolerates inappropriate behavior,” according to a review of the agency’s culture by the inspector general’s office for the Department of Homeland Security.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Widespread Misconduct Is Found in the Secret Service ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Widespread Misconduct Is Found in the Secret Service', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Michael S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T17:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/261676ef-f5b9-5401-b248-6998779e2b0f', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/261676ef-f5b9-5401-b248-6998779e2b0f'}, {'abstract': 'The move is likely to erode the dominance of the African National Congress ahead of elections and reorder the politics of a country it has governed with huge majorities since the end of white rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/world/africa/south-africas-biggest-union-pulls-support-for-anc.html', 'snippet': 'The move is likely to erode the dominance of the African National Congress ahead of elections and reorder the politics of a country it has governed with huge majorities since the end of white rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — South Africa’s largest trade union withdrew its support for the African National Congress on Friday, a move that is likely to erode the party’s dominance ahead of national elections next year and reorder the politics of a country the party has governed with huge majorities since the end of white rule two decades ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Africa’s Biggest Trade Union Pulls Its Support for A.N.C.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Africa’s Biggest Trade Union Pulls Its Support for A.N.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polgreen, Lydia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN NATIONAL CONGRESS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T17:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7ffea85-3b3b-58a2-bc17-ad583b80572f', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7ffea85-3b3b-58a2-bc17-ad583b80572f'}, {'abstract': 'The director relieved the stress of rewrites on “Her” by voicing the foul-mouthed video game character that appears in the film.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/spike-jonze-video-game-character/', 'snippet': 'The director relieved the stress of rewrites on “Her” by voicing the foul-mouthed video game character that appears in the film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 12:25 p.m. | In some ways, the Spike Jonze romance “Her” is a different beast for the inventive director-writer-prankster – it’s the first feature he wrote on his own – and in some ways it’s a lot like his other films (“Where the Wild Things Are,” “Being John Malkovich,” “Adaptation”). All take a long time in the editing room, up to a year. They’re naturalistic in performance, but not heavily improvised – though the story can sometimes change after they finish filming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/spike/spike-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/spike/spike-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 798}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/spike/spike-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/arts/spike/spike-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1540, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 