t were canceled.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/city-opera-ticket-holders-have-to-get-in-line-with-other-creditors/', 'snippet': 'A judge overseeing New York City Opera’s bankruptcy case said the company could not yet refund money to people who bought tickets for performances that were canceled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the New York City Opera filed for bankruptcy on Oct. 3 it asked the court if it could refund $323,000 worth of ticket income to subscribers who had faith in the increasingly shaky company. At the same time, it mailed a letter to those ticket buyers, expressing confidence that the court would grant that request but suggesting that patrons could also waive their right to a refund and donate the money to the failed company instead. Enough ticket buyers agreed to reduce the debt by about $30,000.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Opera Ticket Holders Have to Get in Line With Other Creditors', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T17:56:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc407568-8c55-5fa3-bfb0-9fd55418d00b', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc407568-8c55-5fa3-bfb0-9fd55418d00b'}, {'abstract': 'When Kumar Natarajanaidu was 10 years old in India, he had a vision that led him to Flushing, Queens, where he opened a shop with DVDs, flowers 