ifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49b446e0-64b7-52d2-a6e1-acf9db7e567e', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49b446e0-64b7-52d2-a6e1-acf9db7e567e'}, {'abstract': 'Are you a parent, teacher or student who has experienced a school lockdown? Let us know what you experienced.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/have-you-been-through-a-school-lockdown-tell-us-about-your-experience/', 'snippet': 'Are you a parent, teacher or student who has experienced a school lockdown? Let us know what you experienced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, when an 18-year-old student walked into Arapahoe High School in Colorado with a pump-action shotgun and began shooting, teachers and students and administrators knew almost immediately how to respond. Classroom doors slammed shut. Students huddled in the corners and stayed quiet. A resource officer inside the school sprang to action. Nearby, other schools locked down until they knew whether they, too, faced any threat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/blogs/21arapahoe/21arapahoe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/21/blogs/21arapahoe/21arapahoe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/blogs/21arapahoe/21arapahoe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/blogs/21arapahoe/21arapahoe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', '