}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7a51e67f-d615-589a-b907-a75aede392b9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7a51e67f-d615-589a-b907-a75aede392b9'}, {'abstract': 'A Spanish tortilla delivers luscious, velvety potatoes, thanks to lots of olive oil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/dining/a-potatos-postcard-from-spain.html', 'snippet': 'A Spanish tortilla delivers luscious, velvety potatoes, thanks to lots of olive oil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before I had ever tasted a tortilla Española, the traditional Spanish potato omelet, I couldn’t imagine what the fuss was about. What could be so special about a dish made from only eggs, potatoes and onion?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Potato’s Postcard From Spain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Potato’s Postcard From Spain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tortillas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potatoes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T19:40:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/964f632c-557f-58c7-bf4f-1ea4345a9d17', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964f632c-557f-58c7-bf4f-1ea4345a9d17'}, {'abstract': 'The man was arrested in Central Park after a police officer noticed him working a horse that was visibly injured.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/nyregion/carriage-horse-driver-is-charged-with-animal-cruelty.html', 'snippet': 'The man was arrested in Central Park after a police officer noticed him working a horse that was visibly injured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A carriage horse driver with a checkered history was charged on Friday with animal cruelty after a police officer observed him working a horse that was visibly injured, according to court documents.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carriage Driver Is Charged With Animal Cruelty', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carriage Driver Is Charged With Animal Cruelty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colarusso, Saverio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T19:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1af3a4f0-c949-5f55-ac5a-783daf88532e', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1af3a4f0-c949-5f55-ac5a-783daf88532e'}, {'abstract': 'Unusual and memorable marriage proposals that all seemed to do the trick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/fashion/weddings/engaging-shenanigans-big-surprises.html', 'snippet': 'Unusual and memorable marriage proposals that all seemed to do the trick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written in the sand. It was asked under the big top and with bells on. There was a bended knee followed by a “Will you marry me?” on an elevator ride, and a proposal made on a hotel rooftop to a soundtrack of whirling propellers. There are many other memorable and creative ways to ask that age-old question. So, since that query is often posed during the holiday season, now may be a good time to review some of the most interesting proposals submitted this year to the Vows pages of The Times.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22FIELDNOTES/22FIELDNOTES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22FIELDNOTES/22FIELDNOTES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22FIELDNOTES/22FIELDNOTES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22FIELDNOTES/22FIELDNOTES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1640, 'width': 1640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22FIELDNOTES/22FIELDNOTES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22FIELDNOTES/22FIELDNOTES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22FIELDNOTES/22FIELDNOTES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Engaging Shenanigans, Big Surprises', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Engaging Shenanigans, Big Surprises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mallozzi, Vincent M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T19:41:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vincent M. Mallozzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vincent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/048dd37d-c237-57ba-90a9-26cab83b64e4', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/048dd37d-c237-57ba-90a9-26cab83b64e4'}, {'abstract': 'Spike Jonze’s film “Her,” like a recent exhibition of work by the artist Daniel Arsham in Miami, explores our new fear that we, like our gadgets, are destined for rapid obsolescence.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/observed-art-and-entertainment-that-makes-us-feel-old-before-our-time/', 'snippet': 'Spike Jonze’s film “Her,” like a recent exhibition of work by the artist Daniel Arsham in Miami, explores our new fear that we, like our gadgets, are destined for rapid obsolescence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For much of the 20th century, scientists believed that the slower one’s metabolism, the longer one’s life. This is called the rate of living theory, and although it is not actually true for humans, it feels increasingly accurate of our machines. The faster our computers get, the faster they seem to break, burn out or become obsolete. The average life span of an American cellphone is 18 months. No wonder the members of my superconnected demographic — young, urban, educated, “creative,” often described as “millennials” — are all afraid we’re shooting to obscurity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/Prickett-Jonze/Prickett-Jonze-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/Prickett-Jonze/Prickett-Jonze-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/Prickett-Jonze/Prickett-Jonze-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/Prickett-Jonze/Prickett-Jonze-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1288, 'width': 1988, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/Prickett-Jonze/Prickett-Jonze-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/Prickett-Jonze/Prickett-Jonze-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/t-magazine/Prickett-Jonze/Prickett-Jonze-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art and Entertainment That Makes Us Feel Old Before Our Time', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arsham, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonze, Spike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Her (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T19:42:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Nicole Prickett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Nicole', 'lastname': 'Prickett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9b245f4-3fa3-5b13-bc7a-f86294fc192f', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9b245f4-3fa3-5b13-bc7a-f86294fc192f'}, {'abstract': 'Want to contact the government to complain about the F.D.A.’s toothless animal antibiotics ruling? Here’s how.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/how-to-make-noise-about-antibiotics/', 'snippet': 'Want to contact the government to complain about the F.D.A.’s toothless animal antibiotics ruling? Here’s how.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of you have asked me how best to make your opinions heard about routine use of antibiotics in animals, the subject of my column this week. You could:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make Noise about Antibiotics', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T19:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}],