': 'nyt://article/4231cb22-8dac-554d-9d2b-ff330c3dddf7'}, {'abstract': 'Using a GPS launcher, police can attach a tracking device to a vehicle and follow it via computer instead of by a high-speed chase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/automobiles/a-virtual-alternative-to-the-hot-pursuit.html', 'snippet': 'Using a GPS launcher, police can attach a tracking device to a vehicle and follow it via computer instead of by a high-speed chase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If StarChase, a maker of GPS-tagging systems for police departments, has its way, cable TV stations will soon be looking for new material to fill slow news days. That’s because the Virginia Beach company has developed a device meant to eliminate the high-risk car chases that draw viewers and seem, inevitably, to end in tears.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/automobiles/STARCHASE1/STARCHASE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/automobiles/STARCHASE1/STARCHASE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/automobiles/STARCHASE1/STARCHASE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/automobiles/STARCHASE1/STARCHASE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1093, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/automobiles/STARCHASE1/STARCHASE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/automobiles/STARCHASE1/STARCHASE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/automobiles/STARCHASE1/STARCHASE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Virtual Alternative to the Hot Pursuit', 'kicker': 'Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Virtual Alternative to the Hot Pursuit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'StarChase', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T20:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/492bc979-80df-5192-b085-bc224553e0b2', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/492bc979-80df-5192-b085-bc224553e0b2'}, {'abstract': 'Although it has a few features that seem dated, the Kodo-styled CX-9 handles well, akin to a much smaller crossover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/automobiles/video-the-mazda-cx-9-has-aged-well.html', 'snippet': 'Although it has a few features that seem dated, the Kodo-styled CX-9 handles well, akin to a much smaller crossover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced in 2007, the Mazda CX-9 crossover has been refreshed twice, and I’ve now reviewed it three times. Some vehicles seem dated after just a few years on the market, but with its most recent Kodo design face-lift, the CX-9 retains a youthful appearance. We should all be so lucky.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: The Mazda CX-9 Has Aged Well', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mazda Motor Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T20:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/557b07bf-3421-5da4-8f8a-8372d4ccb0c8', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/557b07bf-3421-5da4-8f8a-8372d4ccb0c8'}, {'abstract': 'The Seven is a home-built E.V. that its owners say travels 200 miles on a charge. It competed for the Automotive X Prize in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/automobiles/afterlife-for-an-x-prize-contender.html', 'snippet': 'The Seven is a home-built E.V. that its owners say travels 200 miles on a charge. It competed for the Automotive X Prize in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a background in chemical engineering and his job as an air quality regulator for the Illinois Environmental Protection Agency, Kevin Smith might seem an unlikely sort to be spending his free time building a car in a backyard garage. But Mr. Smith’s education and experience no doubt contributed to his home-built car’s being refined far beyond a typical shade tree effort.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':