e', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f41ab62-2376-5f2a-a776-29d7af2d0c19', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f41ab62-2376-5f2a-a776-29d7af2d0c19'}, {'abstract': 'A device that plugs into your car monitors its condition and location and lets owners share that information with family and friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/automobiles/a-car-monitor-that-also-talks-to-facebook.html', 'snippet': 'A device that plugs into your car monitors its condition and location and lets owners share that information with family and friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even cars that have reached their teenage years can now enjoy the benefits of social networking. Their ability to stay connected comes with the introduction of Zubie, a plug-in device and service that not only monitors a vehicle’s condition and location but also lets owners share that information with family and friends.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Car Monitor That Also Talks to Facebook', 'kicker': 'Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Car Monitor That Also Talks To Facebook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T20:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Quain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Quain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': ''