': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clymer, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hodinkee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T21:45:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/796067c7-be7a-51ca-a813-73f71fcbd5a8', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/796067c7-be7a-51ca-a813-73f71fcbd5a8'}, {'abstract': 'A climate scientist charts a responsible path from climate science to advocacy.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/climate-scientists-then-and-now-espousing-responsible-advocacy/', 'snippet': 'A climate scientist charts a responsible path from climate science to advocacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve long appreciated Gavin A. Schmidt‘s approach to doing and communicating climate science. Schmidt, deputy director of NASA’s Goddard Institute for Space Studies, has endured many slings and arrows, not to mention hacks and legal tangles, in building RealClimate.org into what I’ve called a vital online touchstone for anyone trying to understand research on the human influence on the planet’s thermostat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/blogs/dotgavin/dotgavin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 285, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/blogs/dotgavin/dotgavin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 285, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/blogs/dotgavin/dotgavin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/20/blogs/dotgavin/dotgavin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/20/blogs/dotgavin/dotgavin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Scientists, Then and Now, Espousing ‘Responsible Advocacy’', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T21:45:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05796c9e-dc98-57d1-a4c1-ac57c04214a6', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05796c9e-dc98-57d1-a4c1-ac57c04214a6'}, {'abstract': 'Traditional Christmases aren’t for everyone, but that does not mean the spirit of the holiday should be rejected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/fashion/Celebrate-Christmas-Celebrations-Merry-Christmas-Holiday.html', 'snippet': 'Traditional Christmases aren’t for everyone, but that does not mean the spirit of the holiday should be rejected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We skitter, we dodge. My boyfriend and I will be flying to India on Christmas Day. Jetting off on Santa’s Judgment Day is not unusual for me; I’m among that tiny percentage of the population who hears “Santa’s helpers” and thinks “skycaps.” Part of my seasonal wanderlust lies in the belief that a Christmas celebrated by two adults and no children can be eerily quiet, a Beckett play performed in a canyon on the moon. But the larger part lies in my conviction that the most beautiful and tinselly bauble to be found on Dec. 25 is reduced airfare.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22JPCIRCANOW_SPAN/22JPCIRCANOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22JPCIRCANOW_SPAN/22JPCIRCANOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 188}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22JPCIRCANOW_SPAN/22JPCIRCANOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22JPCIRCANOW_SPAN/22JPCIRCANOW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22JPCIRCANOW_SPAN/22JPCIRCANOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22JPCIRCANOW_SPAN/22JPCIRCANOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22JPCIRCANOW_SPAN/22JPCIRCANOW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ho, Ho, Ho? Oh, No, No, No!', 'kicker': 'Circa Now', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ho, Ho, Ho? Oh, No, No, No!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alford, Henry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T21:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Alford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11928186-5aab-521d-8314-a20f601d0ecf', 'word_count': 1489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11928186-5aab-521d-8314-a20f601d0ecf'}, {'abstract': 'The judge said that Utah’s amendment barring same-sex marriage violated the United States Constitution. If the ruling is upheld, Utah will become the 18th state to permit same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/us/utahs-gay-marriage-ban-is-ruled-unconstitutional.html', 'snippet': 'The judge said that Utah’s amendment barring same-sex marriage violated the United States Constitution. If the ruling is upheld, Utah will become the 18th state to permit same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Salt Lake County began issuing marriage licenses to jubilant same-sex couples on Friday, hours after a federal judge ruled that Utah’s amendment barring same-sex marriage violated the United States Constitution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/us/UTAH/UTAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/21/us/UTAH/UTAH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/us/UTAH/UTAH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/us/UTAH/UTAH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/21/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Judge Rules That Same-Sex Marriage Is Legal in Utah', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Judge Rules That Same-Sex Marriage Is Legal in Utah', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T21:49:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c17c14a-0cfb-5e15-a071-127921e11183', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c17c14a-0cfb-5e15-a071-127921e11183'}, {'abstract': 'There will be no tried-and-true reforms on the Commodity Futures Trading Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/20/who-will-keep-financial-reform-going/', 'snippet': 'There will be no tried-and-true reforms on the Commodity Futures Trading Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late November, nine Democratic senators sent President Obama a letter about a vacancy on the five-member Commodity Futures Trading Commission, the agency charged under the Dodd-Frank law with regulating most of the multi-trillion dollar market in derivatives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Will Keep Financial Reform Going?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-20T21:51:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Tritch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tritch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2817d49a-636f-5e77-b0df-8b8633b0d6ee', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2817d49a-636f-5e77-b0df-8b8633b0d6ee'}, {'abstract': 'Young adults do not think and act alike, as it turns out. In fact, some do not want to be called millennials at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/fashion/Millenials-Millennials-Generation-Y.html', 'snippet': 'Young adults do not think and act alike, as it turns out. In fact, some do not want to be called millennials at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know them when you see them. They are tapping on their smartphones, strolling into work late and amassing Instagram followers faster than a twerking cat. They complain. They “disrupt” stuff. They simultaneously (and somewhat improbably) like both Kanye West and Kenny Chesney. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22CULTURALSTUDIES2/22CULTURALSTUDIES2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22CULTURALSTUDIES2/22CULTURALSTUDIES2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/fashion/22CULTURALSTUDIES2/22CULTURALSTUDIES2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1021, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 