wn-on-risk-shifting-deals/', 'snippet': 'Regulators are concerned that banks may at times use these complex deals to evade the stiffer regulations that have been introduced since the 2008 financial crisis', 'lead_paragraph': 'A major banking regulator moved on Friday to curb a type of financial maneuver that banks can exploit to make themselves look stronger than they actually are.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed to Crack Down on Risk-Shifting Deals', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T00:03:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8627d923-9b4a-552d-8d71-343e37f4bc5a', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8627d923-9b4a-552d-8d71-343e37f4bc5a'}, {'abstract': 'The performance of gestures, services and kind acts has quite likely been a driving force of life in New York at least since the days of the New Amsterdam colony. But we roll now in ways the Dutch could not have foreseen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/nyregion/a-favor-economy-in-which-kind-acts-come-with-expected-reciprocity.html', 'snippet': 'The performance of gestures, services and kind acts has quite likely been a driving force of life in New York at least since the days of the New Amsterdam colony. But we roll now in ways the Dutch could not have foreseen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some years ago, I had a friend who moved to New York with various aspirations, and until they were fulfilled he supported himself working at a restaurant. The place was cultish and bohemian — artists had started it — and interesting people worked there. Eventually my friend got to know the daughter of a famous actor there. On various occasions, he ate out with this woman and her father, noticing that when they did, the bill rarely arrived. This led my friend to one of his most astute and enduring observations about New York: “Only rich people eat for free.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22FAVOR_SPAN/22FAVOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22FAVOR_SPAN/22FAVOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 652}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22FAVOR_SPAN/22FAVOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 944, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22FAVOR_SPAN/22FAVOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1887, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22FAVOR_SPAN/22FAVOR_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/nyregion/22FAVOR_SPAN/22FAVOR_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'captio