: None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/171a9502-1904-55aa-b46c-09aaa17c928e', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/171a9502-1904-55aa-b46c-09aaa17c928e'}, {'abstract': 'Israeli forces fatally shot a Palestinian man who approached the border fence separating Gaza from Israel and wounded five others at several points along the fence, Palestinian medical officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/world/middleeast/israel-palestinian-killed-near-border.html', 'snippet': 'Israeli forces fatally shot a Palestinian man who approached the border fence separating Gaza from Israel and wounded five others at several points along the fence, Palestinian medical officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Israeli forces on Friday fatally shot a Palestinian man who approached the border fence separating Gaza from Israel and wounded five others at several points along the fence, Palestinian medical officials said. The Israeli military said that Palestinians had thrown rocks at soldiers near the fence and fired a mortar shell into Israel. Ouda Hamad, 22, was the third Palestinian to be killed in clashes with Israeli soldiers this week. On Wednesday and Thursday, Israeli forces in the West Bank killed two Palestinians, one during arrest raids in the Jenin refugee camp and one in Qalqilya. The military said the man killed in Qalqilya had fired on the soldiers. A spokesman for the Palestinian president, Mahmoud Abbas, condemned the West Bank killings as a “dangerous Israeli escalation” meant to undermine peace negotiations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Palestinian Killed Near Border', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Palestinian Killed Near Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T01:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7d69d3a-5f47-59b5-bc7e-dc776a6d51d8', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7d69d3a-5f47-59b5-bc7e-dc776a6d51d8'}, {'abstract': 'A monk in a Tibetan region of western China died after setting fire to himself on Thursday afternoon, according to two Tibet advocacy groups based outside China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/world/asia/china-tibetan-sets-himself-on-fire.html', 'snippet': 'A monk in a Tibetan region of western China died after setting fire to himself on Thursday afternoon, according to two Tibet advocacy groups based outside China.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A monk in a Tibetan region of western China died after setting fire to himself on Thursday afternoon, according to two Tibet advocacy groups based outside China. The monk, Tsultrim Gyatso, was the 125th person inside a Tibetan area of China to commit self-immolation as an act of protest since 2009, according to Kate Saunders, a spokeswoman for the International Campaign for Tibet. Another group, Free Tibet, put the total at 123, with 27 this year. The latest protest took place in a town that Tibetans call Amchok, in the Chinese province of Gansu. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Tibetan Sets Himself on Fire', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Tibetan Sets Himself on Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Tibet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Campaign for Tibet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T01:05:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/42ec6b80-969d-5b55-ad84-b06e3a6d4536', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42ec6b80-969d-5b55-ad84-b06e3a6d4536'}, {'abstract': 'The bells at the Church of Our Saviour in Midtown Manhattan used to toll twice a day, but a new pastor stepped up the chime schedule to 13 times a day, irritating some neighbors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/nyregion/murray-hill-churchs-neighbors-would-prefer-to-look-at-the-clock.html', 'snippet': 'The bells at the Church of Our Saviour in Midtown Manhattan used to toll twice a day, but a new pastor stepped up the chime schedule to 13 times a day, irritating some neighbors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Christmas season, with its silver bells, silent nights and packed pews, might not be the most opportune time to take issue with your local Catholic church. But a group of neighbors of the Church of Our Saviour in Midtown Manhattan are doing just that, complaining that — of all things — the incessant ringing of church bells has produced a heavy helping of bad cheer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/nyregion/church1/church1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/21/nyregion/church1/church1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/nyregion/church1/church1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/nyregion/church1/church1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/nyregion/church1/church1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/21/nyregion/church1/church1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/21/nyregion/church1/church1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Murray Hill Church’s Neighbors Would Prefer to Look at the Clock', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murray Hill Church’s Neighbors Would P