 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rana Plaza Building Collapse, Bangladesh (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Primark Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Loblaw Cos Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T02:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/00f0e554-f183-55d1-a27f-b10c13218cd7', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00f0e554-f183-55d1-a27f-b10c13218cd7'}, {'abstract': 'After being criticized for its lack of onstage diversity, “Saturday Night Live” is poised to hire a black female cast member.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/opinion/snl-stops-joking-about-casting-problems.html', 'snippet': 'After being criticized for its lack of onstage diversity, “Saturday Night Live” is poised to hire a black female cast member.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After coming under intense criticism for its lack of onstage diversity, “Saturday Night Live” is poised to hire its first black female cast member since Maya Rudolph left the show in 2007. Lorne Michaels, the executive producer, told The New York Times that “S.N.L.” recently held special auditions and that one or two black women would most likely join the cast in January — a good thing for notions of balance, of course, but also for the show’s relevance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘S.N.L.’ Stops Joking About Casting Problems', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘S.N.L.’ Stops Joking About Casting Problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Saturday Night Live (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michaels, Lorne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T02:40:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fed4674-7621-5e42-b57a-a612bd2556d9', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fed4674-7621-5e42-b57a-a612bd2556d9'}, {'abstract': 'A Libyan dissident, Abdel Hakim Belhaj, cannot pursue in a British court his “well founded” claim that he was unlawfully abducted in 2004, and later tortured.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/world/europe/britain-judge-rejects-libyans-rendition-case.html', 'snippet': 'A Libyan dissident, Abdel Hakim Belhaj, cannot pursue in a British court his “well founded” claim that he was unlawfully abducted in 2004, and later tortured.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Libyan dissident, Abdel Hakim Belhaj, cannot pursue in a British court his “well founded” claim that he was unlawfully abducted in 2004 in a joint MI6-C.I.A. operation, and later tortured, because the case involved other countries and could damage Britain’s relations with the United States, a British high court judge ruled Friday. The judge, Peregrine Simon, ruled, “with hesitation,” that Mr. Belhaj could not sue MI6, the foreign intelligence service, and a former foreign secretary, Jack Straw, even though parliamentary oversight and police investigations were “not adequate substitutes” for a decision by a court. He dismissed the case, he said, because American, as well as British, officials were involved in the rendition of Mr. Belhaj and his pregnant wife to Libya in 2004 and agreed with the British government that a case in open court would harm its relations with Washington. Mr. Belhaj will appeal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Judge Rejects Libyan’s Rendition Case', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Judge Rejects Libyan’s Rendition Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belhaj, Abdul Hakim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Secret Intelligence Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Straw, Jack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T02:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0c7a36e-0e6e-5902-8a21-76f466f9c11b', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0c7a36e-0e6e-5902-8a21-76f466f9c11b'}, {'abstract': 'The office of the state comptroller will start routinely auditing all companies that provide services for disabled preschoolers in New York State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/nyregion/law-will-tighten-oversight-of-special-education-providers.html', 'snippet': 'The office of the state comptroller will start routinely auditing all companies that provide services for disabled preschoolers in New York State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to reports of fraud and abuse, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo this week signed into law a bill to strengthen oversight of New York State’s preschool programs for disabled children.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Law Will Tighten Oversight of Special Education Providers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Law Will Tighten Oversight Of Special Education Providers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Javier C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller (NYS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T02:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63bb37f4-f7ce-5dd7-8fd1-c923bc51c37d', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63bb37f4-f7ce-5dd7-8fd1-c923bc51c37d'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Saturday, December 21, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-saturday-december-21-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Saturday, December 21, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“They’re frustrated. Everybody was thinking that Obamacare was going to come in with more affordable rates. Well, they’re not more affordable.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, December 21, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T02:46:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/db92e5a6-1fcb-5192-871e-32494dda0dc7', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db92e5a6-1fcb-5192-871e-32494dda0dc7'}, {'abstract': 'The Food and Drug Administration proposed a rule that requires major food producers to develop a plan to prevent intentional attempts to contaminate the food supply.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/us/plan-sought-to-protect-food-supply-from-terrorism.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration proposed a rule that requires major food producers to develop a plan to prevent intentional attempts to contaminate the food supply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration proposed a rule\xa0on Friday\xa0to require major food producers to develop a plan to prevent intentional attempts to contaminate the food supply. The agency said it favored the rule, not because such a criminal act is likely, but as an extra precaution. Under the rule, open to public comment until the end of March, companies would need plans to address vulnerabilities in production processes, particularly to acts of terrorism. They would have one to three years to comply. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan Sought to Protect Food Supply From Terrorism', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan Sought To Protect Food Supply From Terrorism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavernise, Sabrina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T02:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/882a430f-80ea-5440-b16e-874cc6061d29', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/882a430f-80ea-5440-b16e-874cc6061d29'}, {'abstract': 'The beginning of the end for the Federal Reserve’s stimulus program, a big investment by General Motors and the theft of credit card data by hackers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/12/21/business/weekly-business-photos.html', 'snippet': 'The beginning of the end for the Federal Reserve’s stimulus program, a big investment by General Motors