ted States aircraft flying into a heavily contested region of South Sudan to evacuate American citizens were attacked on Saturday morning and forced to turn back without completing the mission, American officials said. Four service members were wounded, one seriously.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attack on U.S. Aircraft Foils Evacuation in South Sudan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Aircraft Are Attacked in South Sudan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nairobi (Kenya)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bor (South Sudan)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T17:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27eb721a-b6d4-5a11-937d-ff88ade80403', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27eb721a-b6d4-5a11-937d-ff88ade80403'}, {'abstract': 'The All-Star center Brook Lopez broke the fifth metatarsal in his right foot, an injury he had sustained before. The Nets said a timetable for his return would be better known next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/sports/basketball/nets-season-takes-another-hit-with-injury-to-lopez.html', 'snippet': 'The All-Star center Brook Lopez broke the fifth metatarsal in his right foot, an injury he had sustained before. The Nets said a timetable for his return would be better known next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Health has been everything for the Nets this season: the ominous variable that threatened to derail their season even before it began, the fickle state they lacked during their disastrous start, the factor they enthusiastically linked to their brief moments of success. As a vague and mutable concept, it still offered hope that the Nets could turn around their season. Now that seems far less likely. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sports/22lopez1/22lopez1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/sports/22lopez1/22lopez1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sports/22lopez1/22lopez1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sports/22lopez1/22lopez1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sports/22lopez1/22lopez1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/sports/22lopez1/22lopez1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sports/22lopez1/22lopez1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets’ Lopez Breaks Bone in Foot and Could Miss Rest of Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nets’ Lopez Breaks Bone in Foot And Could Miss Rest of Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Brook', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T17:21:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa69788b-a5b7-511c-b0db-b719b4a3b962', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa69788b-a5b7-511c-b0db-b719b4a3b962'}, {'abstract': 'The long rally fueled by the Federal Reserve’s bond-buying program is one to remember, but sooner rather than later storms will return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/your-money/a-great-ride-but-reality-is-returning.html', 'snippet': 'The long rally fueled by the Federal Reserve’s bond-buying program is one to remember, but sooner rather than later storms will return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been the kind of year that makes an average investor feel like a genius: You could just put your money in a stock index fund and watch the market speed ahead. Why not take a few moments to savor it? ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-STRA/22-STRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-STRA/22-STRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-STRA/22-STRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-STRA/22-STRA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1115, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-STRA/22-STRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-STRA/22-STRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-STRA/22-STRA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Great Ride, but Reality Is Returning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Great Ride, but Reality’s Returning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T17:26:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Sommer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sommer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c1cf167-ea99-5e4b-9a30-9cdc26bf1c1a', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c1cf167-ea99-5e4b-9a30-9cdc26bf1c1a'}, {'abstract': 'The American political system allows for more change than its current reputation suggests, an economist says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/business/dont-mistake-this-for-gridlock.html', 'snippet': 'The American political system allows for more change than its current reputation suggests, an economist says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Economic policy in the United States is ruled by gridlock. That’s the common belief, and it’s easy to see the evidence for it in the daily headlines. Immigration reform didn’t even come up for a vote in Congress this year, and the budget deal approved by the Senate last week managed to amend the sequestration but was far from a “grand fiscal bargain.” It was the best that could be accomplished, given gridlock.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-VIEW/22-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-VIEW/22-VIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-VIEW/22-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-VIEW/22-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-VIEW/22-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-VIEW/22-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/business/22-VIEW/22-VIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Mistake This for Gridlock', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No, It Only Looks Like Gridlock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowen, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T17:27:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'B