s Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/275b2864-2b87-5751-85f4-202551cbc275', 'word_count': 2001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/275b2864-2b87-5751-85f4-202551cbc275'}, {'abstract': 'Americans were bracing for a Monday deadline to sign up for health insurance, after a series of changes that has caused uncertainty among insurers and confusion among consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/us/health-care-enrollment-deadline.html', 'snippet': 'Americans were bracing for a Monday deadline to sign up for health insurance, after a series of changes that has caused uncertainty among insurers and confusion among consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For most Americans, Monday is the deadline to sign up for health insurance that takes effect on Jan. 1. It was supposed to be a turning point in the troubled history of the new health care law, the moment when the spotlight would shift from the federal government’s online marketplace to the insurance companies providing coverage to hundreds of thousands and eventually millions of people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/us/INSURERS-1/INSURERS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/us/INSURERS-1/INSURERS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/us/INSURERS-1/INSURERS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/us/INSURERS-1/INSURERS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mixed Messages Add Anxiety as Deadline Nears in Health Act', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Momentum Amid Uncertainty as Deadline for Health Care Enrollment Nears', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T19:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/278b069b-6b89-591d-82f0-086878701317', 'word_count': 1185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/278b069b-6b89-591d-82f0-086878701317'}, {'abstract': 'Of taxi fares, wages, and recessions.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/21/uber-and-the-macro-wars/', 'snippet': 'Of taxi fares, wages, and recessions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday I offered a brief history of the civil war in macroeconomics, in which I explained that it really began over the question of apparent wage and price stickiness. It was an obvious empirical fact that wages generally don’t fall in recessions, and that as a result changes in nominal spending are reflected in real output. (Just as a reminder — this does NOT mean that wage flexibility would improve our current situation — on the contrary, thanks to the overhang of household debt, it would make things worse).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uber and the Macro Wars', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T19:04:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9427816c-4f23-5455-862c-02865075e0b0', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9427816c-4f23-5455-862c-02865075e0b0'}, {'abstract': 'The Affordable Gift Act will lower costs across the tree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/opinion/sunday/santacare-is-coming-to-town.html', 'snippet': 'The Affordable Gift Act will lower costs across the tree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To my American constituents, of both the naughty and nice parties, I’m pleased to announce the rollout of the Affordable Gift Act, referred to by the name of its sponsor — yours truly — as Santacare.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santacare Is Coming to Town', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Santacare Is Coming to Town', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T19:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teddy Wayne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teddy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wayne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d68d29af-5344-5ea8-904e-4d8fdce4645a', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d68d29af-5344-5ea8-904e-4d8fdce4645a'}, {'abstract': 'I wanted to publish some books. But first I would have to convince our chief financial officer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/opinion/sunday/triumph-of-the-english-major.html', 'snippet': 'I wanted to publish some books. But first I would have to convince our chief financial officer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I REMEMBER the moment when I finally decided that I was pulling my weight, or at least some of it, in the great collective effort that is, or used to be, the American economy. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sunday-review/22ENGLISH/22ENGLISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/sunday-review/22ENGLISH/22ENGLISH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sunday-review/22ENGLISH/22ENGLISH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sunday-review/22ENGLISH/22ENGLISH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 1799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/sunday-review/22ENGLISH/22ENGLISH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name':