pe': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a389c9f-854a-5b69-a042-b2a0c2dc1a16', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a389c9f-854a-5b69-a042-b2a0c2dc1a16'}, {'abstract': 'A new agreement to rescue failing banks is inadequate and overly bureaucratic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/opinion/sunday/europes-flawed-banking-deal.html', 'snippet': 'A new agreement to rescue failing banks is inadequate and overly bureaucratic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'European finance ministers have agreed on a plan to rescue failing banks. It is not a good one. Policy makers at key institutions like the European Parliament and the European Central Bank should push for a better deal. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s Flawed Banking Deal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe’s Flawed Banking Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T19:43:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/52f9f667-ae36-51c7-a17d-3da068e4b315', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52f9f667-ae36-51c7-a17d-3da068e4b315'}, {'abstract': 'A judge and a presidential panel slam the N.S.A.’s snooping as a mass invasion of privacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/opinion/sunday/bad-times-for-big-brother.html', 'snippet': 'A judge and a presidential panel slam the N.S.A.’s snooping as a mass invasion of privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been a long week for the National Security Agency. Last Monday, a federal judge ruled for the first time that the agency’s continuing sweep of Americans’ phone data — a once-secret program legally sanctioned for seven years and illegally conducted for five years before that — was very likely unconstitutional. Judge Richard Leon denounced the agency’s activities in collecting data on all Americans’ phone calls as “almost Orwellian.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bad Times for Big Brother', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Times for Big Brother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T19:43:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/56b04969-05b3-5453-84ab-c2f89ed1e50d', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56b04969-05b3-5453-84ab-c2f89ed1e50d'}, {'abstract': 'Anti-American chants can still be heard in Tehran, but there is a real desire for change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/opinion/sunday/what-iranians-say-now-about-the-great-satan.html', 'snippet': 'Anti-American chants can still be heard in Tehran, but there is a real desire for change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — The old American Embassy building in the heart of this capital city was recently opened to tours for Westerners. It is now a museum run by the Revolutionary Guard and its Basiji paramilitary allies, where they keep alive a paranoid narrative of American malice and deceit by showcasing dust-encrusted spy equipment and a modern mural of alleged American perfidies.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Iranians Say Now About ‘the Great Satan’', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Sunday Observer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Iranians Say Now About ‘the Great Satan’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-21T19:43:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 