ginal': 'By Jennifer Homans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Homans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d4956ee-fcf3-54e8-aae9-ce71ac5debd8', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d4956ee-fcf3-54e8-aae9-ce71ac5debd8'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Schechter, then Ensign Schechter, a Navy pilot during the Korean War, was at the heart of one of the most electrifying air rescues in American military history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/us/kenneth-a-schechter-83-dies-with-help-he-flew-blind.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Schechter, then Ensign Schechter, a Navy pilot during the Korean War, was at the heart of one of the most electrifying air rescues in American military history.', 'lead_paragraph': '“On the ninth of my planned 15 bomb runs, at 1,200 feet, an enemy antiaircraft shell exploded in the cockpit. Instinctively, I pulled back on the stick to gain altitude. Then I passed out. When I came to a short time later, I couldn’t see a thing. There was stinging agony in my face and throbbing in my head. I felt for my upper lip. It was almost severed from the rest of my face. I called out over the radio through my lip mike (which miraculously still worked), ‘I’m blind! For God’s sake, help me! I’m blind!’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/us/22bull-schechter-obit/22bull-schechter-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/22/us/22bull-schechter-obit/22bull-schechter-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 464}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/22/u