/debating-the-nsas-data-collection-and-a-panels-findings.html', 'snippet': 'A former C.I.A. acting director argued that the National Security Agency’s data collection remained important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington — A member of President Obama’s advisory committee on signals intelligence, the panel that recommended major restrictions on the National Security Agency’s data collection, on Sunday countered the notion that the panel had found no value in the agency’s activities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debating the N.S.A.’s Data Collection, and a Panel’s Findings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Intelligence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T19:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bfd345a-7bec-5cc6-a4cf-b555ca043a67', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bfd345a-7bec-5cc6-a4cf-b555ca043a67'}, {'abstract': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/in-our-pages-december-23/', 'snippet': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': '1938: Firemen Battle To Save Invalides Monument Roof', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Our Pages: December 23', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T20:06:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dec579bf-3ce1-5bee-ab3e-6a6f72e4034e', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dec579bf-3ce1-5bee-ab3e-6a6f72e4034e'}, {'abstract': '“The Sleeping Beauty” being performed by the Paris Opera Ballet is notable for its length and what Rudolf Nureyev may have been trying to convey between the lines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/arts/dance/the-sleeping-beauty-at-the-paris-opera-ballet.html', 'snippet': '“The Sleeping Beauty” being performed by the Paris Opera Ballet is notable for its length and what Rudolf Nureyev may have been trying to convey between the lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Rudolf Nureyev’s “The Sleeping Beauty,” currently being performed by the Paris Opera Ballet, is ornate, ceremonious and very, very long. It also hints at Nureyev’s ambivalence toward the Russia he left behind when he defected to the West in 1961 at 23 while on tour with the Kirov Ballet. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/BEAUTY/BEAUTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/BEAUTY/BEAUTY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/BEAUTY/BEAUTY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/BEAUTY/BEAUTY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1323, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/BEAUTY/BEAUTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/BEAUTY/BEAUTY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/BEAUTY/BEAUTY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nureyev Ballet, With a Hint of Ambivalence, Takes Its Time', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Nureyev Ballet, With a Hint of Ambivalence, Takes Its Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Sleeping Beauty (Ballet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulcas, Roslyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nureyev, Rudolf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Opera Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T20:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8eb30a3-ad56-5146-8059-4febe0117093', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8eb30a3-ad56-5146-8059-4febe0117093'}, {'abstract': 'Giorgio Vasari’s “The Last Supper,” a work from 1546 that was all but ruined in a 1966 flood, is slowly coming back to life in Florence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/arts/design/bringing-giorgio-vasaris-the-last-supper-back-to-life.html', 'snippet': 'Giorgio Vasari’s “The Last Supper,” a work from 1546 that was all but ruined in a 1966 flood, is slowly coming back to life in Florence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than most Renaissance artists, Giorgio Vasari knew the perilous existence of human creations. In “The Lives of the Artists,” the chronicle of the great quattrocento painters and sculptors for which he is best known, he describes how a stone bench, hurled off a parapet by an anti-Medici mob in Florence in 1527, “chanced, as Fortune would have it,” to land on Michelangelo’s “David,” breaking one of its arms into three pieces.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpvarari1/jpvarari1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 497, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpvarari1/jpvarari1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 497}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpvarari1/jpvarari1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 849, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpvarari1/jpvarari1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1654, 'width': 1996, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpvarari1/jpvarari1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpvarari1/jpvarari1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpvarari1/jpvarari1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Deluge, the Restoration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Deluge, The Restoration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vasari, Giorgio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opificio delle Pietre Dure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty, J Paul, Museum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T21:13:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/801138f7-5e13-5c45-a893-0de5b008f21e', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/801138f7-5e13-5c45-a893-0de5b008f21e'}, {'abstract': 'Surely the holiday-theme variety television specials of yesteryear — Carol Burnett’s, Danny Kaye’s, Dean Martin’s — were superior to this season’s offerings, right? Guess again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/arts/television/long-ago-shows-from-stars-like-perry-como-and-dean-martin.html', 'snippet': 'Surely the holiday-theme variety television specials of yesteryear — Carol Burnett’s, Danny Kaye’s, Dean Martin’s — were superior to this season’s offerings, right? Guess again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The spurious “war on Christmas” bemoaned on Fox News notwithstanding, a war really has been going on in recent years at the holidays: a war between traditional television Christmas specials and that aggressive musical interloper, the singing-competition finale. It’s a mismatch. With December now dominated by singing competitions — “The X Factor” and “The Voice” wrapped up last week; “The Sing-Off” ends Monday night — the old-fashioned variety-show-style Christmas special feels as if it could go extinct any year now. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpOLDCHRISTMAS/jpOLDCHRISTMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpOLDCHRISTMAS/jpOLDCHRISTMAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpOLDCHRISTMAS/jpOLDCHRISTMAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpOLDCHRISTMAS/jpOLDCHRISTMAS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1235, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpOLDCHRISTMAS/jpOLDCHRISTMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpOLDCHRISTMAS/jpOLDCHRISTMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/jpOLDCHRISTMAS/jpOLDCHRISTMAS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Haunted by Holiday Shows Past', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haunted By Holiday Shows Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Como, Perry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Dean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, Carol', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaye, Danny', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T21:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstnam