 the officials and his players, the Jets scored 17 straight points on their way to a solid win over the Cleveland Browns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Rex Ryan stamped. He shouted. He cursed and snarled and appealed, releasing a reservoir of fury on a man who was in position to make a very important decision. When he had finished pleading, Ryan had what he wanted.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/sports/football/23jets/23jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/sports/football/23jets/23jets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/sports/football/23jets/23jets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/sports/football/23jets/23jets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1550, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/sports/football/23jets/23jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/sports/football/23jets/23jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/sports/football/23jets/23jets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets Ride Ryan’s Power of Persuasion to Victory Over Browns', 'kicker': 'Jets 24, Browns 13', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets Follow a Fired-Up Ryan’s Lead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Browns', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Geno', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pace, Calvin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Idzik, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T21:47:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6d28f16-214a-55f2-8088-b5262b1169f3', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6d28f16-214a-55f2-8088-b5262b1169f3'}, {'abstract': 'A former Italian senator who received books that went missing from the Girolamini Library in Naples is trying to distance himself from one of the biggest rare-book-theft scandals in history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/books/book-theft-in-italy-with-a-hint-of-politics.html', 'snippet': 'A former Italian senator who received books that went missing from the Girolamini Library in Naples is trying to distance himself from one of the biggest rare-book-theft scandals in history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — For years, the books kept coming. A precious edition by Thomas More. Leather-bound volumes from the Italian Renaissance. Some stolen from the Baroque-era Girolamini Library in Naples, given as gifts to an influential longtime consigliere to former Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/theft24_cap/theft24_cap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/theft24_cap/theft24_cap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/theft24_cap/theft24_cap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/theft24_cap/theft24_cap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/theft24_cap/theft24_cap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/theft24_cap/theft24_cap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/theft24_cap/theft24_cap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Theft in Italy, With a Hint of Politics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Book Theft In Italy, With a Hint Of Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'n