 '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/26b8529d-475f-54ac-808a-e3b2011074b7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/26b8529d-475f-54ac-808a-e3b2011074b7'}, {'abstract': 'The Make Music Winter celebration in Prospect Park was marked by a participatory performance and unseasonably warm weather.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/arts/music/blink-brought-bicycles-to-make-music-winter-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'The Make Music Winter celebration in Prospect Park was marked by a participatory performance and unseasonably warm weather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, Make Music Winter, the annual solstice celebration of participatory performance, took place with an emphasis on its final word. I joined in “Winterize,” the baritone Christopher Dylan Herbert’s peripatetic outdoor version of Schubert’s “Winterreise,” at the Brooklyn Botanic Garden on a raw, gray afternoon as chilly as the melancholy score.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Romp, Meant to Ring in the Cold, Feels Like Spring', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Romp, Meant to Ring In the Cold, Feels Like Spring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Make Music Winter (Festival)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Make Music New York (Festival)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T21:58:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5861617-803b-5a8a-81ea-1a0baae9edd5', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5861617-803b-5a8a-81ea-1a0baae9edd5'}, {'abstract': 'Bobby Womack, 69, despite advancing age and what he said was Alzheimer’s disease, was in fine fettle on Friday at City Winery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/arts/music/bobby-womack-reviews-his-career-at-city-winery.html', 'snippet': 'Bobby Womack, 69, despite advancing age and what he said was Alzheimer’s disease, was in fine fettle on Friday at City Winery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Classic soul singing is, among countless other things, the art of the interjection. “Whoo!” “Mmmmm.” “Ohhhhhh.” “HahahaHA!” “Owww.” “Yeah, yeah!” “Am I lying?” Can I take my time?” “Listen to me!” “Do you feel it?” Used right, those interjections can be percussion, comedy, respiration, tension, release and more. Bobby Womack, 69, used them all at City Winery on Friday night, wearing a red leather suit, a red hat and red sunglasses as he started a three-night stand. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/WOMACK/WOMACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/WOMACK/WOMACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/WOMACK/WOMACK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/WOMACK/WOMACK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1274, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/WOMACK/WOMACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/WOMACK/WOMACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/arts/WOMACK/WOMACK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reaching for Soul’s High Ground', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reaching for Soul’s High Ground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Womack, Bobby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Winery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T22:04:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eb25e97-2034-565a-a8e3-e70a766bae98', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eb25e97-2034-565a-a8e3-e70a766bae98'}, {'abstract': 'Following annual trade and commerce talks with China, a senior Obama administration official discusses hopes for economic reforms announced in a Communist Party conference last month and progress on a government procurement deal and protection of trade secret and patents.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/q-and-a-u-s-commerce-secretary-penny-pritzker-on-china-trade-talks/', 'snippet': 'Following annual trade and commerce talks with China, a senior Obama administration official discusses hopes for economic reforms announced in a Communist Party conference last month and progress on a government procurement deal and protection of ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since a key Communist Party conference issued a plan in November to advance market reforms, a series of foreign envoys have rolled through China seeking to capitalize on some of its more business-friendly initiatives. Top American trade officials took the same tack during talks in Beijing last week, but made clear afterward that it would take time for United States businesses to reap dividends from the conference, known as the Third Plenum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: U.S. Commerce Secretary Penny Pritzker on China Trade Talks', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Procurement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Industrial Espionage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pritzker, Penny', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huawei Technologies Co Ltd', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T22:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Ansfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ansfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce9d7631-d78b-5ed0-b9e2-53bb221dc6c5', 'word_count': 1600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce9d7631-d78b-5ed0-b9e2-53bb221dc6c5'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement to bring the iPhone to China Mobile could, at least initially, give Apple a big lift into the vast Chinese market, analysts say, increasing its global sales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/technology/apple-and-china-mobile-sign-iphone-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement to bring the iPhone to China Mobile could, at least initially, give Apple a big lift into the vast Chinese market, analysts say, increasing its global sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just about any way you slice it, 763 million customers is a huge potential pie.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/business/23apple-web/23apple-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/business/23apple-web/23apple-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/business/23apple-web/23apple-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/business/23apple-web/23apple-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, '