nnel, and property, including our embassy, in South Sudan.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/obama-says-further-action-possible-in-south-sudan/', 'snippet': 'President Obama sent a letter Sunday to top congressional leaders in which he said he might take “further action to support the security of U.S. citizens, personnel, and property, including our embassy, in South Sudan.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONOLULU — After an attack on three United States aircraft attempting to evacuate American citizens from South Sudan, President Obama sent a letter Sunday to top congressional leaders in which he said he might take “further action” to support United States citizens and interests in the contested region.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Says ‘Further Action’ Possible in South Sudan', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Powers Act (1973)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T22:53:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/079a8d9a-549b-5460-b0e3-525684d19cc8', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/079a8d9a-549b-5460-b0e3-525684d19cc8'}, {'abstract': 'In which we give credit to Michael Blake and Andrea Carla Michaels for a smooth Monday solving experience.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/22/believe-you-me/', 'snippet': 'In which we give credit to Michael Blake and Andrea Carla Michaels for a smooth Monday solving experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — There is nothing better for my solving ego than a Monday Andrea Carla Michaels puzzle, and it’s not just because it’s Monday. It’s because she, along with her collaborator, Michael Blake, fills her puzzles with wonderful things that they and Will Shortz clue in such a way that my pencil never stops moving until the entire grid is filled. And when it’s done, I might not remember filling in all of the entries because it was just that smooth, but I know that I’ve had a good time. You really can’t ask for more than that on a Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Believe You Me', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T23:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6551ffec-0b6b-5161-a6f4-965f9582f3fe', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6551ffec-0b6b-5161-a6f4-965f9582f3fe'}, {'abstract': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/business/economy/treasury-auctions-set-for-the-week-of-dec-23.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Monday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for the Week of Dec. 23', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T23:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24293e11-ef6b-5bab-a5c0-43d819ec6944', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24293e11-ef6b-5bab-a5c0-43d819ec6944'}, {'abstract': 'In a holiday-shortened week, the Commerce Department will release data on personal income and spending in November, and durable goods figures for November will be reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/business/economy/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-dec-23.html', 'snippet': 'In a holiday-shortened week, the Commerce Department will release data on personal income and spending in November, and durable goods figures for November will be reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INCOME AND SPENDING On Monday, the Commerce Department will announce the data on personal income and spending in November. Economists on Wall Street are looking for an increase of 0.5 percent for both figures, according to Bloomberg, but a stronger reading would allay fears of weak overall economic growth in the fourth quarter of 2013. Growth is expected to slow substantially from the robust 4.1 percent annual pace recorded in the third quarter, but recent data has been a bit more positive so experts will be watching to see if that continued in November with personal income and spending.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week of Dec. 23', 'kicker': 'Looking Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economic Reports for the Week of Dec. 23', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Durable Goods (Economic Indicator)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-22T23:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e804262-25fe-558f-9396-9e22bf31cff6', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e804262-25fe-558f-9396-9e22bf31cff6'}, {'abstract': 'Readers reply to editorials in the “Numbers Crunch” series, about school systems here and abroad and about gifted students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/opinion/our-teaching-methods-and-theirs.html', 'snippet': 'Readers reply to editorials in the “Numbers Crunch” series, about school systems here and abroad and about gifted students.', 'lead_paragraph': ' ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/opinion/1223LETTERS/1223LETTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/23/opinion/1223LETTERS/1223LETTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 754}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit