}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63572497-7689-505e-88bf-eec25b0e2e69', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63572497-7689-505e-88bf-eec25b0e2e69'}, {'abstract': 'After his surprise release, Mikhail Khodorkovsky, once the richest of Russia’s oligarchs, challenged his fellow citizens to “take responsibility for their own fate.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/opinion/insights-into-democracy-refined-in-a-russian-prison.html', 'snippet': 'After his surprise release, Mikhail Khodorkovsky, once the richest of Russia’s oligarchs, challenged his fellow citizens to “take responsibility for their own fate.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — “I tried to look at my situation pragmatically,” Mikhail Khodorkovsky said quietly, trying to explain how he kept himself going for 10 years in prison and labor camps. “I said, O.K., so they got me; O.K., so the situation is bad. But it has certain possibilities.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insights Into Democracy, Refined in a Russian Prison', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Insights Into Democracy, Refined in a Russian Prison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovsky, Mikhail B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-23T02:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge Schmemann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmemann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5084328-507e-5040-bb66-1931d2dd4069', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5084328-507e-5040-bb66-1931d2dd4069'}, {'abstract': 'Viewers expect and deserve the show to bring its A game when it takes on a huge issue like the N.S.A., to serve as a stand-in for the American people and ask the uncomfortable questions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/business/media/when-60-minutes-checks-its-journalistic-skepticism-at-the-door.html', 'snippet': 'Viewers expect and deserve the show to bring its A game when it takes on a huge issue like the N.S.A., to serve as a stand-in for the American people and ask the uncomfortable questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, a study commissioned by the president concluded that the National Security Agency had reached too far into the private lives of Americans. The study, which came after a series of journalistic revelations exposing the agency’s surveillance practices, recommended numerous reforms that would curb the N.S.A.’s prerogatives. President Obama said he was “open to many” of the suggestions. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/13/business/carr-headshot-new/carr-headshot-new-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subTy