hazi (Libya)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-23T02:35:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5e89dfa-1bc8-5c40-a70e-28638e08e9dc', 'word_count': 1471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5e89dfa-1bc8-5c40-a70e-28638e08e9dc'}, {'abstract': 'British officials are considering solutions as large numbers of British youths go out on the weekends to get thoroughly, blindingly and often violently drunk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/world/europe/partying-until-drunk-and-disorderly-in-britain.html', 'snippet': 'British officials are considering solutions as large numbers of British youths go out on the weekends to get thoroughly, blindingly and often violently drunk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NORTHAMPTON, England — It was just after 4 a.m., the last clubs were closing and the police had three young men pinned against a brick wall and a fourth on the ground. The young men, gloriously incoherent, some of them bleeding, could barely stand, let alone answer the questions from the officers, who were responding to a fight. As the scene in downtown Northampton unfolded, another drunken young man slugged a passer-by, then fled.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Partying Until Drunk and Disorderly in Britain', 'kicker': 'Northampton Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Partying Until Drunk and Disorderly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name':