_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/051941da-b503-59a9-a91c-d7d0870b0ba9'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a policy against using plants that breach safety laws, the United States government spends more than $1.5 billion a year at overseas factories with a pattern of violations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/world/americas/buying-overseas-clothing-us-flouts-its-own-advice.html', 'snippet': 'Despite a policy against using plants that breach safety laws, the United States government spends more than $1.5 billion a year at overseas factories with a pattern of violations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — One of the world’s biggest clothing buyers, the United States government spends more than $1.5 billion a year at factories overseas, acquiring everything from the royal blue shirts worn by airport security workers to the olive button-downs required for forest rangers and the camouflage pants sold to troops on military bases.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Flouts Its Own Advice in Procuring Overseas Clothing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buying Overseas Clothing, U.S. Flouts Its Own Advice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urbina, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-23T03:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_d