ytimes.com/2013/12/23/small-businesses-showing-little-interest-in-state-shop-exchanges/', 'snippet': 'In part, it’s because businesses that want to offer health insurance to employees can find other ways to do so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For advocates of the Affordable Care Act, a central reform to help small businesses buy health insurance was the creation of state-run exchanges. As the law’s designers intended, a small company could go onto the exchanges and compare the virtues of competing plans. It could then offer its employees a choice from among several policies, even from different carriers — a benefit few companies now use. It could enroll in those plans online, and if the business were small enough, it could get temporary tax credits to offset the cost.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Small Businesses Showing Little Interest in State SHOP Exchanges', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-23T12:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/924de933-c6e9-5560-8e62-34bf23c85f50', 'word_count': 1316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/924de933-c6e9-5560-8e62-34bf23c85f50'}, {'abstract': 'A study suggests that being treated f