trucks and 25 armored vehicles were sent to Syria for the latest phase of the plan for destroying the stockpile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Russian defense minister, Sergei K. Shoigu, said Monday that 50 trucks and 25 armored vehicles had been delivered to the Syrian port of Latakia in recent days to help with the removal of the country’s chemical weapons stockpile, the latest sign of progress in that effort despite the grinding civil war.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Sends Vehicles to Syrian Port to Aid in Removal of Chemical Weapons Stockpile', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Sends Vehicles to Syrian Port to Aid in Removal of Chemical Weapons Stockpile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-23T19:08:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn and Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8a6316e-e246-5557-adbc-34a5eb2b4f17', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8a6316e-e246-5557-adbc-34a5eb2b4f17'}, {'abstract': 'A colorized broadcast of two “I Love Lucy” episodes outperformed a Peanuts Christmas special and the perennial holiday film “It’s a Wonderful Life” on Friday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/23/viewers-found-much-to-love-in-lucy-christmas-show/', 'snippet': 'A colorized broadcast of two “I Love Lucy” episodes outperformed a Peanuts Christmas special and the perennial holiday film “It’s a Wonderful Life” on Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be that television viewers are tiring of shows and characters that have become fixtures of Christmas programming, but that is not to say that they are necessarily hankering for something new. On Friday night, NBC presented “It’s A Wonderful Life,” the Jimmy Stewart-Donna Reed classic, and drew 5.37 million viewers, according to Nielsen figures, while Fox attracted 2.64 million viewers with “Happiness Is a Warm Blanket, Charlie Brown,” the most recent (2011) Peanuts Christmas special. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Viewers Found Much to Love in ‘Lucy’ Christmas Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-23T19:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a51f96ff-acad-5834-94ff-2a73d4768bd3', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a51f96ff-acad-5834-94ff-2a73d4768bd3'}, {'abstract': 'Parents with young children are buying them tablets and other devices, while the toy industry stalls, but retro toys, perhaps in a backlash, are resurgent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/business/for-babes-these-days-toyland-has-a-digital-bent.html', 'snippet': 'Parents with young children are buying them tablets and other devices, wh