t': 'Jonathan Miles’s novel “Want Not” follows a cast of New Yorkers and their encounters with one another and with trash, road kill and human waste.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Want Not,” Jonathan Miles’s second novel, opens with an immensely satisfying first paragraph, in which a city dweller named Talmadge looks at snow-covered trash bags along the sidewalk and, being thoroughly stoned, sees them as “alpine peaks.” Untying their knots, he imagines himself as “a god disassembling the Earth.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 472, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 472, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/book/book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Man’s Trash Is Another’s Treasure, and Another’s Crime', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Man’s Trash Is Another’s Treasure, And Another’s Crime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miles, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 