://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/science/on-new-caledonia-a-lone-survivor.html', 'snippet': 'The Amborella plant is the only direct descendant of the ancestor of all flowering plants on earth. Scientists have sequenced its genome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Found only on New Caledonia in the South Pacific, the Amborella plant is the only survivor in a lineage descending directly from the ancestor of all flowering plants. Scientists announced last week that they have sequenced its genome, which indicates that the explosion of flowering plants in the late Cretaceous period followed a “genetic doubling event” — a profusion of excess DNA in cells of the ancestor plant that eventually enabled a variety of new functions. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/science/24FLOA_SPAN/24FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/24/science/24FLOA_SPAN/24FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/science/24FLOA_SPAN/24FLOA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/science/24FLOA_SPAN/24FLOA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 950, 'width': 1425, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/science/24FLOA_SPAN/24FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/24/science/24FLOA_SPAN/24FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwi