bnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/multimedia/opdoc-santadrew/opdoc-santadrew-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/multimedia/opdoc-santadrew/opdoc-santadrew-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/multimedia/opdoc-santadrew/opdoc-santadrew-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christmas Icon Reform', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T00:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'Drew Christie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Drew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/ad25b785-2b56-506b-993e-310840dd3293', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/ad25b785-2b56-506b-993e-310840dd3293'}, {'abstract': 'Santa has gone too soft on kids, argues this animated Op-Doc, prompting the need for more frightening holiday icons like the German Krampus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/opinion/christmas-icon-reform.html', 'snippet': 'Santa has gone too soft on kids, argues this animated Op-Doc, prompting the need for more frightening holiday icons like the German Krampus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am by no means a Bah Humbug type about the Christmas season. Every year I buy a real tree and hang ornaments and stockings, and I’m constantly chastised for whistling Christmas tunes year round (“The Twelve Days of Christmas” and “Good King Wenceslas” being the favorites).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Christmas Icon Reform’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T00:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Drew Christie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Drew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e2a7c1f-754d-5812-a3b2-0626de239068', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e2a7c1f-754d-5812-a3b2-0626de239068'}, {'abstract': 'A grand jury found no evidence of criminal behavior by a Houston doctor who performs late-term abortions and was accused by anti-abortion groups of killing live-born babies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/us/texas-grand-jury-clears-abortion-provider.html', 'snippet': 'A grand jury found no evidence of criminal behavior by a Houston doctor who performs late-term abortions and was accused by anti-abortion groups of killing live-born babies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A grand jury in Harris County found no evidence of criminal behavior by a Houston doctor who performs late-term abortions and was accused by anti-abortion groups of killing live-born babies. In May, in a tape distributed by Operation Rescue, some former clinic employees accused Dr. Douglas Karpen of performing sloppy procedures and killing babies after they emerged from the womb, comparing him to Dr. Kermit Gosnell of Philadelphia, who had been convicted of murder that month after similar allegations. But in a statement issued Saturday, Devon Anderson, the Harris County district attorney, said: “An independent grand jury concluded, after lengthy investigation and deliberation, that the evidence does not justify an indictment." ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Grand Jury Clears Abortion Provider', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Grand Jury Clears Abortion Provider', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Operation Rescue', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karpen, Douglas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T00:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcf17316-1631-5699-8a25-35907aa4bdd4', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcf17316-1631-5699-8a25-35907aa4bdd4'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Brooks’s tenure and prolific output on New York’s first all-news radio station made him one of the most recognized voices on the radio for more than 40 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/nyregion/stan-brooks-a-familiar-voice-on-1010-wins-dies-at-86.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Brooks’s tenure and prolific output on New York’s first all-news radio station made him one of the most recognized voices on the radio for more than 40 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stan Brooks, a reporter whose long tenure and prolific output on New York’s first all-news radio station, 1010 WINS, made him one of the most recognized and consistent voices on the radio for more than 40 years, died on Monday in Manhattan. He was 86, and had worked until a month before his death, delivering his last report from City Hall on Nov. 20.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/nyregion/BROOKS-obit/BROOKS-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/24/nyregion/BROOKS-obit/BROOKS-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 767}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/nyregion/BROOKS-obit/BROOKS-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/nyregion/BROOKS-obit/BROOKS-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1603, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/nyregion/BROOKS-obit/BROOKS-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/24/nyregion/BROOKS-obit/BROOKS-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201