'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Molly Wood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Molly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de6e81ca-9e8d-55fb-a7d4-f57b4732a833', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de6e81ca-9e8d-55fb-a7d4-f57b4732a833'}, {'abstract': 'Simone Gorrindo recalls saying goodbye to her husband as he left for Afghanistan last December.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/deployed-before-christmas/', 'snippet': 'Simone Gorrindo recalls saying goodbye to her husband as he left for Afghanistan last December.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my husband and I have prepared for Christmas this year — picking up last-minute gifts, trying our hand at eggnog recipes, sharing wine late into the night — memories of last year’s season have been returning to me, clear and stark. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deployed Before Christmas', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Benning (Ga)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T14:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simone  Gorrindo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorrindo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cdd517f-59c5-5d98-bbf4-7462a3fe3850', 'word_count': 1413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cdd517f-59c5-5d98-bbf4-7462a3fe3850'}, {'abstract': 'A fresh look at NASA’s iconic Earthrise moment.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/nasas-christmas-eve-earthrise-revisited-and-revisualized/', 'snippet': 'A fresh look at NASA’s iconic Earthrise moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Chaikin, a historian of the Apollo space program, alerted me yesterday to a new NASA visualization of the moment, 45 years ago today, when the Apollo 8 astronauts, amid pre-planned operations, suddenly noticed the Earth “rising” over the lunar horizon. [On this Christmas Eve, two astronauts on the International Space Station are in the midst of a “spacewalk” (there has to be a better term) to repair cooling equipment. Live video is here.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NASA’s Christmas Eve ‘Earthrise,’ Revisited and Revisualized', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apollo Project', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T14:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d734f872-5b57-5e87-a1d0-07fd53c2198f', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d734f872-5b57-5e87-a1d0-07fd53c2198f'}, {'abstract': 'The crisis in South Sudan has broadened into a conflict in which longstanding ethnic divisions are fueling the violence and civilians are not accidental victims of the fighting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/world/africa/south-sudan-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'The crisis in South Sudan has broadened into a conflict in which longstanding ethnic divisions are fueling the violence and civilians are not accidental victims of the fighting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUBA, South Sudan — The security forces went house to house, rounding up civilians by the dozens and binding the wrists of some with wire, survivors said. Some were summarily shot in the street, they said, while others were hauled off to crowded cells. Bodies of the executed were tossed into shallow graves, one recalled. Another jail where civilians had been taken reeked of death, a witness said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/world/SUDAN-1/SUDAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/25/world/SUDAN-1/SUDAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/world/SUDAN-1/SUDAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/world/SUDAN-1/SUDAN-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1445, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':