'“Grudge Match” teams Sylvester Stallone and Robert De Niro as onetime boxing champions in an unlikely rematch 30 years after their last bout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Old jocks never die; they just team up. One veteran action hero may not be able to open a movie nowadays, but put two or more shoulder to shoulder in the same film, as in the “Expendables” series, and there’s gold to be mined and a senior male fan base to be activated. That’s the shrewd marketing philosophy behind “Grudge Match,” the overlong, drab, not-so-funny sports comedy that teams Sylvester Stallone and Robert De Niro as onetime boxing champions in an unlikely rematch 30 years after their last bout. Rocky versus the Raging Bull; how about that for a tagline? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Resentments Come Up Swinging', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Resentments Come Up Swinging, Making Plenty of Contact', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Grudge Match (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stallone, Sylvester', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Niro, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Segal, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T16:51:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b60ce9ce-30b6-5f1a-b4de-295c46e43f4e', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b60ce9ce-30b6-5f1a-b4de-295c46e43f4e'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Thomasson, a professor at Canisius College, in Buffalo, N.Y., owns the world’s largest collection of video games, with 10,607, according to the “Guinness World Records 2014 Gamer’s Edition.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/new-york-man-holds-largest-collection-of-video-games-guinness-says/', 'snippet': 'Michael Thomasson, a professor at Canisius College, in Buffalo, N.Y., owns the world’s largest collection of video games, with 10,607, according to the “Guinness World Records 2014 Gamer’s Edition.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Video game fanatics who find a copy of the new “Guinness World Records 2014 Gamer’s Edition” under their trees will discover that Richard Lecce, the king of collectors, first listed in the 2010 edition, has been deposed. The new Guinness-certified owner of the world’s largest video game collection is Michael Thomasson, a game designer and professor at Canisius College, in Buffalo. (Mr. Thomasson’s subjects are video game history, graphics and game design.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Man Holds Largest Collection of Video Games, Guinness Says', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T16:52:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f64a7ace-fa50-54a7-950f-efc3180954bd', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f64a7ace-fa50-54a7-950f-efc3180954bd'}, {'abstract': 'One member of a seized Greenpeace vessel’s crew received a pardon, and if the amnesty covers the rest, it will draw to a close one of the more contentious chapters in the organization’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/world/europe/russian-amnesty-now-includes-greenpeace-case.html', 'snippet': 'One member of a seized Greenpeace vessel’s crew received a pardon, and if the amnesty covers the rest, it will draw to a close one of the more contentious chapters in the organization’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A sweeping amnesty that is underway in Russia was extended on Tuesday to a member of the crew of the Arctic Sunrise, the Greenpeace International ship seized on the open seas three months ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amnesty by Russians Includes Greenpeace Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vast Amnesty By Russians Includes Case Of Greenpeace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T16:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material'