ong-young-musicians/', 'snippet': 'The prizes recognize musicians in the early stage of their careers who demonstrate “artistic excellence, outstanding work ethic, a spirit of determination and great potential for leadership.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The\xa0Sphinx Organization, a national training program devoted to getting black and Hispanic students involved in classical music performance, announced the winners of its 2014 artist scholarships on Tuesday. The awards, for musicians in the early stages of their careers who demonstrate, as Sphinx puts it, “artistic excellence, outstanding work ethic, a spirit of determination and great potential for leadership,” include a $50,000 career-development scholarship and the organization’s Medal of Excellence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sphinx Awards Highlight Promise Among Young Musicians', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sphinx Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T18:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/232aa355-0e37-5f8f-9874-c38386d81063', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/232aa355-0e37-5f8f-9874-c38386d81063'}, {'abstract': 'She took in a Los Angeles performance of the one-person show, which stars Bette Midler as Sue Mengers, Ms. Streisand’s former agent.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/streisand-sees-ill-eat-you-last-at-last/', 'snippet': 'She took in a Los Angeles performance of the one-person show, which stars Bette Midler as Sue Mengers, Ms. Streisand’s former agent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the question that loomed over Broadway last spring: Would Barbra Streisand attend a performance of “I’ll Eat You Last,” the one-woman play starring Bette Midler as the real-life Hollywood agent Sue Mengers, whose falling-out with Ms. Streisand is the juicy meat of the show? Ms. Streisand never went, but her publicist confirmed this week that the actress and director did see “I’ll Eat You Last” during its run this month at the Geffen Playhouse in Los Angeles. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/24artsbeat-bette/24artsbeat-bette-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/24artsbeat-bette/24artsbeat-bette-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/24artsbeat-bette/24artsbeat-bette-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/24artsbeat-bette/24artsbeat-bette-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/24artsbeat-bette/24artsbeat-bette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/24artsbeat-bette/24artsbeat-bette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/arts/24artsbeat-bette/24artsbeat-bette-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Streisand Sees ‘I’ll Eat You Last’ at Last', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Logan, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mengers, Sue', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Midler, Bette', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streisand, Barbra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Geffen Playhouse', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T18:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfbaf6b1-3a1c-5f21-918d-2565076255cc', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfbaf6b1-3a1c-5f21-918d-2565076255cc'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Secret Life of Walter Mitty,” Ben Stiller is an office drone with an active fantasy life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/movies/the-secret-life-of-walter-mitty-stars-ben-stiller.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Secret Life of Walter Mitty,” Ben Stiller is an office drone with an active fantasy life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As imagined by Ben Stiller, Walter Mitty is a man out of step with his time. An archetypal daydreamer introduced to the public by James Thurber as a henpecked suburban husband and later impersonated on screen by Danny Kaye as a misunderstood, starry-eyed sweetheart with a lovely singing voice, Walter has evolved into a modern office drone with an unusually active fantasy life. He is also, in some respects, the opposite of just about every other comic hero in American movies today, including many played by Mr. Stiller. And “The Secret Life of Walter Mitty,” directed by Mr. Stiller (who takes the title role), has a dreamy, melancholy tone quite different from what you might expect to find in a big-budget holiday comedy. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Can Balance a Checkbook, but Not His Imagination ', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Can Balance a Checkbook, but Not His Imagination', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Secret Life of Walter Mitty (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiller, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T18:28:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f13a05e9-93b2-5f1f-bb9d-37ee4f279e81', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f13a05e9-93b2-5f1f-bb9d-37ee4f279e81'}, {'abstract': 'Reader suggestions for how to stem an insect invasion.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/24/13-solutions-for-fighting-crazy-ants/', 'snippet': 'Reader suggestions for how to stem an insect invasion.', 'lead_paragraph': '