 be greatly helped if they unearth a file containing “The Wolf of Wall Street,” Martin Scorsese’s three-hour bacchanal of sex, drugs and conspicuous consumption. Then as now, the movie is likely to be the subject of intense scholarly debate: Does it offer a sustained and compelling diagnosis of the terminal pathology that afflicts us, or is it an especially florid symptom of the disease?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Greed Was Good (and Fun)', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Greed Was Good (and Fun)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiCaprio, Leonardo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Wolf of Wall Street (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T20:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5822b5f-8a19-551c-bb2a-fe19e8104f67', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5822b5f-8a19-551c-bb2a-fe19e8104f67'}, {'abstract': 'In training camp with a group of high achiever, quirks and bizarre rituals become apparent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/sports/soccer/genius-or-insanity.html', 'snippet': 'In training camp with a group of high achiever, quirks and bizarre rituals become apparent.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Here’s to the crazy ones — the misfits, the rebels, the troublemakers, the round pegs in the square holes. The ones who see things differently — they’re not f