trying once again to hack into media organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a happy hacker holiday once again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/technology/24bits-sea/24bits-sea-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/24/technology/24bits-sea/24bits-sea-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/technology/24bits-sea/24bits-sea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/technology/24bits-sea/24bits-sea-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/technology/24bits-sea/24bits-sea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/24/technology/24bits-sea/24bits-sea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/technology/24bits-sea/24bits-sea-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Syrian Electronic Army Is at It Again', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syrian Electronic Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T23:43:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/527ea2d8-1268-5722-841a-fc59ff33a612', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/527ea2d8-1268-5722-841a-fc59ff33a612'}, {'abstract': 'For a Jewish kid, in Leningrad and then Queens, disguises were mystifying. They still are.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/opinion/its-the-most-unknowable-time-of-the-year.html', 'snippet': 'For a Jewish kid, in Leningrad and then Queens, disguises were mystifying. They still are.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE of my first childhood memories: New Year’s Eve, Leningrad, 1976. The doorbell rings, my mother opens it, and a bear walks in on his hind legs. Four-year-old me starts trembling. Bear! Bear! Soon I will be eaten. No, my mother tells me: “It’s Grandfather Frost,” the secular, socialist-friendly Russian equivalent of Santa Claus, with New Year’s standing in for Christmas. And it’s true. On top of his shabby gray-white fur that makes him so uniquely ursine, the bear sports a red hat and a flowing white beard made of cotton balls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/opinion/1225OPEDdoliveux/1225OPEDdoliveux-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/25/opinion/1225OPEDdoliveux/1225OPEDdoliveux-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 595}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/opinion/1225OPEDdoliveux/1225OPEDdoliveux-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1016, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/opinion/1225OPEDdoliveux/1225OPEDdoliveux-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 1560, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/opinion/1225OPEDdoliveux/1225OPEDdoliveux-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/25/opinion/1225OPEDdoliveux/1225OPEDdoliveux-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/opinion/1225OPEDdoliveux/1225OPEDdoliveux-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s the Most Unknowable Time of the Year', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s the Most Unknowable Time of the Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shteyngart, Gary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T23:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Shteyngart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shteyngart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cdef3fc-a06a-5066-b640-40ebf761aff9', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cdef3fc-a06a-5066-b640-40ebf761aff9'}, {'abstract': 'Light fixtures reminiscent of the industrial age relieve rooms of a feeling of preciousness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/garden/ruggedly-handsome-lamps.html', 'snippet': 'Light fixtures reminiscent of the industrial age relieve rooms of a feeling of preciousness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An advocate of a laid-back California style, the interior designer Trip Haenisch, 51, works hard to create rooms that don’t appear precious. He wants people “to feel like they can just jump on a sofa and put their feet up, or move furniture around,” he said, even if those people are celebrities. (Courteney Cox and Hank Azaria are among his clients.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruggedly Handsome Lamps', 'kicker': 'Shopping With Trip Haenisch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seen in a Rough Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKeough, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lamps and Lampshades', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haenisch, Trip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-24T23:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdd6dc1a-2c5c-5514-9c34-e2b832987ff1', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdd6dc1a-2c5c-5514-9c34-e2b832987ff1'}, {'abstract': 'Neither leukemia nor a daunting number of new constructions kept the author of “A Field Guide to American Houses” from extending her life’s work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/12/26/garden/20131226-MCALESTER.html', 'snippet': 'Neither leukemia nor a daunting number of new constructions kept the author of “A Field Guide to American Houses” from extending her life’s work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neither leukemia nor a daunting number of new constructions kept the author of “A Field Guide to American Houses” from extending her life’s work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/garden/20131226-MCALLISTER-slide-69UK/20131226-MCALLISTER-slide-69UK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/26/garden/20131226-MCALLISTER-slide-69UK/20131226-MCALLISTER-slide-69UK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/garden/20131226-MCALLISTER-slide-69UK/20131226-MCALLISTER-slide-69UK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/garden/2