 Field Guide to American Houses” from extending her life’s work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/garden/virginia-savage-mcalester-leading-the-ultimate-house-tour.html', 'snippet': 'Neither leukemia nor a daunting number of new constructions kept the author of “A Field Guide to American Houses” from extending her life’s work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dallas — If Virginia Savage McAlester were going to die of leukemia, the right time would have been before she ordered a new Texas historical marker for her house. Space on the plaque was at a premium: The 6,000-square-foot home has been in the family since 1921, and her patrician forebears have played an influential role in the city for most of those years.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia Savage McAlester: Leading the Ultimate House Tour', 'kicker': 'At Home With', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She Leads The Ultimate House Tour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorello, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAlester, Virginia Savage', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T00:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tortorello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tortorello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd9aa884-00e0-52c6-a757-8275f63a3