year. But it is the most joyous and the most richly seasonal. Around Christmas Day orbit the lesser holidays that help account for the texture of this season: days of shopping and decorating, the days of Advent and Christmas Eve, the liturgical 12 days that end in Twelfth Night, better known to most of us as Jan. 5. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Day of Good Cheer', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Day of Good Cheer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T01:24:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1919e7-6e9f-5751-a730-6795e39997e9', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1919e7-6e9f-5751-a730-6795e39997e9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Wolfenson and his partner, Harvey Ratner, returned N.B.A. basketball to Minnesota in 1989, nearly 30 years after the Lakers had departed for California.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/sports/basketball/marv-wolfenson-87-dies-led-an-nba-rebirth-in-minnesota.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Wolfenson and his partner, Harvey Ratner, returned N.B.A. basketball to Minnesota in 1989, nearly 30 years after the Lakers had departed for California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marv Wolfenson, who with his longtime business partner, Harvey Ratner, brought N.B.A. basketball back to Minnesota in the form of the Timberwolves, died on Saturday in the La Jolla section of San Diego. He was 87.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non