re are no official religious holidays celebrated in China, so the observation of Christmas there, where an American business owner has set up a subsidiary, requires explanation.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/celebrating-christmas-in-china/', 'snippet': 'There are no official religious holidays celebrated in China, so the observation of Christmas there, where an American business owner has set up a subsidiary, requires explanation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was a little girl, I raised money for missionaries who were taking Bibles into China. As the daughter of a preacher, it was one of many similar projects I undertook, like going door to door to collect money for starving children in Africa and gathering wheelchairs and crutches to send to missionary doctors in South America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Christmas in China', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weidenhamer, Deb', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auction Systems Auctioneers and Appraisers Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T12:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Weidenhamer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename':