s and pool the results.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/tragedy-tricorders-and-aspiring-to-map-ones-body/', 'snippet': 'A year inside a hospital gave a technologist an idea: Why can’t medical devices be more like software products, relying more on algorithms, iteration and data sharing? The result is a consumer product that promises to allow people to map their bod...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Walter De Brouwer puts his head to something, he can produce single-handedly what usually takes several hospital machines and labs. His single hand, it should be said, holds a small and promising device with which Mr. De Brouwer, the co-founder and chief executive of Scanadu, hopes to remake medicine.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/business/24bits-scandu/24bits-scandu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/24/business/24bits-scandu/24bits-scandu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/business/24bits-scandu/24bits-scandu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/business/24bits-scandu/24bits-scandu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/business/24bits-scandu/24bits-scandu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/24/business/24bits-scandu/24bits-scandu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/24/business/24bits-scandu/24bits-scandu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Personal Tragedy, Tricorders and the Idea of Mapping One’s Body', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hurt Son Inspires Father’s Invention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Brouwer, Walter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IndieGoGo.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scanadu', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T12:59:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a982a073-0064-590a-aabd-8e4407dc427a', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a982a073-0064-590a-aabd-8e4407dc427a'}, {'abstract': 'An ode to the nuance and narrative of smaller video games in a world dominated by big-budget titles.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/game-theory-the-year-of-the-indie/', 'snippet': 'An ode to the nuance and narrative of smaller video games in a world dominated by big-budget titles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Increasingly this year, I’ve enjoyed games made by passionate coteries of video game artisans, so much so that for me this is the Year of the Indie. Not that independent games are new. The other day, cold and shivering, I arrived early at the Museum of the Moving Image’s “Indie Essentials” exhibition to take in 25 games quietly, meditatively. I was warmed, then moved, by this recent history of indies, spartanly staged in low light, each a gem of shining creativity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Game Theory: The Year of the Indie', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T13:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harold Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harold', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5deafe1-a98b-53a3-88de-4f43208885a6', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5deafe1-a98b-53a3-88de-4f43208885a6'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: When a passenger decides to engage in conversation with his taxi driver, he discovers a common bond.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/an-armenian-christmas-surprise/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: When a passenger decides to engage in conversation with his taxi driver, he discovers a common bond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary,', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Armenian Christmas Surprise', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Armenians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'g