E.T.A. Hoffmann’s “Nutcracker and Mouse-King”; Beatrix Potter’s “The Tale of Two Bad Mice”), but there’s usually a difference between the two. Though mice are often portrayed as naughty, they are rarely as utterly repellent as rats. The sweet “Mouse House Tales,” by Susan Pearson with illustrations by Amanda Shepherd, and the hilarious and down-and-dirty “Cheese Belongs to You!,” by Alexis Deacon with illustrations by Viviane Schwarz, perpetuate this traditional polarity. But whatever your feelings about rodents, these two books shouldn’t be missed, even if you have to perch on a chair to read them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/books/25childrens-1/25childrens-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 303, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/25/books/25childrens-1/25childrens-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 303}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/books/25childrens-1/25childrens-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 518, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/books/25childrens-1/25childrens-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1036, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/books/25childrens-1/25childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/25/books/25childrens-1/25childrens-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty