perJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/world/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/world/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/25/world/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/world/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86/20131225_XMAS_337-slide-VD86-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christmas Around the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T18:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e9239e36-8252-5799-817e-3e5502381f54', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e9239e36-8252-5799-817e-3e5502381f54'}, {'abstract': 'Audiences got an early taste of a resurrected Holmes in a seven-minute episode that made its debut this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/a-teasing-online-return-for-sherlock/', 'snippet': 'Audiences got an early taste of a resurrected Holmes in a seven-minute episode that made its debut this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was never a doubt that Benedict Cumberbatch would return to the role of Sherlock Holmes, the modernized incarnation of Arthur Conan Doyle’s consulting detective he plays on the hit BBC series “Sherlock.” Despite a second-season finale in 2012 that seemed to show Holmes falling to his death, Mr. Cumberbatch’s star has risen considerably since then (in films like “Star Trek Into Darkness” and “The Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug”), and besides, the BBC had already committed to a third season of “Sherlock.” (The series is shown in the United States on PBS’s “Masterpiece.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Teasing Online Return for ‘Sherlock’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holmes, Sherlock (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumberbatch, Benedict', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doyle, Arthur Conan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T18:51:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1553640-ba8b-5081-901d-2b5aecc44152', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1553640-ba8b-5081-901d-2b5aecc44152'}, {'abstract': 'Cut off from the world for much of her life, Hanny Lerner built her business in part by learning how to ask for help.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/an-entrepreneur-who-bypassed-fear-and-embraced-networking/', 'snippet': 'Cut off from the world for much of her life, Hanny Lerner built her business in part by learning how to ask for help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We just published\xa0a conversation with Hanny Lerner, the founder and president of MOD Restoration, a furniture reupholstering company in Brooklyn. In the interview, Ms. Lerner, 29, who grew up in a Hasidic community with limited information about the outside world, discussed how she managed to get up to speed and grow her business, which had 2013 sales of just under $2 million and employs about 10.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bypassing Fear and Embracing Networking', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Entrepreneurs' Organization", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T19:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc24b44b-d739-5e57-935b-2fccafff7ebc', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc24b44b-d739-5e57-935b-2fccafff7ebc'}, {'abstract': 'Terence Winter, creator of “Boardwalk Empire,” talks about crime and locations in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/travel/mapping-a-darker-side-of-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Terence Winter, creator of “Boardwalk Empire,” talks about crime and locations in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City has long been associated with crime, in drama and in reality. From early 