, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c852e5c-4f42-501a-84a1-4095ad52a074'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets delivered yet another halfhearted performance in a loss to the Chicago Bulls, and the fans at Barclays Center let them know about it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/bulls-third-quarter-outburst-sinks-nets.html', 'snippet': 'The Nets delivered yet another halfhearted performance in a loss to the Chicago Bulls, and the fans at Barclays Center let them know about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chorus of boos and jeers started with about half a minute left in the game, when Tornike Shengelia tried to dribble the ball behind his back but instead felt it stripped away. Shengelia, an infrequently used reserve, was far from the object of the fans’ ire, but he was the Nets player unfortunate enough to be standing there when it all finally boiled over. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/26nets-1/26nets-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/26nets-1/26nets-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 806}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/26nets-1/26nets-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 763, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/26nets-1/26nets-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1525, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/26nets-1/26nets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/26nets-1/26nets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/26nets-1/26nets-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets’ Effort Questioned, by Fans and by Coach', 'kicker': 'Bulls 95, Nets 78', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Nets Collapse, Fans and Bulls Let Them Have It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibson, Taj', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T19:51:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1a90bbf-5a56-55c2-817c-bafc6d7e6c84', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1a90bbf-5a56-55c2-817c-bafc6d7e6c84'}, {'abstract': 'Kent Tritle led the Oratorio Society in Handel’s “Messiah” for a capacity crowd at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/arts/music/messiah-by-the-oratorio-society-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Kent Tritle led the Oratorio Society in Handel’s “Messiah” for a capacity crowd at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Oratorio Society, under the direction of Kent Tritle, performed Handel’s “Messiah” in front of a capacity crowd on Monday at Carnegie Hall. The stage was also filled to capacity. The society’s choir has close to 200 singers. The alto section alone, with 59 members, is more than twice as big as, say, the entire Choir of Trinity Wall Street, whose “Messiah” I also reviewed this month.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26ORATORIO/26ORATORIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26ORATORIO/26ORATORIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26ORATORIO/26ORATORIO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26ORATORIO/26ORATORIO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1245, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26ORATORIO/26ORATORIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26ORATORIO/26ORATORIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26ORATORIO/26ORATORIO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Handel Well Populated, Onstage and Off', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Handel Well Populated, Onstage and Off ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tritle, Kent', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handel, George Frederick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oratorio Society of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T19:54:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8918678b-80b3-50ea-b2b3-eaba072274f8', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8918678b-80b3-50ea-b2b3-eaba072274f8'}, {'abstract': 'The artist created a limited edition of seven tiny gold masks, one to represent each day of the week. Today’s is a silly cure for a case of the Mondays.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/25/feeling-for-ugo-rondinones-miniature-wearable-art/', 'snippet': 'The artist created a limited edition of seven tiny gold masks, one to represent each day of the week. Today’s is a silly cure for a case of the Mondays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art is my job and my passion. I look at it, think about it, talk about it and write about it. Now, thanks to the artist Ugo Rondinone, I dream of wearing it. Rondinone made a splash earlier this year when an installation of his nine colossal stone sculptures, often likened to Stonehenge, inhabited Rockefeller Center. A few months later, in collaboration with the creative couple Sebastien and Stephanie Jannssen, Rondinone created mythical little masks that fit into the palm of your hand. The seven 23-karat-gold sculptures, created in a limited edition of six (plus three artist’s proofs), represent each day of the week and can be worn as a pendant. This enigmatic piece is sure to cure any case of the Mondays by making even the most cynical among us smile. Like most great works, it’s an investment piece. But as any art lover will tell you, it’s impossible to own all the art you want. That’s what dreams are for. Price upon request; sorrywereclosed.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/t-magazine/25rondinone-gassmann/25rondinone-gassmann-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/25/t-magazine/25rondinone-gassmann/25rondinone-gassmann-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 731}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/t-magazine/25rondinone-gassmann/25rondinone-gassmann-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/t-magazine/25rondinone-gassmann/25rondinone-gassmann-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1208, 'width': 991, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/25/t-magazine/25rondinone-gassmann/25rondinone-gassmann-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/25/t-magazine/25rondinone-gassmann/25rondinone-gassmann-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'captio