ect', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T20:25:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd0ab9e5-2f9e-5199-a610-857da2854bbe', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd0ab9e5-2f9e-5199-a610-857da2854bbe'}, {'abstract': 'Bridge deals, though, can resemble a boxing match. One side tries to deliver the telling blow, when the other sidesteps and lands the lethal counterpunch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/crosswords/bridge/how-a-bridge-deal-can-resemble-a-boxing-match.html', 'snippet': 'Bridge deals, though, can resemble a boxing match. One side tries to deliver the telling blow, when the other sidesteps and lands the lethal counterpunch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Britain and other countries in the Commonwealth, Dec. 26 is known as Boxing Day. It has nothing to do with pugilism. Instead, in the Middle Ages, the landed gentry would deliver gifts in boxes to their serfs on this day.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26cardIMg/26cardIMg-jumbo.png', 'height': 524, 'width': 284, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26cardIMg/26cardIMg-superJumbo.png', 'height': 524, 'width': 284, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/arts/26cardIMg/26cardIMg-