ness start-ups as a key to the future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/business/international/japanese-entrepreneurs-receive-tentative-embrace.html', 'snippet': 'While prejudice against entrepreneurs lingers in Japan, the nation is increasingly trying to encourage business start-ups as a key to the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The 20-somethings in jeans sipping espresso and tapping on laptops at this Tokyo business incubator would look more at home in Silicon Valley than in Japan, where for years the surest signs of success were the gray suits of its corporate salarymen. But for those hoping the nation’s latest economic plan will drag Japan from its long malaise, the young men and women here at Samurai Startup Island represent a crucial component: a revival of entrepreneurship.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Start-Up Spirit Emerges in Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Start-Up Spirit Emerges in Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koizumi, Junichiro', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horie, Takafumi', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-25T22:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fa