': 'nyt://article/d6e29450-5cc9-54d9-b4db-eb1ae4f21016'}, {'abstract': 'A new exhibit at the National Archives, “Record of Rights,” makes clear that the Constitution is still a work in progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/opinion/greenhouse-a-work-still-in-progress.html', 'snippet': 'A new exhibit at the National Archives, “Record of Rights,” makes clear that the Constitution is still a work in progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the country observed the Constitution’s 200th anniversary back in 1987, two narratives vied for public acceptance. There was the triumphalist narrative celebrated in Philadelphia, where a quarter-million people took part in a 15-hour-long gala, lining the route for a parade with floats that included a 40-foot replica of a parchment scroll.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/linda-greenhouse/linda-greenhouse-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/linda-greenhouse/linda-greenhouse-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/linda-greenhouse/linda-greenhouse-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/linda-greenhouse/linda-greenhouse-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/linda-greenhouse/linda-greenhouse-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'th