e/9e7a489f-0a1d-5cab-b23d-9905ad415e69'}, {'abstract': 'With Kobe Bryant out with a fractured kneecap, the overmatched Lakers lost to the Heat as LeBron James, Chris Bosh and Dwyane Wade made enough plays when they needed to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/sports/basketball/without-bryant-a-rivalry-goes-unfulfilled-as-the-lakers-lose-to-the-heat.html', 'snippet': 'With Kobe Bryant out with a fractured kneecap, the overmatched Lakers lost to the Heat as LeBron James, Chris Bosh and Dwyane Wade made enough plays when they needed to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Kobe Bryant, a creature of habit and one of symbolism, too, acknowledged it was a strange feeling to wake up on Christmas morning for the first time in 15 seasons without a basketball game to play.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/yyylakers/yyylakers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1033, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/yyylakers/yyylakers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1033}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/yyylakers/yyylakers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 596, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/yyylakers/yyylakers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1191, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/yyylakers/yyylakers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/yyylakers/yyylakers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/26/sports/yyylakers/yyylakers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rivalry Goes Unfulfilled as the Lakers Fall to the Heat', 'kicker': 'Heat 101, Lakers 95', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rivalry Goes Unfulfilled as the Lakers Fall to the Heat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Kobe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T02:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e46abad8-3a66-544d-8a5e-cba63861b201', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e46abad8-3a66-544d-8a5e-cba63861b201'}, {'abstract': 'To cope with a worsening crisis, the Federal Housing Finance Agency should jump-start a trust fund program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/opinion/a-step-toward-affordable-housing.html', 'snippet': 'To cope with a worsening crisis, the Federal Housing Finance Agency should jump-start a trust fund program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Melvin Watt, a Democrat of North Carolina, who was confirmed earlier this month as the director of the Federal Housing Finance Agency, will need to use all of his agency’s powers to cope with a worsening affordable housing crisis that is placing poor and elderly Americans at risk of homelessness and forcing many of the nation’s 43 million renters to skimp on food and medical care to meet the rent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Step Toward Affordable Housing', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Step Toward Affordable Housing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watt, Melvin L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Housing Finance Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Housing Trust Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T02:13:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4054aade-afce-5690-b89a-729ae474171c', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4054aade-afce-5690-b89a-729ae474171c'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge did not recognize that the threat to religious liberty comes from employers trying to impose their religious views on workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/opinion/mistaken-ruling-on-contraception.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge did not recognize that the threat to religious liberty comes from employers trying to impose their religious views on workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The contraception mandate in the new health care reform law accommodates religious beliefs. It exempts houses of worship from having to provide contraceptive coverage without a co-pay. Church-affiliated organizations like schools and hospitals need only send a short form to their insurance administrator, which takes care of the coverage. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mistaken Ruling on Contraception', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mistaken Ruling on Contraception', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cogan, Brian M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T02:15:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c208d54f-d45f-57a8-9da9-34de80dcbea5', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c208d54f-d45f-57a8-9da9-34de80dcbea5'}, {'abstract': 'After 16 years of stories that raised as many thoughts and ideas as animals and pets, this is the last installment of The Rural Life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/opinion/farewell.html', 'snippet': 'After 16 years of stories that raised as many thoughts and ideas as animals and pets, this is the last installment of The Rural Life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first Rural Life appeared on the editorial page nearly 16 years ago. This is the last. This seems a good season to leave, with a long winter ahead, the wood stove burning, and plenty of hopes and plans for the coming year. When The Rural Life began, I didn’t imagine that it would last so long or chart so many changes in my life. Nor did I imagine that it would find so many good readers. But it has, and I’m grateful for that.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Farewell', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Farewell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinkenborg, Verlyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T02:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_ma