ument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ece81414-b6a3-5d3a-92c2-250ec9d0a578', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ece81414-b6a3-5d3a-92c2-250ec9d0a578'}, {'abstract': 'Gotham Chamber Opera has earned a strong reputation in recent seasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/arts/music/chamber-opera-and-rachmaninoff.html', 'snippet': 'Gotham Chamber Opera has earned a strong reputation in recent seasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gotham Chamber Opera has earned a strong reputation in recent seasons, presenting unusual repertory, innovative productions and excellent young singers. Here it partners with the equally estimable music forces of Trinity Church for a staging in St. Paul’s Chapel by Andrew Eggert of “La Descente d’Orphée aux Enfers” (“The Descent of Orpheus to the Underworld”). This chamber opera by Marc-Antoine Charpentier will be conducted by Neal Goren, Gotham’s artistic director. The cast includes Daniel Curran as Orphée. (7 p.m., Wednesday and Friday, Broadway and Fulton Street, Lower Manhattan; 212-868-4460, gothamchamberopera.org.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chamber Opera and Rachmaninoff', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chamber Opera And Rachmaninoff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:25:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0da54785-4b13-5547-acad-87319c1f350f', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0da54785-4b13-5547-acad-87319c1f350f'}, {'abstract': 'Where and how to ring in the New Year is a perennial question. If you’re feeling festive and want to make a full night of it, there are several theater-related offerings to choose from.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/theater/legendary-ways-to-ring-in-the-year.html', 'snippet': 'Where and how to ring in the New Year is a perennial question. If you’re feeling festive and want to make a full night of it, there are several theater-related offerings to choose from.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where and how to ring in the New Year is a perennial question. If you’re feeling festive and want to make a full night of it, there are several theater-related offerings to choose from. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GUIDE3_SPAN/29GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GUIDE3_SPAN/29GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GUIDE3_SPAN/29GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GUIDE3_SPAN/29GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GUIDE3_SPAN/29GUIDE3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GUIDE3_SPAN/29GUIDE3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GUIDE3_SPAN/29GUIDE3_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Legendary Ways to Ring in the Year', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Legendary Ways To Ring In the Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:26:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c7f8a0e-262e-5291-835b-161afd779f0b', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c7f8a0e-262e-5291-835b-161afd779f0b'}, {'abstract': '“The New Rijksmuseum,” Oeke Hoogendijk’s beautifully shot film presents the countless concerns that went into a $500 million transformation of Amsterdam’s signature museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/movies/armchair-travels-to-amsterdam.html', 'snippet': '“The New Rijksmuseum,” Oeke Hoogendijk’s beautifully shot film presents the countless concerns that went into a $500 million transformation of Amsterdam’s signature museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine if the Metropolitan Museum of Art suspended operations for almost a decade to undergo a major makeover. That gives you an idea of the scale in “The New Rijksmuseum,” Oeke Hoogendijk’s almost-four-hour documentary, playing as a Film Forum double feature through Wednesday. Ms. Hoogendijk’s beautifully shot film presents the countless concerns — among them unending revisions demanded of architects; a transition between general directors; and contentious meetings with politicians, contractors and the very vocal Dutch Cyclists Union — that went into a $500 million transformation of Amsterdam’s signature museum.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Armchair Travels, to Amsterdam', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Armchair Travels, To Amsterdam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2f97c27-2d03-5ef3-ba7a-be5278b49672', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2f97c27-2d03-5ef3-ba7a-be5278b49672'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet presents final performances of “George Balanchine’s The Nutcracker,” while Momix continues its illusionary, body-conscious spectacle at the Joyce Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/arts/dance/holiday-soul-and-illusion.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet presents final performances of “George Balanchine’s The Nutcracker,” while Momix continues its illusionary, body-conscious spectacle at the Joyce Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s that end-of-December feeling: The last thing you want to do is step into a shop. Mercifully, there are mood-altering alternatives. New York City Ballet presents final performances of “George Balanchine’s The Nutcracker,” while Momix continues its illusionary, body-conscious spectacle at the Joyce Theater with Moses Pendleton’s “Momix reMIX.” And for some holiday soul, Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater continues its season with three programs. On New Year’s Eve, “Revelations” will feature Ailey veterans of the past and present, including Linda Denise Fisher-Harrell, Renee Robinson, Guillermo Asca, Elizabeth Roxas-Dobrish, Dudley Williams and Donna Wood Sanders. Next Sunday, there’s the season finale, showcasing excerpts from Ailey’s dances and the season’s new works along with “Revelations” in its entirety. It would have been Ailey’s 83rd birthday. Bring your party hat.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Soul and Illusion', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holiday Soul And Illusion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bf323e3-ad83-55ab-b142-4500cfce89e1', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bf323e3-ad83-55ab-b142-4500cfce89e1'}, {'abstract': 'In this episode of Teton Gravity Research’s “Behind The Line,” the skier Sage Cattabriga-Alosa has to tunnel through a snow mass to get to a ski run in Alaska.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/100000002621218/pro-skier-hacks-into-death-defying-run.html', 'snippet': 'In this episode of Teton Gravity Research’s “Behind The Line,” the skier Sage Cattabriga-Alosa has to tunnel through a snow 