dline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teton Gravity Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:27:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'Teton Gravity Research', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teton', 'middlename': 'Gravity', 'lastname': 'Research', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/cf97674a-7045-5681-a3b0-0570064df6fb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cf97674a-7045-5681-a3b0-0570064df6fb'}, {'abstract': 'The new Egyptrixx album, “A/B Til Infinity,” is a lustrous and resonant thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/arts/music/grooving-to-egyptrixx.html', 'snippet': 'The new Egyptrixx album, “A/B Til Infinity,” is a lustrous and resonant thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Egyptrixx album, “A/B Til Infinity,” is a lustrous and resonant thing. Released on the Night Slugs label, home to some of the most challenging but danceable music of the last couple of years, it relies heavily on texture, scrape and atmosphere for its effect, and only sometimes slips into outright groove. Compared to its predecessor, 2011’s “Bible Eyes,” as well as several EPs, this album by Egyptrixx (the recording alias of David Psutka) shows him drilling down to one coherent idea about dance music: The thing that moves the body need not be rhythm, but rather a primal response to sound. With Sinden and Judge Wise. (11:30 p.m., Friday, the Glasslands, 289 Kent Avenue, Williamsburg, Brooklyn; theglasslands.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grooving to Egyptrixx', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grooving To Egyptrixx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9892524-0c1f-511e-81a3-c14d2332fc49', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9892524-0c1f-511e-81a3-c14d2332fc49'}, {'abstract': 'The New Year is once again coming up roses for HGTV, that champion of the fantasy lifestyle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/arts/television/a-parade-wedding-and-a-dream-home.html', 'snippet': 'The New Year is once again coming up roses for HGTV, that champion of the fantasy lifestyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Year is once again coming up roses for HGTV, that champion of the fantasy lifestyle, which heralds 2014 from its traditional perch at the 125th\xa0Rose Parade. Starting at\xa011 a.m.,\xa0Vin Scully, the Hall of Fame sports broadcaster and grand marshal, will lead nearly 50 floats, centered on the theme “Dreams Come True” and adorned with more botanical elements — black lichen, Spanish mosses, safflower blossoms, cordon puffs, coconut flakes and even chive and onion seed — than the average florist might go through in five years, down Colorado Avenue in Pasadena, Calif. The “Property Brothers,” Drew and Jonathan Scott and Nancy O’Dell will provide a play-by-play of the nuptials of Danny Leclair and Aubrey Loots on the AIDS Healthcare Foundation’s wedding-cake float with the tagline “Love Is the Best Protection.” And eight former Women Airforce Service Pilots from World War II expected to ride atop a float titled “Our Eyes Are on the Stars.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parade Wedding and a Dream Home', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Parade Wedding And a Dream Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:32:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75966602-d56f-5c05-8f2a-5b12818bdad1', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75966602-d56f-5c05-8f2a-5b12818bdad1'}, {'abstract': 'Before New Year’s revelers overtake Times Square, art lovers can have their own countdown to midnight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/arts/design/art-films-at-moma-and-times-square.html', 'snippet': 'Before New Year’s revelers overtake Times Square, art lovers can have their own countdown to midnight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before New Year’s revelers overtake Times Square, art lovers can have their own countdown to midnight. At 11:57 each night through Monday, an abbreviated version of Isaac Julien’s film “Playtime” is being shown on electronic billboards and kiosks as part of the “Midnight Moment” art program presented by the Times Square Alliance and the Times Square Advertising Coalition. The full-length version of “Playtime” explores the international art market from the perspectives of five characters with varying levels of access and privilege. One is an auctioneer in London, another a worker in Dubai.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Films at MoMA and Times Square', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Films at MoMA And Times Square', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf4690e0-0378-5171-b951-051230f9e359', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf4690e0-0378-5171-b951-051230f9e359'}, {'abstract': 'In this episode of Teton Gravity Research’s “Behind The Line,” professional skier Sage Cattabriga-Alosa has to tunnel through a school bus-sized mass of snow to access a ski run in Alaska.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/sports/video-pro-skier-hacks-into-death-defying-run.html', 'snippet': 'In this episode of Teton Gravity Research’s “Behind The Line,” professional skier Sage Cattabriga-Alosa has to tunnel through a school bus-sized mass of snow to access a ski run in Alaska.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Behind the Line is a video series produced by Teton Gravity Research that takes you into the minds of skiers. In each episode, the athletes will look back on a line, a jump or a session, and discuss the moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Pro Skier Hacks Into Challenging Run', 'kicker': 'Behind the Line', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teton Gravity Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T16:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c63556c3-5f91-51e3-b8d7-84eda204141a', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c63556c3-5f91-51e3-b8d7-84eda204141a'}, {'abstract': 'Francesca Gregorini discusses her new film, “The Truth About Emanuel.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/movies/francesca-gregorini-and-the-truth-about-emanuel.html', 'snippet': 'Francesca Gregorini discusses her new film, “The Truth About Emanuel.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The creepy thriller “The Truth About Emanuel” deals with “loss and heartbreak and madness and mortality,” the writer and director Francesca Gregorini said recently. “Every artist is haunted by specific themes, and those, for better or for worse, seem to be mine.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29SNAPSHOT/29SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1178, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29SNAPSHOT/29SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1178}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29SNAPSHOT/29SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 522, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29SNAPSHOT/29SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1476, 'width': 752, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29SNAPSHOT/29SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'le