s regarding optimizing search results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/business/media/google-penalizes-rap-genius-for-gaming-search-rank.html', 'snippet': 'The site rapgenius.com, which offers annotated song lyrics, acknowledged that it had violated Google’s rules regarding optimizing search results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google has apparently punished a provocative music-lyrics website after learning it had unscrupulously tried to improve its search rankings.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Penalizes Rap Genius for Gaming Search Rank', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google Punishes Site In Ranking Scheme', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaufman, Leslie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RapGenius.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T18:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75248806-30a8-554c-970c-dda058e7edbe', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75248806-30a8-554c-970c-dda058e7edbe'}, {'abstract': 'The criminal conviction of Msgr. William J. Lynn was overturned by a Pennsylvania appeals court after the court rejected the argument that a child welfare law applied to employers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/us/conviction-overturned-for-church-official-accused-of-covering-up-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'The criminal conviction of Msgr. William J. Lynn was overturned by a Pennsylvania appeals court after the court rejected the argument that a child welfare law applied to employers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Pennsylvania appeals court on Thursday overturned the criminal conviction of a Roman Catholic official who was accused of covering up sexual abuses by priests he supervised. The court rejected the legal basis for a prosecution that was viewed as a milestone in holding senior church officials accountable for keeping abuse reports secret in past decades and transferring predatory priests to unwary new parishes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/us/CHURCHweb/CHURCHweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/us/CHURCHweb/CHURCHweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/us/CHURCHweb/CHURCHweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/us/CHURCHweb/CHURCHweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/us/CHURCHweb/CHURCHweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/us/CHURCHweb/CHURCHweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/us/CHURCHweb/CHURCHweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Philadelphia Monsignor’s Conviction Overturned in Cover-Up of Sexual Abuse ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philadelphia Monsignor’s Conviction Overturned in Cover-Up of Sexual Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yaccino, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynn, William J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T18:44:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm and Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb9450d5-a420-5b16-a339-66a9d01d642f', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb9450d5-a420-5b16-a339-66a9d01d642f'}, {'abstract': 'HBO’s “Game of Thrones” tops a list of the most-pirated TV shows in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/game-of-thrones-is-a-hit-with-tv-pirates-too/', 'snippet': 'HBO’s “Game of Thrones” tops a list of the most-pirated TV shows in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a few fans of “Game of Thrones” are so eager for the murder, villainy, depravity and wedding banquets gone horribly wrong depicted on that series that they don’t mind engaging in a little piracy to see the show. The hit HBO fantasy series enjoyed the dubious distinction of placing first on a list of the year’s most pirated television shows, compiled by TorrentFreak.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Game of Thrones’ Is a Hit With TV Pirates, Too', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BitTorrent', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T18:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27e7bcd1-817f-58fb-a4a7-cb1453ad185a', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27e7bcd1-817f-58fb-a4a7-cb1453ad185a'}, {'abstract': 'This collection offers eight films, including prizewinners and other noteworthy entries, from the most recent edition of the Sundance Film Festival in Park City, Utah.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/movies/2013-sundance-film-festival-short-films-at-ifc-center.html', 'snippet': 'This collection offers eight films, including prizewinners and other noteworthy entries, from the most recent edition of the Sundance Film Festival in Park City, Utah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A diverse sampler, “2013 Sundance Film Festival Short Films” bundles together prizewinners and other notables from the most recent edition of the festival in Park City, Utah. As with many collections of shorts, there’s a slight danger of whiplash (to borrow the title of one selection) when each filmmaker introduces a look, sets a mood, sketches a story. Over the course of the eight-film selection, you might see a foulmouthed teacher berating a nervous drummer, photographs of working-class villagers by the sea in 1980s northern England, a dead man rising and pieces of furniture roaming the countryside in Ireland.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1076, 'width': 1834, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN/27SUNDANCE01_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name