tion party, who remains under pressure for his handling of an ethnic riot 11 years ago, won a victory on Thursday in one of the many disputes dogging him as he seeks to become India’s next prime minister, but faced a setback in another.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/world/asia/27india/27india-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 812, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/world/asia/27india/27india-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 812}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/world/asia/27india/27india-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/world/asia/27india/27india-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1513, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/world/asia/27india/27india-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/world/asia/27india/27india-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/world/asia/27india/27india-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Victory, and Setback, for Indian Opposition Leader', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Victory, and Setback, for Indian Opposition Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Hari', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T19:06:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris and Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ccee3a3-1ea5-51e1-90a6-43762d6414b0', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ccee3a3-1ea5-51e1-90a6-43762d6414b0'}, {'abstract': 'Addressing a difficult family reunion, a potential romantic interest, being ignored and an empty gift card.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/fashion/widening-the-family-circle.html', 'snippet': 'Addressing a difficult family reunion, a potential romantic interest, being ignored and an empty gift card.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We have been estranged from our son for a couple of years (thanks mostly to his difficult and dominant longtime girlfriend). Still, we followed your advice and wrote him a loving letter for Hanukkah, which he returned in kind. We’ve spoken on the phone a few times since then and even set a date for New Year’s brunch. Now he’s told us that he wants to bring the girlfriend to our reunion. Is there a nice way to let him know that we want to keep it just family for now? ',