ocations', 'value': 'Dyker Heights (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, C J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T19:18:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b67751ff-580d-534e-8424-037e5730dbae', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b67751ff-580d-534e-8424-037e5730dbae'}, {'abstract': 'Karyn Meek and Royce Love Russell, the stage and house managers, respectively, of “Natasha, Pierre and the Great Comet of 1812,” do much more than traditional ushers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/theater/in-natasha-pierre-house-managers-are-part-of-the-action.html', 'snippet': 'Karyn Meek and Royce Love Russell, the stage and house managers, respectively, of “Natasha, Pierre and the Great Comet of 1812,” do much more than traditional ushers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They may be friendly, or they may be brusque, but the ushers who point the way to your theater seat have only so much to do with your experience once the curtain goes up. In the new world of immersive theater, where lines between the audience and the performers are blurred, it’s a little more complicated. “Here Lies Love” at the Public Theater featured a squadron of helpers in neon pink jumpsuits, moving the standing audience around a dance floor as the show’s set whirled and reconfigured.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/arts/29GREATCOMET_SPAN/29GREATCOMET_S