_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97f67fbf-bc66-5165-bfe0-2ea6f0aaab70'}, {'abstract': 'Film Forum’s survey of Barbara Stanwyck’s movies concludes on New Year’s Eve. On Friday and Saturday, there’s her classic noir “Double Indemnity” (1944).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/movies/barbara-stanwyck-festival-at-film-forum.html', 'snippet': 'Film Forum’s survey of Barbara Stanwyck’s movies concludes on New Year’s Eve. On Friday and Saturday, there’s her classic noir “Double Indemnity” (1944).', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the main qualities we look for in a diva is a variety that somehow stays the same; we want from our great artists both adventure and safety. But Barbara Stanwyck pushed her range further than most. She was sometimes a femme fatale and sometimes a screwball comedian; she was a noble missionary’s wife in “The Bitter Tea of General Yen” (1933) and a scheming con artist in “The Lady Eve” (1941).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27WOOLFE/27WOOLFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27WOOLFE/27WOOLFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 483}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27WOOLFE/27WOOLFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27WOOLFE/27WOOLFE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1648, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27WOOLFE/27WOOLFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27WOOLFE/27WOOLFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27WOOLFE/27WOOLFE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lady Barbara', 'kicker': 'Last Chance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lady Barbara', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanwyck, Barbara', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Forum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T21:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e686f4f1-af77-5d4d-b373-f5682e32137d', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e686f4f1-af77-5d4d-b373-f5682e32137d'}, {'abstract': 'More than any other opera this year, “Falstaff” deserves a second viewing to savor the details.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/arts/music/falstaff-at-metropolitan-opera-a-bundle-of-energy.html', 'snippet': 'More than any other opera this year, “Falstaff” deserves a second viewing to savor the details.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two memorable new productions book-ended the year at the Metropolitan Opera: François Girard’s painfully human “Parsifal,” set in a post-apocalyptic no-man’s land, and Robert Carsen’s zippy “Falstaff,” set in a 1950s England of Technicolor opulence. For a director approaching “Parsifal,” the challenge is to come up with ideas to populate the dramaturgical moonscape that are Wagner’s interminable monologues in this five-hour-plus opera. Verdi’s comedy “Falstaff,” by contrast, is teeming with action, and the task of the director — no less difficult — is one of traffic control.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Ruling Falstaff’s Roost', 'kicker': 'Last Chance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Women Ruling Falstaff’s Roost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Falstaff (Opera)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T21:36:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7baea54-be8f-5240-b18c-ec07a14addd4', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7baea54-be8f-5240-b18c-ec07a14addd4'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said the suspect was struggling with an officer over a loaded gun when a second officer fired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/nyregion/police-fatally-shoot-an-armed-robbery-suspect-in-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said the suspect was struggling with an officer over a loaded gun when a second officer fired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A police officer shot and killed a suspect in an armed robbery in the Bronx early Thursday as the suspect struggled over his loaded gun with another officer, the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer Kills Armed Suspect in the Bronx', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officer Kills Armed Suspect in the Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Torres, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T21:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e69c7785-c727-5f6d-939d-28e222681f3d', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e69c7785-c727-5f6d-939d-28e222681f3d'}, {'abstract': 'The immersive theater show “Queen of the Night” is opening New Year’s Eve at the Paramount Hotel’s Diamond Horseshoe supper club, which is back in business for the first time since 1951.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/theater/queen-of-the-night-opens-at-the-new-diamond-horseshoe-club.html', 'snippet': 'The immersive theater show “Queen of the Night” is opening New Year’s Eve at the Paramount Hotel’s Diamond Horseshoe supper club, which is back in business for the first time since 1951.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN its heyday, Billy Rose’s Diamond Horseshoe was quite the thing — “the most zestful, gorgeous and lovable pleasure palace in town,” a critic for The New York Times wrote shortly after it opened in December 1938. Buried deep in the basement of what is now the Paramount Hotel on West 46th Street in Manhattan, the theater transported audiences back to New York in the Gay Nineties, the era of Diamond Jim Brady and Lillian Russell, in a revue stacked with old vaudeville troupers and glamorous showgirls. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27DIAMONDjp/27DIAMONDjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27DIAMONDjp/27DIAMONDjp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 767}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27DIAMONDjp/27DIAMONDjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27DIAMONDjp/27DIAMONDjp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1563, 'width': 1223, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27DIAMONDjp/27DIAMONDjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27DIAMONDjp/27DIAMONDjp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27DIAMONDjp/27DIAMONDjp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'