i recordings. This August we came up with our favorite recordings of Wagner, who also had a big bicentennial year. As with Wagner, Verdi has been as central to the history of recordings as he is to the history of music.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27VERDI/27VERDI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 921, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27VERDI/27VERDI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 921}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27VERDI/27VERDI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27VERDI/27VERDI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1992, 'width': 1298, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27VERDI/27VERDI-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27VERDI/27VERDI-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27VERDI/27VERDI-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That’s Vintage Verdi, That ’61 ‘Otello’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That’s Vintage Verdi, That ’61 ‘Otello’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verdi, Giuseppe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T22:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini, Zachary Woolfe, Vivien Schweitzer and Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9031204-e52b-54fd-8f27-849eea10c93e', 'word_count': 2627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9031204-e52b-54fd-8f27-849eea10c93e'}, {'abstract': '“See It Loud: Seven Post-War American Painters,” running through Jan. 26 at the National Academy Museum, features works from the collection of a former trustee, Henry Justin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/arts/design/see-it-loud-at-the-national-academy-museum.html', 'snippet': '“See It Loud: Seven Post-War American Painters,” running through Jan. 26 at the National Academy Museum, features works from the collection of a former trustee, Henry Justin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'However often it is bent, the rule still holds: People who govern public art museums must set aside self-interest in carrying out their institutional duties. Maintaining higher standards is especially urgent when a museum runs into trouble, as the National Academy did five years ago,  when it sold two Hudson River School paintings to cover budgetary shortfalls and briefly considered selling its Fifth Avenue building to resolve its debts. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27POSTWAR01/27POSTWAR01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27POSTWAR01/27POSTWAR01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 505}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27POSTWAR01/27POSTWAR01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27POSTWAR01/27POSTWAR01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1725, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27POSTWAR01/27POSTWAR01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27POSTWAR01/27POSTWAR01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27POSTWAR01/27POSTWAR01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Representational Work in Years When Abstract Was Hot', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Representational Work in Years When Abstract Was Hot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy Museum and School of Fine Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Justin, Henry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T22:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e78daac-d8d7-565b-926c-ad5061602242', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e78daac-d8d7-565b-926c-ad5061602242'}, {'abstract': '“Jewels by JAR” is devoted to the work of Joel Arthur Rosenthal, who creates pricey jewels for a handpicked clientele from his shop in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/arts/design/jewels-by-jar-joel-arthur-rosenthal-at-the-met-museum.html', 'snippet': '“Jewels by JAR” is devoted to the work of Joel Arthur Rosenthal, who creates pricey jewels for a handpicked clientele from his shop in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who visits museums has spent time looking at costly luxury goods and status symbols cherished by the upper echelons and ruling classes of bygone eras. The list of objects elevated to unprecedented heights of artistry includes Japanese lacquer boxes, Fabergé eggs, French porcelain, Roentgen furniture, bejeweled objects from the treasuries of this cathedral or that court. Almost without exception, they dazzle the eye with astounding craftsmanship, superb design and carefully orchestrated material extravagance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27JEWELRY_SPAN/27JEWELRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27JEWELRY_SPAN/27JEWELRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27JEWELRY_SPAN/27JEWELRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27JEWELRY_SPAN/27JEWELRY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27JEWELRY_SPAN/27JEWELRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27JEWELRY_SPAN/27JEWELRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/arts/27JEWELRY_SPAN/27JEWELRY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All That Glitters (and a Lot That Shines)', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All That Glitters (and a Lot That Shines)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Joel Arthur', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T22:08:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb55d456-97de-5f35-8509-87be50fb195b', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb55d456-97de-5f35-8509-87be50fb195b'}, {'abstract': 'Specialty theaters like the Picture House in Pelham, Jacob Burns Film Center in Pleasantville and the Alamo Drafthouse in Yonkers offer alternatives to the usual multiplex experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/nyregion/in-the-holiday-movie-crush-a-few-twists.html', 'snippet': 'Specialty theaters like the Picture House in Pelham, Jacob Burns Film Center in Pleasantville and the Alamo Drafthouse in Yonkers offer alternatives to the usual multiplex experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Fourth of July it’s fireworks. Thanksgiving Day it’s turkey. Christmas week, it’s movies, and lots of them. Schools release their students, studios release their awards contenders and the box office totals swell.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSWE1_SPAN/29ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSWE1_SPAN/29ARTSWE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit