', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/12/27/arts/music/27popcast.html', 'snippet': 'Jon Pareles, Jon Caramanica and Ben Ratliff discuss the dominant ideas and themes in pop in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jon Pareles, Jon Caramanica and Ben Ratliff discuss the dominant ideas and themes in pop in 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Year in Pop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T22:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/81ffc019-1ffe-567c-a7b1-9f560570068e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/81ffc019-1ffe-567c-a7b1-9f560570068e'}, {'abstract': 'The $1 trillion spending bill would give the once mighty congressional Appropriations Committees a chance to reassert control over the way federal dollars are spent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/us/politics/nearing-a-1-trillion-measure-and-budget-normalcy.html', 'snippet': 'The $1 trillion spending bill would give the once mighty congressional Appropriations Committees a chance to reassert control over the way federal dollars are spent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With the next budget deadline just weeks away, top lawmakers said this week that they had made significant progress negotiating a huge government-wide spending bill that gives the once mighty congressional Appropriations Committees an opportunity to reassert control over the flow of federal dollars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Cite Progress on Budget Near Deadline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawmakers Cite Progress on Budget Near Deadline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hulse, Carl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Harold Dallas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T22:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90b68ada-5a19-5359-a580-d2f986d336ca', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90b68ada-5a19-5359-a580-d2f986d336ca'}, {'abstract': 'A show at the Museum of Fine Arts, Boston, of work by female photographers from the Muslim world, challenges stereotypes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/arts/design/mideast-photography-at-museum-of-fine-arts-boston.html', 'snippet': 'A show at the Museum of Fine Arts, Boston, of work by female photographers from the Muslim world, challenges stereotypes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Middle Eastern women, supposedly powerless and oppressed behind walls and veils, are in fact a force in both society and the arts. They played a major role in the Arab Spring and continue to do so in the flourishing regional art scene — specifically in photography — which is alive and very well indeed. Some Middle Eastern photographers have taken their cameras to the barricades, physical ones and those less obvious, like the barriers erected by stereotypes, which they remain determined to defy. The Museum of Fine Arts, Boston, takes note in “She Who Tells a Story: Women Photographers From Iran and the Arab World,” an ambitious and revealing exhibition of work by 12 women, some internationally known. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamic World Through Women’s Eyes', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Islamic World Through Women’s Eyes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Fine Arts (Boston)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-26T22:22:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vicki Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vicki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/aed83659-0563-5e8e-90e9-859636ce71d1', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aed83659-0563-5e8e-90e9-859636ce71d1'}, {'abstract': 'The Museum of Fine Arts, Boston, presents an ambitious and revealing exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/12/27/arts/design/20131227-PHOTOGS.html', 'snippet': 'The Museum of Fine Arts, Boston, presents an ambitious and revealing exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of Fine Arts, Boston, presents an ambitious and revealing exhibition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None