: 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4b40c00-f4ac-5857-a064-b92a80296b31', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4b40c00-f4ac-5857-a064-b92a80296b31'}, {'abstract': 'Should we be more forthcoming about what we do to enhance our looks?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2013/12/26/when-beauty-is-not-exactly-truth/', 'snippet': 'Should we be more forthcoming about what we do to enhance our looks?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Beauty Is Not (Exactly) Truth', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T02:07:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46d1fea9-41e3-56fc-ba12-14a4b3266b65', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46d1fea9-41e3-56fc-ba12-14a4b3266b65'}, {'abstract': 'About 2,000 officers are assigned to the city’s public housing projects, and the housing authority pays for it. That arrangement may end, and there is concern about a possible effect on safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/nyregion/policing-the-projects-of-new-york-city-at-a-hefty-price.html', 'snippet': 'About 2,000 officers are assigned to the city’s public housing projects, and the housing authority pays for it. That arrangement may end, and there is concern about a possible effect on safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After riding the elevator to the top floor of a building in the Louis H. Pink Houses in Brooklyn and scanning the rooftop, the police officers made their way back down, floor by floor, searching the stairwells and hallways. On the sixth floor, slumped against the stairs, was a man who said he was waiting for his ex-girlfriend. The officers ran a warrant check on the 49-year-old man and arrested him after learning he was wanted for a parole violation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/housing-police-1/housing-police-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/housing-police-1/housing-police-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/housing-police-1/housing-police-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/housing-police-1/housing-police-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/housing-police-1/housing-police-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/housing-police-1/housing-police-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/housing-police-1/housing-police-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Policing the Projects of New York City, at a Hefty Price', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Policing the Projects, at a Hefty Price', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navarro, Mireya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing Authority (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T02:11:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro and Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a70bad4-729b-57b3-9680-e465a6ec9ce5', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a70bad4-729b-57b3-9680-e465a6ec9ce5'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Abe’s visit to a controversial war shrine is detrimental to relations with China and South Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/opinion/risky-nationalism-in-japan.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Abe’s visit to a controversial war shrine is detrimental to relations with China and South Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, one year after coming to power, Prime Minister Shinzo Abe visited Yasukuni, the controversial Shinto shrine that honors Japan’s war dead, including war criminals from World War II. China and South Korea swiftly criticized the move, as did the United States. Mr. Abe’s visit will worsen Japan’s already tense relations with China and South Korea, which see the shrine as a symbol of imperial Japan’s wars of aggression and colonialism. The United States Embassy said America was “disappointed that Japan’s leadership has taken an action that will exacerbate tensions with Japan’s neighbors.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Risky Nationalism in Japan', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Risky Nationalism in Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T02:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae51fbe1-11f9-5dfc-a142-484192a61663', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae51fbe1-11f9-5dfc-a142-484192a61663'}, {'abstract': 'A recent vote by the American Studies Association to boycott Israeli academic institutions has led some leaders to issue condemnations that emphasize the importance of academic freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/education/academic-leaders-denounce-israel-boycott.html', 'snippet': 'A recent vote by the American Studies Association to boycott Israeli academic institutions has led some leaders to issue condemnations that emphasize the importance of academic freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Studies Association’s endorsement this month of a boycott of Israeli academic institutions continues to stir passions, with four colleges and universities announcing their withdrawal from the association, a second leading higher-education association denouncing the boycott and a rising tide of college presidents speaking out against it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Prominent Scholars, Citing Importance of Academic Freedom, Denounce Israeli Boycott', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prominent Scholars, Citing Importance of Academic Freedom, Denounce Israeli Boycott', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Studies Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACADEMIC FREEDOM', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T02:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cffdc94-1d02-5720-91ec-0d087d7c5782', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cffdc94-1d02-5720-91ec-0d087d7c5782'},