a’s Affordable Care Act have experienced so many problems and delays that they are threatening to withhold millions of dollars in payments to the company and even seek refunds.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 States May Seek Refunds From Health Site Creator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 States May Seek Refunds From Health Site Creator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyman, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CGI Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T02:35:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Lyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b2a1505-8b0b-5de6-9c62-0422611bda2e', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b2a1505-8b0b-5de6-9c62-0422611bda2e'}, {'abstract': 'Critics of state tax incentives to ESPN, the multibillion-dollar sports media powerhouse, say the money would be better spent on smaller companies that are in greater need.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/sports/for-espn-millions-to-remain-in-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Critics of state tax incentives to ESPN, the multibillion-dollar sports media powerhouse, say the money would be better spent on smaller companies that are in greater need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRISTOL, Conn. — The governor of Connecticut arrived at ESPN’s expansive campus here to celebrate the groundbreaking of the sports media giant’s 19th building, a digital center that would be the new home of “SportsCenter.” It was August 2011, and this was the third visit in a year by Gov. Dannel P. Malloy, whose first was about three weeks before his election. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/Y-JP-ESPN/Y-JP-ESPN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/Y-JP-ESPN/Y-JP-ESPN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/Y-JP-ESPN/Y-JP-ESPN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/Y-JP-ESPN/Y-JP-ESPN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/Y-JP-ESPN/Y-JP-ESPN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/Y-JP-ESPN/Y-JP-ESPN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/Y-JP-ESPN/Y-JP-ESPN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For ESPN, Millions to Remain in Connecticut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For ESPN, Millions to Remain in Connecticut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malloy, Dannel P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T02:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Eder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a46b2bf9-0712-5d56-ac39-5a2f493b3e5b', 'word_count': 1998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a46b2bf9-0712-5d56-ac39-5a2f493b3e5b'}, {'abstract': 'Dive into a challenging and fun Friday by Ian Livengood and the J.A.S.A. Crossword Class.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/26/homicidal-psycho-jungle-cat/', 'snippet': 'Dive into a challenging and fun Friday by Ian Livengood and the J.A.S.A. Crossword Class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — If you’re just joining us, the J.A.S.A. Crossword Class is a wonderful resource in New York City for those who want to learn how to construct a puzzle. Caleb Madison used to teach it, and when he went off to college (no, that’s not a typo), Ian Livengood took over the teaching duties. There’s a link at the bottom of this post if you’d like to learn more about the class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/crosswords/27skytower/27skytower-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 269, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/crosswords/27skytower/27skytower-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 269, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/crosswords/27skytower/27skytower-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/crosswords/27skytower/27skytower-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/crosswords/27skytower/27skytower-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Homicidal Psycho Jungle Cat', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T03:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba3927da-51b4-524d-844c-c8f3cfee069a', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba3927da-51b4-524d-844c-c8f3cfee069a'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, December 27, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-friday-december-27-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Friday, December 27, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“When you think about the U.S., you can’t just think about New York and L.A. Don’t get me wrong, L.A. is fabulous. New York is great. But if you want to connect with American life, it’s Toledo.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Friday, December 27, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T03:02:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/15a22ade-e99e-53e7-a6b9-488ec16c01da', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15a22ade-e99e-53e7-a6b9-488ec16c01da'}, {'abstract': 'With plans to attend a prestigious school in New York, José del Carmen Arias’s life ground to a halt when his green card was confiscated after an extended stay in the Dominican Republic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/nyregion/his-green-card-returned-doors-re-open.html', 'snippet': 'With plans to attend a prestigious school in New York, José del Carmen Arias’s life ground to a halt when his green card was confiscated after an extended stay in the Dominican Republic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On July 22, 2011, José Arias and José del Carmen Arias, then 19, were just another father and son in a long security line at the San Juan Airport in Puerto Rico. Both had green cards showing they were lawful residents of the United States. They had made this journey — from the Dominican Republic, where both were born, back to Puerto Rico, where they lived — many times before. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/neediest/neediest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/neediest/neediest-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/neediest/neediest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/neediest/neediest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/nyregion/neediest/neediest-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Green Card Returned, Doors Reopen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'His Green Card Returned, Doors Re-Open', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Charities Archdiocese of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T03:06:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0620541d-9cec-59c2-b4f5-74a41a46f632', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0620541d-9cec-59c2-b4f5-74a41a46f632'}, {'abstract': 'The results of games played the day after Christmas left four teams — Arsenal, City, Chelsea and Liverpool — separated by only 3 points at the top of the standings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/sports/soccer/a-boxing-day-bounty-for-premier-league-fans.html', 'snippet': 'The results of games played the day after Christmas left four teams — Arsenal, City, Chelsea and Liverpool — separated by only 3 points at the top of the standings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Only in England is the day after Christmas such an inclusive day of sports. It might be cold out there, but racehorses pull in bumper crowds. Followers of cricket sit through the night, knowing that England faces a humiliating whitewash in Australia. And anywhere there is a soccer club, most seats in the house are sold because it is a time-honored tradition in Britain to fill Boxing Day with sports, like filling children’s stockings with gifts.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/soccer/27onsoccer-1/27onsoccer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/soccer/27onsoccer-1/27onsoccer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/sports/soccer/27onsoccer-1/27onsoccer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'su