 cabernet and malbec.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Argentina, where the malbec grape is king, winemakers have put an intriguing spin on what is usually known as a Bordeaux blend. Instead of the typical mix of cabernet sauvignon, cabernet franc and merlot, they are relying primarily on cabernet sauvignon and malbec.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/dining/01ARGENTINA1/01ARGENTINA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/01/01/dining/01ARGENTINA1/01ARGENTINA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/dining/01ARGENTINA1/01ARGENTINA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/dining/01ARGENTINA1/01ARGENTINA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/dining/01ARGENTINA1/01ARGENTINA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/01/dining/01ARGENTINA1/01ARGENTINA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/01/dining/01ARGENTINA1/01ARGENTINA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina Tries to Give Malbec More Status', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina Tries to Give Malbec More Status', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mendoza (Argentina)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T16:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1bf1474-8327-59c3-b711-72c587ac4756', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1bf1474-8327-59c3-b711-72c587ac4756'}, {'abstract': 'Authors of some of the Book Review’s Best Books of 2013 share their favorite reading experience from the year just ended.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/05/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Authors of some of the Book Review’s Best Books of 2013 share their favorite reading experience from the year just ended.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Best of the Best: The Book Review has had its say; a few weeks ago, we named our 10 Best Books of 2013. But in the interests of inclusiveness — and, O.K., advance planning before the holidays — I wondered what our 10 best authors would pick as their favorites. So I asked them. The rules were simple: Tell us the best book you read this year (whether it was published in 2013 or not) and, briefly, describe it. Not everybody responded — I wasn’t the only one beleaguered by sugarplums — but enough did to devote the column this week, and next, to their replies: the best books as chosen by the authors of the best books, a sort of chain letter of terrific reading ideas. Here they are.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05list-img/05list-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 264, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05list-img/05list-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 264, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05list-img/05list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05list-img/05list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/01/05/books/review/05list-img/05list-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T16:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03d38047-87a3-5df7-a3c9-9d8fe416641d', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03d38047-87a3-5df7-a3c9-9d8fe416641d'}, {'abstract': 'There was no immediate claim of responsibility, but local officials say they suspect the Shabab, an Islamist militant group based in Somalia with links to Al Qaeda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/world/africa/mogadishu-restaurant-attack.html', 'snippet': 'There was no immediate claim of responsibility, but local officials say they suspect the Shabab, an Islamist militant group based in Somalia with links to Al Qaeda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — At least 10 people were killed in Mogadishu, the Somali capital, on Friday when a remote-controlled bomb exploded in a restaurant in the northwestern part of the city, government officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deadly Bomb Attack Rocks a Restaurant in Somalia’s Capital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deadly Bomb Attack Rocks a Restaurant in Somalia’s Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mogadishu (Somalia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T16:08:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86a82568-5b7f-52c9-a4f7-d6e89b8413dd', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86a82568-5b7f-52c9-a4f7-d6e89b8413dd'}, {'abstract': '“The Wolf of Wall Street” was the top-grossing new movie on Christmas Day, taking in about $9.2 million.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/wolf-leads-the-pack-of-newcomers-at-christmas-box-office/', 'snippet': '“The Wolf of Wall Street” was the top-grossing new movie on Christmas Day, taking in about $9.2 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Box-office analysts are typically able to predict with eerie precision whether a movie will be a hit or a miss just by examining opening-day ticket sales. There is one exception: Christmastime. Because studios release so many pictures in such short order and so many moviegoers are on vacation, initial grosses can be deceptive; films that look soft can find their footing or fall off sharply. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Wolf’ Leads the Pack of Newcomers at Christmas Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Niro, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stallone, Sylvester', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiller, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramount Pictures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twentieth Century Fox', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers Pictures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T16:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 