akingviews, is not to make the same mistakes as Japan did in the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China’s banks are racking up foreign assets, driven by trade flows, and the country’s corporate diaspora. Even at the current slow pace, what today looks like “following the client” could soon become “following everyone’s clients.” (See chart.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Banks Are on the Rise', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Agricultural Bank of China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Construction Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Industrial and Commercial Bank of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Chartered Bank PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T16:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Foley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Foley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db2cd8b3-860a-57f3-ba60-3c549ca1fe2b', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db2cd8b3-860a-57f3-ba60-3c549ca1fe2b'}, {'abstract': 'In a new mobile game from the Raddison hotels and Melty Games, players manage a virtual hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/you-too-can-play-the-hotel-game/', 'snippet': 'In a new mobile game from the Raddison hotels and Melty Games, players manage a virtual hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget matching colorful candy pieces or farming zombi