 by their opposition to President Vladimir K. Putin of Russia, and said they were starting a human rights organization.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/freed-pussy-riot-activists-stand-firm-and-shift-focus/', 'snippet': 'The activists, who held a news conference in Moscow, stood by their opposition to President Vladimir K. Putin of Russia, and said they were starting a human rights organization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four days after their release from a Russian prison, two members of the punk band Pussy Riot gave their first news conference to emphasize that they were starting a human rights organization, while sticking by the message that put them in jail: ending the presidency of Vladimir V. Putin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freed Pussy Riot Activists Stand Firm and Shift Focus', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alyokhina, Maria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovsky, Mikhail B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samutsevich, Yekaterina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolokonnikova, Nadezhda', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T17:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad033510-578e-5739-b2dc-3e3c36001a51', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad033510-578e-5739-b2dc-3e3c36001a51'}, {'abstract': 'It may not be easy to reach the seaside village of Xcalak, but when seasonal traditions loom, that could be a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/travel/dodging-a-holiday-in-a-remote-mexican-town.html', 'snippet': 'It may not be easy to reach the seaside village of Xcalak, but when seasonal traditions loom, that could be a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The night before Thanksgiving, while most of my acquaintances were setting tables or stuffing turkeys, I was in a lonesome town in Mexico, watching a salamander eat mosquitoes on a greasy kitchen wall. It was a hungry thing and went about devouring its prey with whip-quick lashes of an energetic tongue. Though I had chosen to avoid the feast day in the north, I didn’t mind the little lizard’s gluttony. Its meal, after all, was untroubled by the usual distractions: by football on TV or, moreover, the familiar family dramas. Despite — or perhaps because of — its enforced veneer of bliss, the month between the Macy’s parade and the Times Square ball drop can often inspire an unseasonable longing to escape.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/travel/29-personal-span/29-personal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/travel/29-personal-span/29-personal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image