, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/23/multimedia/driven-kia-soul/driven-kia-soul-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/23/multimedia/driven-kia-soul/driven-kia-soul-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: 2014 Kia Soul', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kia Motors Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T17:48:00+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/0029e40d-cf9d-5246-8a5c-4552d55f6b7b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/0029e40d-cf9d-5246-8a5c-4552d55f6b7b'}, {'abstract': 'The Syrian security forces struck near the town of Maaloula, north of Damascus, Syrian rebels and government television said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/world/middleeast/syrian-security-forces-kill-dozens-of-rebels-in-ambush.html', 'snippet': 'The Syrian security forces struck near the town of Maaloula, north of Damascus, Syrian rebels and government television said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syrian security forces ambushed and killed dozens of insurgents on Friday near the ancient Christian town of Maaloula, north of Damascus, during fighting close to the Lebanese border, Syrian rebels and government television said. Syrian state television said that government forces killed more than 60 fighters from the Nusra Front, an insurgent group with links to Al Qaeda. A Syrian rebel commander in the area, Abou al-Majd, said the attack killed more than 20 fighters, including Syrian members of Nusra and other local rebels. The Syrian Observatory for Human Rights, an organization based in Britain that tracks the conflict through a network of contacts in Syria, reported that dozens of fighters had been killed, and that 20 had been wounded. A government offensive has been taking place in the mountainous Qalamoun region for several weeks, driving a new wave of refugees into Lebanon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Security Forces Kill Dozens of Rebels in Ambush', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Nusra Front', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T17:48:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/47cad314-1ef3-53ca-9bda-2cb392e8b21f', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47cad314-1ef3-53ca-9bda-2cb392e8b21f'}, {'abstract': 'A 10-room full-floor apartment in a Candela-designed building, with five terraces and views galore, was listed for the first time since 1943.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/big-ticket-a-park-avenue-gem-for-18-million/', 'snippet': 'A 10-room full-floor apartment in a Candela-designed building, with five terraces and views galore, was listed for the first time since 1943.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A full-floor apartment at the Rosario Candela-designed 778 Park Avenue at East 73rd Street, held by the estate of the New York City philanthropist Celeste Bartos, sold for $18 million and was the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records. Listed for the first time since 1943, the 10-room full-floor unit, No. FL17, had a $22.5 million asking price and has $18,658.32 in monthly carrying costs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/realestate/29TICKET/29-Ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/realestate/29TICKET/29-Ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 811}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/realestate/29TICKET/29-Ticket-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/realestate/29TICKET/29-Ticket-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1516, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/realestate/29TICKET/29TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/29/realestate/29TICKET/29TICKET-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/realestate/29TICKET/29TICKET-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | A Park Avenue Gem for $18 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T17:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc65f9ab-70b3-51ce-a555-943db2572a60', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc65f9ab-70b3-51ce-a555-943db2572a60'}, {'abstract': 'Maserati will recall 63 vehicles for electrical problems, and an N.H.T.S.A. investigation of more than 250,000 Mercedes-Benz cars has been upgraded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/automobiles/maserati-recalls-cars-mercedes-benz-investigation-is-upgraded.html', 'snippet': 'Maserati will recall 63 vehicles for electrical problems, and an N.H.T.S.A. investigation of more than 250,000 Mercedes-Benz cars has been upgraded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maserati will recall 63 of its 2014 Quattroporte GTS V8 models because of a possible loss of electrical power and a potential fire risk, according to a report posted on the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration website.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/automobiles/