the city on a Friday night. What is “ready,” anyway?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m haunted by a 3-year-old French girl in a buttercup-yellow dress. She’s a vague remnant from an article I read sometime in the last two to three years about the supreme competence of French children. While her mother chatted with a reporter in the living room, the girl very ably made cupcakes in the kitchen. In the years since I read the article, she periodically appears in my life as a rebuke against too much caution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Children Need To Take Risks, and Parents Need to Let Them', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hanukkah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T19:11:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Messina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Messina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d2328fb-0f97-5aae-9363-8ce1aa239f01', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d2328fb-0f97-5aae-9363-8ce1aa239f01'}, {'abstract': 'The People’s Bank of China has allowed extremely sharp movements in interbank lending rates, discouraging banks from relying too heavily on short-term borrowing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/12/28/business/international/tinkering-by-beijing.html', 'snippet': 'The People’s Bank of China has allowed extremely sharp movements in interbank lending rates, discouraging banks from relying too heavily on short-term borrowing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The People’s Bank of China has all