 '_id': 'nyt://article/361148b3-5a02-55b5-8906-9561f9d76b5a', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/361148b3-5a02-55b5-8906-9561f9d76b5a'}, {'abstract': 'Seagrass Grill is trying to use only fruits and vegetables, dairy products, meats and poultry that are locally produced and, whenever possible, organic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/nyregion/a-review-of-seagrass-grill-restaurant-in-branford.html', 'snippet': 'Seagrass Grill is trying to use only fruits and vegetables, dairy products, meats and poultry that are locally produced and, whenever possible, organic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although chefs at farm-to-table restaurants in Connecticut build their menus around locally sourced ingredients, few match the commitment of Kim Dziubinski, the owner of Seagrass Grill in the Indian Neck neighborhood of Branford. She is making her way through its first winter — it opened in April — with the goal of using only fruits, vegetables, dairy products, meats and poultry that are locally produced and, whenever possible, organic. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29SUBDINECT1/29SUBDINECT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29SUBDINECT1/29SUBDINECT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29SUBDINECT1/29SUBDINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29SUBDINECT1/29SUBDINECT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1262, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': '