ip chronicles the wait for assistance from a Chinese icebreaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Chinese vessel is battling severe weather and ice jams as it tries to make its way toward a research ship wedged in Antarctic ice, and the ordeal has been documented in social media postings by a professor on the ship, Chris Turney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Twitter, Documenting an Antarctic Journey and a Countdown to a Rescue', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Icebreakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T20:10:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea52ce8d-a2f2-5a94-8dcc-73919adc4ae8', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea52ce8d-a2f2-5a94-8dcc-73919adc4ae8'}, {'abstract': 'Olivia Laing discusses her new book, “The Trip to Echo Spring.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/27/book-review-podcast-writers-and-the-bottle/', 'snippet': 'Olivia Laing discusses her new book, “The Trip to Echo Spring.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In The New York Times Book Review, Lawrence Osborne reviews Olivia Laing’s “The Trip to Echo Spring,” which chronicles the alcoholism of six American writers: John Cheever, Tennessee Williams, John Berryman, Ernest Hemingway, F. Scott Fitzgerald and Raymond Ca