et': 'Mark Lewisohn discusses the first installment of his planned three-volume biography of The Beatles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Lewisohn never intended to become a Beatles biographer. His interest was mainly in pure research, and his first books were compilations of facts: an annotated listing of all the Beatles’ concerts (“The Beatles Live,” 1986); a descriptive catalog of the music, released and unreleased, in EMI archives (“The Beatles Recording Sessions: The Official Abbey Road Studio Sessions Notes, 1962-1970,” 1988); and a record of the group’s radio and television appearances (“The Complete Beatles Chronicle,” 1992). Around the time his recording sessions book was published, he described the market for Beatles biographies as oversaturated. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/books/28beatles/28beatles-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 594, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/books/28beatles/28beatles-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 594, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/books/28beatles/28beatles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/28/books/28beatles/28beatles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/books/28beatles/28beatles-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tune In, and Turn On the Reading Light', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lifetime’s Work: Writing the Beatles’ Biography ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewisohn, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T20:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ffbec14-9a9d-53fd-9cd6-3b193cd61230', 'word_count': 1732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ffbec14-9a9d-53fd-9cd6-3b193cd61230'}, {'abstract': 'Gastro pubs popping up across Westchester have brought hundreds of craft beers to the attention of diners, and some chefs, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/nyregion/ales-not-just-for-drinking.html', 'snippet': 'Gastro pubs popping up across Westchester have brought hundreds of craft beers to the attention of diners, and some chefs, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gastro pubs have been popping up across Westchester for several years, bringing hundreds of craft beers to diners’ attention, from light lagers to imperial stouts. Along with interesting food, these gastro pubs will offer 10, sometimes 20 different drafts at a time and dozens of bottled choices, including those from Captain Lawrence, the eight-year-old Elmsford brewery that makes about 15 different brews, and Yonkers Brewing Co., founded in 2010. Peekskill Brewery, an ambitious restaurant in that Hudson River town, even makes its own beer.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The