gine that it could last a decade. But the biannual journal Esopus defied the odds last month when it published its 20th issue, “Special Collections,” which features work by Matthew Weiner, the creator of “Mad Men.” Tod Lippy, the magazine’s affable founder and editor, is a one-man masthead, conceiving and executing every issue with assistance only from interns who get paid in lifetime subscriptions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/t-magazine/27esopus-curkin1/27esopus-curkin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/27/t-magazine/27esopus-curkin1/27esopus-curkin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/t-magazine/27esopus-curkin1/27esopus-curkin1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/t-magazine/27esopus-curkin1/27esopus-curkin1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1210, 'width': 990, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/t-magazine/27esopus-curkin1/27esopus-curkin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/27/t-magazine/27esopus-curkin1/27esopus-curkin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/27/t-magazine/27esopus-curkin1/27esopus-curkin1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Independent Journal Esopus, Still Going Strong After a Decade of Publishing', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldessari, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruscha, Edward', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T21:16:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Curkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Curkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60604faf-389a-5917-a2ad-f9ad65bc8ec6', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60604faf-389a-5917-a2ad-f9ad65bc8ec6'}, {'abstract': '“Francesco Vanni: Art in Late Renaissance Siena” at Yale University Art Gallery, offers a look at European art during an era of revival and reformation of the Catholic church in the 1500s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/nyregion/a-review-of-francesco-vanni-art-in-late-renaissance-siena-at-yale-university-art-gallery.html', 'snippet': '“Francesco Vanni: Art in Late Renaissance Siena” at Yale University Art Gallery, offers a look at European art during an era of revival and reformation of the Catholic church in the 1500s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can generally depend on Italian Renaissance art for tasteful, traditional Christmas imagery, and “Francesco Vanni: Art in Late Renaissance Siena” at Yale University Art Gallery delivers plenty of Madonnas, angels and adorable infants. But it also offers a view of European art at a moment of upheaval and of an artist working in the centers of religious power and responding to these changes.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSCT1/29ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSCT1/29ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 616}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSCT1/29ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 999, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSCT1/29ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1997, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSCT1/29ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSCT1/29ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ARTSCT1/29ARTSCT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spiritual and Prolific, in an Era of Upheaval', 'kicker': 'Arts Review | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spiritual and Prolific, in an Era of Upheaval', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University Art Gallery', 'rank': 2, 'maj