Searching for Sugar Man,” was first seen at the Sundance Film Festival. Ten of the 15 documentaries on the 2014 Oscar shortlist made their debut in the Sundance snow.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SUNDANCE1/28SUNDANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SUNDANCE1/28SUNDANCE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SUNDANCE1/28SUNDANCE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SUNDANCE1/28SUNDANCE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SUNDANCE1/28SUNDANCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SUNDANCE1/28SUNDANCE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SUNDANCE1/28SUNDANCE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Documentaries: Where Sundance Goes, Oscars Follow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Documentaries: Where Sundance Goes, Oscars Follow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T23:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8195a7a6-48a4-584c-844d-82d037d4b508', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8195a7a6-48a4-584c-844d-82d037d4b508'}, {'abstract': 'A Native American hide shirt up for auction in Boston is at the center of a legal dispute that leads back to complicated Indian commerce laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/arts/design/in-a-shirt-indian-family-sees-its-history.html', 'snippet': 'A Native American hide shirt up for auction in Boston is at the center of a legal dispute that leads back to complicated Indian commerce laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, lost to drugs and alcohol, Karen Little Thunder moved back to the Rosebud Indian Reservation in South Dakota, where, she said, she saved her own life by reconnecting to her Lakota heritage, particularly the legacy of her great-great grandfather. He was Little Thunder, a Lakota leader and a contemporary of Crazy Horse, whose life spanned several decades central to the history of the tribe — from the battles it fought across the Great Plains to its resettlement on reservations.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/arts/28SHIRT/28S