, psychologists or clinical social workers than it did for medical services. And Medicare imposed strict lifetime limits on stays in psychiatric hospitals, although no such limits applied to medical care received in inpatient facilities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare to Cover More Mental Health Costs', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-27T23:46:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e178470a-d28b-5724-bc6c-7f4277dbc810', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e178470a-d28b-5724-bc6c-7f4277dbc810'}, {'abstract': 'Books about the impeachment of Gov. William Sulzer; the founding editor of the Jewish Daily Forward; decomposing advertising signs in the city; and Dorothy Parker’s cocktail recipes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/nyregion/urban-melodrama.html', 'snippet': 'Books about the impeachment of Gov. William Sulzer; the founding editor of the Jewish Daily Forward; decomposing advertising signs in the city; and Dorothy Parker’s cocktail recipes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The saga of Gov. William Sulzer’s impeachment a century ago cannot be told often enough, both as an object lesson and as urban melodrama. Jack O’Donnell’s “Bitten by the Tiger” (Chapel Hill Press) is a welcome addition to the growing genre.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 