obert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30d6891b-3dc5-5c65-94c7-12d10767ee65', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30d6891b-3dc5-5c65-94c7-12d10767ee65'}, {'abstract': 'On his day off, the pastry chef François Payard exercises, checks up on some of his shops and spends time with his wife and friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/nyregion/he-makes-madames-toast.html', 'snippet': 'On his day off, the pastry chef François Payard exercises, checks up on some of his shops and spends time with his wife and friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pastry chef François Payard, 47, honed his craft first in France and later at Le Bernardin and Daniel; with the entrepreneur Marlon Abela he now has a dozen patisseries and bakeries in New York, Las Vegas, Japan and South Korea. On Sundays he tries to dial it back, so he can unwind with his wife, Fernanda Capobianco, 32, owner of the bakery Vegan Divas; prepare and share good food with friends in the couple’s Turtle Bay apartment; and take his mind off business for a day.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE4_SPAN/29ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE4_SPAN/29ROUTINE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE4_SPAN/29ROUTINE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty