', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93c3f8c4-d694-5b64-acb6-989feea4a0e4'}, {'abstract': 'Icebreakers sent to free a stranded Russian research ship, the Akademik Shokalskiy, off Antarctica were stopped by heavy ice within sight of the ship, officials said early Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/world/first-attempts-fail-to-free-ship-stranded-by-heavy-ice.html', 'snippet': 'Icebreakers sent to free a stranded Russian research ship, the Akademik Shokalskiy, off Antarctica were stopped by heavy ice within sight of the ship, officials said early Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Icebreakers sent to free a stranded Russian research ship, the Akademik Shokalskiy, off Antarctica were stopped by heavy ice within sight of the ship, officials said early Saturday. A Chinese icebreaker in the area, the Xue Long, or Snow Dragon, was asked to divert toward the Shokalskiy, which is carrying members of the Australasian Antarctic Expedition and became stuck in the ice on Tuesday about 1,700 miles south of Tasmania. A spokeswoman for the Australian Maritime Safety Authority said the Xue Long was about seven miles from the Shokalskiy when the ice became too thick to cut through. A French icebreaker also could not clear a path to the ship, said an expedition spokesman. The ships will await the arrival of an Australian icebreaker, which has a greater icebreaking capacity, he said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Attempts Fail to Free Ship Stranded by Heavy Ice', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Antarctica', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Attempts Fail to Free Ship Stranded by Heavy Ice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Icebreakers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-28T01:17:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5a5e48a-f2f7-58c5-afc8-a2b6e204a403', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5a5e48a-f2f7-58c5-afc8-a2b6e204a403'}, {'abstract': 'A glimpse of fast-food workers, men and women, young and old, some of whom have shed their anonymity and joined a year-old effort to achieve an increased wage of $15 an hour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/nyregion/the-faces-behind-the-counter.html', 'snippet': 'A glimpse of fast-food workers, men and women, young and old, some of whom have shed their anonymity and joined a year-old effort to achieve an increased wage of $15 an hour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we eat at a McDonald’s or a Burger King, we rarely pay attention to the people behind the counter. Our eyes are often focused upward on the brightly lighted menus, or perhaps downward on our smartphones or watches. But according to employment statistics, more than 55,000 people work in fast-food restaurants in New York City, and the number is rapidly increasing. Many of them earn the minimum wage: $7.25 an hour, increasing on Jan. 1 to $8. Forty percent are 25 or older. More than a quarter are parents raising children.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Faces Behind the Counter', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Faces Behind the Counter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feuer, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-28T01:17:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f43aa2e2-a266-5691-90e8-c1b09c01141f', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f43aa2e2-a266-5691-90e8-c1b09c01141f'}, {'abstract': 'A man with a history of drug abuse and mental disorders lost his shared, illegally partitioned apartment during Hurricane Sandy, as well as his confidante and companion, a pet parrot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/nyregion/in-decline-even-before-hurricane-sandy-devastated-it-a-life-now-shows-signs-of-hope.html', 'snippet': 'A man with a history of drug abuse and mental disorders lost his shared, illegally partitioned apartment during Hurricane Sandy, as well as his confidante and companion, a pet parrot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kenneth Silver had little to lose by 2012. His way of life was already severely diminished, and when Hurricane Sandy swept through Coney Island, its waves washed away what little he had left.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/28/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'ar