spair among prisoners who have been in detention for a decade with no hope of getting out. The protest, which at its height involved 106 of the 166 prisoners there this summer, served to put the Guantánamo issue back on the radar in Washington. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despair at Guantánamo', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despair at Guantánamo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-28T02:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab84d16b-d6ab-5199-8920-6ff97478af55', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab84d16b-d6ab-5199-8920-6ff97478af55'}, {'abstract': 'The government must ensure higher pay and an end to the abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/opinion/singapores-angry-migrant-workers.html', 'snippet': 'The government must ensure higher pay and an end to the abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frustration among Singapore’s unappreciated and underpaid migrant workers has been building in recent years as their numbers have grown faster than the country can accommodate them. Tensions boiled over earlier this month, after a 33-year-old Indian migrant worker was killed by a bus in the Little India neighborhood. A crowd of fellow workers from South Asia gathered at the scene. Their anger quickly escalated, with some 400 people pelting stones, attacking emergency responders and setting fire to vehicles. It was the worst riot to hit Singapore, one of the world’s most orderly countries, since 1969. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singapore’s Angry Migrant Workers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Singapore’s Angry Migrant Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Singapore', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant Labor (Agriculture)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-28T02:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad1181ae-480f-57b5-85a5-e748b1de9506', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad1181ae-480f-57b5-85a5-e748b1de9506'}, {'abstract': 'Congressional action is urgently needed after a federal court upholds the N.S.A. phone dragnet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/28/opinion/this-week-mass-surveillance-wins.html', 'snippet': 'Congressional action is urgently needed after a federal court upholds the N.S.A. phone dragnet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Has the National Security Agency’s mass collection of Americans’ phone records actually helped to prevent terrorist attacks? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week, Mass Surveillance Wins',