ghazi and the roles they played.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABDUL SALAM BARGATHI A commander in a militia, the Preventive Security Brigade, and an old friend of Ahmed Abu Khattala. He says he told the Libyan guards at the mission to flee rather than try to hold off the attackers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Militia Leaders in Benghazi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militia Leaders and the Roles They Played', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khattala, Ahmed Abu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ansar al-Shariah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-28T20:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d7c085-b520-5004-82f8-b8d0a0d2187d', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d7c085-b520-5004-82f8-b8d0a0d2187d'}, {'abstract': 'Recent developments in Idaho have alarmed those who want to protect the gray wolf from its human predators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/opinion/sunday/wolf-haters.html', 'snippet': 'Recent developments in Idaho have alarmed those who want to protect the gray wolf from its human predators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government removed the gray wolf from the endangered list in the Northern Rocky Mountains in 2011,\xa0essentially leaving wolves’ fates in the hands of state fish-and-game departments, hunters and ranchers.\xa0The predictable happened: hunting resumed, and the wolf population fell. In states like Idaho, Montana and Wyoming, an age-old antipathy to wolves flourishes, unchecked.\xa0', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/sunday-review/29editorial/29editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/29/sunday-review/29editorial/29editorial-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/sunday-review/29editorial/29editorial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/sunday-review/29editorial/29editorial-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/sunday-review/29editorial/29editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/29/sunday-review/29editorial/29editorial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/29/sunday-review/29editorial/29editorial-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wolf Haters', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wolf Haters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downes, Lawrence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Idaho', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-28T20:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b79d0add-eb44-503c-b429-80fe8d5c1cb6', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b79d0add-eb44-503c-b429-80fe8d5c1cb6'}, {'abstract': 'The archetype of the politician who uses power to punish enemies and reward supporters is well known in politics. Here are some examples.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/opinion/sunday/the-elected-bullies.html', 'snippet': 'The archetype of the politician who uses power to punish enemies and reward supporters is well known in politics. Here are some examples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a certain personality type in politics that the public has come to know all too well. The politician, invariably male, rises to power with a gaudy indifference to manners and derision for all that came before. He is sarcastic and loves to lecture, sneers at special pleaders and whiners, and his caustic energy persuades fed-up voters that he is the one who can finally take a cattle prod to a fat and unresponsive government.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Elected Bullies', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': No