 Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb20e8cf-b441-5366-9017-2694e0e923c5', 'word_count': 1296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb20e8cf-b441-5366-9017-2694e0e923c5'}, {'abstract': 'An adoptive family’s support for the Organization to Support Albania’s Abandoned Babies goes far beyond financial, and is repaid in ways expected and less so.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/charities-that-inspire-kids-angels-cradle/', 'snippet': 'An adoptive family’s support for the Organization to Support Albania’s Abandoned Babies goes far beyond financial, and is repaid in ways expected and less so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this month, I asked readers to share stories of charities that had touched and inspired their families and sparked an urge to give in their children. As we head through what’s often a week of charitable giving for many and into 2014, we’ll post some of those stories here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charities That Inspire Kids: Angel’s Cradle', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abandonment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-29T13:08:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'rol