ank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T01:59:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/feeadae5-c42a-5dea-9bf5-be8a537684a5', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feeadae5-c42a-5dea-9bf5-be8a537684a5'}, {'abstract': 'Does a fiction writer need to visit a place to describe it accurately?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/29/china-of-my-mind/', 'snippet': 'Does a fiction writer need to visit a place to describe it accurately?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I tell people that I have recently published a novel set in China, one of the first questions they ask is whether I’ve been there. My response seems to be a letdown. The expectant look on their faces shifts as they wonder why I chose to write about a place I’ve never visited. Sometimes I sense incredulity. What makes me think I can write about China? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China of My Mind', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T02:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Virginia Pye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Virginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a56f1a2-3f61-5f81-a4c6-ef517d12acad', 'word_count': 1155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a56f1a2-3f61-5f81-a4c6-ef517d12acad'}, {'abstract': 'Only 2 percent of counties in the United States are responsible for all death sentences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/30/opinion/the-slow-demise-of-capital-punishment.html', 'snippet': 'Only 2 percent of counties in the United States are responsible for all death sentences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More states are coming to recognize that the death penalty is arbitrary, racially biased and prone to catastrophic error. Even those that have not abolished capital punishment are no longer carrying it out in practice. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slow Demise of Capital Punishment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Slow Demise of Capital Punishment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T02:03:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfb01e99-1f73-53a3-b017-f2e74bdf7eb5', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfb01e99-1f73-53a3-b017-f2e74bdf7eb5'}, {'abstract': 'Some authors of a 1990s study worry that it oversold the long-term benefits of medication, discouraging important therapy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/30/health/adhd-experts-re-evaluate-studys-zeal-for-drugs.html', 'snippet': 'Some authors of a 1990s study worry that it oversold the long-term benefits of medication, discouraging important therapy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty years ago, more than a dozen leaders in child psychiatry received $11 million from the National Institute of Mental Health to study an important question facing families with children with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder: Is the best long-term treatment medication, behavioral therapy or both?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/us/STUDY/STUDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/30/us/STUDY/STUDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/us/STUDY/STUDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/us/STUDY/STUDY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A.D.H.D. Experts Re-evaluate Study’s Zeal for Drugs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A.D.H.D. Experts Re-evaluate Study’s Zeal for Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwarz, Al