count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b002f66-7634-555f-a672-c4d6e06ea9da'}, {'abstract': 'A distributor reacting to an online outcry withdrew Italian posters minimizing Chiwetel Ejiofor’s role in “12 Years a Slave.” Meanwhile Michael B. Jordan says he felt the weight of his own expectations in taking on the lead role in “Fruitvale Station.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/30/a-distributors-online-pressure-and-an-actors-personal-pressure/', 'snippet': 'A distributor reacting to an online outcry withdrew Italian posters minimizing Chiwetel Ejiofor’s role in “12 Years a Slave.” Meanwhile Michael B. Jordan says he felt the weight of his own expectations in taking on the lead role in “Fruitvale Stat...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Context matters, as Chiwetel Ejiofor can confirm. The star of “12 Years a Slave” was minimized on posters for the Italian version of the drama, which instead prominently featured Brad Pitt and Michael Fassbender. Mr. Pitt is a producer and has a small but pivotal part in the film; Mr. Fassbender, playing a brutal slaveholder, has drawn some acclaim. But neither are the lead, nor have they received the kind of attention that Mr. Ejiofor has for his searing performance. After an outcry online that the advertising was racist, the company that produced the posters withdrew them and apologized.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Distributor’s Online Pressure and an Actor’s Personal Pressure', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ejiofor, Chiwetel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, Michael B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T15:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3948702f-e8f8-5415-b384-49a3635b1cf3', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3948702f-e8f8-5415-b384-49a3635b1cf3'}, {'abstract': 'Bob’s Discount Furniture joins other retail investments by Bain like Michaels Stores and Burlington Stores. Bob Kaufman, pitchman extraordinaire, plans to remain the face of the company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/12/30/bain-to-buy-control-of-bobs-discount-furniture/', 'snippet': 'Bob’s Discount Furniture joins other retail investments by Bain like Michaels Stores and Burlington Stores. Bob Kaufman, pitchman extraordinaire, plans to remain the face of the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The private equity firm Bain Capital announced on Monday that it had agreed to buy a majority stake in Bob’s Discount Furniture, the chain of stores known for its low-tech commercials featuring its founder, Bob Kaufman.The company’s management team will continue to own a “significant stake” in the business, according to a news release announcing the deal on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bain to Buy Control of Bob’s Discount Furniture', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apax Partners LP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Bob's Discount Furniture", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KarpReilly LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T15:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'secti