ons', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Volgograd (Russia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T16:36:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f6c41cea-fc4c-578e-98b5-1506ae0d08c0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f6c41cea-fc4c-578e-98b5-1506ae0d08c0'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Springsteen’s new album, “High Hopes,” is due for release on Jan. 14, but was temporarily made available for download on Saturday by Amazon.com.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/30/springsteen-album-leaked-through-amazon-download/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Springsteen’s new album, “High Hopes,” is due for release on Jan. 14, but was temporarily made available for download on Saturday by Amazon.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Springsteen’s new album, “High Hopes,” made a brief appearance in MP3 form in the music download section of Amazon.com on Saturday, just over two weeks before its scheduled release date. Although the album could not be purchased and downloaded as a whole, all 12 of its songs could be purchased individually, Billboard reported. Except in the case of the title track, which has been available since Nov. 25, the\xa0loophole was closed quickly, but the album appeared on several file-sharing sites within hours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/30artsbeat-springsteen/30artsbeat-springsteen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 860, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/30artsbeat-springsteen/30artsbeat-springsteen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarge