n': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6daeb69-1537-564a-945a-2776466e418d', 'word_count': 1531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6daeb69-1537-564a-945a-2776466e418d'}, {'abstract': 'When a mechanic forgot to put oil in a Volvo S60, the oil pressure warning light never came on, alerting Volvo to a problem with the sensors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/automobiles/volvo-recalls-31000-cars-for-oil-pressure-sensor-problem.html', 'snippet': 'When a mechanic forgot to put oil in a Volvo S60, the oil pressure warning light never came on, alerting Volvo to a problem with the sensors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Volvo will recall nearly 31,000 S60 sedans with 5-cylinder engines from the 2011 and 2012 model years because of a problem with the oil pressure warning sensors. The automaker discovered the defect after a mechanic performing routine maintenance on one of the cars forgot to put oil in the engine before the owner drove it off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31VOLVO-image/31VOLVO-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31VOLVO-image/31VOLVO-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31VOLVO-image/31VOLVO-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31VOLVO-image/31VOLVO-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height':