14ed5f8d9'}, {'abstract': 'Schumacher is in a coma after hitting his head skiing; IndyCar announces that it is suing the company that promoted a 2013 series event in São Paulo, Brazil.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/automobiles/monday-motorsports-formula-one-champion-michael-schumacher-hospitalized-after-skiing-accident.html', 'snippet': 'Schumacher is in a coma after hitting his head skiing; IndyCar announces that it is suing the company that promoted a 2013 series event in São Paulo, Brazil.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Schumacher, the seven-time Formula One world champion who retired for the second time in 2012, underwent emergency surgery for brain trauma Sunday after a skiing accident in the French Alps. His manager, Sabine Kehm, said that he was skiing with his son on backcountry terrain near the Méribel ski resort when he fell and hit his head on a rock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31MOTORSPORTS-image/31MOTORSPORTS-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31MOTORSPORTS-image/31MOTORSPORTS-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31MOTORSPORTS-image/31MOTORSPORTS-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31MOTORSPORTS-image/31MOTORSPORTS-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31MOTORSPORTS-image/31MOTORSPORTS-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31MOTORSPORTS-image/31MOTORSPORTS-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/automobiles/31MOTORSPORTS-image/31MOTORSPORTS-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Motorsports: Formula One Champion Michael Schumacher Hospitalized After Skiing Accident', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumacher, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ecclestone, Bernie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T17:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7e3dec2-4f0d-5f2b-8f63-6067d9894987', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7e3dec2-4f0d-5f2b-8f63-6067d9894987'}, {'abstract': 'Since the early days of the Soviet Union, state officials have cared more about reporting good results than achieving them.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/30/powerlessness-and-pretense/', 'snippet': 'Since the early days of the Soviet Union, state officials have cared more about reporting good results than achieving them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Within two hours of a deadly bombing Sunday at the main railroad station in Volgograd, officials announced that they had identified the female suicide bomber. A name, a photo and a biography spread from news agency to news agency; law enforcement supplied journalists with details, including the tidbit that she had been married to two different Chechen rebel fighters, both now dead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Powerlessness and Pretense', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-30T17:27:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3e760f1-a2ac-5d5c-9ce9-e637525a70bc', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3e760f1-a2ac-5d5c-9ce9-e637525a70bc'}, {'abstract': 'The preparation for filming “August: Osage County” included a powerful book of back stories for each character.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/30/on-the-porch-in-osage-county/', 'snippet': 'The preparation for filming “August: Osage County” included a powerful book of back stories for each character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Weinstein Company gambled that opening its dark family dramedy “August: Osage County” two days after Christmas, instead of on Christmas (when everyone has enough dark family dramedy to contend with), would pay off at the box office. In five theaters, its take ranked with this season’s other dysfunctional family stories, like “Nebraska,” but may not have had the surge the studio was hoping for.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/augustcast/augustcast-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/augustcast/augustcast-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/augustcast/augustcast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/augustcast/augustcast-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/augustcast/augustcast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/augustcast/augustcast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/augustcast/augustcast-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'w