ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d96c841c-fea8-5395-a93d-6396ef09c9dc', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d96c841c-fea8-5395-a93d-6396ef09c9dc'}, {'abstract': 'Six institutions were chosen to explore how to set safety standards for commercial and private drones, train and certify their ground-based pilots, ensure that the aircraft will operate safely and avoid collisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/us/politics/us-names-domestic-test-sites-for-drone-aircraft.html', 'snippet': 'Six institutions were chosen to explore how to set safety standards for commercial and private drones, train and certify their ground-based pilots, ensure that the aircraft will operate safely and avoid collisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Aviation Administration will authorize test sites for drone aircraft in upstate New York, New Jersey and at least eight other states, the agency said on Monday, preparing for a time when unmanned aircraft of various shapes and sizes cruise over the landscape.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/us/DRONES/DRONES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/31/us/DRONES/DRONES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/us/DRONES/DRONES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/us/DRONES/DRONES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'