akdown,” on the shortlist for best foreign-language film, explains why he thinks observers liken this Belgian film to an American indie project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly everything about “The Broken Circle Breakdown,” Belgium’s shortlisted submission for the foreign-language Oscar, is improbable, starting with what first inspired it. When George W. Bush placed limits on stem-cell research in his first term, the Belgian playwright and actor Johan Heldenbergh was so angry that he decided to write a theater piece as a way of venting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Belgian’s American-Seeming Film', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baetens, Veerle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Groeningen, Felix van', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heldenbergh, Johan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T14:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81832ff1-8db6-5f93-aa2f-7f52a88c1e0d', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81832ff1-8db6-5f93-aa2f-7f52a88c1e0d'}, {'abstract': 'The archives of Kitchen Sink Press have been donated to the Rare Book & Manuscript Library at Columbia University.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/columbia-rare-book-library-gets-the-kitchen-sink/', 'snippet': 'The archives of Kitchen Sink Press have been donated to the Rare Book & Manuscript Library at Columbia University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cartoonists R. Crumb, Art Spiegelman and Al Capp have one thing in common. All were published, at one time or another, by Kitchen Sink Press, whose archives were recently donated to the Rare Book & Manuscript Library at Columbia University by Denis Kitchen, the press’s founder. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/30artsbeat-crumb/30artsbeat-crumb-jumbo.png', 'height': 642, 'width': 474, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/30artsbeat-crumb/30artsbeat-crumb-superJumbo.png', 'height': 642, 'width': 474, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/30artsbeat-crumb/30artsbeat-crumb-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/30artsbeat-crumb/30artsbeat-crumb-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/30/arts/30artsbeat-crumb/30artsbeat-crumb-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Columbia Rare Book Library Gets the Kitchen Sink', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitchen, Denis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T14:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/240a63dd-cd01-5457-8cec-e997c1f57680', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/240a63dd-cd01-5457-8cec-e997c1f57680'}, {'abstract': 'Governments aren’t always irresponsible.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/cynical-fantasies/', 'snippet': 'Governments aren’t always irresponsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing that happens when you try to have a rational discussion of Bitcoin, gold, and/or other libertarian causes is that you get a lot of cynical remarks about government (which is one of the clues that this is, to an important extent, about politics.) You say that there’s nothing putting a floor under Bitcoin’s value? Well, how do you know that the government won’t debase the dollar to nothing? Huh? Huh?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cynical Fantasies', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T14:13:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6bea19b-0ddb-5e0e-94cb-bb44bae2803c', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6bea19b-0ddb-5e0e-94cb-bb44bae2803c'}, {'abstract': 'The former Formula One champion Michael Schumacher, who sustained brain injuries in a skiing accident, remained in critical condition after a second operation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/sports/autoracing/michael-schumacher.html', 'snippet': 'The former Formula One champion Michael Schumacher, who sustained brain injuries in a skiing accident, remained in critical condition after a second operation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Doctors treating Michael Schumacher for the brain injuries he sustained in a skiing accident in the French Alps said Tuesday that there was “a slight improvement” in his condition after an overnight operation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Schumacher’s Condition Improves Slightly, Doctors Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Schumacher’s Condition Slightly Better, Doctors Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, John F', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumacher, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traumatic Brain Injury', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T14:32:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e387d8e6-2802-5ae4-a0c1-f819f4ef6897', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e387d8e6-2802-5ae4-a0c1-f819f4ef6897'}, {'abstract': 'A slice of Epiphany, a special glass for Coca-Cola an