yt://article/f76afe5e-fe21-5801-acae-3f738d0ee7ae'}, {'abstract': 'City investigators have made a curious finding: Compared to other municipal employees, a disproportionately large number of election workers died in the last two years.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/monitoring-elections-could-kill-you-well-sort-of/', 'snippet': 'City investigators have made a curious finding: Compared to other municipal employees, a disproportionately large number of election workers died in the last two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe it’s true, after all. There really was a lot of deadwood at the city’s much-maligned Board of Elections. Or perhaps all that pressure massaging the balky new electronic machines was too much. Or the thousands of openings for $200-a-day election inspectors on Election Days just happen to attract a high number of older retirees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monitoring Elections Could Kill You. Well, Sort Of.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T15:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e1ec194-8e5c-5129-ad27-9772a8253de6', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e1ec194-8e5c-5129-ad27-9772a8253de6'}, {'abstract': 'Depending on the interpreter, “The Wolf of Wall Street” is an irresponsible ode to fraudulent behavior or a guide to getting ahead in legal gray areas.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/the-many-lessons-wolf-teaches-us/', 'snippet': 'Depending on the interpreter, “The Wolf of Wall Street” is an irresponsible ode to fraudulent behavior or a guide to getting ahead in legal gray areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Depending on whom you ask, “The Wolf of Wall Street” is either a cautionary tale or a gleeful fable. (The screenwriter, Terence Winter, thought it was neither, preferring to present the facts without judgment.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/arts/wolfone/wolfone-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/31/arts/wolfone/wolfone-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/arts/wolfone/wolfone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/arts/wolfone/wolfone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/arts/wolfone/wolfone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/31/arts/wolfone/wolfone-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/31/arts/wolfone/wolfone-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Many Lessons ‘Wolf’ Teaches Us', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'pr