birth-of-the-greenback/', 'snippet': 'How the Supreme Court saved the dollar bill — and, perhaps, the Union cause during the Civil War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 30, 1861, Elbridge Gerry Spaulding, the chairman of the House Ways and Means Subcommittee on Banking and Currency, gave a speech on the House floor declaring that the nation was “never in greater peril than at this moment.” The Civil War was eight months old, but Spaulding’s concern wasn’t martial, but fiscal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Birth of the Greenback', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T17:22:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dawinder S. Sidhu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dawinder', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Sidhu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbc2063b-6c8d-5109-8353-a09a271bef83', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbc2063b-6c8d-5109-8353-a09a271bef83'}, {'abstract': 'What makes him think this subject is important enough to occupy his first days in office?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/12/31/deblasios-first-move-carriage-horses/', 'snippet': 'What makes him think this subject is important enough to occupy his first days in office?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor-elect Bill de Blasio, for all of his good qualities, has a problem prioritizing. While we wait for him to appoint his team (oh so slowly) and we wonder what his policies are going to be, exactly, on things like schools, Mr. de Blasio announced yesterday that one of his first acts will be … to ban carriage horses from Central Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DeBlasio’s First Move: Carriage Horses', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T17:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7beeaf46-404a-5b39-9062-851f079a8306', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7beeaf46-404a-5b39-9062-851f079a8306'}, {'abstract': 'It was not Beyoncé’s fault after all, and the blackout’s biggest impact was on the game itself, seeming to change the momentum and turning a snoozer into nail-biter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/sports/football/lacking-a-villain-super-bowl-power-failure-proves-the-hero.html', 'snippet': 'It was not Beyoncé’s fault after all, and the blackout’s biggest impact was on the game itself, seeming to change the momentum and turning a snoozer into nail-biter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks before flying to New Orleans to cover Super Bowl XLVII, I had finally crossed “The Dark Knight Rises” off my list of movies to watch.', 'source': 'The New York Ti