, is a source of heated debate in France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Wednesday, 12:52 p.m. | Until three days ago, when a French soccer star celebrated a goal for his club in England with a form of stiff-armed salute devised by a stand-up comic who stands accused of inciting hatred of Jews, the English-speaking world was largely unaware that the meaning of the gesture, called a quenelle, is a source of heated debate in France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Comic’s ‘Anti-System’ Salute Is Frequently Used to Mock Jewish Suffering', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dieudonne (1966- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-12-31T23:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5575132e-986a-5e6f-a761-496bceeb3197', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5575132e-986a-5e6f-a761-496bceeb3197'}, {'abstract': 'Judge Edward R. Korman of the Eastern District of New York found that the government does not need reasonable suspicion to examine or confiscate a traveler’s electronic device.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/01/01/business/judge-upholds-us-right-to-search-devices-at-border.html', 'snippet': 'Judge Edward R. Korman of the Eastern District of New York found that the government does not need reasonable suspicion to examine or confiscate a traveler’s electronic 